  "realms": {
    "Larion": {
      "name": "Larion",
      "basicInfo": "Larion is the physical world of the living — its lands, seas, and skies, and everything that walks under the sun. Its continents span tundra and desert, jungle and grassland, and civilizations have risen and fallen across them, leaving ruins and relics behind. In the present age, realms of varying size and power hold an uneasy balance, while vast stretches of wilderness remain unexplored. Its people range from ordinary folk living quiet lives to those who wield arcane power or serve the gods. Creatures both kindly and monstrous dwell in the wild places between settled lands.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Shadelands": {
      "name": "The Shadelands",
      "basicInfo": "The Shadelands is the plane of the dead: a grey country where restless spirits linger. Most of the dead pass on and are gone. Those who will not — too angry, too proud, too bound by things unfinished — stay, and sour, and turn to haunts and hungering dead. The dead shape the grey to their will: a weak shade raises a thin, formless mist, a strong one a vivid world held by its rage or grief or longing — a hall lit warm as the night it died, a garden in impossible bloom. The Shadelands presses against Larion wherever the dead break through. When a haunting will not rest, when the dead keep rising, the root of it runs down to here.",
      "known": false
    },
    "The Underworld": {
      "name": "The Underworld",
      "basicInfo": "The Underworld is the dark beneath the world: endless caverns and tunnels running under every land, threaded through the ruins of empires that fell in ages past and were buried where they stood. Little light reaches here that someone did not bring or make. Underground peoples have raised fortresses called deepholds among the dead cities, and many have no love for the surface. The old world keeps its wealth in the walls — relics and lost work, left for those bold enough to come down for it.",
      "known": false
    }
  },
