      "x": 0,
      "y": -1,
      "realm": "Larion",
      "known": true,
      "basicInfo": "Whitemoor is a country of open moor and drowned fen where the dead do not stay buried. Three old kingdoms once held it; two lie drowned out in the fen, and the third survives as Aldwall, the one walled town still standing, built of pale dwarf-stone no one can match now. Its king holds the town, and above it the Knights Vigilant keep their cliff-fortress — a sworn order of radiant arms who ride out against the moor's dead. The barrows of an older age cover the dry heath, and the drowned crowns sit full of grave-gold and grave-silver under the still water, for those hard enough to take it from the dead that guard it.",
