      "basicInfo": "An old oak-and-chestnut wood in Whitecliff Downs, famous for the moonbloom truffles beneath its roots. Pale chalk banks rise between the trees, and narrow paths wind through fern-filled hollows.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The kobolds from nearby Whitehill Kobold Warren regard moonbloom truffles as disgusting but know what halflings will pay for them. They dig around old harvesting holes, follow foragers, steal baskets, and sell their finds back to the villages. Their best customers are wealthy halflings unwilling to come into the woods themselves.\n\nThe finest moonblooms lie deep beneath undisturbed roots. Trained truffle-hogs can scent them where the kobolds find nothing.\n\nThe woodland crews are ordinary kobold scavengers concerned with food, money, and their own skins. They bluff, bargain, set crude snares, and attempt theft. They would rather escape with a basket than fight over it.",
