    "Ardan's Watch": {
      "name": "Ardan's Watch",
      "x": 10,
      "y": 4,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Silvervale",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Ardan's Watch is a prosperous, cosmopolitan city at the meeting of the Silverflow and Great North rivers, named for Ardan, the ancient hero who founded it. At its heart stands the Watchtower, an ancient elderstone tower and the seat of the League of Adventurers, from which roads and portals reach out across Larion. The city is a free state, governed by the Council of Champions — retired adventurers raised by merit rather than birth.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Lord Mayor runs the city day to day; the Council of Champions sets its course, and the City Guard answers to the Council. The League governs Ardan's Watch directly, but holds no authority beyond it — elsewhere it works by trust, contracts, and being useful enough that rulers ask its advice. From the Watchtower it tracks trouble across Larion and points adventurers toward whichever road needs them. Older elderstone spires stand among the roofs, repurposed or sealed.\nThe city is the most mixed place in Larion: ratfolk porters and scribes, foreign envoys, retired Champions, dwarven smiths, halfling teamsters, beastfolk guards, students down from Tarnholme, every kind of adventurer, and imps thickest in the Basement below. Horns, wings, tusks, tails, and stranger marks draw less notice here than a bad debt.\nOld Town belongs to the Thieves' Guild, and they are thieves in the ordinary way: they pick pockets, fence stolen goods, run the dice rooms and the pit, and smuggle. They keep an honor code — they hold their own turf, and they do not deal in bodies or prey on the helpless. The Syndicate keeps no such code, and wants the Basement: the buried market is the city's richest artery, and the Guild will not sell. The Guard enters Old Town carefully, by an old understanding.\nBelow Old Town lies the Basement, the city's lantern-strung buried market and pleasure district. From the Basement, the Delvers' Lift drops to Grell Hollows in the Underworld: adventurers ride down to delve the kobold-claimed imperial ruins, and the kobolds raid up out of the dark.\nThe Delvers' Lift is the only way down from Ardan's Watch into Grell Hollows: reach it by going through Old Town into the Basement, then ride it to The Scrabble.\nOutside the walls, the Field of Valor lies west, the City of Ancestors northwest, Gallows Wood north on the High Road, and Muckside across the river.",
      "areas": {
        "Thousandlights Market": {
          "description": "Just inside the gates, Ardan's Watch opens into Thousandlights Market: an old colosseum rebuilt into a permanent market of stalls, shops, balconies, and lantern-strung arches. At its heart is the Hearthfire, a great stone firepit with common benches where food and drink come from the surrounding stalls and a stranger who eats once is rarely a stranger by the time they leave. Outfitters, map-sellers, smithies, armorers, shield-schools, charm peddlers, and bootmakers crowd the outer ring. Ardan's statue stands near the market mouth, one bronze foot worn smooth by centuries of hands touching it for luck. The Watchtower rises above the market arches, and new adventurers spill into Thousandlights at all hours.",
          "paths": [
            "Watchtower - League Hall",
            "The Way of Coin",
            "The Sacred Way",
            "The Bargain Hoard"
          ],
          "images": {
            "establishingShot": {
              "crop": {
                "focus": {
                  "x": 50,
                  "y": 50
                },
                "zoom": 100
              },
              "imageUrl": "https://images.aidungeon.com/generated_content/0/images/area_images/fae96e03-b2f0-406a-a6b5-02ce7eb39982.png"
            }
          }
        },
        "The Bargain Hoard": {
          "description": "A deep stall built into one of the old colosseum's vaulted arches, its counter cut from a single slab of dark wood and its back wall shelved to the ceiling. Sef Pellanor's stock is arranged like a hoard rather than a shop: armour and blades racked by weight, potions in a locked case, and the few pieces worth real coin kept behind the counter where he can reach them without turning his back.",
          "paths": [
            "Thousandlights Market"
          ]
        },
        "Watchtower - League Hall": {
          "description": "The Watchtower's ground floor: a bright League hall lined with stained glass of famous adventurers. Long tables fill the center where crews form up, veterans compare routes, and young Coppers measure each other before their first outings. A Silvervale map and changing boards occupy one wall, while Mona Vashti, the hallmaster, keeps a table in view where newcomers receive guidance, introductions, and directions. Adventurers arrive, return, train, argue, and find their footing here.",
          "paths": [
            "Thousandlights Market",
            "Watchtower - Map Room",
            "Watchtower - Training Yard"
          ],
          "images": {
            "establishingShot": {
              "crop": {
                "focus": {
                  "x": 50,
                  "y": 50
                },
                "zoom": 100
              },
              "imageUrl": "https://images.aidungeon.com/generated_content/0/images/area_images/7b96a4a6-c8c8-41e7-a7fa-6f68777f81f6.png"
            }
          }
        },
        "Watchtower - Training Yard": {
          "description": "A quiet elderstone chamber set aside for combat training. Broad worn rings divide the floor, with chalked boundaries, low ward-lines, weapon racks, and target frames set into the walls. A few simple magical practice figures stand in recessed alcoves, their jointed bodies dull until called to motion. The open ground is large enough for a party to test movement, attacks, defenses, and control without an audience.",
          "paths": [
            "Watchtower - League Hall"
          ]
        },
        "Watchtower - Map Room": {
          "description": "A high floor of the Watchtower with tall windows looking over Thousandlights, the rivers, and the roads out of Ardan's Watch. The walls hold working maps of Silvervale, the Duchy of Drusavia and its city Drusavia, Carendon, Jade Tarn and Tarnholme Academy, Westmarch and Marrenford, Whitecliff Downs and Hillhome, Whitemoor and Aldwall, Redrock and the Citadel of the Pact, and the wider roads beyond. Boards around the walls gather copied letters, pins, route-markers, missing caravans, monster signs, grave-news, border rumors, and chapterhouse reports, so adventurers can read the shape of trouble before choosing which road to take.",
          "paths": [
            "Watchtower - League Hall",
            "Watchtower - Portal Hall"
          ],
          "images": {
