    "Muckside": {
      "name": "Muckside",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 3,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Silvervale",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A condemned district across the river from Ardan's Watch proper. Old warehouses and dockhouses list at bad angles where the ground has slowly given way beneath them. Most have partially collapsed. The city wrote it off generations ago rather than shore it up. No one lives here by choice — squatters, outcasts, and gang crews claim the sturdier ruins and fight over what's left. The bridges from the city side are unofficial crossings, rotting timber and rope.",
      "hiddenInfo": "No Watch patrols cross the river. The district polices itself, badly. Squatter camps and a few small gangs claim the sturdier buildings — they answer to the Thieves' Guild loosely if at all. Violence is common but small-scale. Most people here just want to be left alone and will be wary but not hostile to outsiders unless provoked. Ratkin are common here — more than anywhere else in the city.\n\nBeneath the ruins is a foundation layer called the Muckwarren, and below that, sealed plague crypts from a long-ago epidemic. Strong local taboo forbids entering the crypts — even the gangs won't go near. The bridges to Ardan's Watch are the only lifeline. Old Town's gangs treat Muckside as overflow territory.",
      "areas": {
        "The Dregs": {
          "description": "A muddy clearing ringed by leaning warehouse shells, the closest thing Muckside has to a town square. Fire pits mark where squatter camps have staked their ground. Across the river, Ardan's Watch rises clean and lit — close enough to hear the bells.",
          "paths": [
            "The Still Standing",
            "The Junkheap",
            "The Muckwarren"
          ]
        },
        "The Still Standing": {
          "description": "A squat dockhouse that earned its name by not falling down. The ground floor is a tavern — one long room, a tapped barrel, benches made from old cargo pallets. The crowd is Muckside locals: squatters, gang runners, people between worse places. Not welcoming, but not looking for trouble with strangers who buy a round.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dregs"
          ]
        },
        "The Junkheap": {
          "description": "An open-air market in a rubble-strewn yard where sellers lay out goods on tarps and blankets. Dented armor, mismatched boots, lockpick sets, unmarked bottles. No one asks where anything came from. Prices are negotiable and so are the weights.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dregs"
          ]
        },
        "The Muckwarren": {
          "description": "The old foundation layer beneath Muckside, reached through cracked cellar floors and half-collapsed stairwells. Low ceilings, standing water, the sound of the river filtering through the walls. Smuggler caches and fugitive camps in the drier chambers. The passage deeper — toward the plague crypts — is marked with old warnings scratched into the stone.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dregs",
            "The Plague Crypts"
          ]
        },
        "The Plague Crypts": {
          "description": "Sealed chambers where Muckside's dead were entombed during an epidemic rather than carried across the river to the City of Ancestors. The old seals are iron-banded stone, marked with faded ward-signs. The air is dead and dry. Niches line the walls, still occupied. No one from Muckside comes here willingly.",
          "paths": [
            "The Muckwarren",
            "The Hall of Skulls"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Skulls": {
          "description": "The deepest chamber beneath Muckside. A vast crypt with a vaulted ceiling held up by pillars of stacked stone sarcophagi. The dead here are old — older than the epidemic, older than the district above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Plague Crypts"
          ]
        }
      },
