    "Clachmore Village": {
      "name": "Clachmore Village",
      "x": -15,
      "y": -13,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Highheath",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "basicInfo": "A giantborn village in a broad mountain valley, where the Stone-Born clan raises highland cattle renowned throughout the region. The giantborn here claim descent from divine ur-giants who shaped the mountains in the first age. They settle disputes through wrestling and feats of strength, take their honor deadly seriously, and throw celebrations that shake the valley walls. Their annual cattle drive to the summer pastures is a highland tradition.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Stone-Born are gentle enough in peace but carry the old jotnar fire in their blood - insult their honor and you'll face a challenge that ends in broken bones or worse. Chief Brennan Big-Voice has led the clan for thirty years and still wins most wrestling matches despite his age. His daughter Ula wants to prove herself by driving cattle through disputed clan territory this summer, which could either earn her legend-status or start a feud. The village needs steady work done - fences mended, predators driven off, cattle retrieved from places too small for giantborn to reach - and they pay fairly in coin, cattle, or favors. They remember debts and grudges alike for generations.",
      "areas": {
        "The Drove Road": {
          "description": "A wide track worn by generations of cattle and the massive feet of their herders, winding down into a green valley ringed by peaks. Clachmore spreads across the valley floor ahead - stone longhouses sized for folk half again as tall as humans, cattle pens stretching toward the river, smoke rising from a dozen chimneys. The lowing of cattle carries on the wind. A standing stone marks the village boundary, carved with the clan's bull-head sigil.",
          "paths": [
            "The Village Green"
          ]
        },
        "The Village Green": {
          "description": "An open common at the village's heart where the Stone-Born gather for contests, celebrations, and moots. A ring of standing stones marks the wrestling ground - the grass inside worn to bare earth by generations of grappling. Lifting stones of graduated weights line one edge, the heaviest a boulder that supposedly only three giantborn have ever raised. Chief Brennan's longhouse dominates the north side. The Horned Hall tavern anchors the south, its doors sized for giantborn but with a smaller entrance cut alongside for ordinary visitors.",
          "paths": [
            "The Drove Road",
            "The Bull Pens"
          ]
        },
        "The Bull Pens": {
          "description": "Massive stone enclosures where the clan's prize bulls are kept separate from the main herds. These animals are enormous - shaggy, horned, and ill-tempered with strangers. The Stone-Born speak to them like old friends. A giantborn youth named Cormac tends the pens and knows each bull's lineage back seven generations. Beyond the pens, the valley opens into grazing lands where the main herds dot the hillsides, watched by herders with dogs and long crooks.",
          "paths": [
            "The Village Green"
          ]
        }
      },
