    "Fire Mountain": {
      "name": "Fire Mountain",
      "known": true,
      "x": 3,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Black Fells",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The smoking peak at the northern cape of the peninsula. A recent eruption split the mountainside and laid bare doors of black stone buried since the elder ages—and the doors stand broken open from within. The Greater Goblinate garrisons the mountain's exterior and the Church of the Pyre keeps rites at the breach. No one climbs here without the Goblinate's leave, and what the Pyre is doing in the dark below the mountain is the reason the whole peninsula was raised to war.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Fire Mountain is the most heavily guarded and most dangerous ground on the peninsula. The exterior is held by elite Goblinate troops and Church of the Pyre archpriests who treat any unauthorized approach as an enemy assault. Deeper in, a thing of blue fire wards the deep door and destroys all who are not the Dragon Queen's servants.\n\nThe mountain is a binding-works wrapped around a fire-breach in its heart. Ward-chambers, runic seals, and silent mechanisms hold the breach shut, laid over the colossal halls of an older age—giant-cut stone sized for beings three times a man's height, pillars carved with victories no one can read. The arch-djinn that Suleyvan the Sealer bound to keep the deep door. The guardian no longer keeps everyone out. Its watch is corrupted: it admits the Dragon Queen's servants and destroys everyone else, the seal turned into a gate. The doors of the breach stand broken open from within, and the mountain leaks heat and fire-things up through its halls—the eruption that split it was the Queen's power pressing through from below.\n\nThe Church works the breach to open the door the rest of the way. It sends standing demands down the Iron Road for what its rites require—relics of the elder ages, rare reagents, seal-touched objects, prisoners of particular descriptions—and convoys deliver them under escort to the garrison.\n\nAt the bottom of the mountain is the dormant gate: a lake of magma that is also a door, ringed with the heaped plunder of a dozen kingdoms, arranged and waiting for an arrival. The Dragon Queen, Atravoraxis, waits on the far side of it. She is absent by default and comes through only when the long work of the main quest turns the key; until then the prepared hall stands ready for someone who has not yet come.",
      "areas": {
        "The Queen's Door": {
          "description": "A Goblinate siege-camp ringing the breach high on the mountainside: palisades, watch-platforms, and barrack-tents pitched on the ash-slope, with elite troops and Pyre archpriests holding the approaches. Convoys are unloaded here under guard, their crates stacked and tallied. The split doors of the Fissure loom above the camp, smoke pouring from the gap.",
          "paths": [
            "The Fissure"
          ]
        },
        "The Fissure": {
          "description": "The rent in the mountainside where the eruption tore it open: a chasm of broken black rock venting smoke and heat, and within it two doors of black stone forty feet high, cracked apart and hanging from their hinges. The doors were forced from the inside, the stone around their frames shattered outward. A passage leads down through the broken doorway into the dark of the mountain.",
          "paths": [
            "The Queen's Door",
            "The Halls of the Mountain King"
          ]
        },
        "The Halls of the Mountain King": {
          "description": "Vast halls cut by giants in an age beyond memory, the ceilings lost in shadow, every doorway and stair built for beings three times a man's height. Colossal pillars carry carved friezes of forgotten victories. Over all of it, finer and far later, runs dwarven seal-work—runes and bindings chased across the elder stone. Wide ways lead deeper and down.",
          "paths": [
            "The Fissure",
            "The Wards"
          ]
        },
        "The Wards": {
          "description": "The binding-works the dwarven wardens raised in the mountain's depths: a complex of ward-chambers, runic seal-rings set into floor and wall, and silent mechanisms whose purpose is half-forgotten. Heat bleeds up through the stone, and the seal-light has guttered or gone dark in places. At the heart of the works stands the chamber of the deep door, where a watcher of blue fire keeps its corrupted guard. A final descent opens beyond it.",
          "paths": [
            "The Halls of the Mountain King",
            "The Magma Portal Sanctum"
          ]
        },
        "The Magma Portal Sanctum": {
          "description": "The lowest hall of the mountain, a great vaulted chamber built around a lake of molten rock that glows and seethes in the dark. The plunder of a dozen kingdoms is arranged around the lake—heaped gold, arms, regalia, and treasures without number, set out as if for an arrival. The magma's surface is the dormant gate, still and waiting. Heat fills the chamber to the edge of bearing.",
          "paths": [
            "The Wards"
          ]
        }
      },
