    "Clanhold Deepfire": {
      "name": "Clanhold Deepfire",
      "x": -23,
      "y": -12,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whiteholds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A forge-city built into the caldera of a volcanic vent in the white peaks, where Clan Deepfire has bent the mountain's fire to their craft. Lava channels light the streets and feed the forges, and the city's smiths and miners are the boldest in the Whiteholds — the ones who dig deepest, forge hottest, and take what the mountain is loath to give.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Clan Deepfire are the delvers, and their creed is heat, hunger, and the deep vein. They believe the mountain's wealth is meant to be taken by those bold enough to go down for it, that fire is the tool that opens stone and the spirit that drives a dwarf onward, and that caution is the comfort of clans with nothing left to win. They are proud, ambitious, acquisitive, and brave past the edge of sense. Their forges work emberglass and fire-craft no other hold can equal, and their miners cut deeper than any sane dwarf would.\n\nThe clan's wealth and pride run on the deep, which is also their unspoken shame. Their deepest delve, chasing a rich vein, broke into old sealed workings beneath the kingdom not long before Stonehome fell into the dark. Deepfire holds, loudly, that the delve was no sin and the fall was not their doing — that the seals failed because they were rotten, that the dead of Stonehome dug their own graves through neglect, not Deepfire's daring. They will not say aloud, even among themselves, that it was their vein that ran toward the dark. The clan that blames them is Icerune, and the grudge between them is a wound that does not close.\n\nDeepfire is split on the gold rush at Deepgate, but the loudest voices welcome it. The delvers swarming the pit are kindred spirits to them — bold folk braving the deep for what it holds — and the clan profits handsomely supplying them with fire-arms and forge-work. The cautious among them mutter that the Deep should never have been opened, but they are outvoted by those who say the deep was always meant to be braved.\n\nThane Kolvar Deepfire is ancient even for a dwarf, kept hale past his years by a lifetime breathing the volcanic heat, and he remembers the kingdom whole. He drove the clan's ambitions for a century and he will not hear that the great delve was a mistake. The clan's forges can work metals no other smiths can handle, and emberglass comes off their fires by the crate.",
      "areas": {
        "The Lava Terrace": {
          "description": "The heart of Deepfire's street-life, a broad district of homes and halls stepped down the caldera's inner wall on natural stone shelves, linked by bridges and stairs over the glowing lava channels below. The lava-light never fades, throwing warm orange across the carved stone faces of the buildings. The Cooled Cup tavern anchors the terrace, its doors thrown wide, its common room loud with smiths and miners come off the forges — famous across the white peaks for ale cooled deep in the rock, a rare luxury this near the fire. Stalls and shopfronts crowd the terrace-road, selling fire-craft and forge-work, and the talk runs as hot as the channels.",
          "paths": [
            "The Forge-Market",
            "The Lavaworks",
            "Cinderwing Eyries"
          ]
        },
        "The Forge-Market": {
          "description": "A bustling market terrace where Deepfire's work changes hands — blades and armor and tools laid out on stone counters, the orange shimmer of emberglass among the steel, traders come up from the lower holds to buy fire-craft found nowhere else. Apprentices run errands between the stalls and the forges, and the masters who sell here are proud, particular, and glad enough of custom. Bridges arch off over the lava channels toward the residential shelves, and the great forge-hall glows at the district's end.",
          "paths": [
            "The Lava Terrace",
            "The Lavaworks"
          ]
        },
        "The Lavaworks": {
          "description": "The great forge-hall at the city's heart, built around a channeled lava flow that gives endless heat. Smiths' stations are ranged in rings around the molten core, the most skilled closest to the fire, and the din of hammers never stops. Finished work cools on the racks — blades, armor, tools of rare make, the orange shimmer of emberglass among the steel. Apprentices haul coal and water through the heat-haze while journeymen work the great bellows.",
          "paths": [
            "The Lava Terrace",
            "The Forge-Market",
            "Cinderwing Eyries"
          ]
        },
        "Cinderwing Eyries": {
          "description": "A high warm gallery above the lava channels, open to the caldera's rising heat and strung with chains, perches, and little stone nesting-cups. Here Deepfire handlers raise cinderwings: small winged fire-salamanders, bright-eyed and coal-scaled, that glide on the heat rising from the channels and curl around a favored dwarf's shoulders like living embers. They are clever, vain, and loyal once bonded, useful for carrying sparks, finding warm seams, and warning of bad air in the deep cuts. Young cinderwings flit through the rafters and snap at thrown coal-beetles while handlers teach patient visitors how not to get singed.",
          "paths": [
            "The Lava Terrace",
            "The Lavaworks"
          ]
        }
      },
