    "Whitefang Hold": {
      "name": "Whitefang Hold",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A frost giant stronghold in the highest peaks of the north, a hollowed mountain held by a people three times the height of a man. It is reached only by the North Wind Pass, one of the most brutal roads in the world, where the wind comes off the peaks hard enough to put a traveler on the ground.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The frost giants of Whitefang Hold are a wild people of the high ice, proud, loud, and old in their ways, and the cold that killed the Northrealm is nothing to them — they were always here and always will be. They live as they always have: feasting, boasting, hunting, and settling rank by who can out-do, out-fight, and out-tell the rest. They are not a marauding horde; they are neighbors, on their own terms, dangerous chiefly to those who give them reason or bore them.\n\nThe giants and the ice drakes of the White Wyrmspire are locked in an old feud that neither side will end. Young giants prove themselves by climbing the Wyrmspire and stealing a drake's egg; the drakes answer by raiding the giants' herds and hunting their stragglers. It costs lives both ways, every generation, and both peoples seem to want it that way. A party seen near drake eggs may be taken for giants poaching the proof of manhood — or hired by giants too canny to make the climb themselves.\n\nIMPORTANT: The giants are not hostile by default, but they are perilous to anyone who fails their measure. They respect courage, endurance, and a good story, and they despise cowardice and flattery. A smallfolk who impresses them — by daring, by strength, by a tale well told, by surviving something — is fed, housed, and may find the giants will do things for them that no coin could buy. A smallfolk who bores them, lies to them, or shows weakness is, at best, pelted off the mountain. Jarl Magnar Longtooth rules the hold, and his favor is worth more than any door.",
      "areas": {
        "North Wind Pass": {
          "description": "A high mountain road through a notch in the peaks, where blizzards rage more often than not and the wind funnels through hard enough to knock a traveler flat. Sheer rock to either side, deep snow underfoot, and no shelter the length of it. The only way through is forward.",
          "paths": [
            "The White Gate"
          ]
        },
        "The White Gate": {
          "description": "The entrance to the hold — a rough-hewn opening in the mountainside, wide enough for three giants to pass abreast. No doors, no portcullis. High ledges flank the opening on both sides, set with stacked boulders, and sentries watch from them, deciding whether those who approach are worth announcing or worth pelting.",
          "paths": [
            "North Wind Pass",
            "The Jarl's Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Jarl's Hall": {
          "description": "A vast cavern where the giants gather, its ceiling lost in the dark above. Fire-pits blaze along the floor, throwing heat and shadow across stone slabs heaped with food and drink. The giants feast here, bellowing songs and challenges the length of the hall. The high seat stands at the far end, raised above the rest.",
          "paths": [
            "The White Gate",
            "The War Grounds"
          ]
        },
        "The War Grounds": {
          "description": "An open plateau behind the hold where the giants train, wrestle, and settle disputes — though to an outsider's eye the line between sport, contest, and a real fight is hard to find. The ground is bare rock and packed snow, worn down by heavy use. Trophies and trophy-poles from hunts and raids stand driven into the frozen earth.",
          "paths": [
            "The Jarl's Hall"
          ]
        }
      },
