    "The White Wyrmspire": {
      "name": "The White Wyrmspire",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 39,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A lone peak in the high north where ice drakes have nested since before the Northrealm. The drakes are enormous, ancient, and territorial, and they suffer no trespass. Hunters climb anyway, because drake bone, scale, and eggs are worth more than most people see in a lifetime, and a single rimebone haul buys a whole winter.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The ice drakes default hostile to anything on their peak and do not parley. They are not beasts but cunning, patient hunters with long memories. The eldest, the White Eye, has outwitted giant raiding parties for generations and remembers the faces of those who flee. Drakes glide down silent from the high ledges, strike, and climb out of reach to wait; they will harry a party for hours rather than commit to a losing fight, and they hold grudges across seasons.\n\nThe white bearfolk of Whitefang Hold and the drakes are locked in an old feud: young giants prove themselves by stealing drake eggs, the drakes answer by raiding the giants' herds, and neither side will stop. A party seen taking eggs may be mistaken for giants, or used by them.\n\nRimebone — the cold-bound bone of an ice drake — is the prize, worked into frostjade's rival as the answer to fire-things; scale armors against cold, and a single egg is worth a fortune to giants, collectors, and worse. The eggs sit in the nesting shelf; the oldest and richest remains lie in the White Eye's lair near the summit, where the cold is past natural and the climb back down is the hard part.",
      "areas": {
        "The Approaches": {
          "description": "The lower slopes, where the mountain narrows toward its peak. Open rock and wind-packed snow with little cover and a long fall on the outward side. Sheltered overhangs along the climb are wide enough to shelter a camp, screened from the wind and from the ledges above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Nesting Grounds"
          ]
        },
        "The Nesting Grounds": {
          "description": "A broad windswept shelf high on the peak. Nests of packed ice and stone, each the span of a wagon, cradle eggs the size of ale-barrels. The ledges above overlook the shelf on three sides, and old bone lies thick between the nests. The only cover is the nests themselves.",
          "paths": [
            "The Approaches",
            "The White Eye's Lair"
          ]
        },
        "The White Eye's Lair": {
          "description": "A deep cave near the summit. The entrance passage tightens to a crawl, then opens into a high vault of blue-white ice. Frozen spoil is set into the walls and floor — arms, bone, and the leavings of old kills, locked in the ice. A single way in and out.",
          "paths": [
            "The Nesting Grounds"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [],
