    "The Crevasse": {
      "name": "The Crevasse",
      "x": 14,
      "y": 31,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A great glacier in the high north, split clean down the middle, with the ruins of a white-stone city standing in the walls of the chasm — towers and halls part-crushed by the ice, part-exposed. The architecture matches nothing else in Larion, and no living people claim it. What can be carried out of it sells for a fortune to those who collect such things, which is reason enough for some to climb down.",
      "hiddenInfo": "No one knows who raised the white city or how long the ice has held it. It is older than the Northrealm, older than the oldest stories of the white bearfolk, and nothing the dwarves have recorded names it. The builders are still here, and they do not welcome visitors.\n\nIMPORTANT: The city's dead and its guardians default hostile to intruders who go deep, and they do not parley. Its old rulers remain as ice-mummies — the desiccated, frost-preserved dead in their halls, cold and patient and slow to rouse, but relentless once they do. They command the coldstone constructs: figures of the same white stone as the city, carved and bound by the builders, which stand motionless until the mummies wake them and then move to defend the halls. The constructs are the muscle; the mummies are the will behind them. Disturbing the deep chambers wakes both.\n\nThe white-stone relics of the city — devices, ornaments, and worked pieces of the builders' craft — are the prize, and the deepest and richest of them lie in the White Hall with the mummy-lords that keep them. The relics do not always behave: some are inert, some are not, and which is which is not always plain until carried.",
      "areas": {
        "The Rim": {
          "description": "The lip of the chasm, where the glacier splits in two. The gap runs for miles and drops hundreds of feet. Below, white towers and broken walls jut from both ice faces at angles, half-encased, half-clear. The only ways down are rope and a long, exposed climb against the ice.",
          "paths": [
            "The Crevasse Floor"
          ]
        },
        "The Crevasse Floor": {
          "description": "The bottom of the chasm, between two walls of glacier shot through with buried white stone. Fallen masonry and sheared blocks of ice litter the ground, with intact sections of the city standing among them. The light is blue and dim, filtered down through the ice overhead. Sound is close and muffled here.",
          "paths": [
            "The Rim",
            "The White Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The White Hall": {
          "description": "A great structure part-exposed in the ice wall, entered through a gap where the glacier has sheared it open. Within, a vaulted hall of white stone stands cracked but whole, its floor smooth and its columns sized larger than a hall for men would need. Figures of white stone stand among the columns. The cold deepens toward the back, where the hall runs into unbroken ice.",
          "paths": [
            "The Crevasse Floor"
          ]
        }
      },
