    "Fort Redclaw": {
      "name": "Fort Redclaw",
      "x": -18,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "An ice-fort in the high north, carved from glacier and packed snow by the claws of the white bearfolk who hold it — the nanukin, a towering people of the cold, sheathed in white fur and armored for war. Fort Redclaw is the seat of the Redclaw line, who keep this stretch of the ice for the nanukin Kingdom of Aurora. Walls of packed ice stand thick enough to turn a battering-ram, and the tunnels run wide enough for an armored bearfolk to pass at the shoulder.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The white bearfolk (nanukin) of Fort Redclaw were never broken by the cold the way the snowlanders were. The freeze that killed the Northrealm is, to them, only the weather of home — they were always a people of the high ice and they live well in it. They hold the fort as a garrison of the nanukin Kingdom, maintaining the line's claim on the southern ranges, and they regard the human survivors clinging to their warm springs with something between pity and bafflement.\n\nThey are not hostile to outsiders. They are pragmatic and direct: they tolerate visitors who are useful or interesting, trade and share what they know, and hire capable smallfolk for work that wants someone smaller or quicker than a bearfolk. They have no patience for flattery or empty words. Everything here runs on dominance and respect, and respect is bought with deeds — a hard task done, a strong hand in a contest, courage shown rather than claimed. A stranger who proves themselves rises in their regard from tolerated, to trusted, to one the chief will hear; a stranger who wastes their time does not.\n\nChief Redclaw rules from the great hall, where the Ice Throne is hacked from a single block of glacier. Each chief carves a new throne with their own claws on taking command, and the old thrones are broken, so the seat in the hall is always the work of the one who sits it.",
      "areas": {
        "The Ice Road": {
          "description": "A track across open glacier toward a white mass that barely shows against the white land behind it — the fort is hard to make out until you are close on it. Armored nanukin sentries watch from the walls, tall and pale and unhurried.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gate"
          ]
        },
        "The Gate": {
          "description": "A passage cut through walls of packed ice many feet thick, the surfaces scored deep with the claw-marks of their making. The way is wide and high — built to the scale of armored bearfolk, who stand guard to either side, a head taller than a tall man and broad as a door.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ice Road",
            "The Great Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Great Hall": {
          "description": "The fort's central chamber, carved from solid glacial ice. The Ice Throne stands at the far end — a rough seat hewn from a single block, still bearing the claw-marks of the chief who cut it. Fire-pits burn down the length of the hall, and the nanukin gather here to eat, drink, argue, and settle matters by strength.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gate",
            "The Dens",
            "The Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Dens": {
          "description": "Tunnels branching off the great hall into sleeping chambers carved from the ice, wide and low. The nanukin den in groups for warmth, armor and weapons stacked within reach.",
