    "Dun Solas": {
      "name": "Dun Solas",
      "x": -7,
      "y": -38,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Highheath",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A dwarven city in a vast cavern lit by the Eye, a great circular opening in the ceiling far above. At the cavern's bottom lies Lake Two-Waters, fed by underground rivers and by Skyriver, a waterfall pouring down through the Eye. From the lake the walls curve up and away in tiered ring-roads, each lined with beautiful stonework facades cut from the living rock. The terrace farms grow rare mushrooms and lichens famed in brewing and alchemy, and the city is renowned for fine metalwork and mechanisms so delicate they seem alive. It is a Free City, beholden to no clan, busy and prosperous and welcoming to those who respect its ways.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Dun Solas is the heart of trade, coin, and crime in Highheath and it stays free by keeping its two great neighbors at each other's throats just gently enough. Clan Stonewall and Clan Stormhammer both keep kin-halls and factors in the city, and both are openly working to own it without being seen to own it — chasing council seats, trade-shares, contracts, marriages brokered for advantage, and the question of whose law runs on which ring. The merchant council that governs the city survives by keeping the two from open feuding.\n\nA generation back a Stonewall–Stormhammer wedding meant to seal the peace turned at the feast — a pointed toast, an old word about Varric's Span — and within an hour the whole city had picked a side and a wedding had become a festival had become a five-ring, lake-to-summit dwarf melee that took three days to burn out and nearly brought the Iris down to stop it.\n\nThe Trade Guild is the city's competent neutral institution and the surest way for a clanless adventurer to make a name. The Guild keeps the overland roads safe — the passes, the caravans, the high country where the trade runs — and solves the city's own troubles: theft rings, contract fraud, a clan faction reaching too far, a fixer rigging a contest, a fence moving rustled cattle. The Guild also holds the only sanctioned passage to the deep roads beneath the city and guards who goes down.\n\nBeneath the honest city run the Undervaults, where the Syndicate keeps the dark side of every trade above — smuggling past the clan tolls,, fixing council contracts, and moving soulstones north toward buyers in the white mountains. Renegade and exiled dwarves, oath-broke factors, and clan castoffs do the work nobody clean will touch.\n\nIn crisis the city seals itself by closing the Iris, a great mechanism of metal plates that slides across the Eye.",
      "areas": {
        "Edge of the Eye": {
          "description": "A broad stone platform high on the cavern wall, ringing the topside aperture of the Eye where it opens to the sky. The Waterdrop's pulley-lifts descend from here into the city below, and the great metal plates of the Iris stand ready around the opening's rim. The Long Stair spirals down the inside of the cavern wall alongside the lifts, little used by choice.",
