    "Deepgate": {
      "name": "Deepgate",
      "x": -1,
      "y": 29,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whiteholds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A boomtown sprawled around the great crater in the white peaks where Stonehome, the dwarves' shared capital, fell into the dark. At the crater's bottom gapes the mouth of the Darek Deep — the buried halls of the elder dwarves, full of ancient treasure and the constructs that still guard it. Adventurers come from across Larion to delve the fallen city and the dead halls beneath it, and a lawless rush-town has grown around the rim to outfit them, buy their hauls, and bury the ones who don't come back.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Deepgate is a delver-city built on a grave. Stonehome was the seasonal capital both clans shared, and when its seals failed it dropped whole into the dark, empty but for its dead, opening into the Darek Deep below — the Underworld halls of the elder dwarves who served the demon-princes of Ur in the old empire. It was sacrilege, for ages, to seek the Darek dark. Now it is torn wide open, and a gold rush has swarmed the crater: crews, sellswords, tinkers, wizards, and fortune-hunters of every species, all here to plunder the dead city and the elder halls beneath. The town is loud, rough, and rich, and no single authority holds it.\n\nThe prize underneath is the kingdom itself. Stonehome's throne-hall lies down in the dark now, and whoever reclaims it reclaims the crown neither clan will yield. So both clans keep a presence on the rim and grind at each other in the open: Clan Deepfire half-backs the rush, the delvers being kindred spirits and the trade rich, holding that the deep was always meant to be braved; Clan Icerune wants the Deep sealed again and the sacrilege ended, and seethes that they cannot simply wall a pit with a whole city grown around its mouth. Neither will yield the throne to the other and neither can take it, so they circle, deal, and undercut one another while the crater fills with strangers.\n\nThe Syndicate has come for the Deep in force. The High Men who rule the Syndicate have named the Darek dark their highest prize, and they do not need open war with dwarf clans to take it — they have coin enough to simply buy the rush. They fund crews, fence Darek salvage, and corner the trade in soulstones coming up the pit, and their hand in Deepgate is Greloq's Company, the richest and most hated delving outfit on the rim, who hold the Old Keep above the town and get to the best finds first by every dirty means there is.\n\nThe Deep gives nothing freely — the elder constructs still guard the halls, the morlocks press up from below, and sometimes something climbs the pit on its own. The town's rhythm is the delve: gear up, form a crew, go down, fight for what you find, and haul it back up to sell. The Deep End is where it all happens — crews form there, deals are struck, and the veterans who lived through a delve tell you which halls will kill you.",
      "areas": {
        "The Rimside Market": {
          "description": "Where the road ends and Deepgate begins, a sprawl of stalls and counters ringing the lip of the great crater, the fallen city's broken towers just visible tilting into the dark far below. The trade is Darek salvage and the gear to win it — black iron blades, construct-shell bracers, ward-stones, soulstones sealed in lead cases, and stranger finds that change by the day — sold by hawkers shouting over one another. Tinkers pull apart elder mechanisms at their benches. Two stone halls face each other across the market's width, one flying Deepfire's colors and one Icerune's. Adventurers, sellswords, and folk of half the species in Larion crowd the rim.",
          "paths": [
