    "Fallsmeet": {
      "name": "Fallsmeet",
      "x": 1,
      "y": 1,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Fallsmeet is a prosperous walled village in a green Drusavian dale, built where two upland streams plunge past a rocky spur and meet below Castle Twinfall. Its Open Games draw competitors, patrons, and visitors from across Larion for martial, magical, and athletic contests. Craftspeople sell fine equipment, local households back new talent, and the taverns fill with rivals and friends.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Since the Liberation ended the vampire lords' rule in Drusavia, Fallsmeet has accepted House Avarre as its ruling family. The house's claim rests on both the adventurer couple at its root and its enduring compact with the dragonkin households whose forebears were held as the old lord's guards and hound-handlers. Those households now hold land, workshops, Games offices, and commands in the village watch.\n\nMost residents are human or dragonkin, with established dwarf and gnome households among them. Dwarves are prominent among Fallsmeet's smiths, stoneworkers, competitors, and weapons judges. Gnomes are common among its alchemists, performers, and Games officials.\n\nThe Open Games hold martial, magical, and athletic contests on the riverside grounds and across nearby meadows, woods, slopes, and streams. Competitors face one another and the terrain in duels, races, archery matches, magical trials, and team contests. New competitors enter their first trial as the Uncolored, without an announced title, patron, or public history. Afterward, local workshops, taverns, households, and clubs may offer their colors, equipment, training, or sponsorship. House Avarre provides judges and maintains the grounds but never sponsors competitors or wagers on them.\n\nTwinfall Hounds are enormous living dogs with mortal bodies and Shadeland ancestry. They can track living and spectral quarry through darkness, fog, and lesser concealment, but Fallsmeet raises them as affectionate watch, rescue, and tracking animals. Dragonkin kennel families maintain the oldest lines.\n\nColonies of intelligent mistbats—great cave bats clever enough to learn complex signals and carry a lightly equipped rider—live in the high caves above the falls. Trained mistbats carry riders, rescue slings, messages, and light lines across the ravines.\n\nFallsmeet closes its gates before dark. Twinfall Hounds patrol the walls, while mistbat riders search for travelers caught in the hills.",
      "areas": {
        "The Meeting Waters": {
          "description": "The two streams reunite beneath a many-arched stone bridge inside Fallsmeet’s lower wall. The lower gate, village road, and riverside paths meet beside grassy banks, broad steps, and a calm pool. From the bridge, the village terraces rise toward Castle Twinfall between the two falls; the White Wheel stands over one bank and the Open Grounds spread along the river below.",
