      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Earthsky is a volcanic island famous for its glassworkers, who turn its mineral-rich black sand into everything from common bottles to enchanted mirrors. At dusk the islanders light thousands of handmade glass lanterns until the whole island glows, a constellation of earthbound stars that ships can see from miles out across the dark water.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Earthsky is a quiet, prosperous island and one of the few easy places in the Swordlaw sea — no flag flies here, no crew holds it, and people come down to it between voyages to rest, spend, and be no one for a while. It lives by glass. The black volcanic sand yields glass of unusual clarity and strength, and the common trade in bottles, panes, and vessels is only the floor of it. The real money is in the magical work: enchanted mirrors that show a shapeshifter's true face or break an illusion, spirit-bottles that trap ethereal things, scrying orbs, and glass blades and arrowheads keen enough to matter. A buyer who wants such work comes to Earthsky for it.\n\nThe island is welcoming to outsiders and runs on a few warm customs rather than any law. The lantern-lighting at dusk is the heart of it: flame passed wick to wick across the island until it glows. A dark house on Earthsky is an empty one, and a visitor is given a lantern of his own before he leaves — the islanders hold that no one should sail away from Earthsky unlit.\n\nGoods here are the glasswork itself: fine bottles and mirrors, spirit-bottles and scrying orbs, glass weapons, and made-to-order enchanted pieces from the master enchanters on Glassworks Row. Loot is the same trade — a spirit-bottle worth a fortune to the right buyer, a true-seeing mirror, a glass blade.",
