    "Wolfpack Lodge": {
      "name": "Wolfpack Lodge",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A fortified warrior lodge of massive rough-hewn timber, raised on the open Wold within reach of the Gods-Anvil. Home of the Wolfpack, an orc-founded company of hunters, fighters, shamans, scouts, healers, beast handlers, berserkers, and beast-bonded champions who take the hunts and battles too great for ordinary warriors. The compound is both home and training ground. It is open to any people who master themselves, stand by their companions, and defend the Wold against those who would conquer it.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Rowdy, competitive, intense, and reverent all at once. Sparring never stops, feats of strength are celebrated loudly, and the walls are hung with the trophies of slain monsters. The Wolfpack is a warrior society first and a mercenary company second: it takes gold, but its loyalty is to the pack and to the Wold, and it will not take work that harms either.\n\nThe Wolfpack's standing is earned in public. An outsider may enter as a Trial-Hunter and attempt one witnessed proving deed. Success earns a pack clasp and recognition as a Packmate. Three further recognized pack deeds earn the name Proven Hunter. A Proven Hunter may choose to seek a beast-spirit at the Spirit Hearth; if hunter and spirit both accept the bond, the hunter becomes Beast-Bonded. Four serious recognized deeds after the bond may earn recognition as a Pack-Captain trusted to lead lodge contracts and other packmates. The singular Pack-Leader governs the lodge; Pack-Captains do not replace that office.\n\nThe heart of the lodge is its spirit-tradition. Proven Hunters may meet a beast-spirit at the Spirit Hearth and borrow its senses, protection, and physical nature. Wolf is traditional, but bear, boar, great cat, raptor, serpent, and stranger Wold beasts may answer. The bond is voluntary and mutual, never assigned merely from a hunter's class or ancestry. Fury is a respected discipline here, but neither Berserker training nor Fury is required for membership, advancement, or the bond. The Spirit Cellar is not where bonds are made: it is a place of containment for those who lose themselves to fury or an uncontrolled shape.\n\nThe lodge knows the dark mirror of its own craft. The Wrath-Speakers took battle-fury and gave it to demons for raw, ruinous power. The Wolfpack despises them as everything its discipline is meant to prevent, and gladly takes contracts against them and the Oathbreakers they serve.\n\nThe Wolfpack hires out for coin and for cause. Hunts against dangerous beasts, war against raiders and Oathbreakers, rescue, escort, and muster when the Wolds are pressed all count as pack work when they protect people, companions, or the land. Recognition comes through named deeds reported before the Great Lodge, not paperwork.",
      "x": -19,
      "y": -2,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Orc Wolds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Palisade Gate": {
          "description": "The sole entrance to the compound, heavy timber gates set in walls of sharpened logs. Watchtowers flank the entry, manned by archers.",
          "paths": [
            "The Training Grounds"
          ]
        },
        "The Training Grounds": {
          "description": "A broad, muddy central yard of sparring circles and wooden practice dummies, the hub of the lodge's daily life. Warriors of every kind train here, duel for standing, and keep their gear; the ground connects every building in the compound.",
          "paths": [
            "The Palisade Gate",
            "The Great Lodge",
            "The Iron Forge",
            "The Beast Kennels",
            "The Spirit Hearth"
          ]
        },
        "The Great Lodge": {
          "description": "A massive longhouse that serves as mess hall, sleeping quarters, and meeting place, a central fire-pit burning at its heart. Contracts are posted here, and it is the lodge's social hub—drinking, gambling, boasting, and the trading of rumor and news from across the Wold.",
          "paths": [
            "The Training Grounds",
            "The Pack-Leader's Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Iron Forge": {
          "description": "An open-air smithy for repairing heavy armor and sharpening oversized weapons, built for durability over beauty. A place for trade, repair, and the crafting of the heavy gear the pack's shock troops favor.",
          "paths": [
            "The Training Grounds"
          ]
        },
        "The Beast Kennels": {
          "description": "Enclosures housing the great war-wolves that fight alongside the pack. Handlers train and bond with the animals here, and recruits learn to fight beside a beast before any are deemed ready to bond with a spirit.",
          "paths": [
            "The Training Grounds"
          ]
