    "Garden": {
      "name": "Garden",
      "x": -2,
      "y": -11,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Elfwood",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "basicInfo": "A wood elf village spread across clearings in the deep Everwood, where homes of stone and wood stand among towering trees. Gardens grow beside wildflowers along the banks of a river that feeds a clear lake. Halflings, humans, and gnomes live here alongside the wood elves.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The wood elves of Garden say the settlement dates to the Sundering of elvenkind. In the Kindred War, those who would become wood elves refused to fight their brethren. A legendary figure called He Who Walks Beside is said to have guided them to this safe place and then perished in its defense. In his memory, wood elves mark births, arrivals, and deaths by repeating his last words: 'May you walk in beauty.'\n\nGarden has no leaders. Decisions happen by talk at the Hearth until everyone agrees or gives up, and the wood elves consider this the height of wisdom. They are certain they were right to walk away from the war — they pity Canopy its politics and Adamant its glory.\n\nThe place runs on its regulars more than any rule. An elder holds court at the Hearth and settles quarrels by outlasting them. The halflings have annexed the best sun-patches on the Green and boast about what they can coax out of cold soil. And the rangers — the finest in the Everwood, and quietly the only ones in Garden who pay attention to the world outside it — bring the news, escort the travelers, and carry a private, affectionate exasperation at how relaxed everyone else gets to be. They know the deep forest better than anyone alive and are the best source of word on what stirs beneath the canopy.",
      "areas": {
        "The Trackless Way": {
          "description": "One minute, forest. The next, the trees widen, light softens, running water burbles. A tended herb bed here, a woodpile stacked neatly against a trunk there. As if out of nowhere, cottages with smoke rising from them. No one can say exactly where the forest ends and Garden begins.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hearth",
            "The Green",
            "Lakeside"
          ]
        },
        "The Hearth": {
          "description": "The gathering place at Garden's center, where an ancient oak shades long tables and stone fire pits. Meals are communal and everyone is welcome, including the stranger who arrived an hour ago and is already being argued at. An elder usually holds the head of the table, settling disputes by talking until the parties forget what they were fighting about. A small shrine to the Lady of the Hearth stands where the oak's roots break the surface, tended with wildflowers; nearby, a carved stone bench marks a shrine to the Lord of the Open Hand.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trackless Way",
            "The Green",
            "Lakeside",
            "The Lodge",
            "Roothold",
            "Newgarden"
          ]
        },
        "The Green": {
          "description": "Garden plots and orchards spread between the trees - vegetables, herbs, berry bushes, medicinal plants, some cultivated, some wild. The halflings have claimed the best sun-patches and grow things that have no business surviving this far north, a fact they will explain to anyone who slows down enough to be caught. The healers work here too, drying herbs on racks and brewing tinctures in an open-air workshop.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trackless Way",
            "The Hearth",
            "Roothold"
          ]
        },
        "Lakeside": {
          "description": "A clearing where the river opens into a still lake. The water is clear to the bottom, cool and bright. Smooth rocks line the shore. Wood elves swim here at every opportunity, and consider anyone who won't a little tragic.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trackless Way",
            "The Hearth",
            "The Lodge"
          ]
        },
        "The Lodge": {
          "description": "A long timber hall where Garden's rangers gear up before heading out. Bows and traveling cloaks hang from pegs. A map of the region covers one wall, marked with sightings and warnings. The rangers are Garden's connection to the world beyond - they bring news, escort travelers, and deal with whatever the forest sends, while the rest of the village gets to pretend the world beyond is someone else's concern.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hearth",
            "Lakeside"
          ]
        },
        "Roothold": {
          "description": "A grove of ancient trees where the eldest wood elves teach whoever wants to learn, for as long as they want to learn it - druidic arts, old magic, herbcraft, the speech of birds, the patterns of weather, the slow deep knowledge of the forest. A few carved benches. A fire circle.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hearth",
            "The Green"
          ]
        },
        "Newgarden": {
          "description": "A clearing at Garden's edge where a few homes stand and space remains for more. Someone is always halfway through building something, unhurriedly.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hearth"
          ]
        }
      },
