    "The Ashfield": {
      "name": "The Ashfield",
      "x": 36,
      "y": -11,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Elfwood",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "basicInfo": "A stretch of blighted ground where nothing grows right. The trees are blackened but alive, the soil is warm to the touch, and ash falls like snow from a sky that's clear everywhere else. A great battle of the Kindred War was fought here, and elves of both kindreds hold it cursed ground, forbidden to enter.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Hundreds of elves died here by fire-magic, and the ground remembers. The ash that falls is no natural ash; it is a magical echo of the battle, repeating without end. Fire-magic runs strong here and all other magic falters, which is why the Church of the Pyre has claimed the place as holy ground. The Pyre preaches that the rotten old world must be burned away, and to them a battlefield that still burns an age later is altar and proof at once. Their rites here are slowly making the blight worse, widening the dead ground year by year, and if they are left to finish, the burning could spread across a great stretch of the Everwood.\n\nThe elven taboo is deeply felt — both high elves and dark elves lost kin here, and both peoples' histories record the battle as a shame. That makes the field impossible to garrison permanently. The Pyre knows this and trades on it. The cultists do not live here; they rotate in for their rites and withdraw into the forest or underground, and their camps are built to be abandoned in an hour. When the High Wardens break taboo to sweep the field, they find cold fire-pits and scorched circles and no one to punish. The cultists always come back.",
      "areas": {
        "The Ashfall": {
          "description": "Where the blight begins. Healthy forest gives way to blackened trunks and warm ground over a few dozen paces. Ash drifts down from nowhere. The air tastes of smoke.",
          "paths": [
            "The Burning Ground"
          ]
        },
        "The Burning Ground": {
          "description": "The battlefield's heart, where the earth is bare and cracked and warm enough to feel through boot soles.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ashfall",
            "The Scar Pit"
          ]
        },
        "The Scar Pit": {
          "description": "A crater at the field's center where the killing blow of the battle landed.",
          "paths": [
            "The Burning Ground"
          ]
        }
      },
