    "Sanctuary": {
      "name": "Sanctuary",
      "basicInfo": "The one great city of the deep Everwood, and the only place in it where outsiders may live. Sanctuary stands by the Pact of Sanctuary, the old agreement that lets a walled city exist in the high elves' wood - its stone raised by its founders, its wards woven by the elves, neither permitted without the other. There is no room to spread inside the walls, so the city climbs and delves, packed tight and loud, every quarter stacked on the last. The wood presses close on every side.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Sanctuary governs itself through a city council, by the high elves' leave under the Pact. The city watch keeps the peace within the walls; the high elves' wardens keep it beyond them, in the wood.\n\nEvery people of Larion has a foothold here, because Sanctuary is the one place in the Everwood that will have them. Dwarves hold the Underhalls below and work the forges; halflings terrace the Greenwarren; humans run the canals. High elves come and go as the wood's masters but keep no quarter of their own. The lower lanes are as mixed as any in Larion - gnome artificers, foxkin and ratfolk traders, demonborn and the odd minotaur, wood elves passing through.\n\nThe city runs hot and close. With every people of Larion stacked atop the last and no ground to spare, the quarters bicker like neighbors over a shared wall - whose festival has the canal this week, whose forge-smoke is fouling whose terrace, whose guild had the dock first. It is a proud city for all that, and a generous one in its rough way: a stranger who pulls their weight is a neighbor by the second week, and a stranger who doesn't is talked about in four languages. Newcomers arrive daily off the forest roads, and Sanctuary finds room, because finding room is the one thing it has always had to do.",
      "x": 1,
      "y": 2,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Sanctuary Vale",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "Pact Square": {
          "description": "The great square at the city's heart. Council Hall and the Watch Tower stand over the high end; the rest is market, packed wall to wall and stacked up the surrounding tenements. At the center stands the Pact, carved into a tall stone — the agreement that lets the city be, with the day's proclamations and bounties nailed to the post below it where a herald reads them out. An herbalist sells salves, spell ingredients, and charms. A row of stocks stands under the Watch Tower, whatever petty offenders the watch has taken left in them for the crowd. Food-stalls crowd the gaps.",
