        "The Shrine of Mother Mayreth": {
          "description": "A small freestanding shrine wedged between tenements off Pact Square. Inside, the centerpiece of the vaulted chamber is a masterwork wooden statue of Mother Mayreth, depicted as a beautiful half-elf woman with a shepherd's crook. In her day, Mayreth, a cleric of the Lady of Mercy, uncovered a plot to kidnap poor girls of the city. Her followers have sought to put an end to the ongoing abductions ever since. The walls are hung with carved plaques left in thanks by the families of girls brought safely back. A Keeper tends the shrine and takes word of any gone missing, organizing the search for the newly lost and efforts to catch those responsible.",
