    "Adamant": {
      "name": "Adamant",
      "x": -21,
      "y": -26,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Elfwood",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "basicInfo": "A high elven fortress-city built into a gorge of silver-white adamant stone. Waterfalls pour through the chasm in sheets of mist and thunder. But step through the Gorge Gate and the fortress reveals a green valley along the river, warm and sheltered, where gardens and orchards grow beneath the high walls. The Legion of the Vigil garrisons the fortress and guards the Everwood.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Adamantines believe Canopy has grown soft, too taken with trade and politics, and has forgotten why the Sundering happened. They see themselves as the true defenders of elvenkind and the Everwood. The Legion recruits outsiders and treats them as equals once they've proven themselves — a radical stance by high elven standards. New recruits drill hard but are welcomed into a brotherhood. Veterans who settle in the valley raise families, tend gardens, and answer the horn when it sounds.\n\nSecretly, the Legion conducts raids into the dark elf tunnel network. The Sundering's terms forbid both sides from entering each other's territory. Adamant has stopped respecting this bargain. They hit dark elf outposts and collapse tunnels; the dark elves retaliate; and this quiet war has been escalating for decades. It is why dark elf incursions near Adamant run worse than anywhere else in the Everwood, though only the Legion knows the true reason.",
      "areas": {
        "The Gorge Gate": {
          "description": "The main entrance where the river flows out through a narrow gap in the adamant walls. Twin watchtowers carved from living stone flank the passage. Beyond, the valley opens in a rush of green and the sound of falling water.",
          "paths": [
            "The Greenway"
          ]
        },
        "The Greenway": {
          "description": "The valley floor along the riverside - the heart of Adamant and the reason people stay. Cottage gardens and small orchards line the water. A tavern called The Seventh Bell serves everyone from mud-spattered recruits to off-duty commanders. Market stalls sell valley produce and Legion surplus. Children fish in the shallows while veterans mend gear on their porches.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gorge Gate",
            "The Veil Stair",
            "The Legion Grounds"
          ]
        },
        "The Legion Grounds": {
          "description": "Where the Legion of the Vigil trains and musters, at the valley's far end where the gorge narrows again. Barracks, armories, the sparring yard where recruits learn that elven swordsmanship is faster than they thought. The mess hall is the social center - long tables, loud arguments about technique, and a tradition that new recruits buy the first round. A board posts current assignments and open patrols.",
          "paths": [
            "The Greenway"
          ]
        },
        "The Veil Stair": {
          "description": "A switchback stair carved into the gorge wall, climbing behind the largest waterfall to the cave-temple above. The spray soaks everyone who climbs. At the top, the Skymirror opens onto a ledge of still pools at the cliff's edge.",
          "paths": [
            "The Greenway",
            "The Skymirror"
          ]
        },
        "The Skymirror": {
          "description": "A temple in the caves behind the great waterfall, where the roar of water drowns all but shouts. Still pools reflect the sky through gaps in the stone, and the same waters have run this gorge since before the Sundering and have never once stopped. Before these pools the Legion of the Vigil swears and renews its oaths - the unbroken water for the watch that does not break. A recruit takes the oath here on the day the brotherhood accepts them, and a Legionnaire returns before every hard road.",
          "paths": [
            "The Veil Stair"
          ]
        }
      },
