    "Velantami": {
      "name": "Velantami",
      "basicInfo": "A vast hollow oak deep in the Everwood, the seat of the Wildkeepers - the fellowship of druids, rangers, and priests sworn to the wild places. Its trunk could hold a castle, carved by centuries into chambers and halls, and Wildkeepers of every people study, train, and shelter here. They take in those who would learn the wild's ways, arm them against what fouls it, and send them out into the wood to do the work: to drive back the burners and poachers, to cleanse blight and break corrupt spellcraft, and to keep the balance the wild cannot keep for itself.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Wildkeepers hold that the wild must never be owned or tamed, only kept free and alive in its natural balance. A Wildkeeper protects that balance and is the enemy of whatever breaks it: the poacher and the grove-feller who strip the wood for gain, the blight and the foul spell that corrupt its cycle, and most of all the warlord who would burn the forest to ash. They answer to no king, no court, and no written law - only to what each knows he owes the wild.\n\nA major enemy is the Bloodsworn crusaders, the blood-cult out of Westmarch who cross into the Everwood to burn it back.\n\nSeveral pressures converge on the Everwood. In the Eastwood, Bloodsworn war-parties cross from Westmarch to burn groves while renegade elves raid back, keeping the frontier in motion. An old understanding with Yslaine is no longer dependable, and no one knows why; fey paths and creatures from the edge of her demesne are appearing closer to Wildkeeper routes. Hired bands from Sanctuary also enter the wood for contracts, profit, or security, and sometimes worsen the conflicts they claim to contain. The Wildkeepers' sacred charge is to keep the Everwood alive and free while deciding which danger must be met first.\n\nThe Wildkeepers are not the city's servants and not its enemies. They keep the wood, not Sanctuary, and they suffer the walled city because a city at peace does the wild less harm than a war would. They will guide the honest traveler and aid those who pass through with respect; they have no patience for those who come to take.",
      "x": 15,
      "y": 29,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Sanctuary Vale",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Hollow Hall": {
          "description": "The great chamber inside the oak's trunk, wide as a village square and warm with a fire pit that never dies. Wildkeepers eat at the long tables, swap stories and take up the work that needs doing. The eldest of the fellowship hold court here.",
          "paths": [
