    "The White Tower": {
      "name": "The White Tower",
      "x": -16,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Jade Tarn",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A peculiar, immaculately kept white stone tower standing alone in the woods, every stone sound and every window whole, as though its keeper had only just stepped out. Nothing about it has been allowed to fall into the disrepair of an abandoned place, and yet no one lives here — or no one who answers a knock.",
      "hiddenInfo": "THE STANDING MANAHAUNT. The tower belonged to a wizard who died when a working to give her own spells some measure of life and will of their own turned on her. Her spells did not die with her. Soaked in the strong mana of the region, they took on lasting shape and a fixed, simple purpose, and they have kept the tower ever since — a household of spellforms, each a single casting given a body and a will, each doing the one thing it was made to do, forever and with no one left to do it for. The mages of Tarnholme, were they to come and look, would call the whole tower a manahaunt: a place so steeped in loose magic that the magic has grown into beings and made the building its own.\n\nTHE SPELLFORMS. Each is a spell wearing a shape, and each wants only to fulfill its purpose, in ways grown strange with the years and no master to aim them. Mend scurries the rooms as a ghostly handyman, repairing all it finds — and it has repaired its dead mistress too, so that her body still sits preserved and whole in her study chair, mended past all decay. Prestidigitation frets and tidies as a house-sprite; Fire Bolt lives in the hearth as a salamander of flame; Detect Thoughts drifts the library as a weeping eye, finding and grieving over the secrets in the books; Shield stands at the door as a translucent knight; and others keep their own rooms. Some have begun trying to leave the tower, though crossing the threshold seems to pain them, as though the working that bound them will not let them go.\n\nHANDLING THEM. A spellform can be fought, and it can sometimes be reasoned with after a fashion, though its reason runs only as deep as its one purpose. Taken or unmade, a spellform gives up the spell it is: the fading shape of one, caught before it goes, is a casting held at the moment of its undoing, and one who knows how to spend it may loose that same spell once more, weakly and but once.",
      "areas": {
        "Tower Entry": {
          "description": "The ground-floor entrance, a round flagstoned hall with a wide door standing open to the woods and a stair winding up within. The hall is spotless, the stone scrubbed and the door-hinges oiled and silent, and a faint translucent shimmer keeps to the doorway as though something stood watch there.",
          "paths": [
            "The Living Room",
            "Library Level"
          ]
        },
        "The Living Room": {
          "description": "A cozy chamber off the entry, kept warm and clean, with deep chairs drawn up to a wide hearth in which a fire always burns though no one tends it. The mantel and shelves are tidy and dusted, and the firelight moves strangely in the grate.",
          "paths": [
            "Tower Entry",
            "Kitchen Level",
            "Library Level"
          ]
        },
        "Kitchen Level": {
          "description": "A well-kept kitchen of scrubbed boards and hanging copper, where the fire is laid and the table wiped and the floor swept, all of it perpetually in order. Pots stir and settle on their hooks and crockery shifts on the shelves with no hand near them.",
          "paths": [
            "The Living Room",
            "The Workshop"
          ]
        },
        "Library Level": {
          "description": "A floor of shelved books rising wall to ceiling, the volumes straight and dusted and the reading-table clear. The air is close and the quiet is broken now and then by a small sound like weeping somewhere among the stacks.",
          "paths": [
            "Tower Entry",
            "The Living Room",
            "The Workshop"
          ]
        },
        "The Workshop": {
          "description": "The dead wizard's laboratory, the most-kept room in the tower, every instrument polished and every shelf in order and a chair drawn up to the central bench. The figure seated in the chair is whole and untouched by time, perfectly preserved, and the room is mended around her endlessly.",
          "paths": [
            "Kitchen Level",
            "Library Level",
            "Observatory"
          ]
        },
        "Observatory": {
          "description": "The tower's top, an open-roofed chamber of brass instruments and star-charts under the sky, kept clean and ordered like the rest. The air stirs here without wind, and from the high windows the whole green country and the distant white towers of Tarnholme lie spread below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Workshop"
          ]
        }
      },
