    "Eanleana": {
      "name": "Eanleana",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Eanleana. In the Common Tongue it means 'Eternal City' or 'Final City'. The last refuge of the Undying Elves, who achieved immortality centuries ago but lost the ability to bear children. Built among ancient silverwood trees, the city rises in graceful tiers of grown wood and shaped stone, with delicate bridges spanning between platforms and towers that spiral up massive trunks.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The city is beautiful, vast, and largely empty. Fountains burbles, gardens bloom in riotous beauty, and halls built for thousands echo with the footsteps of the few who remain. The Undying welcome visitors with ancient courtesy, eager for news of the changing world beyond their borders. The immortality is bound to the city itself - Undying who venture beyond its boundaries age rapidly and die within days. They call this 'The Final Walk' and it's considered an honorable end when one grows too weary of eternity. The city's magic sometimes captures wanderers who stumble into its borders, offering them the same immortality if they choose to stay. Several humans and halflings from different centuries now dwell here as adopted Undying, though they too can never leave. The remaining elves are vastly powerful mages and warriors with centuries to perfect their arts, but they use their powers mainly to maintain the city and create small wonders to break the monotony of endless time.There are no children, only adults.",
      "x": -27,
      "y": 6,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Elfwood",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Arrival Garden": {
          "description": "A magnificent garden where paths from the outside world enter the city. Flowers from every season bloom simultaneously here, and fountains create rainbow mists in the eternal sunshine. A Sentinel is always waiting to receive visitors.",
          "paths": [
            "The Plaza of Eternity",
            "The Lower Halls"
          ]
        },
        "The Plaza of Eternity": {
          "description": "A vast circular plaza paved with white stone, surrounded by graceful colonnades. At its center stands an enormous tree: the Tree of Eternity. The remaining elves gather here for their seasonal celebrations. Benches of living wood offer places to sit.",
          "paths": [
            "The Arrival Garden",
            "The Hall of Chronicles",
            "The Sunward Towers"
          ]
        },
        "The Lower Halls": {
          "description": "Residential quarters built for thousands, now mostly empty. Doors stand open to furnished homes where no one has lived for centuries. The few occupied dwellings are scattered far apart, their windows glowing with soft light. Gardens between the buildings grow wild but beautiful, and occasionally an Undying can be found tending them, taking decades to perfect a single arrangement.",
          "paths": [
            "The Arrival Garden",
            "The Hall of Chronicles",
            "The Workshop Quarter"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Chronicles": {
          "description": "A library containing the accumulated knowledge of millennia, its shelves reaching up three stories. The Undying librarians know every book's location but sometimes take years to retrieve a requested volume. Reading alcoves provide comfortable spaces where scholars might spend decades on a single subject.",
          "paths": [
            "The Plaza of Eternity",
            "The Lower Halls",
            "The Workshop Quarter"
          ]
        },
        "The Workshop Quarter": {
          "description": "Studios and workshops where the Undying pursue their crafts with infinite patience. A sculptor might spend a century on one statue, a musician decades composing a single symphony. The tools here are ancient but perfectly maintained.",
          "paths": [
            "The Lower Halls",
            "The Hall of Chronicles",
            "The Sunward Towers"
          ]
        },
        "The Sunward Towers": {
          "description": "The highest spires where the eldest Undying dwell, connected by bridges so delicate they seem made of spider silk. From here, one can see to the city's boundaries - the invisible line between eternal life and certain death. The towers' balconies are where Undying stand when contemplating the Final Walk, looking out at the mortal world they can never rejoin.",
          "paths": [
            "The Plaza of Eternity",
            "The Workshop Quarter"
          ]
        }
