    "The Celestial Citadel of Alar": {
      "name": "The Celestial Citadel of Alar",
      "x": -41,
      "y": -36,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Redrock Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A sky-fortress of the ancient Sun Kings lies crashed on a broken mountain, pale towers and domes jutting from the rock at wrong angles. Fires burn throughout the wreck day and night, and the dragon Nuur-Suthra is known to lair in its depths. The Church of the Pyre holds the wreck holy and keeps a watch at the gates — though it is said that nothing that has gone past them, the Church's own included, has come out.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Nuur-Suthra is dormant. It does not stir for trespass in the outer halls. Only in the Engine Vault, or for a threat to the engine itself, does the dragon rise.\n\nA Red-cowl watch-post stands outside the Sungate. They cannot enter; the citadel's defenses kill the Church's men like anyone's. Their work is keeping others out, and they attack anyone approaching the gate.\n\nInside, two forces contest the wreck and attack all comers, including each other. The citadel's original defenses still hold the upper halls: stone constructs in the old alcoves, and fire elementals still bound to their posts. From the cracks and deep breaches, wild fire-creatures press up and in. Where the two meet, they fight, and a careful intruder can pass through a battle that has nothing to do with them.\n\nIn the Engine Vault stands the Soul Engine: a vessel of brass and black elderstone, tall as a tower, its sealed seams glowing, unnatural flame roaring from its mouth. It has roared without pause since the empire fell. It is a prison — the soul of a djinn is sealed inside, and the flame is its rage. Sometimes the fire shapes a hand, or a face, and is gone. Nuur-Suthra lairs coiled around it, warming itself, drawing power. In battle the dragon heals from the engine's flame. While the Soul Engine burns, Nuur-Suthra cannot die.\n\nLoot of the halls: Sun Kings' regalia and gilt ornament, construct cores, bound-elemental vessels, star-charts in gold and gemstone, and arms of the old empire untouched since the fall.",
      "areas": {
        "The Sungate": {
          "description": "A colossal archway in the citadel's flank, carved with solar imagery — one great door wrenched off in the crash, the other standing, gold-leafed and scorched. Open rubble-ground before it, no cover for the last hundred paces, and firelight from inside flickering on the stones after dark. Empty guardian-alcoves flank the arch.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of the Sun Kings"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of the Sun Kings": {
          "description": "A cathedral-sized hall canted off level, its pillars carved as robed giants, its mosaic floor split by the crash. Toppled statuary and fallen roof-blocks make cover everywhere; the tilt sends loose rubble sliding at a touch. Firelight comes up through cracks in the floor, and the deeper doorways glow.",
          "paths": [
            "The Sungate",
            "The Burning Stair"
          ]
        },
        "The Burning Stair": {
          "description": "The great processional stair into the citadel's depths, descending along a crash-torn gallery wall. Whole flights hang loose or are gone, forcing climbs across the broken face. Standing fires burn on the landings, the heat climbs with every flight down, and the roar from below grows until the steps tremble with it.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of the Sun Kings",
            "The Engine Vault"
          ]
        },
        "The Engine Vault": {
          "description": "The deepest chamber, a vault of black elderstone with channels radiating from its center like rays of a carved sun. The Soul Engine stands in the middle — a brass and elderstone vessel tall as a tower.",
          "paths": [
            "The Burning Stair"
          ]
        }
      },
