        "The Two-Humped Sultan": {
          "description": "The most crowded coffee-house in Oasis, a warm sprawl of cushioned alcoves, low tables, and shaded roof-terraces, named for the fat camel painted grandly over its door in a sultan's crown. Coffee and sweet smoke go round from morning to deep night, and the talk runs to fortunes won and lost in the sand. Traders strike deals here, crews drink and argue and take on new hands, and every rumor in the desert passes through sooner or later.",
