        "Sky-River House": {
          "description": "Sky-River House is a white-stone courtyard house, its shaded galleries and upper rooms arranged around a lush garden of palms, flowering vines, a small fountain, and a long company table. An ancient mosaic shows the Sky-River—a rare formation of blue-and-gold waterbirds streaming together across the dawn sky—while lost travelers follow it to a desert spring below. “No one wing makes the Sky-River”: in the Dunelands, the old phrase means that fellowship can make a road where the desert offers none. Route maps, work postings, secure stores, and free hammocks on the small roof terrace support crews preparing for or returning from the desert.",
