    "Ghoultown": {
      "name": "Ghoultown",
      "x": 16,
      "y": 1,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Redrock",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A dead town in the badlands, fallen to ruin and standing empty under the sun — empty, but not dead. The tainted ground here killed the place an age ago and would not let its people lie still; they walk it yet as ghouls, drained and mindless and hungry for the living. By day the ruin lies quiet, the husks still among the rubble, and it stirs to terrible life when anything warm comes through the gate. Folk come anyway, for a dead town keeps its wealth, and the ruins and crypts are full of what the dead left behind.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Ghoultown is hostile and there is no parley with what walks here. The ghouls lie still and lifeless until the living come near, then rouse all at once — quick, ravenous, and fearless, swarming a warm body together, biting and dragging it down. They do not flee and cannot be reasoned with. The deeper into the ruin a body goes, the more of them wake and the worse they are.\n\nThe town walks because a soul-eating demon dwells in the vaults beneath it. It devours the souls of the living, and a body emptied of its soul does not die clean — it rises a ghoul, mindless and starving. An age ago the demon worked through the whole town this way, and the husks it left are the ghouls that fill the ruin now. The demon does not hunt; it waits in the dark below, dormant, and lets the living come to it. They do come — plunderers after the dead town's wealth, and others sent to test their steel against the dead — and that trickle is all it needs.\n\nThe ghouls run in a clear order. The fresh husks of the upper ruin are weakest, many but slow to truly threaten a ready hand. The old husks denned in the crypts are far worse — long-drained, grown terrible, fast and strong. And in the lowest vaults waits the soul-eater itself, the source of all of it: a demon that drains the spirit from the living at a touch and turns the slain into more of its kind. Killing it is the only thing that quiets the ruin, and it never stays quiet long, for the tainted ground keeps drawing such things up.\n\nThe dead town is full of loot. The ruins and the bodies hold the coin, arms, and goods of everyone who ever died here or came to plunder and stayed — picked over near the surface, untouched and richer in the crypts below. A slain soul-eater leaves a soul-stone, a dark gem swollen with the spirits it ate, worth a fortune to those who deal in such things.",
      "areas": {
        "The Dead Streets": {
          "description": "The ruined heart of the town, a grid of collapsed mudbrick houses and sand-choked streets baking in the open sun. Fallen walls and roof-beams lie across the lanes, and dark doorways gape on either side. The husks of the dead lie still among the rubble where they fell. The ground slopes down toward the town's old burial ground at one edge, and stairs and broken cellar-mouths drop into the dark beneath the streets.",
          "paths": [
            "The Bone Yard",
            "The Crypts"
          ]
        },
        "The Bone Yard": {
          "description": "The town's old burial ground at the edge of the ruin, open ground crowded with leaning grave-markers and broken tombs, the earth heaped and cracked where the dead were piled in the dying-time. Bone lies thick underfoot, bleached pale by the sun. The yard is wide and exposed, with low ruined walls for the only cover, and a sunken tomb-mouth at its center opens a way down into the vaults.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dead Streets",
            "The Crypts"
          ]
        },
        "The Crypts": {
          "description": "The burial vaults beneath the town, a close warren of brick passages and stacked grave-niches running down into the dark. The air is hot and still and grows hotter deeper in. Side-chambers open off the main ways, their niches broken open and emptied. The passages branch and descend toward the lowest vaults below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dead Streets",
            "The Bone Yard",
            "The Lower Vaults"
          ]
        },
        "The Lower Vaults": {
          "description": "The lowest and hottest chambers under the town, far below the streets, where the brickwork gives way to rough-cut stone and the heat sits like a weight. The vaults here are wide and dark and deathly silent. The way back up runs through the crypts above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Crypts"
          ]
        }
      },
