    "Hillwatch": {
      "name": "Hillwatch",
      "x": -31,
      "y": -1,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Dunelands",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A walled waystation and hill-town on the desert road. A cult called the New Sun holds it now openly: they keep the well and the gates, their word is law within the walls, and they mean to wake the old Sun Kings from their tombs and set them ruling again. They take in all who come in their faith, feed and shelter travelers who give no trouble, and let raiders rest and pass. Cross them, though, and you join the others who vanish into the temple they keep beneath the town.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The New Sun holds Hillwatch openly and does not attack travelers on sight. They permit and make use of those who come in their faith or give no trouble, and let raiders rest and pass. They are not friendly; they watch who enters and what they want, and they turn on anyone who threatens their work, refuses to move along, or pries too far into the temple beneath. The faithful will kill or take such people.\n\nThe New Sun are a cult set on waking the dead god-kings entombed in the old pyramids and seeing them rule the world again. They hold that the day of that waking is near, and everything they do here serves it. They let raiders water and pass because the crews who rob the tombs do their digging for them, and they buy back what is carried out. They preach to those who pass and take recruits from the crews and the desperate; those who accept the faith are welcomed in, and those who interfere are taken below.\n\nThe town is ordinary on the surface: yard, well, beds, and a market the cult runs. Beneath it is their temple, where their rites are kept, the relics carried back from the tombs are gathered, and the taken are held. The deeper into Hillwatch a person goes, the less it is a town and the more it is a shrine, and the temple-heart is held by the cult's own faithful.\n\nLoot is the cult's gathered take and the goods of the town, richest in the temple below. Sun-gold relic: radiant, bites undead, demons, and shadow-things hardest, gathered by the cult. Ritual gold, grave-goods, and the records of the cult's work lie in the temple.",
      "areas": {
        "The Yard": {
          "description": "The waystation's walled court, a dusty open yard with a deep well at its center, stables and water-troughs along one wall, and a low market under awnings against another. The old road runs in through the main gate and out the far side toward the pyramids on the horizon. Sun-marks are painted fresh over the gates and the well, and a stair at the back of the yard leads down beneath the buildings.",
          "paths": [
            "The Rest-House",
            "The Undertemple"
          ]
        },
        "The Rest-House": {
          "description": "The long low building along the yard where travelers are housed and fed: a common room with a hearth and tables, rows of cots in the back, and a counter where supplies and water are doled out. The walls are hung with sun-cloth and the old caravan-charts, and a few private rooms open off the back. Doors lead out to the yard.",
          "paths": [
            "The Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Undertemple": {
          "description": "A stone hall dug beneath the waystation, reached by the stair from the yard, its walls carved and painted with the sun and the old kings. Altars and offering-tables stand along the hall, and side-chambers hold gathered grave-goods, relics laid out on cloth, and shelves of the cult's records. The hall runs back into deeper rooms, dim and close, away from the light of the yard above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Yard"
          ]
        }
      },
