    "Wadi of the Beasts": {
      "name": "Wadi of the Beasts",
      "x": -7,
      "y": -16,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Redrock",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A deep canyon where water runs year-round, the one green cut in a long stretch of dry badland. Because it is the only water for a hard day's travel in any direction, the great beasts of the desert come here to drink — giant scorpions, sand drakes, desert lions, and worse — and so it is the richest hunting ground in the region, thick with creatures whose hides, venom, and trophies are worth good coin. The beasts are many and growing bolder, and the canyon is as dangerous as it is rich.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: the beasts of the wadi are wild animals and hostile when roused, but they are not lying in wait for a fight — they come to drink, and they turn dangerous when crowded, cornered, or hunted. Each kind fights to its nature. Giant scorpions strike from cover with claw and stinging tail and are slow but armored. Sand drakes lie buried in the loose ground and burst up beneath what passes, dragging it down. Desert lions stalk and rush from the reeds in a pride, going for the lone and the strayed. A manticore is the worst of them — a great lion-bodied beast with a tail of driving spikes it flings from a distance, taking to the air when it is pressed and stooping again, and it kills for sport as much as hunger.\n\nThe wadi is kept by desert druids, who live in the caves above the canyon floor. They do not forbid the hunt — they sanction it. Too much water and too much game would let the predators breed past all bounds, and a measured cull is how the keepers hold the balance of the place. They know every beast in the canyon, permit and guide those who come to hunt within reason, and turn sharp on anyone who kills wastefully or fouls the water.\n\nLately the balance is slipping. The beasts have grown more aggressive and more numerous than the keepers can account for, drinking and breeding beyond the canyon's measure, and the cull that once kept the wadi in hand has fallen behind. Something out in the deep desert is stirring them, and the keepers do not know what. The hunt is no longer only sanctioned — it is needed.\n\nThe wadi's beasts are the prize. A giant scorpion yields venom and hard shell-plate; a sand drake, tough hide and scale; a desert lion, a fine pelt; and a manticore, its spikes, hide, and a tail-stinger prized by any weapon-maker. The keepers in the caves will buy beast-trophies and trade in beast-lore, and they hold living beasts penned for study — caged predators a quick or desperate hand could loose.",
      "areas": {
        "The Canyon Floor": {
          "description": "The green heart of the wadi, reached by a winding path down from the desert above. Water runs along the canyon bottom in a thread of stream and standing pool, fringed with reeds and palms, and the ground along it is churned and tracked where the beasts come down to drink. The red cliffs rise sheer on either side, hollowed here and there with caves, and the canyon runs on deeper toward the springs at its head.",
          "paths": [
            "The Springs",
            "The Cliff Caves"
          ]
        },
        "The Springs": {
          "description": "The head of the canyon, where the water wells up from the rock into deep clear pools ringed with green. This is the richest water in the wadi and the most fought-over, the ground around it heavily trodden and the cover thick. The cliffs close in tight here, and the pools run back into shadowed clefts in the rock.",
          "paths": [
            "The Canyon Floor"
          ]
        },
        "The Cliff Caves": {
          "description": "A cluster of caves worn into the canyon wall above the floor, reached by a carved path along the rock. The walls within are covered in old carvings of beasts and the people who hunted and kept them, cut deep ages ago. The caves are dry and cool and look out over the water below, and a passage at the back leads through to the holding-caves.",
          "paths": [
            "The Canyon Floor",
            "The Beast-Pens"
          ]
        },
        "The Beast-Pens": {
          "description": "The holding-caves behind the keepers' dwelling, where the canyon's beasts are kept penned — dug-out pits, barred enclosures, and cages set into the rock. Chains, posts, and feeding-troughs line the chambers, and the air is rank with the animals held here. The only way out is back through the caves.",
          "paths": [
            "The Cliff Caves"
          ]
        }
      },
