      "region": "Redrock",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Cloudtop is a city of golden domes and terraced workshops built across the highest peaks, rising into the sun above a sea of cloud, with the red canyons a long way down and out of sight. Its slender rock spires are crowned with the great nests of the cloudwing condors, and all day the huge gentle birds glide in and out bearing riders and cargo between the peaks and the country far below — the only easy way up to a city this high, and the sight the place is known for. Cloudtop's smiths and jewelers are the finest alive, and its forges, said to burn purer than any below, turn out masterwork blades and brasswork that the whole region covets. It is ruled by the Jeweled Princes and Princesses of House Darawat, whose wealth is bottomless and whose Edicts — proclamations naming the troubles of the land — are answered gladly, for the Princes reward those who serve them very well indeed.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Cloudtop is safe, splendid, and welcoming, the grand hub of the whole region and the high seat above its specialist orders and towns. A traveler comes here to rest in cool clean air, to be armed with the finest gear in the land, and above all to take up the work of the Edicts — for from this height the whole red country spreads out below, and Cloudtop is where its troubles are named and answered. It is the natural place to learn where the region's dangers lie and to set out against them.\n\nThe Edicts of the Jeweled Princes are the engine of the place. House Darawat names the troubles of the land in formal proclamation — a haunted town, a burning canyon, a road gone to raiders — and posts a rich reward for their answer. The proud houses of the city compete fiercely to see these Edicts resolved in their name, for a house that answers an Edict gains the Princes' favor and outshines its rivals. Houses court visiting heroes openly and shamelessly, pressing them to take up an Edict under that house's banner so the house may claim the glory. This is how Cloudtop sends adventurers out across the region: an Edict names a trouble in a distant place, a house offers gold and patronage to whoever will go answer it, and the canyons below are full of such troubles — the dead town where the soulless walk, the canyon that bleeds fire, the ruined city the gnolls hold, and worse.\n\nThe city is built in the empty heights once hallowed by Heliaxes, the great sun-dragon, who dwelt upon these peaks an age ago and departed without a word of why. The smiths hold that their forges burn pure because the air itself remembers him, and it is true that no work below the clouds matches what is made here. The High Forges are the peak of the region's craft: a hunter who hauls up rare materials from the field — the everlasting heart-coal of a fire-demon, the trophies of great beasts, relics out of the ruins — can have them worked into masterwork arms and gear here, by smiths insufferably proud of every piece.\n\nHouse Darawat leads the region but does not rule it. Cloudtop governs only itself; elsewhere the Princes are consulted as peers and honored for their wealth and their forges, but the orders, towns, and clans of the red country answer to themselves. Within the city, status is won by craft and by splendor, and the great houses vie endlessly — in the lavish glory of their revels and in the answering of Edicts both. The population is the most mixed in the high country: humans, mountain dwarves, eaglekin who tend the condors, tunnel-gnomes, and djinnborn and desert folk come up from below to trade. The mines beneath the city, where the forges' metals are cut, are ordinary workings now and hold only the ordinary dangers of deep stone.\n\nThe cloudwing condors are the city's partners and its pride. The huge, gentle birds nest in the eyrie-spires of Cloudtop's rock, and the city has kept and guarded their nests for as long as anyone remembers; in return the eaglekin fly them as mounts, bearing riders and goods up to the peaks and down to the canyon country. They are placid soaring beasts bred for burden, not fighting creatures, and no rider takes one into battle. A traveler who serves the city and earns the Princes' regard is given a condor-whistle, and may call a bird to carry them back up to Cloudtop from anywhere in the region below.",
      "areas": {
        "The Cloud Terrace": {
          "description": "The great edge-terrace where the city meets the sky, a broad platform of pale stone and brass railing standing at the lip of the cloud-sea, the white clouds rolling below and the golden domes and spires of the city climbing into the sun above. Tea-houses and market-stalls crowd the terrace, and a long stair and the condor-landings bring travelers up onto it. From the railing the whole red country lies spread out far below, canyon and mesa to the edge of sight.",
