        "The Court of Edicts": {
          "description": "The grand audience-court of House Darawat, a vaulted hall of gold and jewel-bright tile open to a colonnade and the sky beyond. A great wall of polished brass holds the Edicts of the Princes, each proclamation graven on a hung plate, and the courtiers and house-agents of the city throng the floor before it. The Princes' and Princesses' seats stand on a high dais at the head of the hall, and arched ways lead off to the rest of the palace.",
