        "The Weight and Wind": {
          "description": "This long workshop lies beneath a natural stone arch, filled with hanging ropes, weighted bands, drying wraps, half-finished sandals, and equipment suspended from the rafters. Monks and specialist makers cut, stitch, braid, oil, balance, and repair the gear used by people who routinely ask their bodies to do impossible things. Visitors can buy practical Temple-made equipment, commission repairs, or watch apprentices test a new harness on one of the nearby routes. Nothing here is merely decorative: every strap, sole, and fastening has to survive a real mistake.",
