        "The Ascendants' Spire": {
          "description": "The highest spire rises above the rest of the Temple, its upper halls reached by a sequence of sheer walls, narrow bridges, open stairs, and a final exposed ascent above the cloudline. The Ascendants keep chambers here, teach advanced practitioners, preserve the Temple's oldest disciplines, and receive reports from those undertaking the Descents. The route is physically open to anyone capable of reaching it, but the people at its summit choose carefully whom they teach, judge, or send back into the world. At the top, the entire Unmoored Mountain seems to hang between earth and heaven.",
