      "detailType": "detailed",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Capital of the Greater Goblinate, built in and around ancient ruins rising from the volcanic highlands. Massive carved stone structures of unknown origin now serve as foundations for a sprawling goblin metropolis—forges hammered into ancient chambers, smelters beneath crumbling archways, ramshackle construction climbing the old walls. The city never sleeps. Smoke rises from a hundred vents, visible for miles.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Smoketown is hostile to League-aligned adventurers as such, but it is not a place that attacks strangers on sight—it is a police state with a boomtown's open door. Anyone who looks useful may enter: mercenaries, craftsmen, traders, entertainers. An outsider who is useful and careful can live and work here; one caught spying or moving against the Goblinate is taken and burned.\n\nInhabitants: Goblins—workers, smiths, traders, soldiers on leave. Hobgoblin officers. Bugbear enforcers. Growing numbers of humans, dwarves, demonborn, moon elves, and others drawn by opportunity or recruited into the Foreign Legion.\n\nGovernment: The Governor rules absolutely, answering only to the Dragon Queen. Below the Governor, ministers control different aspects of the city—the Minister of Works oversees industry, the Minister of Revels manages entertainment and morale, others handle trade, military supply, and internal security. Ministers wield enormous power but serve at the Governor's pleasure; failure means execution. They scheme against each other constantly while maintaining public loyalty.\n\nChurch of the Pyre: The Pyre Cathedral is the Church's grandest temple. Archpriests lead public burnings—captured noble banners, foreign books, symbols of Larion's 'corruption'—and preach that the old world must burn. The dragonfire that arms the Goblinate is brewed outside the walls at the Dragonworks, too dangerous to cook in the city; the finished fuel comes in by the Iron Road, and the lances are charged and fitted in the Forge Quarter. The Church and the secular ministry both believe they are the Dragon Queen's true voice, a rivalry nobody dares name aloud and everybody plays—the archpriests and the Governor's ministers court the same favor and undercut each other in everything but public ceremony.\n\nThe Syndicate: Crime works the Crater and the Sprawl, fencing plunder the ministers skim from their own hauls, selling intelligence to every faction at once, forging the papers an outsider needs, and moving people out of the city for ruinous prices.\n\nTensions: The Goblinate champions goblinhood, but the war economy requires non-goblin skills. True believers resent outsider influence. Opportunists don't care as long as coin flows. Informants watch for spies and dissent. Coin flows freely from war plunder and mining wealth. The taverns riot nightly. The forges run day and night. It is a city drunk on its own success, and the party shows no signs of stopping. Goblins consider it a banner announcing their nation's rise. Every evening, firelancers discharge their weapons skyward in celebration—the booms that give the city its nickname ('Boomtown').",
