      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A crooked stone tower on a hill outside the lakeshore, three stories tall and listing slightly, its lower half wrapped in ivy and flowering vine. The upper windows glow at all hours, and a wooden sign by the path reads THE ONEIRARY — Visitors Welcome.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Home of Mikol, a gnomish chronicler at work on a vast and unfinishable book he calls the History of Undiscovered Realms. Small winged cats called volucats come and go through the open windows, and the manuscripts fill the upper floor and have begun to colonize the lower, in an order no visitor could follow — Mikol finds a passage by memory and by asking his enchanted quills, who keep their own idiosyncratic index and do not always agree.\n\nIt is a good place to hear rumor, oblique warning, and fragmentary word of distant places, all of it filtered through Mikol's visionary idiom. Nothing he says is reliable intelligence, and much of it is plainly impossible. But the careful listener finds seeds of real adventure scattered through the ramblings, and Mikol speaks more freely and more strangely about the deep past than any master of Tarnholme will — of an age before the empires, of the gift of magic and the things that came to take it back, of what he insists lies sleeping at the bottom of the Well. The Academy holds him a harmless eccentric. He may be that, and may be something more.",
      "areas": {
        "The Path": {
          "description": "A winding dirt path climbing the hill to the tower, thick with wildflowers on either side and marked by a wobbly hand-painted sign. Small winged shapes circle and stoop above — the volucats, coming and going from the upper windows — and the tower door at the top stands open.",
          "paths": [
