      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Swordlaw Isles",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "North Canal is the wide shipping lane that threads between the outer islands of the Swordlaw sea, the fastest water between the open ocean and the bridged isles. Merchant galleys, fishing boats, and patrols all run it, and so do pirates. Redfin Waystation sits on a rock islet midway down the channel, the one place to shelter, resupply, and trade news between the islands.",
      "hiddenInfo": "North Canal is rich water and everyone uses it, which is why the Feathered Fleet hunts it. The Fleet are birdfolk corsairs who broke the code that even Freehaven keeps — they take fishing boats and small traders, kill crews who fight and ransom those who don't, and burn what they cannot carry. They den in the hidden coves of the outer islands and know the channel's shoals and weather better than any patrol, striking from the rocks and gone before a galley can come about.\n\nThe Fleet's captain on the Canal is Scraw, a pelicanfolk who took his crew by mutiny and runs the worst of the raiding here. The Tevantia Admiralty has posted a standing bounty on him, and patrols sweep the lane, but the Fleet knows the water and the patrols do not. Scraw is one captain of the Fleet, not its head.\n\nRedfin Waystation is neutral ground and means to stay that way — it sells shelter, supplies, and news to anyone who pays, pirate and merchant alike, and asks no questions that would cost it custom. The harbormaster, Gull Makris, is Scraw's uncle, and everyone on the islet knows it; Redfin will warn the Fleet off its own dock to keep the peace but will not lift a hand to help a patrol take him.\n\nIMPORTANT: The Feathered Fleet is hostile to merchant and patrol shipping on the open Canal — they raid to take, and a boat that looks worth taking is a target. They are not hostile at Redfin, which is neutral by custom they keep because they need it too. On the water they hit fast, swarm a deck from the rigging and the rocks, and break off the moment a fight turns even rather than trade lives for a poor prize.\n\nWork on the Canal is escort, bounty, and salvage: guarding a trader down the lane, hunting Scraw for the Admiralty's purse, or recovering cargo the Fleet dumped or cached in the coves. Redfin's tavern is where the work is found and the rumors of the Fleet's next ground are sold.",
      "areas": {
        "Redfin Waystation": {
          "description": "A trading post on a bare rock islet midway down the channel — a stone-and-timber tavern, a chandlery, a harbormaster's office, and a few jetties where boats tie up out of the open water. The Saltspray tavern is the islet's heart, low-beamed and always full, where captains haggle cargo space and crews trade news. The channel runs broad and busy on every side, and the outer islands stand green and broken along the horizon.",
          "paths": [
            "The Canal Waters"
          ]
        },
        "The Canal Waters": {
          "description": "The open shipping lane between the green outer islands, broad and deep down the middle and treacherous at the edges, where rocky shoals and hidden coves crowd the island shores. Merchant galleys, fishing boats, and patrol craft work the channel in all weather. The many coves and rock-stacks along the islands break the sightlines and offer cover to anything waiting off the lane.",
          "paths": [
            "Redfin Waystation"
          ]
        }
