        "The Apothecary": {
          "description": "A tall shopfront on the Sunside market square, and nothing else in the valley looks like it: figured glass, a floor laid in black and white stone, and a wall of polished walnut drawers running to the ceiling with a ladder on a rail. This is the house that made Velmere's alchemy famous — healing draughts, elixirs of clarity, night-sight, tinctures against the cold, restoratives that work when nothing else will — and Syndicate factors come up from Villa Parhelion by the season to buy them by the case. It is also where one buys poison, which is sold openly here, priced accordingly, and better than anyone else's anywhere. It is said the Apothecary can build a poison for one named person and no other, and that none has ever been traced back to her. Nobody in Velmere repeats that where a stranger can hear it.",
