        "Shadeside": {
          "description": "The shore the sun never touches, in permanent blue shade under the wall of the mountain, lamps burning along the waterfront at noon. This half of the village lives at night: the pressing-houses run until dawn with their doors open and the smell of must rolling out over the water, the wharf takes the day's cut fruit off the ferry, and the Good Night never closes. Stone houses with heavy shutters that bar from inside. The Crimson Company's hall stands back from the water under a red sword on black, and one switchback road climbs from the end of the street up to the chateau above — the road the whole valley has walked at least once, at night, in a hurry, with the gate standing open at the top of it.",
