        "The Red House": {
          "description": "A great house on the shaded shore, taken over by the Crimson Company and kept far better than a barracks needs to be. Blades eat together at one long table under a red sword on black, and what is poured is the valley's own — the vintages that go to distant kings, because Lady Isaveau retains this hall and does not stint it. There are hot baths at the back, a wardrobe that issues black and red cut to fit and replaces what gets ruined, and a yard with good horses where the drill is run in the dark. The work board hangs by the door. Off the hall is a warded room holding what the Company has taken and will not destroy — cursed blades, bound things, gear that would see its owner burned anywhere south of the peaks — and the wards on that door are the most expensive thing in the house. Trophies line the wall: pelts, a strigoi skull picked clean, a ghoul's jaw wired open. When the bell goes in the valley, this house empties first.",
