        "Chateau Velmere - Great Hall": {
          "description": "The great hall of the chateau, reached by one switchback road up from the shaded shore and through gardens of night-blooming flowers. The gate at the top stands open, and stays open, because it does not need to be shut: anyone the lady did not want inside her valley would have stopped being a problem somewhere back at the pass. Inside is black stone and silver under a high vaulted roof, a long table, light enough for a court, and tall mirrors down one wall that the lady does not use. This is where she receives, and where she gives the evenings the elite of the north compete to attend: lords, house envoys, Syndicate men up from Villa Parhelion, and whoever she currently finds interesting. They run until dawn and settle more business than any court in the Summits. A household of beautiful young mortals in her own red attends the guests, dressed at her expense and plainly enjoying themselves, and bloodwine is poured here and nowhere else, to guests she counts as her own kind or means to. The gate has been shut three times in living memory, each time with the whole valley inside it. The cellars and the laboratories lie deeper in and are no part of the evening.",
