        "Ashfall Pass South": {
          "description": "The Velmere end of the only road over the range to Val Cendrac: a climb out of the valley's western head, up past the last terraces where the vines give out, to a saddle where the wind never stops. Ash comes over from Cendrac's forges and settles on this side — grey on the snow, grey on the vine rows below — which is what the pass is named for and what Velmere has resented for six hundred years. No gate, no garrison, a stone shelter at the height with a cold hearth. It is watched from both ends by people who have no need to stop anybody, and the old tunnels under the range are watched a great deal less, which is why they keep being cut and keep being collapsed.",
