      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A sealed valley high in the peaks, its one pass blocked by collapsed stone. Once the domain of House Sable, an ancient bloodline known for its mastery of blood magic. Now strigoi hold it — vampires gone feral and mindless — and Keep Sable still stands at the valley's head, black towers against black cliffs.",
      "hiddenInfo": "House Sable made its get alone, holding itself above the rite of two, and fed without limit besides; within a single generation the curse it carried turned the whole valley feral. The strigoi have splintered into territorial packs — some hold the high caves, some the forest, some the outer keep — that compete and sometimes fight. Lady Sable remains in the inner keep, ancient and powerful and utterly mindless, the apex the others will not approach.\n\nThe other lords sealed the pass rather than burn the vale clean, because Keep Sable's library holds the largest store of blood-magic research in Larion, and an assault might destroy it. The Crimson Company holds the cordon at the collapsed pass on the lords' behalf, and kills anyone who comes out without leave. But they watch who comes in, and a capable, desperate-looking arrival may be approached quietly: there is a way through the caves, and House Setharis pays well to learn whether its lost heir, Nerisse, is alive inside.\n\nThe village still has people in it — those who could not flee before the pass was sealed. They hide in cellars and attics, move by day when the strigoi are sluggish, and barricade themselves before dark. They cannot leave; the Company would kill them. They know the vale's patterns: which packs hunt where, when Lady Sable stirs, where things of worth might still be found.\n\nIMPORTANT: the strigoi of the Vale Sable default to hostile and do not parley. They are mindless and serve no one. They hunt anything warm, sluggish by day and fierce after dark, and the packs will fight each other over prey as readily as they take it.",
      "areas": {
        "The Cordon": {
          "description": "A Crimson Company encampment where the mountain road ends at a wall of collapsed stone. Markers declare the valley sealed. Soldiers in red-and-black hold the checkpoint, and a row of heads on the palisade — some withered, some recent — shows what happens to those who come out of the vale without leave. They watch new arrivals closely, and the capable, desperate-looking ones sometimes find a cloaked figure lingering at the camp's edge, who speaks quietly of a way in through the caves and of a house that pays for results.",
          "paths": [
            "The Caves"
          ]
        },
        "The Caves": {
          "description": "A network of natural caverns winding through the mountain, bypassing the sealed pass. The passages are narrow and dark, descending steeply before climbing again. They emerge through a trapdoor in a root cellar beneath a collapsed house on the edge of Sable Village.",
          "paths": [
            "The Cordon",
            "Sable Village"
          ]
        },
        "Sable Village": {
          "description": "Stone houses with slate roofs, like any village in the Shadow Summits — but the doors hang broken, the windows are dark, and dried blood stains the cobblestones. Strigoi hunt the streets after dark. The survivors live in hiding: cellars, attics, passages knocked through cellar walls. They move by day, take what they can from abandoned stores, and barricade themselves before dusk.",
          "paths": [
            "The Caves",
            "The Black Tarn"
          ]
        },
        "The Black Tarn": {
          "description": "The wild heart of the valley between village and keep. Dense forest climbs the slopes, and at the center lies a lake so dark it appears black, reflecting nothing. Strigoi packs hunt here, marking territories in ways only they understand, and the forest floor is scattered with bones. The path to Keep Sable winds along the lakeshore, exposed and dangerous.",
          "paths": [
            "Sable Village",
            "Keep Sable"
          ]
        },
        "Keep Sable": {
          "description": "The castle rises where the valley ends, built into the cliff face — black stone towers against black rock. Keep Sable was part fortress, part laboratory, part library. The outer halls and lower levels are claimed by strigoi now, led by something that might once have been Lady Sable's seneschal; they do not enter the inner keep, which is her domain. The library-laboratory lies at the castle's heart, and somewhere within it, presumably, both Lady Sable and whatever became of Nerisse Setharis.",
          "paths": [
            "The Black Tarn"
          ]
        }
      },
