      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "factions": [],
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A mountain fortress sacred to the vampire lords of the Shadow Summits. The Black Gate is the only place a new lord can be made — a portal to another realm where an aspirant must prove themselves worthy of the Lady of Blood's gift. Each house keeps priest-wardens here, which makes the fortress neutral ground, where rivals can convene, negotiate, and witness a transformation under a truce no house will break.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Gate opens rarely; making a new lord is a matter of weight and risk. Between such occasions the fortress serves as neutral territory for the lords' diplomacy and as a place of pilgrimage for those who venerate the Lady of Blood. The priest-wardens are vampires of middling standing, appointed by their houses. The posting is prestigious in name and tedious in practice — decades can pass between transformations — and the wardens fill the time keeping the fortress, conducting the rites, and pressing their houses' interests in the small disputes that make up daily business. Some come to enjoy the quiet; others go slowly mad of boredom.\n\nThe rite requires the sponsorship of an existing lord, the wardens' approval — rarely refused when the sponsor is powerful enough — and then the trial itself. The aspirant passes through the Gate alone and must defeat and drink the blood of a Fiend of the Blood, one of the Lady's servants that dwell in her realm. Those who succeed return transformed. Those who fail do not return.\n\nOpening the Gate carries its own danger. Things sometimes try to come through. The wards are strong, but the wardens are careful — they do not open the Gate lightly, and they keep defenses ready against whatever might emerge.\n\nDespite the Gate's infrequent use, the fortress sees steady traffic. Envoys treat on neutral ground. Supplicants petition for sponsorship. Merchants supply the garrison. Those with grievances between houses seek arbitration. The wardens hear all of it, which leaves them surprisingly well-informed for so remote a posting.\n\nFor a player, the Black Gate is the path to lordship itself — a choice with real weight, and the one place in Larion where it can be made.",
      "areas": {
        "The Warden's Pass": {
          "description": "The mountain approach to the Black Gate — a narrow road climbing through snow and rock to the fortress above. Waymarkers carved with the sigils of the houses line the path. The fortress shows itself only halfway up: black walls against black peaks, all but invisible until you are upon them.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Witnesses"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Witnesses": {
          "description": "The great hall where the houses convene. Four galleries rise along the walls, one to a house, with the priest-wardens' seats at the cardinal points and a floor of black marble veined with red. Here sponsorships are announced, disputes arbitrated, and — on rare occasions — the houses gather to witness a transformation. Between such events the hall is a forum: envoys meet in the galleries, petitioners wait on the benches along the walls, and rivals who would cut each other's throats anywhere else keep the truce under the wardens' eyes.",
          "paths": [
            "The Warden's Pass",
            "The Supplicants' Quarters",
            "The Preparation Chambers"
          ]
        },
        "The Supplicants' Quarters": {
          "description": "Lodgings for visitors — austere but comfortable chambers cut into the mountain stone. Envoys, merchants, scholars, and petitioners all stay here, sometimes for long stretches while business is done, and a refectory serves simple meals. The quarters have an odd social weather: rivals from feuding houses share tables, petitioners hoping for sponsorship size each other up, and everyone watches everyone.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Witnesses"
          ]
        },
        "The Preparation Chambers": {
          "description": "Where aspirants are made ready for the trial, closed to all but those undergoing it and their sponsors. The chambers are spare — cells for fasting, ritual baths, rooms for meditation. An aspirant may spend days or weeks here readying body and mind for what waits beyond the Gate, while the wardens conduct the preliminary rites: the blessings, the bindings, the formal acceptance of risk.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Witnesses",
            "The Gate Chamber"
          ]
        },
        "The Gate Chamber": {
          "description": "A cavern deep within the mountain, reached only through the Preparation Chambers. The Black Gate stands at its heart — an arch of dark stone that opens onto nothing until the rite wakes it. Opened, it shows the realm of the Lady of Blood: a red darkness where the Fiends wait. The chamber is heavily warded, and the priest-wardens stand ready with bindings and steel when the Gate opens, watching for anything that might try to cross.",
          "paths": [
            "The Preparation Chambers"
          ]
        }
      },
