      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Kingstor is the great tor at the heart of the grass sea, with a permanent town of traders and travelers living at its foot the year round and a sacred Moot-ground at its summit. When the drums sound, beastfolk converge from every corner of the grass to trade, contend, settle disputes, and burn the straw kings. Moot Law holds here: no killing, no feuds past the boundary stones, for any people and any guest.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Kingstor is the one ground all the peoples of the grass share, and its law is older than any of them: no kings, no thrones, no blood spilled past the boundary stones. A breach is answered by every species present at once, which is why it holds. The Moot itself has no permanent leader; each people sends speakers to the summit stones, and what they argue out there settles the grass for a season.\n\nThe town at the foot lives year-round, not just for the Moot. The Trading Ring and the Watering Hole anchor a standing mixed community of traders, herders, road-folk, and drifters of every people, fed and watered and arguing through every season; the Moot only swells it. Non-beastfolk are tolerated as welcome guests but have no voice at the summit.\n\nThe Syndicate is here in the open, and everyone knows what its agents are. They are the face of an armed operation working to own the long road that crosses the grass: way-forts, paid guards, tolls, and quiet violence against anyone on the road who will not deal. The speakers know exactly what the factors are and have no law to stop a thing that only ever offers and never seizes. That is the grass sea's open wound, argued at every Moot and settled at none.\n\nThe League of Adventurers keeps no hall here, only a posting-board the Moot suffers among the licensed factors at the Trading Ring: monster bounties, escort and hunting work, and word of trouble across the grass.",
      "areas": {
        "The Grass Road": {
          "description": "The tor stands visible a full day's walk in every direction, a dark spike against the open sky. The track in runs straight through flat grass to a ring of weathered boundary stones that marks the edge of Moot ground. Past the stones, the camps and the rooftops at the tor's foot come into view.",
