      "region": "Wild Grass Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Mudbank is a boarfolk river settlement of mud-brick buildings, the biggest and most permanent community in the grass sea, built where a wide channel cuts through the grassland. The boarfolk build, farm, and trade — the kind of settled work other peoples of the grass associate with the outside world.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Mudbank is the grass sea's most established settlement. It is mostly boarfolk, who farm the channel-banks and raise mud-brick the way no other people of the grass bothers to, alongside a growing number of outside traders, and other beastfolk pass through constantly because Mudbank feeds anyone who shows up.\n\nThe argument is the road-men. The Syndicate keeps factors living inside the walls and a goods-warehouse on the channel, the only foothold of its kind any beastfolk settlement has granted. To some boarfolk it is prosperity, steady outside coin and a place on the road that crosses the grass. To others it is the first step toward exactly the kind of power the grass sea burns in effigy every season.",
      "areas": {
        "The River Gate": {
          "description": "The channel narrows here between mud-brick walls into a natural harbor, spanned by a wooden gate. The path into town runs along the top of a levee built up over generations with mud and stone. Reed boats and flat barges are drawn up along the banks below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Wallows",
