    "Goldentor": {
      "name": "Goldentor",
      "x": -22,
      "y": 41,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Wild Grass Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Goldentor is a lionkin pride-hold flying bright banners from the tallest tor in the grass sea, visible for miles across the open plain. The pride that holds it keeps a famously lavish table and welcomes all comers, and prides from across the grass come to feast, contend, and settle their disputes in the open before a crowd.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The population is small: one pride and their household. Everyone else is visiting. Lionkin honor runs hot, and disputes are settled by public challenge — combat, contest, or oratory — before an audience that treats a good fight the way other peoples treat theater. Hospitality is a display of wealth, and a visitor is an audience.\n\nThe lionkin carry the knowledge that their own kind produced the tyrant the whole grass sea buried, the king whose conquest gave the land Moot Law. Most prides wear that as a check on themselves and despise the memory. A few mutter that the old king's only failing was weakness, that he simply lacked the strength to finish what he began.\n\nNothing offends Goldentor like the warlord Vaskarn. He is lowborn, clanless, and self-crowned, and he has taken the title Pride of Prides, which the prides hold to be theirs to grant and his to have stolen.",
      "areas": {
        "The Tor Road": {
          "description": "A processional path carved into the tor face, wide enough for lionkin to walk three abreast. It climbs the slope in long switchbacks, exposed to the wind and the open grass below, and the summit's banners stand bright against the sky the whole way up. Stone posts along the path are carved with the marks of prides that have held the tor.",
          "paths": [
