    "Longrun": {
      "name": "Longrun",
      "x": 21,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Wild Grass Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "basicInfo": "Where the great herds pass through during migration, the wolfkin converge. Longrun is a hunting ground, a proving ground, and the closest thing wolfkin have to a homeland. A keeper-pack holds the site year-round, watching the herds and maintaining the runs. When migration season comes, packs from across the grass sea arrive, and the great hunt begins.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Wolfkin are pack-nomads who follow herds and patrol territory. Longrun is the exception — the one place they return to. The keeper-pack is a permanent garrison of sorts, volunteers from multiple packs who've chosen to stay and steward the land. Other packs respect them but consider the choice unusual.\n\nThe great hunt is the most important event in wolfkin culture. It's where young wolves earn their names, where pack alliances are forged or broken, and where pack-leaders prove their worth. Hunts are coordinated across multiple packs. Waste is forbidden — everything taken is used.\n\nSome wolfkin have started staying at Longrun past their pack's rotation. They like the stability, the connections, the sense of place. Their packs consider this somewhere between eccentric and disloyal.\n\nPopulation is predominantly wolfkin. Other beastfolk visit but don't linger — wolfkin hospitality is real but spare, and the pack rhythms of daily life can feel exclusionary to outsiders.",
      "areas": {
        "The Keeper's Camp": {
          "description": "A permanent encampment on a low ridge. Hide shelters built for function, not comfort. A central fire-ring where the keeper-pack shares meals and receives  scouts, traders and visitors.",
          "paths": [
            "The Runs",
            "The Muster Ground"
          ]
        },
        "The Runs": {
          "description": "A wide natural channel between rocky ridges where the great herds funnel through during the season. Outside of migration, it's open grassland marked by old drive-lines of stacked stone. During the hunt, it transforms: wolfkin packs positioned along the ridges, signals passing between them, the ground shaking as the herds move through.",
          "paths": [
            "The Keeper's Camp"
          ]
        },
        "The Muster Ground": {
          "description": "A flat clearing where the packs gather when the herds are close. During season, it's a sprawl of pack-camps, each with its own banner and fire. The pack-leaders meet at a central ring to plan the hunt — who drives, who flanks, who takes the first kill. Between seasons, it's empty and quiet, just trampled grass and old fire-circles waiting.",
          "paths": [
            "The Keeper's Camp"
          ]
        }
      },
