    "Kingsgrave Kurgan": {
      "name": "Kingsgrave Kurgan",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Wild Grass Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A massive earthen mound rising from the flat grass sea, ringed by standing stones and watched by a permanent guard drawn from every beastfolk species. The sorcerer-emperor who once enslaved the grass sea is sealed inside. The wards are ancient, the guardians vigilant. Things still get out, and people still try to get in.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The sorcerer-emperor was a lionkin of immense power who bound the beastfolk through domination magic, turned the species against each other, and built an empire on enslaved minds. The peoples broke him together, and because they could not be sure death would hold him, they sealed him in the kurgan and set a guard. This is a prison, not a tomb, and the thing inside it is not certainly dead.\n\nThe seals are degrading and the knowledge of how they were raised has eroded. What leaks out is bound dead, fragments of compulsion magic, and spirits that trouble wildlife and unlucky travelers. The leaking power answers to radiant weapons — silver, moonstone, the blessed edge — and turns ordinary blades; against the compulsions themselves a strong will is the better armor.\n\nTreasure-seekers are a constant problem, since the emperor was buried with the wealth of his conquests. Worse than the looters are the Kingsworn, who hear the mound's call and answer it, working to wake what sleeps inside and set it ruling again. They probe the breach, buy ways in from the gnolls, and recruit from the proud and the humiliated across every people of the grass.",
      "areas": {
        "The Standing Stones": {
          "description": "A ring of carved stones circles the mound's base, each cut with ward-signs from a different beastfolk tradition. The guardian camp sits among them, practical and permanent: watch-fires, hide shelters, and sentries from several species sharing the watch.",
          "paths": [
            "The Processional",
            "The Breach"
          ]
        },
        "The Processional": {
          "description": "A stone-lined passage drives into the side of the mound, its walls carved with warnings. The light fails quickly past the entrance. A heavy sealed door stands at the end of the guarded stretch, and the carvings grow denser around it.",
          "paths": [
            "The Standing Stones",
            "The Sealed Halls"
          ]
        },
        "The Sealed Halls": {
          "description": "The tomb complex proper: corridors of packed earth reinforced with bone and stone, branching into unmapped chambers. Ward-signs are cut into the walls at the thresholds, some still faintly lit, others dark and cold. The passages run inward and downward toward a burial chamber at the heart.",
          "paths": [
            "The Processional"
          ]
        },
        "The Breach": {
          "description": "A collapsed section on the mound's eastern slope, where something dug its way out from the inside. It has been sealed and has reopened more than once: the current patch is a raw fill of stone, stake, and timber, newer than everything around it, with the old sealed scars layered beside it. The grass grows thin and wrong on the slope here.",
          "paths": [
            "The Standing Stones"
          ]
        }
      },
