    "Hag's Rock": {
      "name": "Hag's Rock",
      "x": -24,
      "y": 8,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Wild Grass Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "basicInfo": "A tor on the grass sea where a community of witches has made their home. The beastfolk call it the Hag's Tor, and even though the reputation of the witches isn't fully compatible with this name, it seems to have stuck. The witches provide healing, potions, and magical services to the beastfolk, who in turn leave them in peace — an arrangement both sides consider ideal. What else the witches get up to on their tor is a matter of lively speculation across the grass sea.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Despite the name, one thing is immediately obvious upon arriving here: none of the witches remotely resembles a hag either in age, beauty or demeanor. In fact, they are all conspicuously young, beautiful and quite friendly to strangers, although they do enjoy pranking visitors by appearing as conventional hags from time to time. The witches settled the grass sea because the beastfolk leave them alone. The understanding is practical — the witches provide healing, potions, midwifery, and magical services to anyone who visits. The beastfolk provide food and a guarantee that nobody comes looking for the witches with torches. Both sides consider this arrangement ideal.\n\nThe community is mostly human and half-elf women, with a few exceptions in every category. They are refugees of a sort — women whose magical talents made them unwelcome in more 'civilized' places. The grass sea doesn't care what you are as long as you don't try to rule anyone.\n\nThe tor's caves are far grander than their entrances suggest — the witches have shaped the interiors with magic into airy, elegant spaces that wouldn't be out of place in a palace. Silk hangings, enchanted lighting, impossibly comfortable furnishings. The contrast between the modest exterior and the lavish interior is deliberate and amusing to the witches. Familiars — cats, ravens, foxes, and stranger things — roam freely. Brooms and implements drift through the air on errands.",
      "areas": {
        "The Tor Path": {
          "description": "A winding path up the tor's gentle slope, lined with herb gardens and wildflowers that have no business growing on bare rock. Cats watch from the ledges. A broom drifts past carrying a bundle of herbs. The smell of cooking drifts down from above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Kitchen",
            "The Apothecary"
          ]
        },
        "The Kitchen": {
          "description": "The social heart of the tor — an open-air cooking and gathering space under a canvas awning, with a long table, mismatched chairs, and a fire that's always going. Familiars weave between the chair legs. The witches eat here, receive visitors here, and conduct most of their business over food and drink.",
          "paths": [
            "The Tor Path",
            "The Apothecary",
            "The Caves"
          ]
        },
        "The Apothecary": {
          "description": "A cave carved into the tor's upper face, shelved floor to ceiling with jars, bottles, dried herbs, and things in suspension that are best not examined closely. The witches' workshop and storefront. Potions, salves, remedies, and more exotic preparations are available for trade. The prices are fair. The advice that comes with them is free and unsolicited.",
          "paths": [
            "The Tor Path",
            "The Kitchen"
          ]
        },
        "The Caves": {
          "description": "The witches' private quarters, carved into the tor and shaped by magic into something that has no right to exist inside a rock. Vaulted ceilings, silk hangings, enchanted lights that follow you from room to room. Brooms and bottles float through corridors on errands. Every cave is different — one witch's chambers are a candlelit library, another's a moonlit garden that can't possibly be underground. Visitors are welcome by invitation. The invitation usually comes with wine.",
          "paths": [
            "The Kitchen"
          ]
        }
      },
