    "Kalanth Landing": {
      "name": "Kalanth Landing",
      "x": -37,
      "y": -7,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Ntar Vanna",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Kalanth Landing is the riverside estate of House Kalanth, the wealthiest family on the lower Saranadi, built where the river bends around their own private landing. Part plantation, part trading house, part pleasure-retreat, it spreads across terraced gardens and spice groves around a great open hall built for entertaining.",
      "hiddenInfo": "House Kalanth is the demonborn merchant-house that grew richest on the lower river, and everyone on the Saranadi knows that the spice and timber are only half of it. The other half is the river's dirty work. The house runs grave-bronze and vitality-amber out of the jungle's demonborn ruins for buyers who want the find to stay quiet, and on the darker side it moves the things dug out of the demonborn dead: Ur-ichor, the black blood that grants demonic strength to whoever drinks it and burns the humanity out of them; wakeful idols that lend power to the one who rouses them and claim a piece of him in return; and cursed demonborn arms and armor that make the bearer stronger and slowly less himself. The family never handles any of it directly and has never once been caught with a thing it shouldn't have. It is too rich, too well-defended, and too useful to too many people for the Council to move against, and the Council knows it.\n\nKalanth is always hiring the right sort — people who can move a shipment quietly, recover something from the Swallowed Cities. A newcomer is received graciously, sized up, and given small work; those who prove useful and discreet rise into the family's trust and its real business. The pay is good, the living is fine, and the work is steadily more lucrative and more dangerous the higher you go.\n\nThe household keeps gardens, spice groves, and a guarded strongroom of coin and leverage around the hall.",
      "areas": {
        "The River Bend": {
          "description": "The estate's private landing on the river bend: a broad stone dock with warehouses behind it and the Kalanth banner flying above. Trade-barges load spice and timber at one end; the family's own boats are moored apart at the other. Goods come and go here without passing the city's downriver inspections.",
          "paths": [
            "The Great Hall"
