        },
        "The Great Hall": {
          "description": "A great open-air hall of pale stone and dark timber facing the water, built for entertaining, with long tables, deep couches, and a view down the river. Guest quarters lie off to one side, conspicuously comfortable; the family's own rooms sit above, private and guarded. The terraced gardens step down toward the water beyond.",
          "paths": [
