    "Sangamadi": {
      "name": "Sangamadi",
      "x": 4,
      "y": 4,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Ntar Vanna",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Sangamadi is a frogkin village built where two great tributaries meet the Saranadi, half on the banks and half on the water — stilt-houses, floating platforms, and boats moored so long they have become buildings. Every vessel going upriver stops here, because past the confluence the river narrows and turns dangerous, and only a Sangamadi pilot knows the way through.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Sangamadi runs the upper river. The frogkin pilot families hold a near-monopoly on the dangerous water above the confluence, and they are cheerfully, completely aware that the whole river depends on them and they depend on no one. They are warm hosts and hard bargainers, unhurried, and serenely certain that Sangamadi is the most important place on the Saranadi — which, since nothing reaches the upper river without them, is difficult to argue. The rival pilot families compete fiercely for the richest upriver contracts, and that rivalry is the village's favorite long-running sport.\n\nInformation reaches Sangamadi before it reaches New Anthara. Every crew that stops to hire or resupply trades news at the floating common, and the frogkin remember all of it. A newcomer who is good company and not in a hurry is made welcome at the table; trust and a pilot's friendship are earned slowly and worth a great deal upriver.\n\nThe grief under the warmth is the Hookmarsh. Ghessek's warband prizes Sangamadi's pilots above any other catch, because a taken pilot brings a ransom and a stranded boat both. Most families here have lost someone to the marsh or paid to get them back, and a pilot gone missing on an upriver run is the village's standing sorrow and its standing call for help.",
      "areas": {
        "The Docks": {
          "description": "The natural anchorage where the two tributaries meet the Saranadi. Boats of every size crowd the moorings, frogkin houses stand on stilts above the waterline, and the pilots' boards advertise routes and rates for the upper river. This is where vessels put in to hire and resupply.",
          "paths": [
            "The Float",
            "The Fish Market",
            "The Still Pool"
          ]
        },
        "The Float": {
          "description": "The village's social heart: interconnected floating platforms anchored in the calmest water, set with cook-fires, low tables, and woven mats, with guest platforms for visitors out at the edge. In the evening the lanterns come out and the whole village gathers on the water. There is always room made at a table for one more.",
          "paths": [
            "The Docks"
          ]
        },
        "The Fish Market": {
          "description": "A broad covered platform where the morning catch is sold, smoked, salted, and cooked. Smoked river-fish packed for New Anthara is a major trade here, and the cook-stalls along the edge compete fiercely over who fries the best of it.",
          "paths": [
            "The Docks"
          ]
        },
        "The Still Pool": {
          "description": "A warm, clear pool fed by a thermal spring and shaded by ancient trees, set apart from the working water. It is sacred to the frogkin, a place of quiet, reflection, and ceremony. Visitors may sit at its edge but do not enter the water uninvited.",
          "paths": [
            "The Docks"
          ]
        }
      },
