    "Shilaghar": {
      "name": "Shilaghar",
      "x": -14,
      "y": 26,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Ntar Vanna",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Shilaghar is the temple-mesa of the serpentkin, a flat-topped height of carved stone rising warm and sun-baked above the canopy over the Saranadi. The serpentkin who hold it are the finest alchemists in the south, masters of medicine, venom, and the craft that lies between, and their cures, antidotes, and poisons travel far up and down the river.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Shilaghar is the south's great school of alchemy, and the place an alchemist comes to be made a master. The serpentkin teach the whole of the craft to a student with the gift — brewing, medicine, venom, antidote, and balance — taken in, taught by degrees over long warm seasons, and set free only once they have learned to hold life and death in the same two hands.\n\nTo the serpentkin the craft is one thing, not two: the knowledge that brews a cure brews a death, and they neither hide it nor make a drama of it. They are warm, unhurried, and dryly funny, gracious hosts with nothing left to prove, and they find the feuding hotheads of the lower river a little exhausting. A guest is welcomed onto the warm stone and fed and made comfortable; the serpentkin are slow to take offense and impossible to fluster, having long since stopped being frightened of anything.\n\nTheir neutrality is real and self-interested. Holding themselves keepers of the balance between life and death, they stay clear of the river's quarrels, which is why every rival power trusts them and no one moves against the mesa.\n\nSome serpentkin turned to the Children of Ur, the cult that digs the demonic things out of the ruins, and went to serve them — the worst breaking of the balance there is. The temple disowns these kin utterly and works against them, and the masters set their proven students and capable outsiders to hunt the cult's work and bring back the corrupted things to be destroyed.",
      "areas": {
        "The Dispensary": {
          "description": "The mesa's broad market terrace, where the serpentkin sell their work from stone stalls and shopfronts: medicines, antidotes, and remedies on one side, venomwood blades and green-glass weapons on another, and the poisons sold plainly alongside the cures for them. Buyers come up from the river to trade here, and the canopy spreads out below the warm terrace edge.",
          "paths": [
            "The Workshops",
            "The Venom Gardens",
            "The Coil"
          ]
        },
        "The Workshops": {
          "description": "Sun-warmed stone halls where the alchemy is taught and done: stills, presses, and worktables of cut green glass, racks of dried reagents, and warded cabinets for the dangerous stock. Masters work at the long benches and set their students to the slow labor of the craft, healing and venom both.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dispensary",
            "The Venom Gardens"
          ]
        },
        "The Venom Gardens": {
          "description": "Terraced gardens stepping down the mesa's flank, planted with venomwood and the herbs, vines, and fungi the serpentkin draw their craft from. Tenders move among the rows in gloves and veils, and the rarest and most dangerous growths are kept behind low walls at the garden's heart.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dispensary",
            "The Workshops"
          ]
        },
        "The Coil": {
          "description": "The warm heart of the mesa: a great open hall at the summit built around a sun-warmed basking-floor, ringed with low couches, quiet pools, and the slow smoke of cook-fires. The serpentkin take their long meals and slow talk here, draped at their ease, and a guest is given a place on the warm stone. The whole river-country spreads out below through the open colonnade.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dispensary"
          ]
        }
      },
