    "Citadel Uchaghar": {
      "name": "Citadel Uchaghar",
      "x": 3,
      "y": 24,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Ntar Vanna",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Citadel Uchaghar is the seat of the Vanarin, a monkeyfolk people, built into and onto a great stone island where the Saranadi narrows between high jungle banks. The Vanarin have held this rock for as long as anyone can remember and have never lost it.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Uchaghar is the seat of the Vanarin and the home of the proudest people on the Saranadi. A High King rules from the summit hall; succession comes by acclaim, challenge, and elaborate contest. The Vanarin are fast, fearless warriors who fight in three dimensions, dropping from the canopy and the rope-slides onto anything that threatens the river-narrows, and they hold that the rock has never fallen because they are the ones holding it.\n\nThe Vanarin are one of the two great martial powers of Ntar Vanna, and they take the open fight to the Children of Ur — ranging upriver and into the demonborn ruins to meet the cult's diggers with steel and burn out what they raise. This is the work that wins regard at the High Court, and a newcomer who fights the cult well can earn a name among them.\n\nThe feud with the gajanari of Durg Sthira is old and bottomless, and at root it is about which of them is the river's true shield. The Vanarin think the gajanari hide behind walls and armor and craft, fighting pretty and slow; they are certain that valor, speed, and the unconquered rock make the Vanarin the first people of the Saranadi. Neither side will ever concede it, and both are proud enough to keep score forever.\n\nThe Vanarin welcome boldness and despise caution. A guest who is brave, generous, and good in a fight is taken up gladly; one who is timid or stingy is mocked openly and without malice.",
      "areas": {
        "The Stone Market": {
          "description": "The broad platform at the island's base where the current slackens and boats put in. Permanent shops and stalls are carved into the rock — jungle fruit, canopy herbs, river fish, woven and carved goods — and the great stone island rises overhead from here, terraces and galleries climbing to the summit far above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Long Drop",
            "The High Court"
          ]
        },
        "The Long Drop": {
          "description": "A tavern and inn set in a natural cave halfway up the rock, with a stone terrace hung with hammocks out over a sheer fall to the river far below. Fruit wines and fermented jungle drinks are served at all hours. The warriors take their ease and their boasting here, lounging at the very edge.",
          "paths": [
            "The Stone Market",
            "The High Court"
          ]
        },
        "The High Court": {
          "description": "The island's summit: a great hall of stone and timber where the High King holds court, receives visitors, and presides over feasts. Banners and the trophies of old fights hang from the rafters, and the throne is carved from the rock of the island itself. The view reaches out over the canopy on both banks.",
          "paths": [
            "The Stone Market",
            "The Long Drop",
            "The Rope Launch"
          ]
        },
        "The Rope Launch": {
          "description": "A platform near the summit where thick braided ropes stretch down and away to the canopy on both banks. The ropes slope outward from the rock, so the Vanarin can launch into the trees at speed but no one can climb them inward. Warriors drill formation launches here, and scouts set out from it into the deep jungle.",
          "paths": [
            "The High Court"
          ]
        }
