    "Durg Sthira": {
      "name": "Durg Sthira",
      "x": 16,
      "y": 16,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Ntar Vanna",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Durg Sthira is a great fortress and town raised by the gajanari, an elephantfolk people, on a bend of the Saranadi. It is the finest built architecture in Ntar Vanna — pale grey walls, towers, and buttresses that seem grown rather than built, set on a bluff of shaped stone above the river. Below the citadel, the town is known across the south for its smiths, artificers, and enchanters, and buyers come from far away for gajanari-forged work.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Durg Sthira is the craft seat of Ntar Vanna and the home of its finest makers. The ruling matriarch governs with the family matriarchs, who remember every agreement, precedent, and debt exactly as it was made — gajanari memory is perfect, and among them memory is law. The town forges the best arms, armor, jewelry, and enchanted work in the south, and the gajanari practice arcane memory: a spell witnessed once is reconstructed through perfect recall. Their war-forgers go to battle in masterwork armor of their own making.\n\nThe gajanari are one of the two great martial powers of Ntar Vanna, and they meet the Children of Ur with weight where the Vanarin meet them with speed. Their war-forgers are the heavy line that goes into the demonborn ruins and holds, and their forges arm the whole fight against the cult. A maker or a fighter who proves themselves against the cult earns standing here.\n\nThe feud with the Vanarin monkeyfolk of Uchaghar is old and bottomless, and at root it is about which of them is the river's true shield. The gajanari hold that the Vanarin are reckless acrobats who fight pretty and die young, all valor and no staying power, while real defense is the wall that holds and the armor that turns the blow.",
      "areas": {
        "The Forge Quarter": {
          "description": "The town's working heart, reached from the stone quays at the river bend: streets of smithies, armories, jewelers, and artificers' workshops climbing toward the citadel. Finished arms, armor, and enchanted goods are sold from the shopfronts, and buyers come from across Larion to commission work.",
          "paths": [
            "The Thunderfoot",
            "The Proving Yard",
            "The Matriarch's Court",
            "The League Chapterhouse"
          ]
        },
        "The Thunderfoot": {
          "description": "The town's largest tavern, built around a courtyard with a stone stage for gajanari musicians and their deep drums, reed pipes, and bass voices. Slow-roasted meat, river fish in banana leaf, and spiced rice are served at long tables. A posting wall along one side carries dangerous work beyond the forge-families' ordinary obligations — stolen masterwork, armed river trouble, cult signs, ruin expeditions, and great beasts requiring more than a town watch. Petitioners mark what they will pay, and gajanari veterans add blunt corrections when a danger has been understated.",
          "paths": [
            "The Forge Quarter"
          ]
        },
        "The Proving Yard": {
          "description": "A broad stone courtyard where finished work is tested and the war-forgers train, sparring in full armor of their own making. Targets, test-frames, and weapon-stands line the walls. Disputes between rival forge-families are sometimes settled here, in the open.",
          "paths": [
            "The Forge Quarter",
            "The Matriarch's Court"
          ]
