      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The capital of the Empire of Light, a city of colonnades, forums, and canals, built on land reclaimed from the lagoon where the old city had sunk. Above it floats the Eye of God, an enormous sky citadel of gold-bright brass. It is the seat of the refounded empire and the busiest port on this coast, and people of every kind come here to trade, to take the empire's coin, and to make a life under its law.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Caranthoria is a bright, orderly city, the capital of the refounded Empire of Light. The empire takes citizens of every people, and the streets show it: humans, lizardfolk and frogkin off the water, turtlefolk masons and engineers, ratfolk in the tunnels below, and outsiders from every region come for the work. The day-to-day is run by the empire's prefects and kept by the legion; the Empress reigns from the Eye and rarely comes down.\n\nThe Eye of God is the citadel floating above the city — the throne of the empire. She raised it from the lagoon when she came home and refounded the empire, and the work of finishing it never stops overhead. No one goes up to the Eye without the Empress's invitation.\n\nThe legion is the city's great institution and always hiring. To swear in is to take three things together: citizenship, the sun-brand at the neck, and the Unity — the mind-bond that lets a century fight as one, shields locking without an order spoken, no soldier ever alone in the line. The Harrowers keep a hall in the Legion Quarter: a small sworn order who hunt the demon-tainted.\n\nThe empire's war runs west into the fens, against the lizardfolk dragon-kingdom of the Reedmoot; the Forum's bounties post swamp-creature culls and outlaw-hunts for that frontier and for the deserter-ruins east of the city.\n\nThe Syndicate works out of the Warrens, smuggling past the legion and fencing salvage the empire would confiscate. It moves nullmetal — a dull grey alloy that deadens the mind-arts and the Unity, which the empire pays bounties to keep off the market.",
