    "The Eye of God": {
      "name": "The Eye of God",
      "x": -2,
      "y": 29,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Great Lagoon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Eye of God floats above Caranthoria, a vast sky-citadel of gold-bright brass raised from the drowned old capital by Empress Aurianax III. Ancient domes, towers, and solar ornaments stand beside new scaffolds and unfinished plates, and a great eye-like lens opens in its underside. The Eye is the throne of the Empire of Light; visitors ascend from the city by invitation, while the work of rebuilding it continues overhead.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Eye of God is not a neighboring site on the ground. Its position beside Caranthoria on the map represents the ascent from the city into the citadel above it. The Imperial Palace below conducts the empire's daily government; the Eye is Aurianax's residence, court, and throne.\n\nAurianax raised the wreck from the lagoon when she returned from Ur. Much of the old citadel is sound, but whole sections remain drowned, broken, or sealed behind ancient defenses. Imperial dredgers recover its fallen fabric from the old city, and engineers, artificers, and labor crews fit those pieces back into the structure. Reconstruction never stops, although the inhabited court is kept bright, orderly, and ceremonially complete.\n\nEntry is controlled. The principal ascent runs from a guarded imperial station in Caranthoria to the Ascension Hall. Invitations are issued for embassies, imperial summonses, judgments, triumphs, and exceptional service; an invitation grants access only to the named guest and the permitted parts of the Eye. Winged approach, climbing the tethers, or entering with the work crews is possible but treated as an attack on the imperial throne.\n\nThe great lens is a weapon of the old Third Empire, built to gather and focus sunlight upon the land below. It is not yet fully restored. The Lensworks and the older mechanisms behind it are among the most restricted places in the empire, and only Aurianax and a small circle of sworn engineers know how near the work is to completion.",
      "areas": {
        "The Ascension Hall": {
          "description": "The formal entrance to the Eye, a many-tiered hall of gold-bright brass where the imperial lift from Caranthoria arrives beneath armed galleries. Winged couriers land on open balconies above it. Guests surrender weapons or declare them, invitations are checked against sealed rolls, and escorts wait beside doors marked for the court, the household, and the work crews.",
          "paths": [
            "The Court of Light",
            "The Hall of Concord"
          ]
        },
        "The Court of Light": {
          "description": "Aurianax's audience hall, built around a long open nave beneath a radiant brass dome. The imperial throne stands on a shallow dais before tall apertures overlooking Caranthoria and the lagoon, so the city lies visibly below every audience. Envoys, commanders, petitioners, and honored servants of the empire are received here under the banners of the refounding.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ascension Hall",
            "The Hall of Concord"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Concord": {
          "description": "A guarded suite of council chambers, map rooms, archives, and offices serving the imperial court. Prefects come up from the palace, legion commanders report from the front, Falmastran advisors attend the Empress, and sealed dispatches arrive from across the empire. Doors from the public chambers lead toward the restricted works deeper in the citadel.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ascension Hall",
            "The Court of Light",
            "The Lensworks"
          ]
        },
        "The Lensworks": {
          "description": "The restricted heart of the rebuilding project: concentric galleries surrounding a colossal lens assembly of glass, crystal, mirrors, and articulated brass. Scaffolds cross the open shaft, salvaged pieces wait under guard, and shutters in the citadel's underside expose Caranthoria and the lagoon far below. Entry is limited to sworn engineers, guarded work crews, and those admitted by the Empress herself.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Concord"
          ]
        }
      },
