    "The Scrabble": {
      "name": "The Scrabble",
      "basicInfo": "A wide, broken cavern in Grell Hollows where the Delvers' Lift from Ardan's Watch lands on a bolted ledge beside the cold pool fed by Moss Gulley. The walls are old cut stone, the buried streets and halls of the dead city choked with rubble and worn into a warren of small chambers. The Scrabble is the League's only regular foothold and main staging place for work in the Hollows: crews form up here, salvage is caged and tagged, maps are chalked on boards, and a League field representative keeps local jobs moving. Kobold raiders attack the landing from the old street-warrens, trying to cut the lift, steal cargo, or drag injured delvers into the dark.",
      "x": -42,
      "y": -20,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Grell Hollows",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": false,
      "hiddenInfo": "The Scrabble is the League's lift-bottom foothold in Grell Hollows, not a safe town. It exists because the Delvers' Lift can bring crews, rope, lamps, stretcher cases, packframes, and guarded salvage straight down from the Basement of Ardan's Watch. Brelka Tharn, the League field representative here, keeps the landing working under pressure: she knows which crews are below, which tunnels are hot, which claims are honest, and which jobs are fit for Copper, Bronze, or stronger adventurers.\n\nUse this location to award Grell Hollows quests while the party is physically in the Grell Hollows region. Appropriate work includes scouting fresh passages, rescuing missing crews, clearing kobold pressure from the landing, escorting salvage, checking monster signs, mapping routes toward the Shrine or the Imperial Baths, and settling immediate field problems before they become disasters. Brelka can report completion, pay hazard bonuses, and send news of larger deeds up to Mona Vashti and the League Hall.\n\nKobolds probe The Scrabble often. They shoot from old doorways, rush the barricades when the lift is loaded, cut lamps, spoil rope, and use flooded side passages to appear where no one expected them. The landing has patched barricades, alarm bells, a casualty cot, supply lockers, and salvage cages, but the dark around it belongs to whoever can hold it. The stream-shaft to Moss Gulley remains a secondary natural route up and down; it is slower, wetter, and more dangerous than the lift.",
      "areas": {
        "Darkwater Cavern": {
          "description": "The lift-bottom landing of Grell Hollows: a wide cavern of broken imperial stone where the Delvers' Lift stops on a bolted ledge above a cold pool. Lantern gantries, patched barricades, a signal bell, salvage cages, a casualty cot, and a chalk route-map crowd the ledge while the old streets of the dead city fan into rubble-dark beyond. The stream from Moss Gulley falls down a shaft along one wall, marking the slower natural climb back toward daylight, and the pool drains through a flooded passage deeper into the Underworld. Kobold raiders strike from the street-warrens often enough that every crew here keeps a weapon within reach.",
