    "The Upper Halls": {
      "name": "The Upper Halls",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -2,
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "Darek Deep",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The top level of the Darek Deep, where the great shaft from Deepgate drops into a hall of huge stone figures of dareks lining the walls. A broad road of polished black stone runs the length of the floor with iron constructs standing on it in a line, all toppled and shattered, a procession that halted and never resumed. Delvers have fortified the ground beneath the shaft, but the hall stretches into darkness in every direction.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Great Hall is the military heart of the dead city. The dareks built their constructs in the forges below, marched them through this hall along the black road, and deployed them along the three ways out. The iron figures on the road are the last march — halted when whatever ended the dareks ended them, shattered, rusted and silent.\n\nDelvers have fortified the shaft-foot into a base camp: lanterns, rope stores, cached supplies, a fire. This is the one safe ground in the Deep, held by numbers and habit. Kobolds and goblins from the Underworld creep into the hall's edges; morlocks come up from the warrens; a construct intrudes now and then. The camp holds, but the dark around it does not belong to the surfacers.\n\nThe three roads out follow the black road's branches. Toward the forges where the constructs were made — machines, black iron, the old works. Toward the warrens where morlocks now live in darek barracks gnawed into dens. Up the high stair toward the seat of rule, the grandest and most dangerous part of the city.",
      "areas": {
        "The Great Hall": {
          "description": "Where the shaft from Deepgate comes down. The cages land in a hall so large the far walls are lost in the dark. Stone figures of the dareks stand along the walls, twice the height of a man, stern and watching. A broad road of black stone runs the length of the floor, and on it iron constructs lie toppled. Delvers have roped off the ground beneath the shaft and built a base camp of lanterns and fire. Beyond the light, the hall belongs to the dead city.",
