    "The Black Forge": {
      "name": "The Black Forge",
      "x": -25,
      "y": 26,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "Darek Deep",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": false,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The forge-halls of the Darek Deep, down the Forge-Road from the Upper Halls, where the dareks made their iron soldiers. Great cold forges and dead machines fill halls that go deeper than a lamp will show. The salvage here is the richest in the Deep — black iron, darek alloy, blank soulstones, and mechanisms worth a fortune topside.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Black Forge is the construct-works of the dead city, and it is actively defended. The constructs here are not dormant sentries that wake when you stumble on them. They are garrison troops holding their facility, and they fight like it: ambushes from side passages, traps rigged from old mechanisms, chutes that drop intruders into lower halls, forge-vents that blast heat, corridors that seal behind you. They use the terrain because they built it and they know every door and mechanism in it.\n\nBlack iron is common here — raw stock, finished parts, weapons. Blank soulstones can be pried from downed constructs: the souls in them can be freed (an act of mercy, since the Princes of Ur bound them there) or the live stones can be taken for the fortune they fetch from wizards and the desperate. The deeper you push, the better the salvage and the smarter the defense.\n\nGreloq's Company runs expeditions here regularly and knows the upper halls well. Independent parties who venture in may find Greloq's crew already working a corridor — or find their exit route suddenly occupied.",
      "areas": {
        "The Forge-Gate": {
          "description": "Where the Forge-Road from the Upper Halls ends at a heavy passage built to be held. The walls narrow, the ceiling drops, and the marks of old fighting are everywhere — gouged stone, broken iron, the wreckage of crews and constructs both. Beyond this chokepoint the halls open into the forges.",
          "paths": [
