    "The Morlock Warrens": {
      "name": "The Morlock Warrens",
      "x": 25,
      "y": -24,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "Darek Deep",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": false,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The lower halls of the Darek Deep where the morlocks live, past the Warren-Mouth from the Upper Halls. Once these were darek halls. Now they are fouled and packed with the nests and refuse of a living people. The morlocks are pale, cunning, and many, and they know these halls better than any delver alive. Not everything in the warrens is ruin. Somewhere deep in the back, past the nests and the hoard, the morlocks keep a place they will not enter themselves.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Warrens are the morlock holdfast of the dead city, reached past the Warren-Mouth from the Upper Halls.\n\nThe morlocks are the dareks — or what became of them. The people who built this city did not all die. Some remained and sank into the dark across uncounted ages, forgetting what they were, dwindling into the pale cunning things that now squat in halls their own forebears raised. They do not know this. They have forgotten everything but habit.\n\nMorlocks are hostile to surfacers. They do not trade, do not parley, and do not tolerate intrusion. They attack from ambush, in numbers, using traps and knowledge of every passage. They are not mindless — they are cunning, coordinated, and fight to kill. A party entering the warrens is in enemy territory against a force that knows every inch of it and wants them dead. Do not have morlocks attempt to communicate, negotiate, or show curiosity toward the party. They are defending their home from invaders and that is all.\n\nThe secret of the Darek Deep is in the Kept Hall, the sanctum at the back of the warrens that even morlocks will not enter. There a single morlock unlike the others works alone among clean darek stone and functioning tools, mending broken constructs with procedures passed down through generations as ritual. The constructs it mends get back up and walk out into the halls. This is why the Deep's guardians have not broken down after an age of neglect.",
      "areas": {
        "The Foul Halls": {
          "description": "The border of morlock country, past the Warren-Mouth. Old darek stone gone black with filth, stacked with bones and nesting material. Morlock sentries watch from the dark. Beyond this point the halls belong to them.",
          "paths": [
            "The Nests",
            "The Hoard-Deep"
          ]
        },
        "The Nests": {
          "description": "The crowded heart of the warrens, where the morlocks den and breed in halls packed close and stinking. They are thickest here and fight hardest for it. The noise is constant — shrieking, scraping, the knock of stone tools. This is their home ground.",
          "paths": [
            "The Foul Halls",
            "The Hoard-Deep"
          ]
        },
        "The Hoard-Deep": {
          "description": "The deepest part of the warrens, where the morlocks keep what they have stolen from the dead city over the ages. Darek treasure, black iron, salvage, and stranger things lie heaped in the dark, guarded by the strongest of them. Past the hoard, a single passage runs further back into a part of the warrens the morlocks themselves avoid.",
          "paths": [
            "The Nests",
            "The Kept Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Kept Hall": {
          "description": "A darek workshop at the back of the warrens, behind the hoard, through a passage the morlocks will not follow. The stone here is clean. The tools on the racks are whole and ordered. A workbench holds a construct laid open, its parts arranged with care. Everything in this room has been maintained while the rest of the city fell to ruin. Something has been working here for a very long time.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hoard-Deep"
          ]
        }
      },
