    "The Temple of Dominion": {
      "name": "The Temple of Dominion",
      "x": 26,
      "y": 24,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "Darek Deep",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": false,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The temple-seat of the Darek Deep, where the dareks ruled and worshipped. This is where the soul-stones were made, and the treasures here are the richest and strangest in the Deep. Grand halls of carved stone climb toward a great sanctum, and over all of it presides a vast idol of the Ur demon the dareks served. It is the deepest the constructs run, and the strongest of them keep these halls.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Temple of Dominion is the holy and cruel heart of the dead city, climbed by the High Stair from the Upper Halls. It holds the deepest lore, the richest singular treasures, and the worst danger in the Deep.\n\nHere the dareks served an Ur demon of dominion — mastery, the owning of others, the binding of the living into endless service. This is the idea behind the whole Deep: every soul-stone is a person made property, every construct a slave that cannot die or rest. The Princes of Ur made the soul-stones in this temple, binding souls into gems by a great rite, and turning the darek arts to their cruelest end.\n\nThe binding-engine still stands in the deepest chamber, but it is destroyed — shattered into pieces and fused and warped, wrecked by some hand of a heroic age and left broken past any working. What it did is still plain, because a huge relief carved in elderstone covers the wall: the rite shown whole, a soul drawn from a bound victim into a waiting stone, darek priests attending, the demon of dominion above them all. And the way to the engine runs through the cells where the victims were held — rows of stone pens, long empty, the bones of the used-up still in them.",
      "areas": {
        "The Processional": {
          "description": "The top of the High Stair, where it opens into the temple. A grand ceremonial way runs inward, lined with tall darek figures carved in stone, worn but still imposing. The grandeur of the dead city is plainest here. The way leads on to the great hall.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of the Idol"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of the Idol": {
          "description": "The great hall of the temple, where the dareks ruled and worshipped. A vast idol of the Ur demon of dominion stands over a high seat, carved in dark stone, looming over the whole chamber. The richest singular treasures of the Deep lie here. Strong constructs keep this hall, and more stand between it and the chambers beyond.",
          "paths": [
            "The Processional",
            "The Cells",
            "The Binding-Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Cells": {
          "description": "Rows of stone pens below the great hall, where the victims were held before the rite. They are long empty now, but the bones of the used-up still lie in them. The way to the deepest chamber runs through here.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of the Idol",
            "The Binding-Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Binding-Hall": {
          "description": "The deepest chamber of the temple, where the soul-stones were made. The binding-engine stands at its center, shattered — broken into pieces and fused and warped, wrecked by some great force long ago. On the wall behind it, a huge relief carved in elderstone shows the binding rite: a soul drawn from a bound victim into a waiting stone, darek priests attending, the demon of dominion above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Cells",
            "The Hall of the Idol"
          ]
        }
      },
