      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Drusavia is the capital of the Duchy of Drusavia: a gracious city of pale stone, steep roofs, arched bridges, and high gothic towers, rich on the wine, timber, and silver of its dales. Two heights crown it. On one stands the Temple of Galard, bright and gothic, raised to the god of courage after the Liberation. Opposite it rises the Black Tower, seat of the Shadow Inquisition, the duchy's hunters of the restless dead. The duke rules from the square between them.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Drusavia is human-led, prosperous, and proud of itself: an old city that broke its vampire lords two hundred years ago and has lived well since. The ducal house governs city and land with a fair hand and a light one; the duke blesses both the Temple and the Inquisition and commands neither, and keeping it that way is the ducal family's oldest skill. A small but wealthy moon elf community lives among the city's upper circles. Its old families keep townhouses near the Grand Galleries and Ducal Square, fund magical workshops and salons, compete for noble patronage, and maintain private traditions of spellcraft, dueling, and courtship. They are not a separate government, but their money and magic open doors that remain closed to most of the city. Dwarves hold many of the finest workshops in the Grand Galleries, working blessed arms, silver, moonstone, jewelry, instruments, and other beautiful commissions for the Temple, the Tower, nobles, and ambitious young buyers. The city keeps the country's customs at city scale: old stone, high manners, strong drink, public ceremony, and a lively appetite for fashion, music, games, and gossip.\n\nThe city runs on the dales' trade — Rovena's wine and cordials, Kolbeck's grimwood and carving, grain, silver, fine clothing, jewelry, food, and high-end craft. Work for capable strangers is everywhere: merchant houses hiring escorts for the dale roads, families wanting someone found or brought home, nobles looking for discreet agents, and the Temple and the Tower recruiting in their own fashion. The Syndicate runs quiet business through the city's fences, but most of Drusavia's daily life is bright, social, and prosperous enough to make people forget how close the old danger remains.",
