    "Black Tower": {
      "name": "Black Tower",
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "radius": 1,
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "x": -6,
      "y": -26,
      "basicInfo": "The Black Tower is the headquarters of the Shadow Inquisition, Drusavia's ghost-hunters and occult investigators. It rises opposite the Temple of Galard, dark and narrow where the temple is bright and open. Accepted Initiates bear the Mark of Rhadan and work one supervised surface case before they may undergo the Rite of Bonding at the Pit of Shadow and become full Shade-Bonded Inquisitors.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Black Tower is not a League chapterhouse and not a ducal office. It is an independent specialist institution blessed by Drusavia because no one else can do its work. The duke blesses the Inquisition but does not command it; the Temple distrusts its methods and depends on the results.\n\nThe Shadow Inquisition is a heroic and prestigious institution in Drusavia. Its Inquisitors are known for striking personal style, distinctive weapons, decisive action, sharp exchanges, and the confidence to face supernatural threats directly. They take pride in protecting the living and in doing difficult work with skill and courage. Drusavians may find the Tower's work unsettling, but they respect its results and rarely obstruct an Inquisitor acting under its authority.\n\nEvery accepted member begins as an Initiate and receives the Mark of Rhadan, an oath-mark that identifies them to the Tower and anchors authorized contact with the Shadelands. The Mark is not Inquisitor rank and does not grant a Shade. An Initiate works one qualifying field case under a mentor. If the case is decisively resolved, the Initiate may return to the Pit for the authorized Rite of Bonding. Only by knowingly accepting that permanent bond and emerging with a Shade are they recognized as a full Inquisitor.\n\nInquisitors investigate hauntings at their root, hunt necromancers and the Gravebound, and cross into the Shadelands when a case cannot be resolved from the living side. After three recognized Inquisitor cases they may be raised to Adept, trusted to lead deep descents and other operatives. After four further recognized Adept cases they may be raised to Master and share authority over the order's deepest work, assignments, methods, and defense of the Pit.\n\nThe order binds Shades through consent and warded rite. A bonded Shade is a supernatural partner and shield, not automatically a servant with a fixed personality. Its manner of communication and relationship with its Inquisitor emerge through play. The bond grants Shade-Sight and forms the basis of the Inquisitor's later Shade techniques.",
      "areas": {
        "Lowlamp Lane": {
          "description": "The narrow lane at the Tower's base, full of low blue lamps, quiet doors, nervous petitioners, and shops that serve people who deal with hauntings.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Shadow",
            "Harran's Place",
            "Silver & Salt Outfitters"
          ],
          "images": {
            "establishingShot": {
              "crop": {
                "focus": {
                  "x": 50,
                  "y": 50
