    "The Temple of Galard": {
      "name": "The Temple of Galard",
      "x": 11,
      "y": -25,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Temple of Galard crowns the bright height of Drusavia: a great gothic temple of pale stone and shield-hung halls, raised after the Liberation to the god of courage, whose shield stands between the living and the dark. It is the seat of the Templars Adamant, Drusavia's elite holy warriors, who wear beautiful blessed armor and wield radiant arms against the restless dead. Beneath the temple lie the honored crypts of Castian — the champion who broke the vampire lords — and the liberation-dead.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Galard is worshipped here as the Shieldbearer: courage as the wall between the living and the dead. The Templars Adamant are not negotiators, mediums, or keepers of shades. They do not bind the dead for questioning, bargain with them, or use them against other enemies. They blind and burn shades with radiant force, destroy the bodies and objects that anchor the dead, and close every breach they can reach. Their long purpose is to seal the Pit of Shadow and shut the Shadelands away from the living world.\n\nThe Temple also keeps Galard's Proving-Year custom, which predates the schism with the Knights Vigilant. Any willing person may take up a plain iron Road-Shield, travel beyond the temple, and return here or to another recognized Galard site with accounts, witnesses, or proof of substantial deeds of courage. Three distinct recognized deeds complete the demanded proof. The aspirant then may seek the Shieldbearer oath here, seek the Swordbearer oath above Aldwall, visit both orders, postpone the choice, or swear neither; the Road-Shield grants no order membership before that choice.\n\nA person who freely swears the Shieldbearer oath enters as a Templar Initiate and receives the White-Silver Shield Clasp. One supervised first shield-work earns reception as a full Templar Adamant trusted with independent work. Three recognized works as a Templar Adamant earn promotion to Templar Captain, with authority to direct warders, sealing rites, and willing Templars in the field. Four further great works as Captain may earn acclamation as Templar Champion, trusted with the order's largest defenses, purges, and strategic campaigns. First Sword and the leadership of the Temple are appointed offices, not ordinary ranks beyond Champion.\n\nThe Temple's board of works offers concrete danger: protect warders while they seal a breach, escort a priest through a haunted village, recover a blessed relic from a grave-site where the dead are following it, purge an undead stronghold, or defend a living person whose presence is keeping a haunting open. The Templars hire capable outsiders for work that requires more hands than their order has, but they expect obedience once the rite begins.\n\nThe duchy supports the Temple publicly but fears its demand to close the Pit. The Shadow Inquisition insists that the dead will continue to return and that sealing the crossing would leave Drusavia unable to enter the Shadelands and answer the threat at its source. The Templars Adamant consider this argument a confession of dependence on the enemy. The duke does not want the two orders to come to open blows.\n\nBeneath the temple lie the crypts of Castian and the liberation-dead: the fallen of the war against the vampire lords, buried with full honor under radiant wards, tended daily and visited by pilgrims from across Larion. These dead rest. The crypts are the Temple's proof that the dead can be kept out, and the Templars guard their peace with absolute force.",
      "areas": {
        "The Temple Steps": {
          "description": "Wide stairs climbing the bright height through votive lamps and shield banners, the city spread below and the temple doors above. Pilgrims, guards, and petitioners come and go all day.",
