    "The Daravaine Reaches": {
      "name": "The Daravaine Reaches",
      "x": 33,
      "y": -21,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Daravaine Reaches are lightly forested hills in the east of Drusavia, strewn with the burned estates of the houses purged after the Liberation. The ruins have never been emptied: grave-goods, hidden plate, and sealed strongrooms still turn up in the cellars, and crews still come to dig for them. The hills are lawless. Petty warlords the dales call the Hill Lords hold ruins and crags here, crack the old crypts, and rob whoever the roads deliver.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The purges burned the estates of the old houses and emptied them of the living, but not of everything else. The cellars and crypts of the Reaches still hold the wealth of broken houses — plate, coin, grave-goods, sealed strongrooms the purges never found — and the restless dead of the purged families that rise when their vaults are opened. Barghests, the black grave-hounds, range the burned estates and hunt the hills at dusk.\n\nIMPORTANT: The Hill Lords are half a dozen rival bands, not one force, and they move — a crag held this season stands empty the next, and a band may be out raiding, digging, or feuding with a rival when travelers pass. Where they are met, they are hostile: they rob whoever they can take and kill whoever resists. Two exceptions, flat: anyone worth coin is ransomed rather than killed, and anyone hard enough to walk into a camp with something to sell can trade — the Hill Lords buy and sell grave-goods, relics, and worse without questions, and their camps are the dirtiest market in the duchy. Syndicate buyers and cultists of the Gravebound both come to that market, and the Hill Lords sell to both without caring which is which.\n\nThe digging is the hills' economy and its danger both. A cracked crypt yields loot or wakes its dead, and the Hill Lords crack them anyway because the odds usually favor them. Independent crews come up from the dales to dig the ruins the bands haven't claimed, and the bands take their hauls on the roads home when they can.",
      "areas": {
        "The Old Estate Roads": {
          "description": "Broken hill roads winding between overgrown fields, blackened gateposts, and toppled boundary markers. Ruined estates show on the heights in every direction, and cart tracks — some old, some fresh — turn off toward the diggings.",
          "paths": [
            "The Burned Estates",
            "The Hill Lords' Crags"
          ]
        },
        "The Burned Estates": {
          "description": "The purged houses themselves: fire-hollowed manors and halls on the hilltops, walls standing roofless, cellar mouths dark under the ruins. Some doorways are choked with rubble, some pried open, and dig-spoil and broken vault-stones lie outside more than one.",
          "paths": [
            "The Old Estate Roads",
            "The Hill Lords' Crags"
          ]
        },
        "The Hill Lords' Crags": {
          "description": "Rocky heights above the estates, crowned with broken watchtowers and fortified ruins. Rough palisades patch the old walls, fire-rings and refuse mark the camps, and here and there a banner no lawful house recognizes hangs from a tower — some camps living, some cold and abandoned.",
          "paths": [
            "The Old Estate Roads",
            "The Burned Estates"
          ]
        }
      },
