    "Fort Blackwing": {
      "name": "Fort Blackwing",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 25,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Fort Blackwing is a burned fortress-estate in the hills of eastern Drusavia, seat of the worst of the necromancer-houses broken in the Liberation. The fires that destroyed the house were also its lords' prison: they were sealed in the cellars below. The fort is considered to be cursed and has never been reoccupied, and travelers give it a wide berth.",
      "hiddenInfo": "House Blackwing was the deepest of the old houses in the traffic with the dead, and its lords had gone far enough that death would not keep them: killed in the storming of the fortress, they began to return. Destroying them for good was beyond the Liberation's armies. So the priests entombed the lords in the house's own cellars and burned the fortress over them as a seal — consecrated fire, the whole house made a ward. It has held for generations. Yet the lords of Blackwing are below still, and every year the seal is older.\n\nIMPORTANT: Cultists of the Gravebound come to dig at the sealed ways, working rites with bound dead as labor and guard; they attack intruders on sight, their bound dead leading. The Shadow Inquisition breaks their workings whenever it finds them, so the cult can never dig in for long, and the fort stands empty and silent more often than not. Inquisitors met here are wary of armed strangers but not hostile, and have work for capable hands. Ward-marks, smashed diggings, and the wreckage of both sides' work lie through the ruin from years of this.\n\nThe riches of a great house remain in the black halls — plate, arms, and the instruments and treasures of the old traffic — untouched, because no robber in Drusavia will enter Blackwing.",
