    "The Hollowhill Catacombs": {
      "name": "The Hollowhill Catacombs",
      "x": -37,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Hollowhill Catacombs are an ancient burial site cut into a wooded hill in the countryside. They were built to seal away the tainted dead defeated in the Liberation. To work the seal, rich grave-goods were laid to rest with them: silver, jewels, blessed arms, the wealth of the Lost Houses. Over the ages, as more and more dead were bound away here, the Catacombs grew upward and outward, until it became too easy for grave-robbers to dig their way in. Now the hillside is riddled with entrances, some collapsed, many open. Yet everyone in Drusavia knows the rule: take from the dead of Hollowhill, and the dead come to take it back.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Catacombs were built downward first: after the Liberation, the victors sealed the vampire lords and necromancer-nobles of the Lost Houses at the hill's root, under the heaviest wards and the richest grave-goods, and each generation since dug new galleries above, cheaper and shallower, until the newest work broke through to cellars, badger-sets, and quarry-cuts all over the hill. No one has been buried here for a generation. The Shadow Inquisition hunts tamperers and puts down the risen, but cannot clear or destroy the site: unsealing or collapsing the vaults in numbers risks waking the hill entire.\n\nIMPORTANT: The dead of Hollowhill lie quiet in their vaults, anchored by their grave-goods. Take from a vault and its owner rises within hours and hunts the taker. Because robbers work the hill constantly, risen dead are a common sight in the galleries, hunting whoever holds their goods and venting their rage on any they cross paths with. The risen do not speak, do not bargain, and do not stop. They are put down by destroying them outright. The oldest dead of the Old Work are the exception: nothing short of returning what was taken, or radiant destruction by capable hunters, ends them.\n\nPlunder runs richer and danger worse with depth: modest silver and weak dead in the Shallows; funerary silver, marked jewels, coin-hoards, and blessed arms among the stronger dead of the Long Galleries; and in the Old Work, armory-grade grave-goods — blessed radiant arms, moonstone, regalia — sealed with the lords of the Lost Houses themselves.\n\nSyndicate bravos work the Catacombs by night in small crews, prying vaults, sacking goods fast, and attacking anyone they run into. Deeper in, cultists of the Gravebound wake the purged dead deliberately, binding them as servitors. The cultists attack any they encounter on sight, their undead minions leading.",
      "areas": {
        "The Hollow Hillside": {
          "description": "A great wooded hill honeycombed with tunnel mouths — some collapsed, some half-hidden by ivy and bramble, some worn open by regular use.",
          "paths": [
            "The Shallows"
          ]
        },
        "The Shallows": {
          "description": "Rough-cut galleries just below the surface, where daylight falls through collapsed roofs and dug break-ins. New vault-stones stand in fresh mortar beside pried-open doors and rubble. Passages descend at every turn, and the newest wards, chalked and silvered, mark the interments of the last few years.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hollow Hillside",
            "The Long Galleries"
          ]
        },
        "The Long Galleries": {
          "description": "Vaulted corridors running beyond lamplight in every direction, tier over tier of sealed doors — some plain, some under defaced heraldry, some standing broken with dark rooms behind. The stonework changes style from gallery to gallery, generations of different hands. Side passages branch, double back, and dead-end without pattern.",
          "paths": [
            "The Shallows",
            "The Old Work"
          ]
        },
        "The Old Work": {
          "description": "Grand halls of flawless masonry at the hill's root, colder and drier than the levels above. Shrouded statues line a processional avenue toward great sealed vaults, each standing alone, each ringed by ward-lines cut deep into the floor. The doors here are unbroken.",
          "paths": [
            "The Long Galleries"
          ]
        }
      },
