    "Kolbeck": {
      "name": "Kolbeck",
      "x": -25,
      "y": -14,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Kolbeck is a rich timber town at the edge of the Harrowwood, famous across Drusavia for grimwood: the blackened oak of the wood's great trees, which the risen dead cannot abide. Its carvers work grimwood into arrows, bows, staves, weapons, and charms, and their craft is on the town itself — bright painted townhouses bearing generations of carved figures, the housewains, that watch over every door and gable.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Kolbeck lives on the Harrowwood: timber, charcoal, and above all grimwood, cut only from the great Watch-Oaks that grow over the wood's staked plots. Ordinary timber is felled year-round; a Watch-Oak is felled rarely, under blessing, with an Inquisitor or a priest of Galard in attendance and hired steel guarding the party. The master-carvers are the town's aristocracy — proud, prosperous, loudly opinionated about each other's work, and feuding for years over whose housewain holds the best corner of the square. They sell finished goods to anyone, but harrow-stakes and blessed pieces only to Inquisitors, Temple folk, and hunters the guild has come to trust.\n\nThe townsfolk are woodsmen and carvers, well-off, hospitable, and matter-of-fact about the wood's dangers the way miners are about damp: there are rules, the rules work, and they are proud of their record. Felling crews hire guards for any work near staked ground, and every crew carries a stake-map. When a stake-line is found pulled or the dead are seen walking, it is reported at the White Rooster first, and the town sends word to the Shadow Inquisition in the city.",
      "areas": {
        "Oldwain Square": {
          "description": "The market square, ringed by tall painted townhouses whose carved facades hold generations of housewain statues — hunters mid-draw, dancers, oxen, laughing woodsmen in blackened oak. Carved poles at the square's center carry the oldest wains in Kolbeck. Around the edges, the carvers' shop-fronts sell grimwood arrows and bolts by the sheaf, bows, staves, hafted weapons and bucklers, and carried charms for the road.",
          "paths": [
            "The White Rooster",
            "The Mustering Ground"
          ]
        },
        "The White Rooster": {
          "description": "The town's tavern, under a grimwood rooster carved mid-crow above the door — regulars touch its foot going in. A long common room with a great hearth, crew tables, and a slate of who is hiring and who is overdue.",
          "paths": [
            "Oldwain Square",
            "The Mustering Ground"
          ]
        },
        "The Mustering Ground": {
          "description": "A broad yard at the wood-road end of town where parties bound for the Harrowwood form up: felling crews assembling at dawn, timber wagons loading for the capital, stacked gear, and a muster-board of posted contracts. The wood-road runs out between the last carved houses into the trees.",
          "paths": [
            "Oldwain Square",
            "The White Rooster"
          ]
        }
