    "The Harrowwood": {
      "name": "The Harrowwood",
      "x": -31,
      "y": -17,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Harrowwood is the great hill-forest around Kolbeck, worked for timber and charcoal along its edges and older and darker at its heart. Parts of the wood are cursed ground: burial plots where the dead rise if the earth is disturbed, each one staked and marked and left uncut. The oldest oaks in Drusavia — the Watch-Oaks — grow over those plots, and their grimwood is worth a fortune.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The cursed plots are scattered through the wood, worst and largest in the deep stands. Each is ringed by a stake-line of grimwood harrow-stakes; the risen dead of a plot are put down by driving a stake through them into the earth of their own grave, and a harrowed plot sleeps until someone disturbs it — pulls the stakes, turns the earth, or buries something in it by the old rite. Nobody knows why the ground does this. The woodsfolk hold it was a battlefield before the duchy; the Temple-minded say a purged house's curse soaked the land; drunks say the purges themselves angered so many dead at once that the earth learned the habit.\n\nIMPORTANT: Whatever is buried in a woken plot by a living hand rises within three nights, bound to the one who buried it. The risen are wrong — obedient, tireless, silent, and not the person they were. Unbound risen from a disturbed plot attack the living on sight. All risen dead flee sunlight and walk only by night or in deep shade; from cockcrow to dusk the wood is safe to work, and crews caught out at nightfall near a woken plot are in serious trouble.\n\nBy day the outer wood is busy: felling crews on the drag-roads, charcoal-burners at their mounds, hunters, and hired guards watching the stake-lines. The deep stands are another matter — the Watch-Oaks stand there, colossal and uncut, over the largest plots, and the best timber in the duchy grows exactly where nobody dares fell it.\n\nCultists of the Gravebound come into the deep stands by night to pull stakes and bury their dead, raising bound servitors. They work in small parties, post lookouts, and attack witnesses rather than leave them. Pulled stakes, fresh-turned earth, and grave-dirt tracks on the drag-roads are the signs they leave. When a waking is found, Kolbeck sends for the Shadow Inquisition, and the harrowing rite — priests or Inquisitors re-staking the plot grave by grave through one night, while everything still risen converges on the ritual — is how a waking ends.",
      "areas": {
        "The Working Wood": {
          "description": "Broad drag-roads and open cuts through hill-forest: stacked timber, charcoal mounds, sawpits, and stake-lines of blackened grimwood posts marking the plots the roads bend around. Wagon tracks run back toward Kolbeck.",
          "paths": [
            "The Deep Stands"
          ]
        },
        "The Deep Stands": {
          "description": "Old-growth forest under a closed canopy, dim at noon. The Watch-Oaks rise here, vast blackened trunks generations older than anything in the outer wood, standing over the largest stake-lines. Between them: overgrown plot-markers, weathered stakes, and here and there raw turned earth.",
          "paths": [
            "The Working Wood"
          ]
        }
      },
