    "Castle Ondrave": {
      "name": "Castle Ondrave",
      "x": -34,
      "y": 26,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Duchy of Drusavia",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Castle Ondrave is a great half-ruined estate in the haunted dales near Rovena. Most of it burned and was never rebuilt: a vast overgrown park, dead wings open to the sky, and the tombs of the household in the woods. One wing still lives. House Ondrave holds it yet — old blood, poor and proud, keeping a hearth that is said never to have gone out.",
      "hiddenInfo": "House Ondrave held its ground in the Liberation. The house fought, the house burned, and most of the house died. The family keeps the sound wing and keeps faith: the names remembered, rites kept at the tombs by daylight, and the great hearth of Ondrave Hall fed every night without fail — for while it burns, the hall is proof against the dead, and the family will not abandon its home. The Ondraves are poor, formal, and proud past their purse, and every generation sends its best to serve: there is an Ondrave sworn at the Black Tower and another in the Temple of Galard's halls. The old lord holds the estate with a small household and receives guests with threadbare grandeur.\n\nIMPORTANT: The ghosts of the burned household rise at night in the park and at the tombs — figures of the old burning, mad with rage and grief, attacking the living on sight. Their touch is chillfear, which kills where it strikes or leaves victims to be carried off and drained in hidden tombs, where they can still be rescued. The ghosts cannot abide sunlight and cannot enter Ondrave Hall while its hearth burns. Radiant weapons and balefire destroy them. By day the grounds are safe to walk.",
      "areas": {
        "The Ondrave Woods": {
          "description": "The estate's park gone to forest: the carriage drive lost under moss and root, burned shells of stables and folly-towers in the green, and garden statuary drowned in briar. Rows of household graves show through the trees on the old lawns.",
          "paths": [
            "Ondrave Hall",
            "The Old Tombs"
          ]
        },
        "Ondrave Hall": {
          "description": "The one living wing of the great house: tall windows lit at dusk, worn splendor within, and a great hearth at the heart of the hall whose fire is banked but never dead.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ondrave Woods"
          ]
        },
        "The Old Tombs": {
          "description": "The family crypt and the graves of the household, deep in the woods: a stone vault-front in the hillside, leaning headstones in ranks, and fresh offerings — flowers, bread, small candles burned to stubs — left by daylight hands.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ondrave Woods"
          ]
        }
