    "Astarieth's Court": {
      "name": "Astarieth's Court",
      "x": -17,
      "y": -8,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Reedmoot Fens",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The drowned western half of an ancient imperial capital, its towers, domes, and colonnades standing to their shoulders in the fen. This is Astarieth the Risen's own ground, and even her lizardfolk kingdom does not enter.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Astarieth keeps the city empty. Her kingdom holds it forbidden: no camps, no court, no pilgrims.\n\nA handful of dragon-champions ward the deep districts — lizardfolk remade by her gift into drake-scaled warriors in gilded hoard-plate. A champion who spots intruders roars a challenge and comes on openly; a challenge anywhere in the deep districts brings the others.\n\nIMPORTANT: the champions attack all intruders without parley. Astarieth sleeps within the Cathedral of Avarice and wakes only when intruders enter it, bursting up from the flooded nave in black water. There is no sneaking past her in her own lair.\n\nChampions fight with greatswords and poison-spit, charge through water, and die before her door.\n\nLoot in the Sunken Palaces: imperial silver bars, gilded arms, jeweled temple-plate, and high-shelf strongboxes the water never reached. Loot in the Cathedral: coin-chests, crowns, regalia, gilded armor, jeweled vessels, reliquaries, and fine weapons heaped in the demon-princess statue's palms and lap.",
      "areas": {
