    "Vaudania": {
      "name": "Vaudania",
      "x": -25,
      "y": 1,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Kingdom of Carendon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Vaudania is an old huntsman village deep in the western wood of Carendon, set where the worked land gives out and the wild wood begins. It is a proud, comfortable place that lives by the hunt — game and fur and the dangerous beasts — but it bars its doors after dark, for the wood beyond is werewolf country.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Vaudania is a proud village of huntsfolk who have lived their whole lives at the edge of a wood that wants them dead, and have decided to be cheerful about it. They hunt the wood for game and fur, feud with the wolves that hunt them back, breed hounds against them, and make the best field-remedies in Carendon because a hunter who can't patch himself dies out here. They are warm to a fellow hunter and short with a soft outsider, full of boasts about the great boar and gallows-jokes about the cousin the wolves took back. The population is ordinary human wood-country folk; the wolves are out in the trees, not in the village.\nWerewolves live in the deep wood, and no one can say why — the curse is old and unexplained, simply a fact of this stretch of the western wood. They take stock and travelers on the bad roads, and now and then a villager who went out too far or too late and did not come home. Whether the missing were eaten or became wolves themselves is the kind of thing nobody knows and Vaudania does not dwell on.\nIMPORTANT: unless a story is already underway here, the village's default is ordinary life — the hunt, the kennels, the trade, drinking and boasting — with the danger out in the wood, not in the streets. Do not stage Vaudania as though a fresh killing or an active hunt is always happening.\nThe wolves answer to the Grey Mother, the old wolf-power deep in the Wolvesholt Range that is the source of the curse. The villagers do not discuss her openly.",
      "areas": {
        "The Village": {
          "description": "The village proper, arrived at where the last fields give way to the trees. A working huntsman's town: hound-runs loud with the breeder's pack, hides and trophies hung to cure, a bowyer at his bench turning out bows and arrows, and the apothecary's shopfront where the woodcraft salves and draughts are sold. The dark wood stands close past the last houses, and everyone keeps an eye on it. A hunter outfits here — a hound, good arrows, the oils and worts that keep you alive in the trees.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hound and Horn"
          ]
        },
        "The Hound and Horn": {
          "description": "The village tavern and its social heart, named by the huntsfolk and a point of some pride. The hunters hold court here of an evening — boasting over their kills, arguing whose hound is finest, trading the gossip of the wood — and it is where a newcomer finds work, a warm welcome if they've the look of a hunter, and people worth knowing.",
          "paths": [
            "The Village"
          ]
        }
