    "Wolvesholt Range": {
      "name": "Wolvesholt Range",
      "x": -7,
      "y": 37,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Kingdom of Carendon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Wolvesholt is a long range of wooded hills in the west of Carendon, the deep heart of the kingdom's wolf-country. Game is rich here and so is fur, but the wood is werewolf-haunted, and the beasts take stock, travelers, and the unwary off the bad roads.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Wolvesholt is the hunting ground at the heart of Carendon's curse — a steep, heavily wooded range west of the worked land, where dire wolves run the draws and werewolves den in the deep folds. The curse is old and unexplained; the wood simply makes wolves of those it takes, and has for as long as anyone remembers. Hunters come here for the richest game and fur in the kingdom and for the bounty on the beasts, and the careful ones treat every run as a hunt that could turn the other way.\n\nThe werewolves are cursed beasts — hungry, dangerous, and pitiable, no more evil than a starving wolf is evil. Some were villagers once; the cull is mercy as much as bounty, and the wood never empties: put one pack down and the curse makes more.\n\nThe standing local craft is ordinary: hunters, trackers, and the hounds bred against the wolves, working out of huts at the wood's edge rather than any garrison.\n\nDeep in the high folds of the range is the Grey Mother, the old wolf-power that is the source of the curse.\n\nIMPORTANT: the wolves and werewolves of the Wolvesholt default to hostile toward people caught in the wood, and hunt by preference at dusk and after dark and on the bad roads. By day, in the worked edges and near the hunters' huts, ordinary life holds — tracking, trapping, curing hides — and the danger is out in the trees.",
      "areas": {
        "The Woodsman's Hut": {
          "description": "A hunter's hut at the foot of the range, where the cart-track ends and the trees begin — smoke from the chimney, hides curing on the rails, a run of lean hounds, and the wood standing close and dark past the last clearing. Whoever keeps it knows these hills better than anyone: what's been moving, where the packs are denning this season, which roads have gone bad. A hunter without a guide of their own can find one here, for coin or good company, and outfit for the trees.",
          "paths": [
            "The Wolvesholt Deep Wood"
          ]
        },
        "The Wolvesholt Deep Wood": {
          "description": "The range proper, climbing away from the worked land into close, steep, trackless forest. Game trails and kill-sign, draws where the dire wolves run, and the deep folds where the werewolves den and come down from at dusk. A hunter cuts sign, runs the beast down or sets where it will come, and gets out before dark.",
          "paths": [
            "The Woodsman's Hut"
          ]
        }
