    "Carendon": {
      "name": "Carendon",
      "x": -1,
      "y": 6,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Kingdom of Carendon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Carendon is the walled capital of the kingdom that shares its name, a gracious and prosperous river-town set in the wooded hills at the heart of the realm. It is the seat of the king and his court, an old city of stone bridges and fine houses grown wealthy on the trade of the wood, and behind its walls it has lived gracefully and safely for centuries while the wild presses close beyond them.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Carendon is the bright, comfortable heart of a wealthy wood-country kingdom: a walled river-city of merchants, courtiers, and the king's household, where the realm's coin is made and spent and the good life is on open display. The population is mixed and human-led, with the forest peoples of the kingdom — elves, half-elves, half-orcs, beastfolk traders, and the dwarf smiths who arm the hunters — passing through its markets and quarters. The city is safe and gracious by long habit; its dangers are political and social, not monstrous, and the monstrous is kept where it belongs, out in the wood.\n\nThe king rules from the Palace on Crownhill with a watch and a standing army for ordinary defense, but monsters are not the crown's work. They belong to the Order of the Silver Sword, the brotherhood of hunters seated at Castle Harstone to the northeast, sworn to no crown and beholden to none.\n\nThe great houses keep their seats on Crownhill, the noble quarter above the town — among them House Harstone, the old family that gave its ancestral castle to the Order and still holds a voice at court. The houses do not deal with strangers; they deal with people who have made themselves worth dealing with.\n\nThe honest trade in monster-parts, silver and steel weapons, and hunters' gear is worked on Silver Row. The dishonest version — poached kills, restricted materials, the things the crown and the Order would control — happens outside the eastern wall at Houndsditch, the squat the gracious city prefers not to look at.",
      "areas": {
