    "Castle Harstone": {
      "name": "Castle Harstone",
      "x": 26,
      "y": 38,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Kingdom of Carendon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Castle Harstone is a great old castle in the wooded hills northeast of Carendon, grand and proud and half-fallen to ruin, given an age ago to the Order of the Silver Sword and held by them since. It is the seat of the brotherhood of monster-hunters called the Silverblades.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Castle Harstone is the home of the Order of the Silver Sword, the kingdom's brotherhood of monster-hunters. It is a great house gone half to moss and ivy — a lordly old seat the Order has neither the coin nor the care to keep whole, its grand wings shut up and crumbling, the parts they use warm and lived-in and hung with the trophies of a hundred kills. The brotherhood is mixed and welcoming to the worthy of any people: human, elf, half-elf, half-orc, beastfolk trackers, weapon-users of every kind, spellcasters, and the dwarf armorers who set the silver. They are hunters sworn to no king, beholden to none, taking contracts from anyone with a monster they cannot answer themselves.\n\nThe Order runs by memory, witness, and reputation. Hunters take work from the Muster board or from senior hunters, then ride out and do it. When they return, they tell the story in the Great Hall, show what they brought back, and answer questions from hunters who know the ground. There are no clerks, filing rooms, or forms in the Order. A hunter's standing comes from the people they bring home, the monsters they overcome, the proof they return with, and the trust of the brotherhood.\n\nA newcomer accepted by the Order begins as an Initiate: a candidate under a Veteran Silverblade, not yet a full Silverblade. An Initiate has no silver blade pin and receives no Order silver. They must complete one supervised trial hunt, making the decisions while the Veteran observes and bears witness. When the quarry has been decisively resolved, the Initiate returns to Castle Harstone, the hunt is recounted before the Great Hall, and the Veteran gives witness. If the Order judges them worthy and they accept the oath, they are admitted as a Silverblade, receive the silver blade pin, and choose Order silver suited to their calling.\n\nThe ranks are Initiate, Silverblade, Veteran Silverblade, and Master of the Hunt. A Silverblade is a full sworn member who takes contracts in their own name. After three recognized Silverblade hunts, they may be judged for Veteran rank and trusted to lead hunts, supervise Initiates, and direct junior hunters. After four further recognized Veteran hunts, they may be judged for elevation to Master of the Hunt, one of the senior authorities who commission great hunts, assign hunters, and judge admissions and promotions.\n\nThe name Silverblade is traditional, not a restriction to swords or even to martial hunters. Full members carry radiant silver in the form their work requires: silvered spears, axes, bows, arrows, knives, hammers, or other weapons; silver-faced shields; and silver-bound magical focuses or implements through which a caster works aspected magic against unnatural quarry. The silver comes from Argenval and is worked by the Order's armorers and the smiths of Silver Row.\n\nThe Master of the Hunt holds the tower and gives the commissions too grave or strange for the common board. House Harstone, the old family that gave this castle away an age ago, keeps only a townhouse in the capital now and a voice at court; why they gave up their ancestral seat is a thing the Order knows and the family does not discuss.\n\nFor Initiates only: in the castle's deep is the Gate, and beyond it the descent that is the true reason the Order holds this place. The Silverblades guard the way down, and their grimmest hunts go through it. An Initiate is kept from it; a sworn Silverblade learns what it is in time. What lies below is not spoken of in the hall, and is not the business of any candidate.",
