    "The Argenval Crags": {
      "name": "The Argenval Crags",
      "x": 37,
      "y": -22,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Kingdom of Carendon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Argenval Crags are the high broken cliffs above the silver-town, troll country since before Argenval was built. A maze of impassable rock and caves without number, it is where the trolls den and the trows breed.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Crags are a maze of cliffs and caves above Argenval, home to the trows that invade its mine and the trolls that prey on its people. The trows breed in the caves below the trolls’ high dens. People reach the warren by the cliff paths; the cracks linking it to the mine are too narrow to follow.\n\nThe trows are the swarming cave-kin of the trolls, lesser things of the same house: cowardly alone, deadly in numbers, denning in the foul branching caves past counting. Above them, far fewer and far worse, are the trolls proper — and the old troll of the warren, the great ancient one the town's tributes were always meant for, lairing in the deep den with the hoard of generations: the livestock-bone and ore and grave-gear of every toll paid and every hunter who climbed this far and did not climb back down.\n\nFor generations Argenval lived by leaving the trolls their toll, and the old tribute-shrine stands in the caves where the trails meet the warren — the place the town left its livestock and ore and, at the worst of it, more, before the crown forbade it.\n\nThe trolls and trows here are resistant to silver, whether the warren bred it over the long years or something made them so.\n\nCRITICAL: the trows and trolls of the Crags default to hostile and hunt by ambush. There is no safe ground here and no ordinary life — this is the warren's own country, climbing from bad to worse the higher it goes. The old troll does not parley as a reasoning creature would, but it is greedy and it remembers the toll.",
      "areas": {
        "The Crag-Trails": {
          "description": "The climbing trails up into the broken cliffs above Argenval, where the worked land ends and the warren's country begins — steep bare rock, cave-mouths in the cliff-faces, and the bones and leavings of the warren scattered on the approaches. The way climbs on into the warren proper.",
