    "Harpy's Peak Ruins": {
      "name": "Harpy's Peak Ruins",
      "x": -24,
      "y": 40,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Kingdom of Carendon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Harpy's Peak is a ruined old fort on a crag above one of Carendon's forest roads, abandoned long ago and given over to the harpies that nest in its broken towers. They roost in the ruin and stoop on the road below, and travelers who must pass it go quickly and watch the sky.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Harpy's Peak Ruins is a fallen frontier fort on a rocky height over an old forest road — a crumbling keep of broken walls and roofless towers, abandoned in some long-forgotten trouble and never reclaimed, because the harpies took it. They nest in the high broken towers in a foul squabbling flock, line their roosts with the leavings of their kills, and stoop on whatever travels the road below — livestock, lone travelers, the careless. They are always here; thin the flock and it breeds back into the towers within a few seasons, so passing the Peak is a standing danger and clearing it a standing contract.\n\nHarpies are vicious, cunning, and greedy for bright things, and their roosts are middens of generations of plunder — the coin and trinkets and gear of everyone they have dragged up to the towers, fouled and scattered among the nests. That hoard is the reason a hunter climbs the Peak beyond the bounty: the harpies themselves are worth nothing, but what they have stolen is worth the climb, if the flock can be put down. The old fort below the roosts holds its own leavings too — whatever the garrison left when it fell, picked over but not empty.\n\nIMPORTANT: the harpies of the Peak default to hostile and attack from the air in numbers. There is no safe ground in the ruin while the flock roosts — they stoop and harry and drive intruders toward the drops.",
