    "Reaver Road": {
      "name": "Reaver Road",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 21,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Kingdom of Carendon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Reaver Road is a long stretch of forest road in Carendon — the old maps give it another name, but no one uses it, because the road is reaver country. Outlaws hold the deep wood along it and prey on the timber-wagons, fur-trains, and travelers that must pass through. The crown's soldiers ride it and drive the bandits back, and the bandits crop up again, and so it has gone for years.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Reaver Road is the bad stretch of Carendon's road-network: a long run of the forest highway, deep in the wood between settlements, where outlaws have preyed on traffic for as long as anyone bothers to remember. The kingdom's wealth travels these roads — timber and fur and the silver out of Argenval — and where rich cargo runs through deep cover, reavers gather. They hold camps back in the trees off the road, hit the wagon-trains and the lone traveler, and melt into the wood when soldiers come. The crown sends patrols and breaks the bands and hangs what it catches, and within a season new men have taken the camps, because the wood is wide, the cover is good, and there is always coin on the road and always the desperate to take it. The road is never clean and never quite lost.\n\nThe reavers are ordinary human trouble: outlaws, deserters, broken men, and the hard sort who find robbery pays better than honest work — some merely desperate, some genuinely cruel, and a quest can pitch a given band either way. They run from a leader who holds the road that season, take prisoners for ransom when the prisoner is worth it, and fence their take where they can. A hunter or a sword-for-hire takes work here from the crown's coin, from a merchant who has lost a train, or from a family whose traveler did not arrive: clear a camp, escort a cargo through, or bring back someone the road took.\n\nIMPORTANT: the reavers of the road default to hostile toward travelers who cannot fight back, and prefer ambush from the cover of the wood. A strong, armed party they may shadow and let pass, or try to parley, or rush if the prize is worth it; a soft mark they take.",
      "areas": {
        "The Road": {
          "description": "The forest highway through reaver country — a long wooded stretch of the kingdom's road, deep cover crowding both sides, with the wrecks of looted wagons rotting in the ditches and the cover thick enough to hide a band a few yards off the verge.",
          "paths": [
            "The Reaver Camp"
