    "Branton": {
      "name": "Branton",
      "x": 7,
      "y": 41,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Westmarch",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A stone-walled hill-village in the northern foothills of Westmarch, a half-day's ride from Marrenford and the closest settlement to the orc lands. Sheep and goats on the thin hill-pastures, a smith, a hedge-healer, and a militia that drills on its own walls. Branton keeps a beacon on its watchtower that signals Marrenford when the border is threatened.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The reeve runs Branton — elected, tough, and short on patience for outsiders who haven't proved useful. Pays honestly for border work.\n\nHuman-led, with a handful of half-orcs among the younger generation. The half-orcs are tolerated and watched — the village has buried family to orc reavers, and the distinction between the enemy's kin and the peace's children is one they make with their heads, not always their hearts.\n\nOrc reavers stage from the Scarps, the broken crag-country an hour northwest. Ogres den in the same crags and sometimes run with the raider bands. The militia are better hill-fighters than the Westmarch Riders — they drill on the walls, know the terrain by feel, and have fought more actions than most professional soldiers.",
      "areas": {
        "Branton Yard": {
          "description": "The open yard inside Branton's gate, packed dirt worn smooth. A smith's forge stands against the wall — working steel, not fine: heavy spearheads, crossbow bolts, frontier armor, and repair work. A hedge-healer's stall nearby sells poultices, herbal remedies, and hill-country antidotes. The reeve posts militia work on a board nailed to the hall's outer wall: patrol shifts, reaver-trail tracking, and bounties on orc raider bands spotted in the Scarps.",
          "paths": [
            "Branton Hall",
            "The Beacon Wall"
          ]
        },
        "Branton Hall": {
          "description": "The village's one hall — court, tavern, and feast-room in the same stone chamber. The reeve holds business at a table by the door in the morning. In the evening the militia drink after watch and shepherds come down from the hills. A veteran militia sergeant teaches ambush tactics, crag-country movement, and the hard arithmetic of defending a walled position with too few people.",
          "paths": [
            "Branton Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Beacon Wall": {
          "description": "Branton's walls and watchtower, with the border beacon at the top. The walls are rough local stone, rebuilt so many times the older courses are a different color from the new. Militia stand watch in shifts and drill between — crossbow from the parapet, spear at the gate, and how to hold a wall with fewer than you need. They will train a willing volunteer. The view north from the tower shows the Scarps and the open hills beyond. On clear nights, Marrenford's lights are visible to the south.",
          "paths": [
            "Branton Yard"
