    "Wolfgar Keep": {
      "name": "Wolfgar Keep",
      "x": 25,
      "y": 40,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Westmarch",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A ruined frontier fortress on a high crag in the contested hills north of the Greatwall. Wolfgar Keep was the war-kings' northernmost outpost, abandoned when the borders pulled back after the peace. Orc reavers shelter in the ruins between raids. The keep is visible from the Scarps and from the Greatwall's watchtowers.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Wolfgar Keep may be hostile. Orc reavers and Bloodsworn crusaders sometimes shelter in the yard and lower tower between raids, and treat intruders as enemies. The keep is not permanently garrisoned — bands come and go. A player may arrive to find it occupied, empty, or mid-arrival.\n\nThe keep was built by Wolfgar, a war-king of Westmarch, at the farthest reach of the old frontier. His name is carved over the gate in letters taller than a man's hand. The stonework is old, heavy, and built to be held by few — a square tower, a walled yard, and an undercroft dug into the crag. When the peace was made and the borders pulled back, it was abandoned.\n\nOrc reavers sometimes use the yard and lower tower as shelter. Fire-blackened walls, stripped fittings, camp-trash, stolen goods stashed under canvas.\n\nBloodsworn crusaders sometimes also use Wolfgar Keep as a gathering-place for their rites. They come in small groups on nights they choose, rarely more than a dozen, and scatter before dawn. Between gatherings the keep holds no trace of them above ground. The undercroft may yield signs of their blood magic activity, including blades with blood-channels and dark stains on the stone.\n\nLoot: orc-forged weapons and stolen Westmarch gear from the reaver camps in the yard. In the upper tower, old war-king era arms and armor. In the undercroft, the Bloodsworn leave their ritual tools between gatherings.",
      "areas": {
        "The Yard and Gate": {
          "description": "The outer wall half-collapsed on the eastern side, the gate still standing with Wolfgar's name carved deep into the lintel. Inside, a trampled yard with the remains of orc reaver camps — fire-pits ringed with blackened stone, stolen goods under canvas, a horse-pen knocked together from salvaged timber. The outbuildings along the wall are roofless and used for storage. The keep's square tower rises from the northern end of the yard.",
          "paths": [
            "The Tower"
          ]
        },
        "The Tower": {
          "description": "A square stone tower, three stories, the top floor open to the sky where the roof collapsed. The ground floor shows signs of being used as a shelter — the marks of cook-fires, and the soot of many seasons on the walls. The upper floors are partially collapsed. The stair down to the undercroft is at the back of the ground floor.",
          "paths": [
            "The Yard and Gate",
            "The Undercroft"
          ]
