      "region": "Westmarch",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A timber-built village on the western border of Westmarch where the farmland meets the Everwood, a few hours' ride west of Marrenford. Waldgate's woodcutters work the forest margin — old-growth Everwood timber, the best in the region. The buildings are master-joinery in heavy beams, carved lintels, craft passed down through generations. A timber-yard trades in lumber and Everwood bows. The ford across the river into Sanctuary Vale is a short walk from the village.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Human-led, with half-elves common among the younger families — the ford brings marriages as well as trade. Wood elf rangers cross occasionally from Sanctuary Vale. The woodcutters are forest-competent and proud of it; they go armed into the margin every working day.\n\nElf renegades raid from the Deadfall Gulleys, a stretch of stream-cut ravines under heavy Everwood canopy a half-day into the forest, where old-growth deadfalls across the gullies make a natural maze. The renegades know the paths; outsiders climb over trunks and walk into arrows. They hit the village, the ford, and cutting crews to provoke conflict between the high elves and the March.\n\nOwlbears nest on the forest margin where the cutting crews work — territorial and aggressive, the most common physical danger of the trade. Giant spiders web the deeper ravines toward the Deadfall Gulleys.\n\nDryads from the deep Everwood kill woodcutters and travelers who go too far under the canopy, and take girls. The village has lost people for as long as anyone remembers. Everyone knows a name.\n\nA Westmarch Ranger is posted at the ford and watches what crosses. Syndicate bravos move contraband through the river-crossing — goods out of Sanctuary Vale's underhalls — and the Ranger knows it and cannot stop all of it.",
      "areas": {
        "Waldgate Green": {
          "description": "The commons inside Waldgate's palisade, ringed by carved-wood buildings. A master fletcher sells Everwood longbows and composites and teaches bowmanship — the best archery training in Westmarch. An enchantress works Everwood timber into staves, wands, and foci for spellcasters. A kennelmaster breeds and trains forest hounds for tracking under deep canopy — working animals a hunter can buy or bond. A board outside the reeve's house posts cutting-crew escort, deep-forest scouting, and bounties on elf renegade bands spotted near the village.",
          "paths": [
