    "Deadfall Gulleys": {
      "name": "Deadfall Gulleys",
      "x": -40,
      "y": -7,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Westmarch",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A stretch of stream-cut ravines under heavy Everwood canopy, a half-day west of Waldgate. Enormous deadfalls — old-growth trees toppled by age and storm — lie across the gulleys like walls, with dense regrowth threading through the gaps. Elf renegades use the Gulleys as a staging ground for raids on Waldgate, the ford, and Westmarch cutting crews.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Deadfall Gulleys are hostile. Elf renegades operate from camps hidden in the ravine maze and treat outsiders as enemies. They are guerrilla fighters, not a garrison — camps shift, trails change, and the maze is different every visit.\n\nThe renegades are Reclaimer-aligned elves who want Westmarch pushed back from the Everwood. They raid to provoke — hitting woodcutters, burning timber-yards, ambushing at the ford — so that Westmarch retaliates against the high elves, and the high elves withdraw the peace. They are skilled archers and forest-fighters who know every gully, root-bridge, and sight-line in the maze.\n\nThey fight at range and withdraw. They pin intruders in the gulleys with arrows from the deadfall tops, then fall back deeper where the ravines narrow and the footing worsens. They do not hold ground — they bleed pursuers and vanish. Chasing them deeper is what they want. A band that cannot withdraw will fight hard with short blades at close quarters in the ravine bottoms.\n\nGiant spiders web the deeper gulleys where the canopy blocks all light. The renegades navigate around the webs or use them as barriers — a pursuing party that breaks through a renegade ambush may stumble directly into silk. The spiders are not allies of the renegades; they are terrain the renegades have learned to use.\n\nEncounter variety for the narrator to draw from: a renegade scouting party watching the forest margin near Waldgate, marking cutting-crew routes. A recently used camp with cold fires and elven boot-prints leading deeper in. An ambush triggered by triplines of spider-silk strung across a game trail. A woodcutter's crew pinned down behind a deadfall, taking arrows from above, needing rescue. A renegade wounded by a spider, willing to talk rather than die in the web. Two renegades arguing in Elvish over whether the next raid should hit the ford or a cutting crew — the player overhears a plan. A deadfall bridge across a deep gully, rigged to collapse under weight.\n\nLoot: elven-made bows and arrows — lighter and better-crafted than anything in Waldgate's shop. Short fighting blades of elven steel. Cloaks and leathers worked for deep-forest movement. Renegade camp supplies, some of which bear marks from Sanctuary Vale — the renegades have supporters across the river who provision them. Spider-silk in quantity, valuable to any enchantress or fletcher who knows how to work it. Occasionally a message-scroll in Elvish, carried between renegade bands, naming targets, dates, or contacts in Sanctuary Vale.",
      "areas": {
        "The Outer Gulleys": {
          "description": "Where the forest floor breaks into shallow stream-cuts under thickening canopy. The deadfalls begin here — trunks broader than a cart blocking the ravines, root-plates standing vertical, regrowth filling every gap. Game trails thread through but the footing is treacherous.",
          "paths": [
            "The Deep Ravines"
          ]
        },
        "The Deep Ravines": {
          "description": "The heart of the maze. The gulleys narrow and deepen, the canopy closes overhead, and giant spider webs span the gaps between deadfalls. Renegade camps sit in hollows beneath root-plates and overhangs — cold fires, elven gear, sight-lines cleared in every direction. The air is still and dark.",
          "paths": [
            "The Outer Gulleys"
          ]
        }
      },
