    "The Outer Ring": {
      "name": "The Outer Ring",
      "x": -2,
      "y": -8,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Sanctuary Vale",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A ring of half-built structures and broken wall outside Sanctuary's walls, where the city once tried to grow outward and the wood took it back. What is left is a wide band of abandoned buildings, with the Everwood grown up through it, roots splitting floors, trees standing in roofless halls, creepers swallowing the stone a little more each year. No watch comes here and no wards hold here. People still go out into it, and some live in it, because past the wards a body can do what the city will not permit.",
      "hiddenInfo": "No watch, no authority, no wards. The Syndicate is the heaviest presence but holds nothing whole - it is too large and too broken for that, and the edges are too dangerous to want. Independent fences, squatters, deserters, and people hiding from law or grudge keep their own corners. Everyone deals with the Syndicate or around them.\n\nThe Ring is where Sanctuary's stolen goods are fenced, where smugglers run cargo past the city's gates and tolls through the broken wall, and where a buyer finds what the watch would seize inside - poisons, restricted reagents, weapons taken off the sanctioned market. Deals are struck at the Halfway House; harder business is done in back rooms and never spoken of.\n\nDanger worsens outward, and so does the wood. The occupied core sells drink, deals, and beds to anyone with coin. The unfinished frames stand empty and half-overgrown, giant spiders webbing the upper floors. At the broken wall the Everwood comes straight in over the rubble, root and branch through every ruin and no wards to hold any of it - an owlbear holds the worst of the gaps, and worse hunts the dead streets at the rim. Name the danger as it is reached: cutpurses and enforcers in the core, spiders in the frames, the wood and what dens in it at the gaps.",
      "areas": {
        "The Dead Ring": {
          "description": "The half-built streets of the failed circuit. The lived-in stretch nearest the wall is where the Ring does its business: a rough market of barrows and blanket-stalls selling what the city would seize, fences weighing goods in doorways, smugglers loading mule-trains for the gaps, and hard-eyed locals on every corner marking who comes and goes. Past the occupied blocks the streets run out into empty shells and deeper overgrowth.",
          "paths": [
            "The Halfway House"
          ]
        },
        "The Halfway House": {
          "description": "The Outer Ring's one real establishment: a finished mansion of the failed district, meant for some family that never came, now tavern, doss-house, and dealing-floor at once. The great hall below is where the Ring drinks and bargains, every table its own quiet negotiation; the upper rooms are let by the night. It is the closest thing the Ring has to neutral ground, and to safe, which is not very. The Syndicate keeps a table here that is always theirs.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dead Ring"
          ]
        }
      },
