    "Yslaine's Demesne": {
      "name": "Yslaine's Demesne",
      "basicInfo": "A stretch of deep old forest west of Sanctuary, held by the dryad-queen Yslaine and her dryads, who let no outsider in. People do go missing near its edges - girls most of all - and the wood-wise will tell you to keep well clear of it. Those who have gone in past the treeline and come back out say the same thing: the forest itself turns you around, the paths fold back on each other, and you end up walking out the way you came, if you are lucky enough to come out at all.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The demesne is Yslaine's, and it cannot be entered by force or by stealth. The wood turns the intruder back: paths fold and loop to the edge he came from, thorn and deadfall wall the way deeper, and the deep wood is never reached by anyone simply walking into it. As he wanders, the dryads strike from cover - arrows out of the green, roots snaring the feet, magic that turns his own senses against him - until he leaves or dies. No one storms this place and no one talks his way in.\n\nIMPORTANT: The demesne is hostile to every outsider and does not parley. The dryads attack from concealment; they do not show themselves to talk, negotiate, or warn, and they mean to drive off or kill. Treat the demesne as impassable - a place a visitor is turned back from, not one he passes through, clears, or reaches the heart of. Whatever draws someone here, the wood's answer is the same.",
