        "The Edgewood": {
          "description": "Where the ordinary Everwood ends and the old wood begins. The trees here are vast - trunks wide as towers, crowns so high and dense the ground lies in green half-light. The undergrowth thickens into walls of thorn and bramble between the trunks, and deadfall lies heaped where great limbs have come down and never been cleared. Little grows low to the ground but moss and pale fungus, and there is no birdsong, no track, no sign of any path worn by foot or hoof.",
