      "complexityType": "complex",
      "areas": {
        "The Open Wood": {
          "description": "The lighter reaches of the Eastwood, open enough to ride through - stands of old timber spaced over fern and leaf-mould, clearings where the canopy breaks, and low ridgelines rising between stream-cut hollows. The wood closes in and darkens toward its depths. In places the ground is churned by the passage of men on the move.",
