    "The Riddlewood": {
      "name": "The Riddlewood",
      "basicInfo": "A stretch of hilly Everwood riddled with caves and hollows, the slopes broken by limestone outcrops and the dark mouths of old sinkholes and worn-out dens. Renegade elves hold it, and a rough host of outsider bandits and cutthroats shelters among them - raiding the forest roads, robbing travelers, and falling back into the caves where no one comes to dig them out.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Riddlewood is a robbers' haven, and it is one because the high elf Wardens hold back from it. The renegade elves who hold the wood have taken in every brigand, deserter, and cutthroat who will fight for a roof and a share, and to come in after them the Wardens would have to kill those outsiders by the score - which they will not do. So the wood is left to Sanctuary and whoever Sanctuary will send, and the renegades and their hired scum range out of it as they please.\n\nThe renegade elves are the core and the cause: they want the outsiders driven from the Everwood for good, and they raid Westmarch, the human region to the east, to push the high elves and the humans toward the war they want. But most of the host is not ideological at all - they are bandits, in it for plunder, drawn by a safe base no authority will raid. The two suit each other. The renegades get numbers and a shield of outsider bodies; the robbers get protection, a launching point, and caves to vanish into. The host grows as word spreads that the Riddlewood pays and the law does not come.\n\nThey stage their raids from camps in the wood and warrens in the caves, strike the forest roads and the lonelier holdings, and carry the take back into the hills. Breaking them means going in after them - clearing the camps, hunting them through the caves, cutting the raids before they ride.\n\nIMPORTANT: The renegade elves and their bandit host default to hostile. They are raiders and killers who take any stranger in the wood for a mark, a threat, or a recruit worth pressing, and they fight to rob, drive off, or kill. The cave country is dangerous in its own right - sinkholes, dark warrens, and the things that den in deep cave-dark away from the light.",
