    "The Cold Iron Caverns": {
      "name": "The Cold Iron Caverns",
      "x": -13,
      "y": 19,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Sanctuary Vale",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A cave-riddled hillside in the Everwood beyond Sanctuary's walls, the one place cold iron is found. The grey ore lies in veins threaded through the deep stone where the roots of the great wood reach down into it, and those after it go in armed and in company, because the caverns are full of things that kill.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Cold iron is forest iron from veins the great wood's roots have grown down through, found nowhere but here. It must be mined and worked cold, never touched by forge-fire, or the wild burns out of it and it is only iron. Worked cold, its edge bites the fey and the magical as plain steel cannot. The diggers haul the rough ore back to Sanctuary, where the Underhalls smiths hammer it cold into blades and heads.\n\nThe ore is not lying about to be gathered. Finding it means searching the worked faces and the root-veins deeper in, and the caverns do not give that time freely - the monsters come while a digger looks. A spell of searching, through a fight or two, turns up a modest amount of ore and no more; no one walks out of the Cold Iron Caverns with a hoard. That is why cold iron is dear, and why the diggers go armed and pay for blades.\n\nIMPORTANT: The caverns are infested and hostile. Pressing into them and moving deeper draws what lives in the dark. The threats are ankhegs that tunnel through the root-and-earth and burst up through a gallery floor; stirges that come off the cave roof; darkmantles that drop from the root-choked ceiling; and gricks that lie still as dead root in the wall-crevices until something passes.",
      "areas": {
        "The Entrance Cave": {
          "description": "The wide cave-mouth where the diggers gather before going in - daylight reaching back over a floor of trodden stone, a few fires, gear and tools stowed against the walls, and the diggers and their hired guards resting, dividing the day's ore, or working up the nerve for another spell in the dark. Armed men watch the deeper passages. Two ways lead on: down into the worked galleries where the cold iron is cut, and off along a dark tunnel that runs toward Sanctuary's Underhalls.",
          "paths": [
            "The Workings",
            "The Underhalls Tunnel"
          ]
        },
        "The Workings": {
          "description": "The cut galleries where the cold iron is dug - stone laced through with the pale roots of the great wood reaching down from above. Pick-marks and abandoned tools mark the worked faces, and the passages run deeper into unworked dark where the roots grow thicker and the water drips. The ground is broken in places where something has come up through it.",
          "paths": [
            "The Entrance Cave",
            "The Underhalls Tunnel"
          ]
        },
        "The Underhalls Tunnel": {
          "description": "A long passage running underground from the caverns toward Sanctuary's Underhalls, old and rough-walled, the roots thinning as it leaves the wood behind and the stone closing in. It is the way the dwarves come and go between the city and the diggings. Nothing tends it and nothing keeps it lit, and what dens in the caverns ranges through it.",
          "paths": [
            "The Entrance Cave",
            "The Workings"
          ]
        }
      },
