    "Terlothis": {
      "name": "Terlothis",
      "x": -21,
      "y": 40,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Sanctuary Vale",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A ruined elven fortress deep in the Everwood, broken and abandoned since the Kindred War and left well alone ever since. Its walls still stand among the trees that have grown up through them, but the dead hold it now. The wood-wise know it by name and give it a wide berth.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Terlothis was a high-elven war-fortress, and it fell in the Kindred War an age ago. The garrison died here, and the dead never left: the ruin is held by restless elven dead who fall on anything living that comes within the walls. They cannot be cleared for good - cut them down and they rise again where they fell, the same as they have for an age - which is why the fortress still stands unclaimed and why even the high elves leave it be. It is more trouble than any treasure in it is worth.\n\nSomething is sealed in the depths beneath the keep. The garrison died with it shut away below them, and whatever it is, it has never been opened, named, or accounted for - the high elves do not speak of it, and no one living knows what was put down there or why. The dead are thickest and worst the deeper one goes. Let the place tell its own story: the sealed door, the dead fallen at their posts as if still holding a line, the elven war-carvings worn under moss - the evidence is there to be read, and the truth of what was sealed is left for the bold to uncover or the foolish to loose.\n\nIMPORTANT: The dead of Terlothis default to hostile and attack the living on sight within the walls. They do not parley, do not speak, and do not relent - they strike to kill.",
      "areas": {
        "The Broken Keep": {
          "description": "The shell of the old fortress, its curtain walls breached and its towers fallen, the Everwood grown up through the courtyards and great halls until root and branch hold the stone together as much as mortar does. Fallen elven dead lie where they dropped an age ago, armor and bone gone green under the moss, some still at the arrow-slits and gatehouse as if the assault never ended. A way leads down beneath the keep, into the dark below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Underkeep"
          ]
        },
        "The Underkeep": {
          "description": "The vaults and lower halls beneath the fortress, unlit and unfallen where the keep above is open to the sky. The elven dead lie thickest here, and the deeper passages run toward a great sealed door of elven work, barred and warded from the outside and never since opened. Old carvings cover the walls about it, worn but not gone.",
          "paths": [
            "The Broken Keep"
          ]
        }
