    "Maanvalta": {
      "name": "Maanvalta",
      "x": 1,
      "y": 1,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "The Rootdark",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "basicInfo": "Maanvalta, the great cavern-city of the dark elves and the capital of their realm beneath the Elfwood. It stands at the center of a tunnel-network that runs under the whole forest and far beyond, built into the stalactites and stalagmites around World-root and the underground lake at its foot, all of it lit by the amber-to-violet glow of the Root-sky. Under the terms of the Sundering the dark elves keep off the surface, but they do not turn surfacers away from the deep — and many make the journey, because dark-elf illusion, craft, and the goods of the deep earth are found nowhere else.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The dark elves were driven below in the Sundering and have spent an age making their exile glorious. Forbidden from the surface of Elfwood except at Ilunethel, they built tunnel-roads that reach under half of Larion and emerge beyond the high elves' realm, carrying dark-elf trade, agents, and influence into the wider world. They are the finest illusionists in Larion and its most accomplished thieves and assassins, and they prize wit, craft, and style the way other peoples prize virtue — being dull is worse than being wrong.\n\nCompeting noble houses run the city's trade and its intrigues, and they court surfacers constantly as agents, partners, and useful fools. A clever visitor can make a fortune here; a careless one finds an early grave. The dark elves are charming, decadent, and hospitable, but charm and the knife are the same hand here, and a guest is rarely sure which he is being offered.\n\nMaanvalta is the hub of the soulstone trade. Its tunnel-network gives it perfect reach into the surface regions where soulstones are banned, and the houses move them at enormous profit along the deep roads no surface power can watch.\n\nThe Unseen, the cross-house brotherhood of spies and assassins seated at the Needle, answer the high elves of Adamant blow for blow: where the Legion of the Vigil raids the dark elves' tunnels in secret, the Unseen retaliate below the line, and the slow war neither capital will admit to is fought hardest in the dark between them.",
      "areas": {
        "The Ledgeways": {
          "description": "A series of carved stone ledges high along the cavern's upper wall, where tunnels open from every direction and paths wind down toward the lake far below. From these ledges the whole city reveals itself at once: the huge World-root piercing the cavern ceiling and descending into the underground lake at its heart, the Root-sky glowing amber to violet overhead, and the stalactites and stalagmites — crowded with carved structures and strung together by bridges — climbing from the dark water. Dark-elf wardens watch the stairhead and mark every surfacer who comes down.",
