    "Ilunethel": {
      "name": "Ilunethel",
      "x": -16,
      "y": 31,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Elfwood",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Ilunethel is a rough, thriving trade-town in the overgrown ruins of a fallen elven city destroyed in the Kindred War, built around the only open way between the surface and the dark-elf realm below. By the terms of the Sundering, it is the one place the dark elves are allowed to walk the surface, and the one place on this whole stretch of the Elfwood where the high elves' law does not reach. The deep's goods are sold in the open, coin buys passage down the stair, and a bold outsider can make a fortune here running the dark elves' business above ground — if the work, or the town, doesn't get them killed first.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The dark elves were driven below after the Kindred War, and Ilunethel is the single place the high elves suffer them above ground. A dark elf caught on the surface within Elfwood, beyond the town's bounds, is killed. The High Wardens watch the edges and will not set foot within, though they are known to spy on the goings-on here through non-elven agents. Still, everyone in Ilunethel knows the Wardens cannot touch them here as long as they do nothing obviously illegal, and the town has the swagger of it.\n\nIt is run by its merchant houses, dark-elf and surface both, who answer to no one and settle their differences themselves, sometimes through open violence. The open trade is real enough — deep-earth spell ingredients, dark elf spells, carved stone and deepwood, dark elf weapons and armor, the metals and gems of the under-earth. The dark elves' other craft is sold more discreetly: false faces, illusion magic, and disguise-work a spy or a thief would kill for.\n\nThe dark elves cannot leave the city, so the houses hire surfacers to do their work above ground, and they are always hiring. Most of that hiring happens over a drink at the Queen of Ales, where house factors and Syndicate fixers work the tables. The jobs run the whole range and the pay runs with them. At the honest end: take this crate to Canopy, collect a debt, carry a message. At the far end the work turns to theft, smuggling, and worse — move a person out of the trees who does not want to go, see that someone stops being a problem.\n\nThe Syndicate holds the other half of the trade. Where the houses are the clients, the Syndicate moves the stolen, the smuggled, and the taken across the surface the dark elves cannot cross, fences what comes up the stair, and runs the routes that link Ilunethel to its buyers across Larion. Its darkest work brokers out of Nethel.\n\nThe Root Arch at the town's heart is the open stair down to Maanvalta, the dark-elf city below. Lawful trade moves in the open and pays its way, so only the soulstone trade and the darkest goods have to move hidden in the honest flow. Nethel, the old city's picked-clean ruins, is an overgrown sprawl of roofless marble halls where the poor and the unwelcome squat, where the Syndicate brokers the work nobody wants brokered in daylight.",
      "areas": {
        "The Undermarket": {
          "description": "The great lit terrace at the town's heart, the rebuilt tiers of the old elven city climbing above it. Stalls and stone-fronted shops crowd the terrace, the goods of the deep laid out in the open: spell ingredients and dark vintages, carved stone and deepwood, worked weapons and armor, the pale metals and gems of the under-earth. It is loud, crowded, and mixed - dark elves and outsiders of every kind, haggling in the open and watching each other over the tables.",
          "paths": [
            "The Root Arch",
            "The Queen of Ales",
            "Nethel"
          ]
        },
        "The Queen of Ales": {
          "description": "A tavern in the one wing of the old palace still standing - the queen's quarters, by the worn carvings, though the rest is rubble and green overgrowth on every side. The great chamber has been made over into a drinking hall: a long bar built along one wall, tables and benches crowded across the old stone floor, a fire in a hearth meant for grander things.",
          "paths": [
            "The Undermarket"
          ]
        },
        "The Root Arch": {
          "description": "At the town's heart the roots of a great tree have been shaped into a vast arch over an open stair going down into the dark. It has no door and no guard, and its lamps are kept always burning. Laden porters, dark elves, and the bold come and go on the steps between the surface and the city below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Undermarket"
          ]
        },
        "Nethel": {
          "description": "Past the reclaimed tiers, the old city lies overgrown and picked clean - broken marble halls open to the sky, columns toppled and grown through with the forest, washing strung between them and cookfires burning in rooms with no roofs. The narrow ways run crooked between the ruins.",
          "paths": [
            "The Undermarket"
          ]
        }
      },
