    "Carrion Spire": {
      "name": "Carrion Spire",
      "x": -28,
      "y": 42,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Elfwood",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "basicInfo": "A broken elven tower standing high above the canopy, half-fallen and open to the sky. Harpies nest in its heights, and the roost is famous for what they have stripped from the dead over the years: worked elven blades, silver ornaments, and old enchanted arms gone green with age, richer pickings than any common nest holds.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The harpies of the Carrion Spire are hostile and do not bargain.\n\nThey hunt by lure and ambush. They mimic the high-elven singing that once filled these ruins to draw climbers up the open stairs, then drop from above in a screaming mob, raking and trying to knock prey off the ledges into the long fall. They fight as a flock, never singly, and press hardest when they have height and numbers. Hurt them badly or kill two or three and the rest break off, wheel out of reach, and wait for a better moment rather than dying for the nest.\n\nThe loot sits at the top, in the roost-midden: generations of stripped kills, and because some of those kills were elves with good gear, the better pickings - worked elven arms, silver, the odd enchanted blade - lie mixed in among the bones and the cheap leavings.",
      "areas": {
        "The Broken Stair": {
          "description": "An open elven stair spiralling the outside of the ruined spire, the treads cracked and gapped, the canopy falling away far below. The stone is old and worked, the wind constant, and there is no rail where the rail has fallen. The way up is exposed the whole climb.",
          "paths": [
            "The Roost"
          ]
