      "hiddenInfo": "The griffons and hippogriffs of Windreach are hostile and defend their nests savagely.\n\nThey open by stooping from above, hard and fast, and try to drive climbers off the ledges before closing to beak and claw. Griffons are the fiercer and fight to hold the nest; hippogriffs are a shade less aggressive and more likely to break off if badly hurt. A beast guarding eggs or young will not retreat at all, and the rest of the crag answers a screaming nest-mate.\n\nThe plunder is in the eyries - griffon nests higher and richer, hippogriff lower and leaner - strung among bones and feathers, with the better gear in the high griffon nests. Eggs and eyasses are there too, for the reckless.",
