    "The Northern Foothills": {
      "name": "The Northern Foothills",
      "x": -11,
      "y": 38,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Orc Wolds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Wold's northern edge, where the grass climbs into cold stony hills beneath the white peaks beyond. The air bites here even in summer, the high ground stays rimed and slick, and the country belongs to the things that come down out of the mountains. Yetis raid the foothills in packs, and the clans ride north to throw them back as they always have.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Yetis are hostile and do not negotiate. They come down out of the white peaks in packs to raid: great white-furred brutes, fast over snow and stone. They hunt by ambush off the high slopes and run down what flees, and they drag their kills and their plunder back to fouled dens in the rocks. A yeti den is worth finding: the brutes carry off everything that glitters, and generations of raiding pile up in the back of a lair — coin, arms and armor off dead herders and raiders, the goods of broken steadings, and the bones beneath it all.\n\nFrost drakes den in the high rocks, and the heights are theirs. No true dragons — cold-blooded crag-lurkers the size of a warhorse that creep the boulder-fields and snow-choked gullies, ambush what comes near, and kill with a breath of killing frost and a serpent's rush. They are hostile and do not parley. They come and go as they please, and do not keep a single fixed lair. A drake hoards as its kind do, dragging kill and carried-off plunder into a hidden den.\n\nThe yetis carry thick white pelts the clans prize against the cold, and long claws and heavy fangs worked into charms and tools. The drake is the greater prize: its hide and scales turn cold aside and are sought by the clans' armorers, its frost-gland a rare thing the shamans and alchemists pay dearly for, its fangs worked into spears.\n\nCombat profile, yeti: fast, strong, pack-hunting brute. Opens from ambush off the high ground, several rushing together to drag down a single target with claw and fang. Fast over snow and broken rock, tireless on the chase, and bold in numbers; a pack that loses badly will break and flee uphill rather than die to the last.\n\nCombat profile, frost drake: ambush predator of the rocks. Lies still among the boulders and breaks cover in a rush, opening with a cone of freezing breath to stagger its prey before it closes with fang and claw. Fast in the first rush, less so in a long fight; if its ambush fails it withdraws into the rocks and stalks again. Defends its den and its heights to the death.",
      "areas": {
        "The Rimed Slopes": {
          "description": "The lower foothills, where the grass thins and breaks against cold grey stone and the wind comes down off the peaks hard and constant. The ground rises in long bare shoulders, frost-slick even in the warm months, with loose scree underfoot that slides and clatters. Sightlines are open and long across the slopes, with little cover but the occasional standing boulder or fold of ground.",
          "paths": [
            "The Boulder-Fields",
            "The High Gullies"
          ]
        },
        "The Boulder-Fields": {
          "description": "Higher ground strewn with great ice-split stones, some the size of huts, fallen from the peaks over ages. The boulders stand close enough to break any line of sight and large enough to hide something huge between them. Ice fills the gaps and sheets the leeward faces; the footing is broken, uneven, and treacherous, and a straight path through is impossible.",
          "paths": [
            "The Rimed Slopes",
            "The High Gullies"
          ]
        },
        "The High Gullies": {
          "description": "Steep snow-choked ravines cut into the upper foothills, climbing toward the white peaks beyond. The gully walls rise sheer and close, packed with old snow and hung with ice, and the floors are loose stone under drift. The cuts branch and narrow as they climb, command is from the high lips above, and the snow muffles sound and hides what lies beneath it.",
          "paths": [
            "The Rimed Slopes",
            "The Boulder-Fields"
          ]
        }
