    "Blood-Altar Mountain": {
      "name": "Blood-Altar Mountain",
      "x": -11,
      "y": 19,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Orc Wolds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A flat-topped mountain of red stone rising from the Wolds, its bare summit streaked dark down the cliffs so that from below it looks like an altar with blood running off it. Forest cloaks the slopes; the red plateau stands bare above. The Wrath-Speakers come here to work their rites, and sacrifices they carry up the mountain do not come down again.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Wrath-Speakers are hostile and do not parley. They are orc shamans who took the spirit-fury that the warrior-lodges master and gave it instead to demons — the Wraths, and the Lady of Wrath they serve — in exchange for power. They do not hold the mountain in force; they come to it for their rites and are gone between them, denning in the wooded slopes when present, leaving only the altar and its dead when not. The Oathbreakers ride here to be blessed before their raids.\n\nThe rite is sacrifice. The Wrath-Speakers take captives — raid-prisoners, travelers, enemies bound and dragged up the slopes — and kill them on the altar to feed the Lady of Wrath, who answers with her blessing: a battle-frenzy that makes the blessed faster, stronger, and unfeeling of wounds until the fury burns out. Captives are held bound in the slope-camps and on the plateau awaiting the knife.\n\nWhen the Wrath-Speakers work, they call the Lady's servants through: Wraths — demons of rage that burn with a fury of their own and throw themselves at anything living — and lesser imp-like things, petty demons summoned in numbers to swarm and harry. These fade when the summoner is killed or the rite broken.\n\nWhat is taken here is worth the climb: the goods of the sacrificed piled by the altar, the Wrath-Speakers' own ritual work — fetishes, bone-charms, and blades blooded for the rite that carry the Lady's fury in them — and offerings of coin and worked metal heaped at the altar's foot. The demon-things leave behind matter the alchemists and shamans prize.\n\nCombat profile, Wrath-Speaker: shaman and frenzy-caller. Fights from the back, working the blessing onto its allies to send them into killing rage, and calls Wraths and petty demons through to fight in its place. Drives the frenzied forward and itself stays clear; cornered, it takes the fury into its own body and comes on heedless of wounds, fighting to the death. Killing the Speaker ends its summons and breaks its blessing.\n\nCombat profile, Wrath: demon of rage. Comes on without caution or self-preservation, fast and furious, throwing itself at the nearest living thing and striking until destroyed. Does not flee, does not relent.\n\nCombat profile, petty demon: imp-like swarmer. Summoned in numbers to harry, claw, and distract; weak alone, dangerous in a mob. Winks out when its summoner dies.",
      "areas": {
        "The Wooded Slopes": {
          "description": "Steep forest climbing the mountain's flanks, the trees red-barked and close, the ground rising in switchbacks and rocky shelves toward the bare summit above. Cover is thick and broken, with hollows and overhangs worked into the slope where the rock breaks through. The canopy hides the plateau overhead and breaks any sightline to more than a stone's throw.",
          "paths": [
            "The Altar Plateau"
          ]
        },
        "The Altar Plateau": {
          "description": "The mountain's flat red summit, bare stone open to the sky and the wind, ringed at its edges by the last of the trees. At its center stands the altar — a great split slab of dark-stained red rock, channels cut into its surface running to its base. The plateau is open ground with no cover but the standing stones and the altar itself, and the whole Wold lies visible below the cliffs on every side.",
          "paths": [
            "The Wooded Slopes"
          ]
        }
      },
