    "Vorren's Hold": {
      "name": "Vorren's Hold",
      "x": 11,
      "y": 13,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Orc Wolds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The great ancestral stone seat of Clan Vorren, raised on a high tor above the iron hills it works, ringed in dark stone walls, its forges burning day and night and its smoke visible across the Wold. The hold is open to traders and to anyone who comes in peace.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Vorren's Hold is safe and welcoming to those who come honestly; the Watch keeps order within the walls and the clan prizes guests, traders, and any outsider who will fight for the Wold. Lead with orcs in any scene here, but the hold is mixed: settled clan-orcs throughout, but non-clan orcs visiting should be quite common as well.\n\nClan Vorren is ruled by its chief and a council of elders, and rule passes by blood and seniority. Vorren hold that the Wold is kept by the wall and the line: by standing fast, building strong, and arming the clans with good iron. They reckon Drokash reckless and Drokash reckons them slow, and the two have warred in the past, but Vorren considers orc infighting a waste of arms needed to defend the Wold against outside threats. Vorren, like Drokash, disowns the renegade orc Oathbreakers utterly.\n\nThe hold's wealth and identity are iron. The Mogra mines in the hills below feed the forges, and Vorren smiths are the finest armorers and weaponsmiths in the Wold. The mines have their own trouble of late, in the deep workings, and the clan pays well to see it handled. South of the hold, in the broken badlands, the Oathbreakers raid and burn, and Vorren riders ride against them; the clan has standing work for any who would hunt kin turned reaver. The land-sharks of the Churn take Vorren cattle off the hill pastures, and the clan's armorers pay good coin for the hides.\n\nVorren is a place to belong: to swear to the clan, take the settled warrior's path of shieldwall and heavy iron, learn the forge-crafts, and rise in the clan's esteem from guest to sworn to honored.",
      "areas": {
        "The Gate Court": {
          "description": "The hold's entry, a broad walled courtyard inside the great iron-bound gates, cut into the living rock of the tor. Wagons of ore come up from the mines and wagons of finished iron roll out for the south; traders' stalls cluster along the walls, and the clan's banners hang from the ramparts above. The forge-smoke hangs over everything, and the ring of hammers carries down from the smithies. From the wall-walk the whole iron-hill country lies open below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Great Hall",
            "The Forge Quarter"
          ]
        },
        "The Great Hall": {
          "description": "The clan's stone feast-hall, vast and beam-roofed, its walls hung with the arms and trophies of generations and the lineage-banners of the Vorren chiefs. Long tables run its length, a fire-pit burns at its heart, and the chief's seat stands at the far end before the council benches of the elders. This is where the clan gathers, where oaths are sworn and feasts held, where work is given and disputes are judged.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gate Court",
            "The Forge Quarter"
          ]
        },
        "The Forge Quarter": {
          "description": "The working heart of the hold, a long district of smithies, foundries, and armories built against the inner wall where the heat can vent. Forge-fires roar in rank, ore from the Mogra mines is smelted and worked, and the clan's smiths — orc and dwarf side by side — hammer out the blades, axes, and heavy armor Vorren is known for. Finished work hangs racked for trade and for the clan's own warriors; the best pieces, the masterwork arms of named smiths, are kept apart and sold dear.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gate Court",
            "The Great Hall"
          ]
        }
      },
