    "The Mogra Mines": {
      "name": "The Mogra Mines",
      "x": 15,
      "y": -4,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Orc Wolds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The iron mines that feed Vorren's Hold, cut deep into the hills below the fortress. The upper workings are busy day and night — Vorren miners hauling ore up to the forges above. But the deepest galleries have been lost. Kobolds broke into the lower workings from somewhere below and have held them since, and the miners no longer go down past the flooded levels.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The upper mine is safe and worked, watched by Vorren mine-guards; the danger is below, in the lost galleries. The kobolds there are hostile and attack intruders in numbers, though they are weak in any single fight and break when badly beaten — only to mass again. They broke through from the deeps and have spread into the lower workings, and the clan culls them without ever clearing them for good.\n\nThe kobolds fight as their kind do: not in open battle but by trap, ambush, and weight of numbers. The galleries they hold are seeded with deadfalls, pits, snares, and rigged collapses; they swarm out of side-passages and crawlways too small for a warrior in armor, loose bolts and stones from the dark, and fall back when met head-on to draw pursuers onto their traps. They see in the dark and know every tunnel; an intruder who brings no light fights blind, and one who brings light is seen first.\n\nCombat profile, kobold: trap-setter and swarmer. Avoids a fair fight; opens with traps and missiles from cover, swarms an isolated or wounded target, and flees the moment a fight turns against it. Dangerous in numbers and on its own ground, where every passage is rigged and every shadow holds another. Cowardly alone; relentless in a mob.",
      "areas": {
        "The Upper Workings": {
          "description": "The active mine: broad timber-shored tunnels and galleries lit by hung lamps. Vorren miners work the faces here, and guards stand at the heads of the shafts that lead down. The main shaft descends past worked levels toward the flooded galleries below, where the lamps end and the timber gives way to older, rougher stone.",
          "paths": [
            "The Lost Galleries"
          ]
        },
        "The Lost Galleries": {
          "description": "The deep workings, below the flooded levels, where the cut stone gives way to a warren of older tunnels and natural crawlways branching off into the dark. The passages are close and lightless, riddled with side-crawls and drops, and the floor is treacherous with rigged ground and old collapse.",
          "paths": [
            "The Upper Workings"
          ]
        }
      },
