    "Camp Drokash": {
      "name": "Camp Drokash",
      "x": -30,
      "y": 7,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Orc Wolds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The great moving seat of Clan Drokash, a tent-city pitched on the open steppe wherever the grass and the season call it. There are no walls here, only horse-lines running to the horizon, hide tents in their thousands, and the chieftain's great pavilion at the heart of it all. Drokash are the roving clan, horse-lords and riders, rich in herds and proud of the open ground no wall can hold. The camp welcomes traders, horse-buyers, and anyone who comes in peace.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Camp Drokash is safe and welcoming to those who come honestly; the riders keep their own order and the clan prizes guests, traders, and any outsider who will fight for the Wold. Lead with orcs in any scene here, but the camp is mixed: roving clan-orcs throughout, traders and herders of every kind, and drifters who follow a tent-city for the work and the coin.\n\nClan Drokash is ruled by a war-chief who won the place by deeds and holds it the same way, with a war-council of the clan's proven riders at the chief's side. Rank here is taken, not inherited — a rider rises by what they do, and a chief who weakens can be challenged. Drokash hold that the Wold is kept by the charge and the open ground: by riding hard and striking first. They reckon Vorren slow and penned, and the two clans have warred in the past, but they agree that orcs must band together to defend their lands from hostile outsiders. Both clans disown the Oathbreakers utterly.\n\nThe camp's wealth and pride are its herds — the finest horses in the Wold, bred and broken here and sold south through Gorren Crossing. The clan has standing work for riders. Rocs out of the Bluffs stoop on the horse-lines and carry off beasts and herders alike, and the boldest riders dream of climbing for an egg and breaking a roc to the saddle; the clan pays for the raptors thinned and prizes the flight-feathers. The saber-tooths of the deep grass take the herds and the hunters both, and to bring one down whole is a deed that makes a name. And when the yetis come down from the Northern Foothills onto the grazing, Drokash musters to throw them back, as the clan always has.\n\nDrokash is a place to belong: to ride with the clan, take the horse-warrior's path of lance and saddle, win a name in the contests and the hunt, and rise by deeds from guest to rider to a voice on the war-council.",
      "areas": {
        "The Muster-Ground": {
          "description": "The open heart of the camp where the riders gather, a broad trampled common ringed by the hide tents and the horse-lines. Mounts stand picketed in their hundreds, riders come and go at the gallop, and traders' wagons cluster at the margins where the camp meets the open grass. Banners on tall lances mark the clan's companies, and the whole steppe rolls away unbroken on every side.",
          "paths": [
            "The Chieftain's Pavilion",
            "The Contest Ground"
          ]
        },
        "The Chieftain's Pavilion": {
          "description": "The great tent at the camp's center, vast and many-poled, its hide walls hung with the trophies and war-banners of the Drokash chiefs and floored with the spoils of a hundred raids and hunts. Here the war-chief holds court among the council of proven riders, feasts are thrown and oaths sworn, work is given and disputes judged, and a stranger comes to be weighed and heard. The fire-pit at its heart never goes cold while the clan is camped.",
          "paths": [
            "The Muster-Ground",
            "The Contest Ground"
          ]
        },
        "The Contest Ground": {
          "description": "A wide stretch of cleared steppe set aside for the trials that win a rider standing: mounted races, the tilt and the lance, wrestling, archery from the saddle, and the breaking of wild horses. Riders test themselves and each other here from dawn, the crowd thick at the rails, wagers passing hand to hand. A name is made on this ground, and the deeds that decide rank in the clan are done in the open for all to see.",
          "paths": [
            "The Muster-Ground",
            "The Chieftain's Pavilion"
          ]
        }
      },
