    "The Underfloes": {
      "name": "The Underfloes",
      "x": -38,
      "y": 21,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A wide plain of fractured sea-ice and frozen flats in the north, where rimewyrms tunnel beneath the surface and burst up through it. The flats are open and look empty, which is the danger. Hunters come for rimewyrm hide and fangs, and for what the wyrms churn up from the deep ice — old wrecks and lost caravans the freeze swallowed, and now and then a vein of frostjade.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Rimewyrms are always hostile and hunt by ambush. A rimewyrm runs beneath the ice and follows vibration — footfalls, sled-runners, a struck blow — then erupts under its prey, strikes, and submerges to circle for another pass. They do not hold ground or guard a den so much as patrol a hunting-stretch, and a heavy, noisy crossing draws them faster than a light one. The young are smaller and burrow in the shallows near the broken ice.\n\nThe flats are a graveyard of the freeze. When the wyrms tunnel, they break open what the ice closed over long ago: foundered ships of the Northrealm, caravans that never reached shelter, the goods and gear of people the cold caught in the open. This wreckage is common in the broken ground and is the steady draw. Frostjade is the rare one — raw veins of the cold-bound stone, exposed only where a wyrm has cut deep, worth the risk to anyone who can carry it out.\n\nThe richest churned ground lies in the Underbreaks, where the ice is most shattered and the wyrms den deepest.",
      "areas": {
        "The Floes": {
          "description": "A vast flat of sea-ice and frozen ground, level and open to the horizon, with no cover and nothing to break the wind. The surface is sound in places and thin in others, scored with old fracture-lines and ridges of heaved ice. Footing is the only warning of what runs below.",
          "paths": [
