    "The Herdways": {
      "name": "The Herdways",
      "x": -14,
      "y": 24,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The open tundra-track in the north where the great herds move on their seasonal circuit — dire elk and winter mammoth in their hundreds, crossing the white in slow rivers of horn and tusk. Hunters and trappers work the migration for hide, meat, mammoth ivory, and the pelt of the dire snow-lynx, which fetches a luxury price in the south. The herds are not the danger. What hunts them is.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The great herds are not aggressive, but they are enormous and easily spooked, and a stampede of winter mammoth flattens whatever stands in front of it. Dire elk lower their horns and drive when cornered; mammoth defend their young without hesitation. The harvest is rich and mostly a matter of patience, weather, and not being underfoot.\n\nIMPORTANT: The dire snow-lynx defaults hostile to a lone or wounded target and hunts by ambush. White against white, it is nearly invisible until it moves — it shadows the herd from cover and ridgelines, drops onto the straggler, the young, or the lame, and is gone before the herd turns. It does not pace prey in the open the way wolves do; it waits above a line of travel and takes the one at the edge. Two or three may work the same stretch without coordinating, which means a kill drawn into the open invites the next.\n\nThe ivory and the pelts are the wealth here, carried south as luxury goods. The lynx den in the broken ground of the Snowveil, where the cover they hunt from is thickest.",
      "areas": {
        "The Migration": {
          "description": "A broad sweep of open tundra and wind-scoured snow, level and exposed, where the herd-track runs from horizon to horizon. The ground is churned and trampled along the route, packed hard by the passage of thousands. There is no cover on the flat itself — only the herds, and the distance.",
          "paths": [
