    "Northport": {
      "name": "Northport",
      "x": -13,
      "y": 4,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Ice Sea West",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The dead capital of the Northrealm, on the northwest coast where a glacier has come down over the old harbor city. In the warm age this was a great seaport, and its fleet is still here — ships at their moorings with the sea frozen solid around the hulls and the ice grown up the masts.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Northport is held by the draugr of the old Northrealm — the armed dead of the city that died here. They do not roam, hunt, or parley. Each holds the ground it was laid in: a doorway, a deck, a barrow, a hall. A draugr lets the living pass until they touch what it guards, then it rises in silence and does not stop. A careful party can move through much of the city; a greedy one wakes it.\n\nThe dead were a seafaring people, and they fall into ranks the way they lived — house-warriors in the streets and harbor, captains aboard their iced-in ships, and the old crowned dead deepest, in the hall above the frozen anchorage. The cold has kept everything: the city is not picked over, because almost no one who goes deep comes back to spend what they found.\n\nThe wealth of a kingdom lies where its dead lie. The arms and grave-gold of the Northrealm are thickest aboard the moored ships and in the high hall, and the regalia of the old crown — the dead-king's circlet and blade — rests with the king himself, on a throne above the harbor where the whole drowned-and-frozen fleet can be seen below.",
      "areas": {
        "The Frozen Harbor": {
          "description": "The old anchorage, where the sea lies frozen hard around a fleet of moored ships. Hulls stand locked in the ice at their berths, masts and rigging sheathed in frost, gangplanks frozen to the stone quays. The waterfront buildings rise behind, half-swallowed where the glacier has pushed through, open where it has not. Ice underfoot and the ships for cover.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ice-Locked City"
          ]
        },
        "The Ice-Locked City": {
          "description": "The streets above the waterline — stone and timber halls of a northern port, roofed in ice, some sound and some crushed where the glacier came down. Lanes run between the buildings, choked with drift and fallen masonry, narrowing where the ice has closed them to one body's width. Doorways stand dark and open. The way climbs toward the high ground at the back of the city.",
          "paths": [
            "The Frozen Harbor",
            "The Hall of the Drowned Fleet"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of the Drowned Fleet": {
          "description": "The great hall on the height at the back of the city, above the frozen anchorage. A long stone chamber, vaulted and rimed, its far end open to a terrace that overlooks the whole iced-in harbor and the fleet locked below. A throne stands at the chamber's head, sized for a man, set so its occupant faces out over the ships. One way in, by the climb from the city.",
          "paths": [
