    "The Temple of the Hearth": {
      "name": "The Temple of the Hearth",
      "x": -25,
      "y": -9,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The greatest shrine of the old Northrealm, raised over a sacred hot spring where the Lady of the Hearth was worshipped — the warmth rising from the earth that kept the Widow's cold at bay. Now the spring has been choked shut and the shrine frozen over,  its fires dead.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Temple of the Hearth is held by the Long Night and its cultists default hostile to any intruder. They are zealots of Hrimnara, the Widow of Winter, and they kill to keep their holy ground and to feed the cold.\n\nThe Long Night holds that the warm age was a lie and the cold is the world's true and final state — and they mean to help the Widow finish it. They choke the springs that keep the towns alive, leave the living and the dead to the cold as offerings, and revere the walking dead of the white as the Widow's own. Killing this temple's spring was their first and greatest work: the murder of the Hearth in her own house. Stillwater was a smaller one. Every failing spring in Aurora is their hand.\n\nThe cult's rites are worked at the dead spring at the temple's heart, and what they have gathered there — relics taken from the towns they have killed, and the ritual goods of their worship — lies with it.",
      "areas": {
        "The Frozen Steps": {
          "description": "The approach to the temple — a broad stair of rimed stone climbing to a pillared front, the whole face sheathed in ice and hung with frozen runoff where warm water once spilled down it. The doors stand open and dark. Carved figures of the Lady flank the way, faces worn and frost-cracked. Open ground, no cover but the pillars.",
          "paths": [
