    "Aurora Icefields": {
      "name": "Aurora Icefields",
      "x": -37,
      "y": 7,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The vast open white at the heart of the north — trackless icefields and wind-scoured snow running flat to the horizon under the auroral sky, with nothing on them but distance, weather, and what the ice has kept. Travelers cross only when they must, and many who cross do not arrive. The aurora stands overhead at night, and the snowlanders say that is the Widow walking.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The open ice is dangerous chiefly for its weather. Blizzards rise fast and without warning, and the wind off the high ice can flay exposed skin, knock a traveler down, and bury a stopped party where it stands. A storm caught in the open kills more surely than any beast, and the white offers no shelter and no landmark to steer by.\n\nWhat moves on the ice is the Widow's. By night, rime-wights — the frozen dead of those the white has taken — cross the fields in slow processions, and the snowlanders' law is plain: stand aside and let them pass. The wights do not hunt and do not heed the living unless the living get in their way, and then they turn and do not stop. Frost drakes hunt the high ground at the edges of the fields, and rimewolves range the open in packs, pacing travelers for miles before they close.\n\nThe ice is a graveyard of the freeze, and buried shapes show through the blue ice on clear days: foundered ships and lost caravans of the Northrealm, common across the fields, and far rarer, the white stone of things older than any kingdom. The dead and the cold have kept what they swallowed, for anyone willing to dig it out of the ice.",
      "areas": {
        "The Open White": {
          "description": "A flat of wind-packed snow and bare blue ice running to the horizon in every direction, featureless and exposed, with no rise or rock to break the wind or mark a path. Shapes show frozen in the ice underfoot in places — timber, iron, the edges of things the freeze took. The sky is wide and the aurora burns across it after dark.",
          "paths": [
            "The Frozen Colossus"
          ]
        },
        "The Frozen Colossus": {
          "description": "A titan of a figure half-buried in the icefield — a vast humanlike shape of grey-white stone, sunk to the chest in the ice, its features worn smooth and its scale beyond anything built by living hands. The ice for a long way around its base is studded with frozen shapes: gear, sledges, and the dead of those who came to it and did not leave. Frost sprites and ice mephits swarm thick here, where the cold runs deepest in all the fields.",
          "paths": [
            "The Open White"
          ]
        }
      },
