    "The Firwood": {
      "name": "The Firwood",
      "x": 1,
      "y": -37,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Aurora",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The great snow-mantled fir forest along Aurora's southern rim. It is the gentlest country in the north — sheltered under the trees, worked by snowlander loggers and charcoal-burners. Old Northrealm holdfasts and hunting-halls stand scattered and ruined through the deep wood, raised when this was a living kingdom, and the gear and goods of the old realm still lie in them, where the snow-trolls den.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The snowlanders who work the Firwood are hardy, plainspoken, and used to strangers coming up the road. The logging steads and charcoal-camps are safe and will trade, shelter, and point a traveler onward.\n\nThe danger is in the deep wood, and it is the snow-trolls. They are great cold-hardened trolls, and they have taken the ruined Northrealm halls scattered through the forest for their dens — drawn to the old stone shelters, denning among whatever the dead kingdom left in them. IMPORTANT: snow-trolls in their dens default hostile and attack anything that comes near, and they heal from any wound that is not burned or seared shut; they go sluggish and slow in the deepest cold and rouse to fury in a thaw or near fire. A troll-held ruin must be taken from the troll.\n\nThe Northrealm built well, and what its people left when the cold drove them out still lies in the ruins the trolls now hold: old arms and armor of fine northern make, worked gear, and the buried goods of a vanished kingdom. The richest of it lies deepest in the wood, in the largest of the old holdfasts, where the biggest trolls den.",
      "areas": {
        "The Logging Steads": {
          "description": "A cluster of snowlander work-camps — carved-timber longhouses, stacked cordwood, charcoal-mounds smoking under their turf, and sledge-tracks running off among the trees. The wood here is thinned by the axe and open to the sky in patches. People work and trade here, and the road runs on north and deeper in.",
          "paths": [
            "The Deep Firs"
          ]
        },
        "The Deep Firs": {
          "description": "The old growth, where the firs stand close and tall and the canopy holds the snow off the forest floor in a dim green hush. Game-trails and overgrown tracks wind between the trunks. Among the trees, ruined stone — fallen walls, broken halls, the mossed-and-rimed footings of old Northrealm holdfasts — stands half-swallowed by the wood, dark openings leading down into them.",
          "paths": [
            "The Logging Steads",
            "The Old Holdfast"
          ]
        },
        "The Old Holdfast": {
          "description": "The largest of the ruined Northrealm halls, deep in the wood — a great stone shell of a building, roof long fallen, walls standing to the height of two men and hung with ice and creeper. The interior opens into cold stone chambers and a way down into vaulted cellars below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Deep Firs"
          ]
        }
      },
