    "Villa Parhelion": {
      "name": "Villa Parhelion",
      "x": -8,
      "y": -39,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Shadow Summits",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "factions": [],
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Villa Parhelion is a vast, windowless, fortress-like structure of black stone on the high pass between the Shadow Summits and the dwarven holds to the south, and the seat of the Syndicate in the north. Most who would trade with the vampire lords, or buy what is outlawed elsewhere, come through Parhelion to do it.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Parhelion was built by a vampire lord who could not bear the sun and would not live without the day. Its vast indoor halls are wonders of magic and mechanisms that seem like sunlit, outdoor spaces. Every bird, beast, and even insect in these worlds is a clockwork mechanism, every tree and blade of grass made of inert but real-seeming materials; all water and air circulating within is moved by hidden pumps and fans.\n\nParhelion's builder was slain by other vampires with the aid of the Syndicate after he grew too ambitious, and now the Syndicate uses it as its base of operations.\n\nThe Syndicate and vampire lords don't trust each other, but need each other: most trade with the vampire lords flows through Parhelion, since normal merchants won't deal with vampires. The goods sold here cannot easily be found elsewhere in Larion: the tools of blood-sorcerers, the workings of blood-magic, the spells and instruments of necromancy and psionic arts prohibited elsewhere.\n\nThe High Men who run the Syndicate gather here: the richest and most feared crime-lords alive, rivals who rule through tribute, debt, and murder. But Parhelion is safe, neutral ground, on pain of being declared an enemy to the entire Syndicate.\n\nThe Grey Guards are the Syndicate's own soldiers and the garrison of Parhelion. They keep the truce within the walls and turn their hands to nothing else: hard, competent, dead serious, courteous to those who merit it and cold to those who do not.",
      "areas": {
        "Parhelion Gate": {
          "description": "The pass road climbs to a gate in a wall of black stone, squat and immense. A sun in bas-relief is carved into the black stone above the gate. The Syndicate's Grey Guards hold the yard and the doors.",
          "paths": [
            "Garden Hall"
          ]
        },
        "Garden Hall": {
          "description": "A vast hall containing a wide formal garden in daylight — gravel walks between clipped hedges, flowering beds, a fountain playing at the center, a false sky overhead. It serves as Parhelion's receiving hall. Guests wait on benches to be seen; servants and Grey Guards move among them and send each where their business lies, to the Market or down into the working halls, and turn none loose to wander. There are rough sorts here as well as fine, and most wait a little nervously.",
          "paths": [
            "Parhelion Gate",
            "Market Hall",
            "Idyll Hall",
            "The Back Rooms"
          ]
        },
        "Market Hall": {
          "description": "A vast hall containing a walled garden of cottages under a gentle false sun, flower-bordered paths running between them, each cottage a quiet shopfront for a different dark trade — the tools of blood-sorcery in one, the instruments of necromancy in another, hexes and curses, the proscribed arts of the mind. A guest is received, judged, and shown within by a servant or a guard, and what is for sale is brought out behind a closed door to those thought worthy of seeing it. The custom here is unhurried and exclusive, the courtesy of a house that asks no questions of buyers who can afford its wares.",
          "paths": [
            "Garden Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Back Rooms": {
          "description": "Service rooms that have no pretense of being out of doors. Hidden doors in the outdoor halls lead to bare stone corridors where the great pumps and fans and engines that drive Parhelion's counterfeit skies run day and night. Here the Grey Guards barrack and take their briefings, and bravos and hired hands wait between jobs. Those who work for the Syndicate may rise from hired hand to trusted to a name the High Men know by doing the deeds that need to be done.",
          "paths": [
            "Garden Hall",
            "The Dungeon Cells"
          ]
        },
        "The Dungeon Cells": {
          "description": "Bare black stone, cell after cell behind iron, with Grey Guards walking the passages. The Syndicate keeps prisoners here for ransom and for leverage.",
          "paths": [
            "The Back Rooms"
          ]
        },
        "Idyll Hall": {
          "description": "A vast hall containing a wide summer meadow at the height of day, tall grass and wildflowers running to a soft bright haze on every side, a still lake at its heart with rowboats drawn up at a little jetty. Fine lodges stand along the shore, and a great hall at the meadow's edge is where the made men of the Syndicate take their ease among comforts looted from a dozen kingdoms. The stair to the high tower climbs from here.",
          "paths": [
            "Garden Hall",
            "Celestial Hall"
          ]
        },
        "Celestial Hall": {
          "description": "At the top of the tower, a vast hall made to seem the very heavens, a chamber of cloud and brilliant gold-white light where one stands as if lifted into a sunlit sky. A great orrery turns slowly at its center, the sun and wandering stars wheeling on golden arms, and a shaft of radiant light falls through it to strike a sphere of polished brass that blazes like a second sun. Beneath the orrery stands a long table where the High Men of the Syndicate meet in a council they call the High Table.",
          "paths": [
            "Idyll Hall"
          ]
        }
      },
