    "The Firewild": {
      "name": "The Firewild",
      "known": true,
      "x": 20,
      "y": -14,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Black Fells",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The unclaimed volcanic badlands east of Smoketown and the works—cinder-flats, sulfur vents, and fields of black lava-glass that even the Goblinate leaves alone. Fire-drakes den in the vents and hunt the open ground; their scales and the raw emberglass underfoot are worth a fortune to anyone who survives the taking.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Firewild is wilderness, not a settlement—the creatures here default hostile to anything warm-blooded that enters their ground, and they do not parley. There are no inhabitants to bargain with.\n\nThe land itself is a threat. Sulfur vents, unstable lava-glass, and sudden ground-heat kill the unready as surely as any beast.\n\nFire-drakes are lesser kin of true dragons, vent-denning, territorial, and aggressive. They open from the air or burst from a vent-mouth, breathe fire, and fight to hold their ground. Their scale, claws, and eggs are the prize. Salamanders bask on the lava-glass and lash with fire when crowded. Magma oozes pool in the cooled tubes, slow and engulfing, dissolving what they catch.\n\nGiant fire beetles scuttle the cinder-flats in numbers, their glands prized for the cold-light they shed; and the odd basilisk suns itself among the glass, deadly at a glance, given a wide berth even by the drakes.\n\nLoot here is fire-aspected material. Drake-scale is thick overlapping plate shed in moltings or stripped from a kill; worked into armor it turns flame and the breath of fire-things. Salamander-hide is supple and heat-proof, prized for fireproof garments and glove-leather. A fire beetle's glands hold a cold blue light that shines for days once cut free, a lantern that needs no flame and gives off no heat. Basilisk parts—the eye, the gizzard-stones—are the base for a salve that wards against petrification, the only common guard against the creature's own gaze. Raw emberglass is the great prize: a volcanic glass that holds fire in its heart, cut from seams in the lava-glass and the vent-walls. A blade or arrowhead of emberglass deals fire damage in place of its ordinary edge, and bites hardest into plants, fungi, trolls, venomous beasts, and things of frost.",
      "areas": {
        "The Cinder Flats": {
          "description": "An open expanse of black ash and grit broken by sulfur vents that hiss and gout. The ground is warm underfoot and treacherous where crusted ash hides soft heat below. Bones of large beasts lie scattered and half-buried. Sightlines run long across the flats, broken only by drifting vent-smoke.",
          "paths": [
            "The Glass Fields",
            "The Vent-Dens"
          ]
        },
        "The Glass Fields": {
          "description": "A plain of black volcanic glass, fused smooth and sharp-edged, glinting where the light catches it. Slabs of it can be quarried with effort and care. The petrified shapes of past wanderers stand here and there among the panes, frozen mid-stride.",
          "paths": [
            "The Cinder Flats",
            "The Vent-Dens"
          ]
        },
        "The Vent-Dens": {
          "description": "A broken country of fissures and old lava tubes where the heat pools thickest. Deep vent-mouths open in the rock, and cooled tubes hold slow-moving pools of molten residue that glow in the dark. Scattered scale and old moltings litter the approaches to the larger openings.",
          "paths": [
            "The Cinder Flats",
            "The Glass Fields"
          ]
        }
      },
