    "The Slag Warrens": {
      "name": "The Slag Warrens",
      "known": true,
      "x": -28,
      "y": -15,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Black Fells",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "An old goblin mine-works dug into the volcanic rock and then abandoned, its tunnels left half-collapsed when whatever broke in from below drove the diggers out. The goblins fled in a hurry and left their hauls behind—ore, tools, and locked caches still sitting in the dark. Something large dens in the deep galleries now, and the gobbos have not gone back.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Slag Warrens are abandoned and hostile—the thing that drove the goblins out still holds the deep galleries and attacks anything that comes within reach. It does not parley. Lesser vermin breeding in the warmth are equally hostile. There are no inhabitants to bargain with.\n\nThe works are unstable. Propped tunnels, flooded lower levels of cooled slag, and bad air in the deep cuts make the place a danger before anything attacks. Old goblin trap-lines, some still set, guard the better caches.\n\nThe deep galleries are denned by an ankheg grown huge in the heat—a burrowing thing with a chitin shell, great serrated jaws, and a spray of acid it spits to soften prey and stone alike. It moves through the rock itself, bursting up through floor and wall without warning, and drags what it catches back underground. It does not hunt the surface; the Warrens are its ground, and it defends them.\n\nGiant fire beetles and worse vermin have bred in the abandoned cuts, swarming the upper tunnels in numbers.\n\nLoot here is what the goblins left and what the burrower's nature provides. The abandoned caches hold raw ore, smithing tools, and coin locked away in the rush to flee—ordinary goods in quantity, the wages of a mine emptied overnight. An ankheg's shell-plates are thick acid-proof chitin, worked into armor that turns acid and the bite of acid-spitting things. Its acid-gland, cut intact, yields a corrosive prized for eating through stone, locks, and hardened metal. The fire beetles here carry cold-light glands: a gland cut free shines blue for days, a flameless and heatless lantern.",
      "areas": {
        "The Mine-Mouth": {
          "description": "The entrance works: a timber-framed entrance driven into the rock, with ore-carts abandoned on rusted rails and a winch-house gone to rot. The framing sags, and rubble half-blocks the way down. Daylight reaches only the first stretch before the tunnels go dark.",
          "paths": [
            "The Upper Cuts"
          ]
        },
        "The Upper Cuts": {
          "description": "A warren of narrow mining tunnels branching and doubling back, propped with failing timber and cut at odd angles to follow old seams. Side-chambers hold stacked crates and locked strongboxes left behind. The air grows close and warm the deeper the cuts run, and several passages end in fresh collapse.",
          "paths": [
            "The Mine-Mouth",
            "The Lower Galleries"
          ]
        },
        "The Lower Galleries": {
          "description": "The lowest workings, where the diggers cut into natural caverns and stopped. The floor is broken and tunnel-bored in places, riddled with holes too large for any goblin tool, and pools of cooled black slag fill the low ground. The heat is heavy here and the dark complete. Bored shafts lead off into the surrounding rock.",
          "paths": [
            "The Upper Cuts"
          ]
        }
      },
