    "The Dragonworks": {
      "name": "The Dragonworks",
      "known": true,
      "x": -14,
      "y": 17,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Black Fells",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Church of the Pyre's great alchemical works, set apart from Smoketown out on the lava-fields where a live fissure feeds the vats. This is where dragonfire is brewed in bulk—the alchemical fuel that charges every Goblinate weapon. Blast-walls of heaped earth ring the yards, the air shimmers with heat and fumes, and the whole place is built to keep its fire from spreading to anything the Goblinate cares about.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Dragonworks is a Church of the Pyre stronghold under heavy guard, and its perimeter shoots first. Pyre wardens and Goblinate marines hold the gates and the walls; the alchemist-priests within suffer no unauthorized step inside the yards. Anyone who reaches the works without leave is treated as a saboteur and killed. The creatures of the surrounding fields are hostile wilderness.\n\nThe works exist because dragonfire is too dangerous to brew inside the city—even the goblins will not sleep beside it. Drawing on the heat of the fissure, the alchemist-priests cook raw reagents down into the finished fuel in great vats, decant it into sealed vessels, and send it up the Iron Road to the Firelance Foundry and the mountain. The labor is done in sealed vestments against the fumes, and accidents take workers regularly.\n\nThe place is built around the danger it makes. The yards are split by earthen blast-berms so a blast in one cannot reach the next. The vat-house holds the cooking. The decanting-floor fills and seals the vessels. The stores hold finished fuel and raw reagents apart from each other, since together they are catastrophe. A fire loosed in the stores or the vat-house would gut the works and cripple the Goblinate's weapon-supply for a season—the place is one spark from destroying itself, which is its great weakness and the reason the perimeter is so absolute.\n\nThe alchemist-priests are zealots who hold that the fire they brew is the holy instrument of the world's burning. They do the work as a sacrament.\n\nLoot here is the finished product and the means of making it. Sealed vessels of dragonfire are the prize: an alchemical fuel that ignites on contact and clings, burning fierce and hard to quench, ready to charge a weapon or set a fire nothing will put out. The alchemist-priests' stores hold rare reagents—the costly stock that goes into the brewing, valuable to any alchemist. Pyre vestments are heat-proof and fume-proof sealed garments, proof against fire and choking air both.",
      "areas": {
        "The Gatehouse": {
          "description": "The single guarded entrance through the earthen ramparts that ring the works: a fortified gate with a checkpoint, watch-platforms, and a killing-ground of open cinder before it. The blast-walls rise beyond, heaped earth and slag taller than a man, with smoke and shimmering heat showing above them.",
          "paths": [
            "The Vat-Yards"
          ]
        },
        "The Vat-Yards": {
          "description": "The heart of the works: a compound of great iron vats and brick furnaces divided into bays by earthen blast-berms, so each stands apart from the next. Pipes and flues run between them, and a fissure glows red at the yard's center, feeding heat to the vats above it. Catwalks cross overhead. The ground is stained and scorched.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gatehouse",
            "The Decanting Floor",
            "The Stores"
          ]
        },
        "The Decanting Floor": {
          "description": "A long shed of workbenches and filling-rigs where the finished fuel is drawn off into sealed vessels and crated for transport. Racks of empty and filled vessels line the walls behind blast-shielding. Loading-bays open onto a yard where wagons are made ready. Everything here is built low and heavy against accident.",
          "paths": [
            "The Vat-Yards"
          ]
        },
        "The Stores": {
          "description": "Two separate magazines set well apart behind their own berms: one for crated reagents, one for finished fuel, kept distant from each other by design. Heavy doors, thick walls, and warning-marks guard both. The ground between them is open and watched from the walls.",
          "paths": [
            "The Vat-Yards"
          ]
        }
      },
