    "The Firelance Foundry": {
      "name": "The Firelance Foundry",
      "known": true,
      "x": -10,
      "y": 6,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Black Fells",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The works where the Goblinate's fire-weapons are built and tested, set on a scorched hillside within reach of Smoketown. Firelances and heavier engines are assembled here, charged with dragonfire, and proof-fired into the bare slope until they are trusted to work. The crack and roar of test-firing carries for miles, and the hillside above the foundry is burned black and littered with the wreckage of weapons that failed.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Firelance Foundry is Goblinate military ground under guard. Hobgoblin master-smiths and goblin crews run the works; marines hold the gates and the proving-slope. Outsiders without leave are taken for spies, and the prototype-stores are the most closely watched ground in the foundry. The surrounding country is hostile wilderness.\n\nThe foundry assembles what the Dragonworks fuels. Tubes, hafts, and fittings are forged and fitted; the finished weapons are charged with sealed dragonfire and carried out to the slope to be proof-fired before they go up the Iron Road. The master-smiths guard their methods jealously, and the newest designs—heavier lances, multi-shot engines, weapons not yet in the field—are kept under lock in the prototype-stores.\n\nThe proving happens on the bare hillside above the works, fired into the empty slope. When a minister or an archpriest visits, the test is sometimes made on bound prisoners instead of the slope, a demonstration dressed as a trial.\n\nThe foundry's true value is its designs. The working weapons can be stolen or copied; the prototypes are worth more than the finished lances, since they are what the Goblinate will field next and what its enemies most need to understand.\n\nLoot here is weapons and the knowledge of them. A firelance is the Goblinate's signature arm: a hafted metal tube, charged with dragonfire, that throws a gout of clinging flame at what it is aimed at—deadly, short-ranged, and dangerous to a careless wielder. The prototype weapons are stranger and stronger: heavier lances that throw farther, engines that fire more than once, designs not yet loosed on Larion. The smiths' design-plates and pattern-books are worth as much as the weapons, the means to build or counter what the foundry makes.",
      "areas": {
        "The Foundry Gate": {
          "description": "The guarded entrance to the works, a fortified gate in a stockade wall with watch-platforms above and a yard of scorched ground before it. Smoke rises from the forge-stacks beyond the wall, and the burned hillside looms over everything, dark and scarred.",
          "paths": [
            "The Assembly Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Assembly Hall": {
          "description": "A long forge-hall of furnaces, drop-hammers, and fitting-benches where weapon-tubes are worked and assembled. Racks of hafts, fittings, and finished lances line the walls. A charging-bay set behind heavy shielding stands apart, where the dragonfire is loaded. Wide doors open onto the proving-slope.",
          "paths": [
            "The Foundry Gate",
            "The Proving Slope",
            "The Prototype Stores"
          ]
        },
        "The Proving Slope": {
          "description": "The bare, blackened hillside above the foundry, fired into until nothing grows on it. Firing-stands and earth-banked positions face the slope from below. The ground is cratered, slagged, and strewn with the burst and twisted wreckage of weapons that failed their test. Chaining-posts stand among the firing-stands.",
          "paths": [
            "The Assembly Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Prototype Stores": {
          "description": "A locked and shielded magazine set apart from the assembly hall, walled in heavy stone and barred at the door. Racks and crates within hold the foundry's newest and most guarded work behind blast-shielding. A single watched approach leads to it.",
          "paths": [
            "The Assembly Hall"
          ]
        }
      },
