    "Dun Teine Watch": {
      "name": "Dun Teine Watch",
      "known": true,
      "x": -29,
      "y": -36,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Black Fells",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A dwarven fortress in the high snows of the southern peninsula, holding the one approach down into the volcanic country below. Its walls are thirty feet of fitted stone and it has never been taken—the Goblinate has reckoned the cost and left it alone. The watch keeps a long vigil over the smoking land and the road that climbs from it.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Inhabitants: dwarves of an old mountain line, the garrison and the families who keep the Watch—smiths, wardens, watch-keepers, and the few traders hardy enough to climb here. Outsiders fleeing the Goblinate, deserters off the works, and adventurers with business below are taken in if they are not a danger. Population is dwarf-led and mixed at the hearth.\n\nThe Watch holds because taking it would cost the Goblinate more than ignoring it does, and because the dwarves keep the one defensible approach down to the volcanic country. They are not strong enough to march on Smoketown and know it; their work is to hold the gate, keep the count, and shelter those who come up off the peninsula alive.\n\nThe Watch keeps the old lore of the mountain below. Its archives and its eldest hold what the Goblinate has forgotten: the deep history of Fire Mountain, the wards the old dwarven vigil raised over the fire-breach, the name and binding of Suleyvan the Sealer, and the thing of blue flame that stands the breach. They keep a tally of what goes up the Iron Road and into the Fissure—the relics, the reagents, the prisoners of particular kinds—and they read in that tally the shape of what the Pyre is preparing.\n\nThe Watch is the natural seat for work on the peninsula. Its people know the ground below: the war-machine and its arteries, the harbor at Loot Landing, the works that brew and build the Goblinate's fire, the mountain and its garrison. They take in those who would move against any of it, and they pay for what hurts the Goblinate or thins the road. Honest goods are sold here at hard prices—frost-gear above all, the rimebone and frostjade and frost-blessed steel that the wilds and the fire-things below make necessary, carried up at ruinous cost.",
      "areas": {
        "The Gate-Tunnel": {
          "description": "The only way in: a stone tunnel driven through the curtain wall, gated and portcullised at both ends, with murder-holes above and guard-niches to either side. Snow drifts against the outer gate. The tunnel opens inward onto the fortress yard, and the cold of the pass gives way to the warmth of stone and fire within.",
          "paths": [
            "The Watch-Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Watch-Yard": {
          "description": "The fortress's central court, ringed by the inner keep, the forge, and the barrack-halls built against the curtain wall. Stairs climb to the wall-walk and the watch-tower above. Snow is kept swept from the flagstones, braziers burn at the corners, and the smoking land below is visible through the embrasures of the high wall.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gate-Tunnel",
            "The Long Hearth",
            "The Forge-Hall",
            "The Watch-Tower"
          ]
        },
        "The Long Hearth": {
          "description": "The great common hall of the Watch, a long stone room dug into the keep with a fire-trench running its length and benches and trestle-tables down both sides. Casks line one wall and a kitchen smokes at the far end. It is warm, low-ceilinged and close, hung with the banners and trophies of an old garrison.",
          "paths": [
            "The Watch-Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Forge-Hall": {
          "description": "The Watch's smithy, built around a deep forge that burns day and night against the cold. Anvils, quenching-troughs, and racks of tools and finished steel fill the hall. Stores of ore and stranger stock—pale frost-metals among them—are kept in side-vaults.",
          "paths": [
            "The Watch-Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Watch-Tower": {
          "description": "The highest point of the fortress, a stone tower above the wall-walk with a railed top open to the wind. From here the whole smoking peninsula spreads below: the road climbing from the lowlands, the haze over Smoketown, and the dark cone of Fire Mountain at the far cape. A signal-brazier and a great horn stand ready at the parapet. Within, beneath the lookout, a vaulted room holds the Watch's scrolls and tomes about Fire Mountain.",
          "paths": [
            "The Watch-Tower-Lookout"
          ]
        },
        "The Watch-Tower-Lookout": {
          "description": "The railed crown of the tower, open to the sky and the cutting wind, where a watcher stands at all hours. The view runs the length of the peninsula in clear weather. The signal-brazier and the warning-horn are here.",
          "paths": [
            "The Watch-Tower"
          ]
        }
      },
