        "The Old Cairns": {
          "description": "A stretch of the upper droveway where the burial-marks cluster — dozens of stone cairns, and among them a handful of true barrows: long low mounds turfed over, entrance-stones half-sunk in the earth. Some mounds have settled and split, showing black gaps into the dark beneath. Carved kerbstones ring the larger barrows, worn but still legible: bulls, knotwork, the marks of droving-families long gone. The grass grows rank and undisturbed here, and even the herd keeps off this ground.",
          "paths": [
