    "The Skarn": {
      "name": "The Skarn",
      "x": 16,
      "y": -14,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whiteholds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A high glacier-pass through the white peaks, where a frozen river of ice grinds down between black cliffs and a field of ice-scoured boulders. It is a hard shortcut between the holds, days faster than the low roads and far more dangerous. Yetis den in the ice-caves along the walls and hunt the pass.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: the yetis of the Skarn default to hostile and hunt the pass as their own ground. They are huge, white-furred, and near invisible against the snow until they are on you, and they take prey by ambush — rushing out of cover, a cliffside, or a snowbank, to seize and drag the catch back toward the ice-caves. They are strong enough to break a dwarf in two and patient enough to stalk a party for a long way before they strike. In a real fight they will haul off a single victim and let the rest flee rather than face a braced and ready crew, then return for the stragglers once the party is strung out and tired.\n\nThe pass is the fast way between holds and the white country beyond, which is why crews keep risking it despite what dens there. Storms close it without warning, whiteouts cut sight to an arm's length, and the ice underfoot hides crevasses deep enough to swallow a wagon.\n\nThe ice-caves where the yetis den hold what they have dragged off the pass over the years — the gear and goods of travelers who did not make it, frozen into the cave-ice and the packed snow. Yeti pelts are thick winter-hide, prized for cold-country gear, and their great claws and fangs are crafting stock.",
      "areas": {
        "The Pass Mouth": {
          "description": "The trail climbs to where the glacier spills down between two black cliff-walls, the ice cracked and blue-shadowed underfoot. The way narrows into the pass ahead, the boulder-field beyond half-buried in old snow. Dark openings notch the cliffs to either side, high and low. Wind drives loose snow down the throat of the pass in stinging gusts, and the light off the ice is hard and white.",
          "paths": [
            "The Boulder Field"
          ]
        },
        "The Boulder Field": {
          "description": "The pass widens into a long field of ice-scoured boulders, some the size of houses, scattered across the glacier's back and packed around with drifted snow. Sightlines break every few strides — a crew can see clearly one moment and be walled in by stone and snow the next. The glacier groans and shifts underfoot, and cracks open here and there into blue depths. The cliffs rise sheer on both sides, pocked with cave-mouths, and the high white peaks crowd close overhead.",
          "paths": [
            "The Pass Mouth",
