    "Wyrmtarn": {
      "name": "Wyrmtarn",
      "x": 9,
      "y": 16,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whiteholds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A frozen mountain tarn high in the white peaks, its surface a sheet of cracked grey ice ringed by snowbound scree. Rimewyrms tunnel through the ice and the frozen ground beneath it — long pale serpents that burst up through the surface to take prey, then vanish back into the dark below. The ice is littered with the wreckage of those they caught: shattered carts, scattered bone, dark holes punched up through the sheet.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: the rimewyrms of the tarn default to hostile and hunt the ice as their hunting ground. They move unseen beneath the frozen surface and the packed earth around the tarn, tracking the tread of anything heavy crossing above by the vibration of it, then erupting up through the ice to seize prey in a single rush before submerging again. They are long, pale, and cold-blooded, blind but for the shaking of the ground, and a crew that stops moving or moves lightly can pass where a heavy, blundering party draws a strike. A wounded wyrm dives and waits rather than pressing a losing fight, and surfaces again when the prey has let its guard down.\n\nThe tarn freezes thick enough to walk and thin enough in places to drop a careless step into black water beneath. The wyrms' tunnels honeycomb the ice and the frozen banks, and the surface can give way over a fresh one.\n\nRimebone is the wyrms' cold-aspected skeleton, and their hide and fangs are crafting stock for those who can take them. The ice of the tarn holds what the wyrms dragged down and lost — gear and goods of past catches, frozen into the sheet and sunk in the shallows where a strike went through.",
      "areas": {
        "The Frozen Shore": {
          "description": "The trail comes down to the rim of the tarn, a flat sheet of cracked grey ice ringed by drifted scree. Dark holes punch up through the surface here and there, rimmed with shattered ice and refrozen at the edges. Wreckage juts from the sheet — a cartwheel, splintered timber, the curve of a ribcage frozen mid-sink. The far shore is a pale blur across the open ice, and the peaks stand white and close around the bowl.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ice Sheet"
          ]
        },
        "The Ice Sheet": {
          "description": "The frozen surface of the tarn, wide and open and offering nowhere to hide. The ice is grey and cracked, clear in patches over black water and snow-dusted over others, and it shifts and booms underfoot with the weight of a crossing. Holes gape across the sheet where things have come up through it, some old and refrozen, some raw. The ice thins toward the tarn's center, and dark shapes move slow beneath it where the light filters down.",
          "paths": [
            "The Frozen Shore",
            "The Sink-Holes"
          ]
        },
        "The Sink-Holes": {
          "description": "The tarn's far edge, where the wyrms' tunnels break the surface in a cluster of jagged holes and the ice is broken into tilted plates. Meltwater pools dark between the slabs, and the frozen banks are bored through with burrow-mouths running down into the earth. Gear and frozen bundles lie caught in the shallows below the broken ice, visible through the murk. The banks rise into snow-choked scree, and the dark openings exhale cold from below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ice Sheet"
          ]
        }
