    "The Coldrun": {
      "name": "The Coldrun",
      "x": 27,
      "y": 32,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whiteholds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A grim stretch of mountain road below Deepgate, where the way runs through narrow cuts and broken ground between the holds and the delving-town. Bandits work this road, preying on delvers carrying hauls up out of the dark and on any traveler who looks worth the trouble. Crews go missing here, gear turns up for sale that belonged to the vanished, and few who travel it alone come through unrobbed.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: the bandits of the Coldrun default to hostile and exist to rob those who pass, above all delvers laden with what they hauled up from the Deep. They do not delve themselves — they let others go down, bleed for the loot, and stagger back up, then take it on the road. They prefer a robbed traveler to a dead one when the taking is easy, so a crew that yields its haul and looks too hard to fight may be let go lighter, while a rich haul or a weak party gets jumped outright. They ambush from the cuts and the high ground, fight with numbers and dirty work, and scatter the moment the one who leads them goes down.\n\nThe gang answers to a thing they call the Foreman — a great iron construct they dragged up out of the rubble and patched back into motion, meaning to make it a guard. It is not a guard. Whatever old will sleeps in the broken stone bound inside it woke enough to take the gang in hand, and it has run them ever since, and run them well. The Foreman plans the ambushes, sets the watches, splits the takings, and holds a pack of squabbling cutthroats sharper and harder than they could ever manage on their own. They half-worship and half-fear it, and do not entirely grasp that the thing they think they own is the thing that owns them. It is huge, iron, and patient, and it fights like something that has done so for an age and forgotten how to lose.\n\nThe gang's holes and camps along the run are heaped with stolen hauls — coin, plate, arms and armor, salvage, raw stone and ore taken off the delvers they robbed. The Foreman is built of old iron and bears a soulstone in its chest, cracked and dimmed but still a thing of rare worth to those who know what it is.",
      "areas": {
        "The Cut": {
          "description": "The road narrows into a steep-walled cut through the cold grey rock, boulders and rockfall choking the verges, the way twisting so a traveler cannot see far ahead or behind. Ledges and clefts notch the walls above, set well for watching the road or dropping onto it. Stripped pack-gear and the wrecks of carts lie shoved into the rocks, picked clean. Wind funnels through the gap in a steady cold rush.",
          "paths": [
            "The Broken Ground"
          ]
        },
        "The Broken Ground": {
          "description": "Past the cut the land opens into a waste of tumbled stone and scrubby snow-pocked hollows, the road threading between knolls and rockpiles that break the sightlines at every turn. Cold campfire-scars and trampled ground mark where the gang has held up. Paths branch away into the rocks toward hidden camps. A ruined stone works squats off to one side — some old mountain holdfast or pump-house, long fallen, its black doorways gaping.",
          "paths": [
            "The Cut",
            "The Fallen Works"
          ]
        },
        "The Fallen Works": {
          "description": "The ruin of an old stone works set into the broken ground, its roof long gone and its walls cracked and soot-stained. Dead machinery rusts in the gloom inside — frozen gears, broken pipework, a silted pit in the floor. The gang's main camp sprawls among the wreckage: bedrolls, cookfires, and stolen goods stacked wherever there is room. A cleared space at the heart of it is swept and ordered against all the surrounding mess, ringed with the best-kept gear, a heavy seat of stacked iron facing the door.",
          "paths": [
            "The Broken Ground"
          ]
        }
      },
