    "Hodremur": {
      "name": "Hodremur",
      "x": -41,
      "y": 28,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whiteholds",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A high snowbound vale in the northern reach of the white peaks, where a war-band of white bearfolk has made its winter-camp. They came down out of the far north and took to raiding — striking the holds, the roads, and the camps of the lower mountains, carrying off plunder and beasts and people, and falling back into the high snow where the dwarves are loath to follow.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: the bearfolk of Hodremur default to hostile and raid the lower mountains for plunder and thralls. They are huge, white-furred, and built for the cold and the kill, and they fight as raiders — fast and savage, hitting hard and pulling back into the snow before a defense can form, or standing and fighting with terrible strength when cornered. They take captives to work the camp and beasts to feed it, and they are not minded to parley with the soft folk of the low holds, though a worthy enemy or a bold guest who proves their strength may earn a hearing where a weak one would only be killed.\n\nThese are renegades, not the whole of their kind. The bearfolk of the far north are a proud people who keep their own law and their own honor, and most would name this band oath-broken and shameful. Whatever drove them south — exile, hunger, a chief's ambition, a feud lost at home — they have set their old law aside and live now by the raid, taking from the weak what they will not work for. Their chief rules by strength and holds the band together by the spoils, and a richer raid is always wanted to keep the war-band fed and loyal.\n\nThe camp is heaped with raid-plunder — coin, arms and armor, furs and stores, fine goods carried up from the holds and roads. Captives are held here to be ransomed or worked, worth more returned alive to those who would pay for them. Beasts taken on the raids are penned among the tents.",
      "areas": {
        "The Snow Road": {
          "description": "A hard climb up into the high vale, the trail buried deep in snow and marked only by the passage of heavy feet and dragged sledges. The peaks crowd close and white on every side, and the wind drives loose snow in stinging sheets. Ahead the vale opens between the heights, and the smoke of fires rises against the cliffs. Trampled tracks and the ruts of laden sledges run up toward the camp.",
          "paths": [
            "The Winter-Camp"
          ]
        },
        "The Winter-Camp": {
          "description": "The war-band's camp, sprawled across the floor of the snowbound vale — great hide tents banked against the drifts, fires burning in pits dug into the snow, racks of drying meat and stacked plunder between them. Pens of lashed timber hold taken beasts at the camp's edge. The largest tent stands at the vale's head, broad and skin-walled and hung with trophies. The cliffs rise sheer and white around the whole of it, and a single buried trail climbs toward the high ground beyond.",
          "paths": [
            "The Snow Road",
            "The High Ground"
          ]
        },
        "The High Ground": {
          "description": "A windswept shelf above the camp, where the cliffs break into snow-choked rock and the whole vale lies open below. Lookout-cairns and the cold ash of watch-fires mark the heights. Drifts lie deep between the stones, and the way climbs on into the trackless white of the high peaks beyond, where the band falls back when the hunt turns against them. The wind never lets up here, and the cold is the killing kind.",
          "paths": [
            "The Winter-Camp"
          ]
        }
      },
