    "Clanhold Stonewall": {
      "name": "Clanhold Stonewall",
      "x": 29,
      "y": 26,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Highheath",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A great ring-fortress of grey mountain stone, seat of Clan Stonewall, built as walls within walls within walls. The Stonewall dwarves are shielddwarves — they fight in a locked shieldwall that does not break, and they hold that a held line beats a wild swing every time. They forge the finest armor and shields in the white peaks, drill the wall like it is the only thing worth doing, and boast that no enemy has ever broken into their hold.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Clan Stonewall are the shielddwarves, and their whole creed is three words: the line holds. They fight locked shield to shield, every dwarf covering the next, moving as one wall, and they believe — loudly, constantly, and with great satisfaction — that discipline beats fury and a wall that does not break beats a charge that does. The wall is half religion and half the best sport in the mountains, drilled in the yards with the cheerful ferocity of folk who are very good at a thing and know it, and their feast-halls are as loud as anyone's once the shields come off.\n\nThe clan's craft is protection. Stonewall armorers forge the finest plate and shields in the white peaks — heavy, beautiful, and proof against nearly anything — and a Stonewall shield is a thing a warrior keeps for life and hands down after. Their hold has never been broken into, and they will tell you so within the first breath of meeting you, and again shortly after.\n\nThe great rivalry is with Clan Stormhammer, and most of it is sport — four hundred years of rustled rams, sabotaged feasts, kill-counts kept on every joint hunt, and a grudge-roll of insults neither clan will let die. Stonewall thinks Stormhammer are reckless louts who mistake breaking things for skill, and says so at every chance, and is delighted when they take the bait. But one grudge is not sport. At Varric's Span, a generation back, a joint muster against a troll-horde broke: Stonewall formed the wall and held it, and Stormhammer charged ahead of the line and died on the bridge, cut off and overwhelmed. Stormhammer says the wall stood fast and watched their kin butchered. Stonewall holds that the charge broke discipline and doomed itself, and that a wall that breaks to save fools saves no one — and they do not joke about that day, because they lost kin watching it happen.\n\nThane Borin Stonewall holds the hold and the wall-creed, a broad old shielddwarf who has never lost a drill-match he cared to win and will cheerfully bury you in opinions about why the wall is superior to the hammer.",
      "areas": {
        "The Muster Yard": {
          "description": "The hold's great drill-yard and gathering-ground, ringed by the innermost wall, where the shieldwall is practiced with more noise and good humor than a battlefield ever sees — ranks locking and wheeling, shields crashing, a sergeant bellowing cheerful abuse at anyone out of step. Spectators line the wall-walks to watch and wager on the day's matches. The clan's armory-hall stands across the yard, its racks bright with shields and plate, and the doors of the Brimfull Boss stand wide at the yard's edge.",
          "paths": [
            "The Armory-Hall",
            "The Brimfull Boss",
            "The Ringwalls"
          ]
        },
        "The Brimfull Boss": {
          "description": "The clan's tavern, loud and warm and packed with off-duty warriors arguing the day's drill, named for the house custom: a dwarf who is toasted must drink from the hollow boss of an upturned shield, which holds a fine pool of ale and sloshes the lot over the inner rim and down the drinker's beard the moment it tilts. A battered drill-shield hangs behind the bar for exactly this purpose, and a soaked beard is the mark of an evening going well. Long tables fill the common room, the ale is strong, and a stranger who buys a round is half a friend by the second.",
          "paths": [
            "The Muster Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Armory-Hall": {
          "description": "The clan's great forge and armory, where Stonewall's famous plate and shields are made — anvils ranged down the hall, smiths working steel into heavy, beautiful armor, finished pieces gleaming on the racks. Shields of every weight hang the walls, from drill-shields scarred to splinters to masterwork pieces fit for a thane. Apprentices haul steel and run errands between the stations, and the masters who work here are glad to show off, glad to sell, and gladder still to tell you why Stonewall steel turns a blow no other will.",
          "paths": [
            "The Muster Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Ringwalls": {
          "description": "The hold's layered defenses, walls within walls climbing the mountainside, gate behind gate behind gate, with killing-grounds and stepped battlements between each ring. From the high walls the whole approach lies open, every road to the hold watched and walled, and dwarves on the wall-walks keep an easy eye on the country below. The stonework is old, fitted, and proud, carved here and there with the marks of musters that held the line. The innermost gate stands open in daylight onto the yard within.",
          "paths": [
            "The Muster Yard"
          ]
        }
      },
