    "The Wonderworks": {
      "name": "The Wonderworks",
      "x": -36,
      "y": 19,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Jade Tarn",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Wonderworks is the island of the College of Shapers, Tarnholme's artificers and enchanters, a steep heap of workshops, forge-galleries, bridges, and rebuilt stairs that changes every term. At its heart is the Piece Pit, a churning shaft of half-living machine parts, and the Claw, the brass arm that deals the day's builders whatever pieces they must make work. Students compete in daily build challenges while clever constructs clatter through the lanes on errands, tests, and mischief.",
      "hiddenInfo": "ACADEMY TONE. Narrate Tarnholme as a lively fantasy school of wizardry, not a modern scientific or technical institution. Use concrete, visual, character-centered magical language: wards flare, charms misbehave, old books answer, summoned beings bargain, and spells take strange shapes. Avoid modern scientific jargon, clinical diagnosis, measurements, technical-system explanations, and pseudo-scientific accounts of how magic works. Do not make Academy life uniformly solemn, dry, or over-serious; preserve wonder, rivalry, humor, danger, craft, and adventure even when the work matters.\n\nThe Shapers build the devices the rest of Tarnholme relies on: portal-rings, lamps, lifts, wards, tools, and enchanted machines. They are quick, cocky, competitive, and convinced every problem can be beaten by a better build.\n\nEach morning the masters post a challenge above the Piece Pit. The Claw deals parts from the heap, and students must solve the task with whatever they are given. Yesterday's constructs go back into the Pit by dawn; the point is speed, invention, and winning with a bad hand.\n\nThe contests are not duels. Constructs win by reaching goals, carrying prizes, or solving terrain. They may dismantle rivals only by immediately attaching the stolen part to themselves; loose theft is a foul, and every legal attack makes the attacker stranger. Sabotage is tolerated as long as it stays clever.\n\nA Shaper's standing is public and argued over constantly: impossible hands turned into victories, builds that made the island stop and watch, and challenge records that survive the season. A newcomer who solves a hopeless task rises fast and becomes tomorrow's favorite target.\n\nParts come in kinds: movers, grippers, eyes, cores, and oddments. A construct can only do what its parts allow, so the whole craft is making a strange hand of pieces solve a real problem.\n\nThe Pit's posts are men's work and they run the day: the deal-caller at the brass lectern who reads the morning challenge off the slate and rings the hand-bell, the pit-wardens who fish yesterday's broken builds out of the churn with long tongs, the forge-masters in the galleries above who set the task and judge the finish, and the wager-takers at the rail who chalk the odds and hold the coins. Shaper students are young men and women in roughly equal number.",
      "areas": {
        "The Ringyard": {
          "description": "The island's portal landing, a paved court at the water's edge where a fluted brass-and-stone ring-arch opens to the other islands. Crates of parts, abandoned frames, wet workbenches, and half-finished constructs clutter the court. A steep lane climbs into the workshops.",
          "paths": [
            "The Workshop Climb"
          ]
        },
        "The Workshop Climb": {
          "description": "A crooked climb of open-fronted workshops, forge-galleries, and tinker-lofts stacked up the slope, joined by stairs and plank-bridges that may not lead where they led last week. Tools and parts spill into the lanes, and half-built constructs wait in every bay.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ringyard",
            "The Piece Pit",
            "The Gallery"
          ]
        },
        "The Piece Pit": {
          "description": "The island's heart: a round shaft filled with a slow-churning heap of brass limbs, lenses, grasping arms, wheels, springs, and glowing cores. Builders work around the rim beneath the Claw's gantry, beside the slate board showing the day's challenge and standings.",
          "paths": [
            "The Workshop Climb",
            "The Gallery"
          ]
        },
        "The Gallery": {
          "description": "The Shapers' commons, a tiered hall of balconies built over the Pit, with long tables, deep chairs, and rails overlooking the work below. Walking trays, word-pour taps, brass messenger birds, and unreliable student gadgets serve the room.",
          "paths": [
            "The Workshop Climb",
            "The Piece Pit"
          ]
        }
      },
