    "The Main Island": {
      "name": "The Main Island",
      "x": -20,
      "y": -2,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Jade Tarn",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Main Island is the shared heart of Tarnholme Academy, the central isle where skiffs arrive from shore and ring-arches lead onward to the five College islands. Its white towers hold the Great Hall, the Practica board, the masters' offices, and the lodgings for newcomers who have not yet joined a College.",
      "hiddenInfo": "ACADEMY TONE. Narrate Tarnholme as a lively fantasy school of wizardry, not a modern scientific or technical institution. Use concrete, visual, character-centered magical language: wards flare, charms misbehave, old books answer, summoned beings bargain, and spells take strange shapes. Avoid modern scientific jargon, clinical diagnosis, measurements, technical-system explanations, and pseudo-scientific accounts of how magic works. Do not make Academy life uniformly solemn, dry, or over-serious; preserve wonder, rivalry, humor, danger, craft, and adventure even when the work matters.\n\nThe Main Island is neutral ground: no College owns it, and every College courts promising newcomers here. New students enter at First Circle, receive the small silver Circle pin, and may choose a College during that first stage without being forced into one. Sentinels teach wards and counter-magic; Shapers transformation and magical construction; Binders summoning, seals, and banishment; Seekers divination and magical investigation; Menders healing, restoration, and curse-breaking. College identity shapes mentors, Practica, training, facilities, and rewards without forbidding broader magic.\n\nThe Practica board in the Great Hall is the Academy's work engine. It posts missions across Jade Tarn and beyond: settle manastorms, investigate haunts, lift curses, identify strange magic, escort masters, or answer dangerous magical phenomena. First Circle students work one supervised Practicum to earn Second Circle. Second Circle students complete two recognized Practica with real field responsibility to earn Third. Third Circle students complete three difficult, substantially independent Practica to earn Upper Circle. Upper Circle students may propose or choose work, use restricted facilities under proper safeguards, represent Tarnholme independently, and mentor lower-Circle students.\n\nCircle recognition is formally granted at Tarnholme by authorized mentors, masters, or Practica officers; the Great Hall is the customary public place for it, but another Academy setting is valid. Advancement should bring concrete change: College-shaped instruction, useful magical equipment, facility access, independence, and eventually authority over junior Practica. The Masters' Wing handles hard assignments, restricted keys, portal access, and leave to descend at Undergate.\n\nOutsiders, visiting scholars, and travelers with Academy business lodge on the Main Island because they have no College of their own. The Gatehouse holds the permanent portal to the Watchtower in Ardan's Watch, the Academy's old road to the wider world.\n\nThe Main Island's offices are in men's hands: the Practica officers who post the board's work and sign a Circle off as earned, the hall-stewards who run the Great Hall and its meals and recognitions, the gate-wardens who keep the permanent portal to the Watchtower and check what comes through it, and the porters who haul newcomers' trunks up from the skiffs to the Newcomers' Hall. The newcomers themselves arrive as young men and women in roughly equal number.",
