            "The Tun and Tale"
          ]
        },
        "The Cellars": {
          "description": "The cool dark undercroft of the village, a warren of stone cellars and vaulted store-rooms dug into the slope behind the malt-houses, where the casks lie racked in their hundreds in the gloom. The air is cold and yeasty, the floors are damp, and the long rows of barrels run back into the dark further than a lamp will show.",
          "paths": [
            "The Green"
          ]
        },
        "The Tun and Tale": {
          "description": "The village alehouse, a low warm timber house facing the green where the brewers drink their own work of an evening. The taps run a dozen brews, the settles are worn smooth, and the talk is all of malt and weather and whose batch came out best this season. Casks line one wall, and a hatch at the back lets down into the cellars.",
          "paths": [
