    "Suleyvan's Folly": {
      "name": "Suleyvan's Folly",
      "x": 29,
      "y": -23,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Redrock",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A vast palace-city half-buried in the sand of a low canyon, beautiful even in ruin — toppled statues, drifted courtyards, columned halls half-swallowed by sand. This was the house of Suleyvan the Sealer, the old master-binder who kept the dangerous spirits of an age sealed in vessels beneath his own roof. The locks held while he lived, but a catastrophe befell the palace after his death, and it has lain abandoned ever since. Even after all these years, many of the old vessels are still here — lamps, rings, jars, bottles by the hundred — and a bold hand can still carry out a fortune.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Suleyvan's Folly is full of bound spirits, sealed in the vessels and still here. The seals are old and failing. Open a vessel, break one, or disturb one too far gone, and the spirit inside comes out — and a freed spirit attacks: a loosed djinn, ifrit, or shaitan that has spent an age in the dark fights the one who freed it. The Folly is dangerous to walk; vessels are everywhere, and a binding can fail on its own.\n\nFreed spirits fight to type. A djinn is wind and force: it hurls a foe across the hall, throws loose stone and brass, and stays in the air out of reach. An ifrit is fire: it burns, throws flame, and sets the room alight, and it kills without speaking. A shaitan is guile: it lies, wears a borrowed face, turns a person's own fears and words against them, and fights dirty.\n\nSome few spirits will deal instead of kill, and these are worth seeking on purpose: an ifrit will swear a single binding favor to whoever frees it and is held to its word; a marid, the rarest sealed here, knows true answers and will trade one for its freedom; a djinn pressed in the dazed moment can be bound into service rather than fought. A shaitan offers bargains too, and a shaitan's bargain is always a trap. Free a spirit blind and it fights; corner the right kind and force the right terms, and it serves.\n\nThe loot is the vessels and what the spirits leave. A sealed vessel — a lamp, ring, jar, or bottle with a spirit still bound inside — is the prize: carried out intact it sells for a fortune to the right buyer, or it can be broken to loose what is in it. A slain ifrit leaves emberglass and fire-cinder, fire-hot materials for a forge or a flame-weapon; a slain djinn leaves stormglass, a wind-charged crystal; a shaitan leaves nothing but the brass it was bound in. Suleyvan's own sealing-gear lies throughout the halls — empty warded bottles, sealing-rings, and binding-chains that a trained hand can use to catch and hold a spirit instead of fighting it. Brass relics, old coin, and jeweled settings from a master's house lie scattered everywhere, thickest and best-sealed in the vault wing and the sanctum.",
      "areas": {
        "The Drowned Gate": {
          "description": "The entrance to the palace-city, a colossal brass gateway toppled and half-swallowed by a dune that pours through the gap and out across the threshold. Beyond it the ruin opens wide — broken towers, sand-filled courts, and columned roofs sunk to their middles in drift, running back toward the canyon wall. Sealing-marks cover the standing stone of the gate.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of a Thousand Seals",
            "The Dune Courts"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of a Thousand Seals": {
          "description": "A great columned audience-hall, its roof open to the sky where beams have fallen, sand banked high against the bases of the pillars. A brass throne stands on a stepped dais at the far end. Alcoves line the walls.",
          "paths": [
            "The Drowned Gate",
            "The Dune Courts",
            "The Vault Wing"
          ]
        },
        "The Dune Courts": {
          "description": "A run of open courtyards between the palace wings, each sunk into a bowl of sand, with the dry stone channels and empty basins of old water-gardens crossing between them. Toppled statuary and the tops of buried walls break the dunes. Doorways open off the courts into the deeper halls.",
          "paths": [
            "The Drowned Gate",
            "The Hall of a Thousand Seals",
            "The Vault Wing",
            "Suleyvan's Sanctum"
          ]
        },
        "The Vault Wing": {
          "description": "A wing of treasury-rooms and store-chambers running deep under the palace, the air close and hot, the floors crowded with sealed vessels and shelved with the brass and goods of a master's house. Sand has forced through cracks into the outer rooms; the inner ones stand dry and dark behind heavy doors carved over with locks.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of a Thousand Seals",
            "The Dune Courts",
            "Suleyvan's Sanctum"
          ]
        },
        "Suleyvan's Sanctum": {
          "description": "The deepest and hottest chamber of the Folly, the master's own workroom. Work-tables, racks, and sealed vessels stand where they were left.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dune Courts",
            "The Vault Wing"
          ]
        }
      },
