    "The Flamebleed": {
      "name": "The Flamebleed",
      "x": 6,
      "y": -20,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "Redrock",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A canyon where fire bleeds up out of the ground. The red rock is split open and burning from within, flame welling from the cracks, and up through the same cracks crawl fire-demons — small, fierce, and many — out of the dark below. A fire-demon is made of living flame, and a slain one can be cut for its burning heart, the prize of any weapon-smith who wants to forge a blade that never goes cold. The canyon has killed treasure-hunters and plunderers for an age, and what they carried is still down there in the ash, for anyone who can take it off the demons that took it first.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: the Flamebleed is hostile and nothing in it will parley. Fire-demons climb up out of the burning seams — quick and fierce, throwing fire from range and rushing in to burn what they reach, bursting back to ash when killed. Fire-imps come in swarms, each weak but many together, and scatter when their nerve breaks. Burned beasts den among the seams too — badland jackals and lean drakes warped by long years in the heat, ember-veined and cracked, that shrug off fire and fight like cornered animals.\n\nThe open fire is its own danger. Seams gout without warning, the glassed ground breaks over pockets of heat, and a fall into a burning crack kills on its own.\n\nA slain fire-demon's heart is a coal of living flame that never cools, prized by a weapon-smith or enchanter for a fire-weapon. The burned beasts yield ember-veined hide and scale that turn fire. Old coin, blades, and gear lie in the ash where the dead were stripped, thickest along the deeper seams.\n\nThere is a greater prize than a dead demon: a live one. The Desert Rose hunters do not kill what they catch — they seal the demon whole into a warded vessel, and a bottled fire-demon is worth a fortune to them and to others who deal in such things. With a warded bottle and a sealing-ring, in the dazed breath after a demon surfaces from a seam, one can be caught and corked alive instead of killed. Some buyers want it locked safely away. Some want it for worse.",
      "areas": {
        "The Mouth of the Bleed": {
          "description": "The open end of the canyon, where the red rock first cracks and the ground begins to smoke. Thin seams of fire thread the walls, faint here and brighter ahead, and the stone is scorched black in patches. The air shimmers down the length of the gorge, and the way runs deeper between steepening, burning walls.",
          "paths": [
            "The Glassways"
          ]
        },
        "The Glassways": {
          "description": "The middle of the canyon, where the walls and floor are burned to black glass, smooth and sharp and glinting with the firelight welling up through them. Wide seams of open flame split the ground, and the rock between them is cracked and uncertain. The gorge narrows and darkens ahead, the glow growing stronger.",
          "paths": [
            "The Mouth of the Bleed",
            "The Quick"
          ]
        },
        "The Quick": {
          "description": "The deepest reach of the canyon, where the seams run together into broad pools and falls of open fire and the heat is fiercest. The black-glass walls glow from within, lit red-gold by the flame beneath them. A narrow, broken path threads between the burning, the rock fractured and bleeding fire on every side.",
          "paths": [
            "The Glassways"
          ]
        }
      },
