    "Redgate Caravanserai": {
      "name": "Redgate Caravanserai",
      "x": 1,
      "y": 4,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Redrock",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A ruined waystation on the canyon road, a square fort of red mudbrick built long ago to shelter caravans for the night — walls, a gate, a courtyard, and stabling, half-fallen now and scoured with sand. Its place on the road makes it a prize for raiders: gnoll bands hold it again and again, denning behind its old walls to fall on the wagons that still must pass this way. A band in the caravanserai means plunder heaped in the courtyard, beasts chained in the stalls, and captives taken off the road penned in the cellars below.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: when a gnoll band holds Redgate it is hostile, and the raiders attack any stranger on sight — there is no toll and no parley here; this is a raider den, not a place that deals. The gnolls fight as a pack: they swarm a target together, the strongest forward and the rest harrying the flanks, and they break and run for the walls or the cellars when their leader falls or their numbers are badly cut. They keep beasts on chains — hyenas and worse — loosed to run down anyone who flees, and a few raiders hold the gate-towers with bows.\n\nCaptives taken off the road are held alive in the cellars for sale, and freeing them is the reason most come to Redgate. The courtyard and the raiders' quarters hold the take of raided caravans — coin, trade-goods, weapons, and gear stripped from dead guards, the better pieces kept by whoever leads the band. The chained beasts can be loosed against their own keepers by a quick hand.",
      "areas": {
        "The Broken Gate": {
          "description": "The road runs straight up to the caravanserai's only entrance, a high mudbrick gateway with one leaf of its great doors fallen and the other hanging. Flanking towers of crumbling brick rise on either side, with a clear line down the road in both directions and up at the walls. Sand has drifted against the base of the walls and through the gap.",
          "paths": [
            "The Courtyard"
          ]
        },
        "The Courtyard": {
          "description": "The open square within the walls, ringed by the collapsed arcades and stalls where caravans once unloaded. A well stands at the center, and broken wagons and the litter of long use clutter the ground. Low doorways open off the yard into the stabling and the ruined lodging-rooms, and a stair at the back corner drops into the dark below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Broken Gate",
            "The Stables",
            "The Cellars"
          ]
        },
        "The Stables": {
          "description": "A long open-fronted range along one wall where the caravans once kept their animals, the stalls now fouled and broken down. Chains and iron posts line the walls. The roof has fallen in along part of its length, letting in bars of light, and a gap in the back wall opens to the canyon outside.",
          "paths": [
            "The Courtyard"
          ]
        },
        "The Cellars": {
          "description": "The vaulted brick undercroft beneath the lodging-rooms, dug to keep stores cool and since partitioned with bars and rough gates into pens. The air is close and the only light comes down the stair from the courtyard. Cramped passages run between the cells, deeper under the fort than the floor above would suggest.",
          "paths": [
            "The Courtyard"
          ]
        }
      },
