    "Saffra": {
      "name": "Saffra",
      "x": -16,
      "y": 13,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Redrock",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A djinnborn town built into a walled box canyon, sheer red cliffs on three sides and one way in at the mouth. Inside, the canyon floor and its terraced walls are crowded with forges, market-lanes, and caravan-yards. The djinnborn here are the finest fire-smiths in the badlands, working brass and metal into blades that hold flame, and they deal openly in the relics that come up out of the ruined city nearby.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Saffra is a safe, friendly town and a welcome stop in hard country — the warm social ground of the canyons and the last easy place before the deep badlands. It is djinnborn through and through: fire-eyed folk, proud and theatrical, generous to a guest who treats them well and sharp with one who does not. Outsiders of every kind pass through to trade, hire, and outfit, and are made welcome.\n\nThe djinnborn of Saffra are the descendants of the nobles who once ruled the ruined city nearby, before it burned. They hold this canyon because the country is theirs by old right, and they have no love at all for the gnoll princes squatting in their ancestors' halls. They are far too few to drive the gnolls out and know it, so the grudge stays a grudge: they trade with the gnolls when they must, despise them always, and would gladly see them gone if someone else did the work.\n\nThe forges are Saffra's wonder and the root of its craft. They burn with a strange blue-white flame, hotter and cleaner than any ordinary fire, fed by small fire-spirits the djinnborn bind into the coals — little living flames a careful eye can see moving in the heat, kept and worked, not tormented. With them the smiths forge blades and gear that hold fire, and they will work the raw fire-materials a hand brings in — a fire-demon's everlasting heart-coal and the like — into finished weapons for the right price.\n\nThe djinnborn know old djinnborn work better than anyone alive, and the relic-dealers of the bazaar buy, sell, and appraise what comes up out of the ruins honestly, telling true relics from gnoll-fenced junk. The caravan-yards outfit and launch the trade across the badlands: mounts, water, supply, guides who know the roads, and guards for hire.",
      "areas": {
        "The Bazaar": {
          "description": "The crowded market filling the floor of the canyon, a sprawl of stalls and awnings strung between the standing rock and the terraced buildings climbing the walls. Goods of every kind are laid out here — metalwork, relics, fire-cured spice and incense, food and cloth — and lanes wind off between the buildings and up the terraces. The red cliffs rise close on three sides, and the way out to the canyon mouth lies at one end.",
          "paths": [
            "The Forges",
            "The Caravan Yards",
            "Fountain Court Inn"
          ]
        },
        "The Forges": {
          "description": "The smithies worked into the lower terraces of the canyon wall, their open fronts glowing with an odd blue-white light that does not look like ordinary fire. The flame in the hearths burns strange and bright, and the air above the terrace shimmers with heat. Finished metalwork and brass hang on display along the fronts, and stepped lanes connect the forges one to the next.",
          "paths": [
            "The Bazaar"
          ]
        },
        "The Caravan Yards": {
