    "Citadel of the Pact": {
      "name": "Citadel of the Pact",
      "x": -5,
      "y": 26,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Redrock",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A fortress-monastery of rose-pink stone, raised on a high crag of the same rock above the red canyons. The stone is desert-rose, which the dark cannot well up through, and the crag is the largest outcrop of it in the land — so the citadel is the one safe ground in a country that bleeds demons, and the demon-hunters of the Desert Rose have made it their home. Brass domes and arches rise warm and rosy over courts and workshops, and at its sealed heart the Order keeps the Gate of Gaol, through which the demons they catch are cast out of the world for good.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Citadel of the Pact is a safe, welcoming place and the home of the demon-hunter in the Redrock. The Order of the Desert Rose holds it — a sworn order, open to any who would learn the work, that takes recruits, trains them, and sends them out under writ against the demon-haunted places of the land. A newcomer who proves willing is taken in and taught; one who proves able rises to ride out as a sworn hunter of the Rose. The Order welcomes outsiders, sells its lore and its craft, and asks only that its work and its Gate be respected.\n\nThe Order's way is neither to kill demons nor to keep them. A demon cannot truly be killed — cut down, it gathers itself again in time — and a demon kept is a demon that will one day get loose. So the Rose bind what they hunt, sealing it whole into a warded vessel, and carry it back here to be cast through the Gate of Gaol and gone for good. This is what it means to keep the Pact: not to slay the dark, but to put it back where it cannot return from. The Order will take in a bound demon a hunter brings and see it banished, and a sealed vessel is worth a great deal to them.\n\nThe Gate of Gaol is a great arch the Order made and keeps, standing in a locked and guarded vault at the citadel's heart. It opens on an abyss — a prison from which nothing comes back — and anything at all that passes through the arch is banished the same as any demon, living or dead, willing or not. For that reason it is sealed away and opened only for the rite, never left for anyone to wander into.\n\nThe demon-hunt is dangerous work and the Order is always short of hands. It sends its hunters across the whole region: into the dead town where the soulless walk, down into the burning canyon where fire-demons crawl up from below, and against any place where the dark breaks through. The Order also knows that the worst wound in the land lies beneath the ruined city the gnolls hold, and watches it with dread. The workshops here make and sell the tools of the work — warded vessels to catch a demon in, sealing-rings, and brass gear — and the masters will teach the binding-craft to those who earn it.",
      "areas": {
        "The Rose Court": {
          "description": "The great open court at the citadel's entrance, floored and walled in warm rose-pink stone, ringed with brass-domed colonnades that throw bands of shade across the ground. A fountain plays at the center, and from the stone of the court itself grow clusters of pale rose-crystal, the desert-rose that gives the place its name and its warding. The court is wide and welcoming, with arched ways leading deeper into the fortress and a long view back over the red canyons far below the crag.",
          "paths": [
            "The Chapter Hall",
            "The Workshops",
            "The Training Yard"
          ]
        },
        "The Chapter Hall": {
          "description": "The Order's great hall, a high rose-stone chamber under a brass dome, hung with the banners and tokens of the Desert Rose and lined with long tables. Here the Order gathers, takes in its own, and gives out its writs. Doorways open from it to the inner fortress, and a guarded passage leads down toward the sealed heart of the citadel.",
          "paths": [
            "The Rose Court",
            "The Vault of Gaol"
          ]
        },
        "The Workshops": {
          "description": "A long brass-roofed hall of workbenches, forges, and crafting-stations where the Order makes the tools of its trade. Warded brass vessels in every size stand on the racks, alongside sealing-rings, chains, and half-finished gear, and the walls are hung with the patterns and diagrams of the binding-craft. Apprentices work the benches beside the masters here.",
          "paths": [
            "The Rose Court"
          ]
        },
        "The Training Yard": {
          "description": "An open rose-stone yard within the walls, set about with marked circles, posts, and warded pens. The ground is scuffed and scorched in places from hard use. Racks of practice-gear and warded vessels stand along one side, and the yard looks out past the parapet to the drop below the crag.",
          "paths": [
            "The Rose Court"
          ]
        },
        "The Vault of Gaol": {
          "description": "A sealed chamber deep in the rose-stone at the citadel's heart, behind locked and guarded brass doors. Within stands the Gate of Gaol: a great ornamental arch of brass and rose-stone, beautiful and intricate, framing a darkness that is not the wall behind it but somewhere else entirely. The chamber is bare otherwise, kept empty and shut, the only way in through the hall above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Chapter Hall"
          ]
        }
      },
