    "Tomb Crags": {
      "name": "Tomb Crags",
      "x": 19,
      "y": -30,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Dunelands",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Rock crags rise from a sand-sea in the open desert, the only high ground for miles. The sand between them is sand-wyrm country: the great worms feel movement through it and come up under anything that crosses. A Sun-King army was broken here in the old age, and the dead still lie on the crags where they fled the worms. Their sun-gold blades and regalia rest among the bones on the high rock. Most reachable crags have been picked over; some have not. Raiders camp on the rises to dig for the gold that is left and to rob whoever else comes for it. The old songs say the Sun-Kings once drove the worms themselves, and no one alive knows how.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The raiders here default to hostile. They are a crew of Khenret's Company working the crags, and they treat every other person in the sand as competition to rob or kill. They may parley if badly outnumbered or offered a cut worth more than a corpse. The sand-wyrms are not hostile in the social sense; they are animals that hunt vibration, and they take anything that moves across open sand.\n\nThe crags are the safe ground and the sand is the killing-floor. The wyrms cannot reach onto the high rock, so everything that works here clings to the crags and crosses the sand only when it must. The crew holds the largest central crag as a camp and ranges out to the others. A fight that spills off the rock and onto the sand ends when the ground opens.\n\nSun-gold lies thickest on the crags farthest out, where the army climbed highest and the dead have not been stripped. The near crags are picked clean. Reaching the far rock means crossing more open sand, which is the trade the place makes: the richer the crag, the longer the run to it.\n\nLoot is found on the bodies and in the old dig-sites among the bones. Sun-gold blade: radiant, bites undead, demons, and shadow-things hardest. Sun-gold regalia: radiant war-ornament of a Sun-King soldier. Wyrm tooth: a cast tooth pulled from the sand, large enough to be worked into a blade-core.",
      "areas": {
        "The Sand-Sea": {
          "description": "An open plain of dunes with the crags standing out of it in the distance, dark rock against pale sand. The footing is loose and shifting, every step sinking and dragging, with no cover and no high ground until the rock. Old tracks and the bleached timber of broken wagons surface here and there where the dunes have shifted, then vanish under the next drift.",
          "paths": [
            "The Near Crags"
          ]
        },
        "The Near Crags": {
          "description": "Low rock rises breaking out of the sand, close enough to the plain's edge to reach without a long crossing. The stone is sun-cracked and scattered with bones and rusted iron, and the ground between the bones is dug over and turned, pocked with old holes where the dead were stripped. From the height the dune-sea spreads on all sides, the far crags standing thin and small against the horizon.",
          "paths": [
            "The Sand-Sea",
            "The Far Crags"
          ]
        },
        "The Far Crags": {
          "description": "Tall rock standing alone far out in the sand-sea, reached only across open dune. The crags here rise steep and high, and the bones lie thick on the upper ledges where men climbed as far as the stone went. Sun-gold catches the light among them, blades and ornament still on the dead, the rock here unturned and undug.",
          "paths": [
            "The Sand-Sea"
          ]
        }
      },
