    "The Mirror-Waste": {
      "name": "The Mirror-Waste",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 43,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Dunelands",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A crater of black glass miles wide, where sky-citadels clashed and fell in the old age, fusing the desert to glass in the impact. The ground is jagged and mirror-bright, spires and sheets of it throwing back the sun and every reflection until a traveler cannot tell a real shape from its image or judge any distance. Great broken pieces of the fallen citadels lie half-sunk in the glass, some whole enough to enter. The citadels' guardians fell with them and still walk the wreck: mirror-bright metal soldiers, near-invisible against the glass until they move. Treasure-hunters come for the sky-empire's make embedded in the crater, and the glass and its guardians take a share of them.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The citadel guardians attack anyone who enters the wreck. They are constructs with no minds to reason with and no reason to spare anyone; they default to destroying intruders and do not stop, parley, or tire. The glass itself is a standing hazard apart from them: its edges cut, its glare blinds at midday, and its reflections hide what is coming.\n\nThe guardians are the sky-citadels' war-automata, mirror-bright metal polished to throw back the glass around them, so they stand unseen among the spires until they move. They hold to the citadel-wreck they fell with and patrol the embedded pieces, thickest around the largest fallen hull. A few fire-things still haunt the crater's hottest stretches, loosed when the djinn-engine that powered the citadels burst and made the glass: salamanders and lesser fire-spirits that never left the heat.\n\nThe loot is the sky-empire's make, embedded in the wreck and carried in the broken hulls. Citadel-shard: a piece of empyrean make worked into brass and sun-bright metal. Guardian-core: the power-stone drawn from a fallen automaton. The constructs are unmade by shock, and their brass eaten by acid; the fire-things take frost.",
      "areas": {
        "The Glass Flats": {
          "description": "The open floor of the crater, broad sheets of black glass flowed smooth and frozen, mirror-bright and blinding under the midday sun. The flats run level for a long way before the ground breaks into spires ahead, and the dark shapes of fallen citadel-wreck stand half-sunk in the glass on the far side. There is no shade and no cover, and the heat off the glass is worst where the surface runs newest and clearest near the crater's heart.",
          "paths": [
            "The Spires"
          ]
        },
        "The Spires": {
          "description": "A field of shattered glass risen in jagged spires and leaning sheets, close-packed and taller than a man, throwing back the light and every reflection from a hundred angles. There is no true line of sight here; the same shape repeats across a dozen surfaces, and distance cannot be judged among the mirrors. Narrow lanes of broken glass wind between the spires toward the wreck beyond.",
          "paths": [
            "The Glass Flats",
            "The Fallen Hull"
          ]
        },
        "The Fallen Hull": {
          "description": "A great broken section of a sky-citadel half-buried in the glass, large enough to walk into, its canted brass corridors and shattered chambers tilted where it struck. Sun-bright metal and empyrean make stud the walls and lie loose in the broken rooms, much of it fused into the glass that flooded in. The passages run deep into the hull, dim and angled, with glare from the crater outside cutting through every break in the metal.",
          "paths": [
            "The Spires"
          ]
        }
      },
