    "Widow's Way": {
      "name": "Widow's Way",
      "x": -23,
      "y": 23,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Dunelands",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The only road through this stretch of open desert, a hard track of sand and broken stone that caravans must take because there is no other way across. Bandits and gnoll packs hunt it, and the burned wrecks of the caravans that did not make it lie strung along its length, their cargo and strongboxes spilled and half-buried in the sand. Travelers call it Widow's Way and cross it anyway, because crossing it is the only way through. The wrecks are picked at by every raider on the road and never quite emptied.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The bandits and the gnoll packs on this road default to hostile and treat travelers as prey and plunder. The bandits may parley if outmatched or paid; the gnolls hunt and do not. Both fall on anyone crossing the road, and on each other when there is no easier kill.\n\nTwo kinds of raider work Widow's Way. Human bandit crews hold the higher ground and the chokes, robbing what crosses and killing what resists. Gnoll packs range the open road and run with giant hyenas, hunting in numbers and dragging off the living along with the dead. The two sides raid the same caravans and fight over the spoils as often as they share the road.\n\nThe loot is what the failed crossings left behind, scattered through the wrecks and buried where wagons fell: trade-cargo, coin, strongboxes, and the goods travelers carried. The wrecks are stripped over and over and never bare, because more caravans keep trying the road. Most of it is ordinary plunder; the rare good piece turns up in a strongbox no raider got open.",
      "areas": {
        "The Open Track": {
          "description": "A long stretch of road running straight across flat open desert, sand drifted over broken paving, with no cover to either side for as far as the eye reaches. Burned wagons and scattered cargo lie along the verges and out in the sand where they were dragged, half-buried and bleached. The ground is hard enough to march and exposed enough that anything on the road is seen from a long way off.",
          "paths": [
            "The Narrows"
          ]
        },
        "The Narrows": {
          "description": "Where the road threads between low rock outcrops and a cut bank, the open desert pinching to a single hard track with high ground close on both sides. Wrecked wagons stand thick here, jammed and overturned where crossings were caught in the choke, their cargo spilled across the road and into the rocks. The high ground overlooks the whole length of the pass.",
          "paths": [
            "The Open Track",
            "The Hollow"
          ]
        },
        "The Hollow": {
          "description": "A sheltered hollow off the road, walled on three sides by rock and screened from the track by a spur of stone. The ground is trodden flat and ringed with old fire-pits and the rotted timber of broken-up wagons, and looted cargo lies stacked and half-sorted against the rock walls. One narrow mouth lets onto the road; tracks run from it down to the track and away into the open sand.",
          "paths": [
            "The Narrows"
          ]
        }
