    "Tomb of the Drowned King": {
      "name": "Tomb of the Drowned King",
      "x": 33,
      "y": -17,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Dunelands",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A pyramid-tomb of the Sun Kings that sank into a buried spring and flooded, its lower halls drowned under cold dark water. Raiders work it half-submerged, wading and swimming through the sunken passages for the grave-goods that lie in the silt and the sun-gold gone green on the dead. The deepest chambers, where the king was laid, are wholly underwater.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The dead here default to hostile and attack anything that enters the flooded halls. They do not parley, tire, or stop. The water is a standing hazard apart from them, dragging at armor and gear and offering no firm footing in the deep chambers.\n\nThe tomb was a Sun-King's, drowned when the ground gave under it, and its honor-guard drowned with it. Water-logged dead crowd the sunken halls, grasping up from below and from the silt, slow on land and quick in the water. Mummified crocodiles, embalmed as the king's tomb-guardians, hunt the flooded passages and strike from beneath the surface. Eels and serpents nest in the drowned rooms. The deepest threats keep to the burial chamber at the bottom, where the water is blackest.\n\nThe loot lies in the silt and on the drowned dead, richest in the lowest flooded chambers. Sun-gold blade: radiant, bites undead, demons, and shadow-things hardest, gone green under the water. Sun-gold regalia: radiant war-ornament of a Sun-King, sunk in the silt. Drowned dead and mummified flesh take fire poorly while wet; the dry upper passages are another matter.",
      "areas": {
        "The Tilted Entrance": {
          "description": "The pyramid's mouth, canted where the ground sank beneath it, half its steps run down into standing water. The upper passages are dry and close, sloping steadily downward until the floor disappears under a black waterline. Old rope and the rotted boats of earlier raiders lie at the water's edge, and the air below is cold and still.",
          "paths": [
            "The Flooded Halls"
          ]
        },
        "The Flooded Halls": {
          "description": "Drowned corridors and chambers half-full of cold dark water, the carved walls running down below the surface into the dark. The water is waist-deep to overhead by turns, with no firm footing and no clear sight beneath it. Sunken grave-goods and the litter of the drowned settle in the silt, and broken galleries open off in every direction.",
          "paths": [
            "The Tilted Entrance",
            "The Sunken Vault"
          ]
        },
        "The Sunken Vault": {
          "description": "The burial chamber at the bottom of the tomb, wholly underwater, a great drowned hall of carved stone vanishing into black water. The king's sarcophagus and the richest of the grave-goods lie below the surface in the silt and the dark. The Crown of the Drowned King may remain among them unless it has already been removed. The water here is coldest and deepest, and no light reaches the floor.",
          "paths": [
            "The Flooded Halls"
          ]
        }
