    "Tomb of the Risen Host": {
      "name": "Tomb of the Risen Host",
      "x": 25,
      "y": -14,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Dunelands",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A pyramid-tomb of the Sun Kings where a king was buried with his army, ranks of his soldiers laid down in formation to rise and guard him. The wrapped dead still stand in their ranks through the halls, armored and ordered, and they do not lie quiet. At the heart lie the king and his winged honor-guard, and the richest war-gear in the necropolis lies with them.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The dead here default to hostile and attack anyone who enters. They do not parley or tire. They fight as soldiers, in ranks and with discipline, and the danger is the order and weight of them rather than sheer numbers; a careful crew can draw the ranks out, fight through a hall, and work toward the center, but the host holds its ground and does not break.\n\nThe tomb was a Sun-King's war-barrow, his soldiers entombed in formation to rise as his guard. Mummified soldiers fill the halls in ordered ranks, wrapped and armored, fighting with shield and spear and holding their lines as they were drilled to. Deeper in stand the heavy dead, the king's chosen, and at the center his honor-guard: mummified empyreans, winged and outsized, the strongest and slowest to fall in the tomb. The ranks are thickest around the king's bier and lighter toward the entrance.\n\nThe loot is the army's war-gear, richest at the center where the king and his guard lie. Sun-gold blade: radiant, bites undead, demons, and shadow-things hardest. Sun-gold war-regalia: the armored ornament of a Sun-King's soldier or his winged guard. The dead are dry and take fire badly, and the armored ranks are broken open by heavy impact.",
      "areas": {
        "The War-Gate": {
          "description": "The tomb's entrance hall, a broad martial approach lined with carved soldiers and the standards of the old empire cut into the stone. Wrapped figures stand in still ranks along the walls, armored and ordered, spears grounded. The hall runs straight and wide inward, opening toward the ranked halls beyond.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Ranks"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Ranks": {
          "description": "A great pillared hall where the dead host stands in formation, rank behind rank of wrapped and armored soldiers filling the floor in ordered lines. The pillars break the hall into lanes, and old weapons and fallen standards lie among the ranks. The formation runs deeper and heavier toward the chambers at the back.",
          "paths": [
            "The War-Gate",
            "The King's Array"
          ]
        },
        "The King's Array": {
          "description": "The burial chamber at the tomb's heart, where the king's bier stands ringed by the heaviest of his dead. Great winged figures stand guard close around the bier, taller than the ranks behind them and richly armored, and the finest war-gear and sun-gold of the tomb lie heaped about the dais. The chamber is high and pillared, the array drawn up tight around the king.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Ranks"
          ]
        }
