    "Tomb of the Beast-King": {
      "name": "Tomb of the Beast-King",
      "x": 38,
      "y": -9,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Dunelands",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A pyramid-tomb of the Sun Kings where a king was buried with his menagerie, his hunting-beasts and sacred animals embalmed to rise and guard him. The wrapped beasts still prowl the halls: great cats, hawks, crocodiles, and serpents, and worse things in the depths. They strike from the dark and the high places, fast and varied, and no two halls are guarded the same way. The king's sun-gold and the gold of his beasts lie deep in the tomb, behind everything that hunts there.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The beasts here default to hostile and attack anything that enters. They do not parley or tire, and they hunt as the animals they were, by ambush, by speed, and from above and below; the danger is being caught off guard by varied attacks rather than worn down by numbers.\n\nThe tomb was a Sun-King's, and his hunting-beasts and sacred animals were embalmed and laid in to rise with him. Mummified great cats stalk the halls and spring from cover. Wrapped hawks and vultures roost in the high dark and stoop on intruders. Embalmed crocodiles lie in the old water-channels and the deeper pools. Bound serpents nest in the niches and the rubble. In the depths stand the heavy beasts, larger things the king kept and hunted, the slowest to fall. The beasts range the whole tomb, thickest around the king's chamber.\n\nThe loot is the king's sun-gold and the gold-worked harness and ornament of his beasts, richest in the deepest halls. Sun-gold blade: radiant, bites undead, demons, and shadow-things hardest. Sun-gold beast-harness: the gilded collar or trapping of an embalmed beast, worked in radiant metal. The beasts are dry and take fire badly.",
      "areas": {
        "The Hunt-Gate": {
          "description": "The tomb's entrance hall, its walls carved with the king at the hunt, lions and hawks and great serpents cut into the stone in long friezes. Wrapped animal shapes lie still in the wall-niches and along the floor, bound and gilded. The hall runs inward past pillars and old dry channels cut into the floor, opening toward the halls beyond.",
          "paths": [
            "The Beast-Halls"
          ]
        },
        "The Beast-Halls": {
          "description": "A run of high pillared chambers broken by dry water-channels, pits, and ledges, the kind of ground the king's beasts were kept and shown in. Cover stands everywhere: pillars, fallen stone, the dark mouths of the channels, and ledges high in the walls above the light. Wrapped beasts lie among the rubble and in the niches, and the halls run on deeper into the dark.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hunt-Gate",
            "The King's Den"
          ]
        },
        "The King's Den": {
          "description": "The burial chamber at the heart of the tomb, a great vaulted hall set like a beast's lair, with pits and channels and high stone ledges ringing the king's bier. The largest of the embalmed beasts were laid here close around their king, and the richest of the sun-gold and the gilded beast-harness lie heaped about the dais. The hall is dim and broken-ground, with cover and high places on every side.",
          "paths": [
            "The Beast-Halls"
          ]
        }
      },
