    "Tombs of the Sun Kings": {
      "name": "Tombs of the Sun Kings",
      "x": 28,
      "y": -9,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Dunelands",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A necropolis of the old desert empire, where great pyramids stand arrayed across the badland flats, raised over the dead god-kings called the Sun Kings. The pyramids are heaped with the kings' sun-gold and grave-treasure and guarded by traps, wards, and the dead, and the desert around them is the staging-ground of the tomb-raiding trade: crews camp on the flats, outfit, and go in for fortune.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The pyramids themselves default to deadly, each guarded by its own dead and wards, and the raider company that holds the First Pyramid attacks rivals on its ground.\n\nThe Sun Kings were the god-kings of the old empire, entombed here with their wealth, their households, their armies, and their beasts, each under its own pyramid. The dead do not rest, and the deeper a tomb is worked the worse its guardians. Many pyramids are scattered across the flats, each a separate grave with its own dead and its own way of killing; the worst of them are sealed and have never been opened.\n\nThe First Pyramid is held by Khenret's Company, a raider crew under the jackalkin Khenret, who took the smallest and most-worked tomb as a base and runs digs from it. They rob what crosses their ground and fight other crews for the richest tombs. The Third Pyramid was broken open and is being dug by the New Sun, the cult that means to wake the Sun Kings; their work in the depths is what has stirred the dead across the whole necropolis worse than before.\n\nThe loot is the kings' sun-gold and the grave-treasure of the tombs, richest in the deepest and least-worked graves. Sun-gold blade: radiant, bites undead, demons, and shadow-things hardest. Sun-gold regalia and grave-gold throughout. The near and most-worked tombs are picked over; the wealth is in the ones still guarded.",
      "areas": {
        "The Plaza of Kings": {
          "description": "The vast flat at the necropolis's heart, where the seven pyramids stand arrayed across the sand in a fixed pattern, their faces sheer and their peaks catching the light. A great cracked altar of stone stands at the center of the arrangement, and the ground between the pyramids is open and trodden, scattered with the camps, tracks, and leavings of the crews who stage here. The pyramids rise on every side, and the open desert runs out beyond them.",
          "paths": [
            "The First Pyramid",
            "The Third Pyramid"
          ]
        },
        "The First Pyramid": {
          "description": "The smallest of the seven pyramids, its entrance open and its upper passages cleared and shored, the traps long since sprung or disabled. The upper chambers have been made over into a camp: cleared rooms, stores, and defended ways, with the old burial-passages running down into the dark below where the lower levels stand sealed. Jackal skulls are set over the entrance.",
          "paths": [
            "The Plaza of Kings"
          ]
        },
        "The Third Pyramid": {
          "description": "A pyramid broken open down its northern face, the collapse laying bare passages and chambers that were sealed for ages. Fresh digging runs through the breach and into the rooms beyond, props and tools and cult-marks left along the way, and the carved doors at the end of the deep hall stand ajar. The passages run down past disturbed sarcophagi into the lower dark.",
          "paths": [
            "The Plaza of Kings"
          ]
        }
      },
