    "Halfway Rock": {
      "name": "Halfway Rock",
      "x": -9,
      "y": 29,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Wild Grass Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Halfway Rock is a lone tor with a cold spring, standing where the long road that crosses the grass meets its own midpoint. The catkin caravan-families who hold it water any traveler, host any traveler, and share the news of three lands over tea.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Halfway Rock belongs to the catkin caravan-families, and they run it the way they run the whole road: by hosting, not by charging. Water, fodder, a safe night, and a place at the lantern-fire go to anyone who asks and plenty who don't. The families are gracious, unhurried, endlessly nosy, and quietly certain the grass would grind to a halt without them.\n\nThe Syndicate has offered to buy the families out, to post its own guards for safety, to set a fair toll and split it, and the families have purred through every offer and granted none. A road given away cannot be owned, and the road-men know it.\n\nThe catkin hear everything. Every line that crosses the grass passes word here, so the families know who is moving, who is hunting whom, and what waits down which track, often before the people involved do. They share it gladly with travelers they have taken a liking to, and they take their time deciding. A stranger earns their way up by proving useful and decent on the road: walk as a hand, drive a wagon, ride as a line-rider, and one day be trusted with the word itself.",
      "areas": {
        "The Wagon-Ring": {
          "description": "The flat ground at the tor's foot, where wagons stand parked nose-to-tail in wide rings, wheels chocked and shafts down. The long road runs in from the grass on one side and out into the grass on the other, straight and pale and visible for miles each way. Lantern-lines on poles cross overhead between the rings, and the spring's overflow runs out in a stone channel toward the fodder-troughs.",
          "paths": [
            "The Lantern-Hall",
            "The Spring"
          ]
        },
        "The Lantern-Hall": {
          "description": "A long hall of grey timber and stretched hide built against the rock, its open sides hung with the same lanterns that light the wagon-rings. Inside are low tables, piled cushions and hides, and a row of iron kettles over a banked fire-trench. The walls are pinned with road-tokens, route-scratches, and the small painted boards caravan-families leave to mark a safe passage.",
          "paths": [
            "The Wagon-Ring"
          ]
        },
        "The Spring": {
          "description": "A worn path climbs the tor's side to the spring itself, a cold pool welling up in a basin of pale rock near the summit. From the top the grass runs flat to every horizon, and the road shows as a thin line dividing it, one way toward the far ports and the other toward the desert road. Old caravan-marks are cut into the rock around the basin, layered over each other for generations.",
          "paths": [
            "The Wagon-Ring"
          ]
        }
      },
