    "The Highgrass": {
      "name": "The Highgrass",
      "x": -14,
      "y": -21,
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "Wild Grass Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Where the grass grows tallest it stands higher than a rider, and the largest beasts in the grass sea live inside it: aurochs in ground-shaking herds, and behemoths the size of barns. Grass that high hides everything until it is already on you.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The danger in the Highgrass is that there is no seeing in it. Grass this tall swallows a behemoth whole; a rider learns what stands in front of him when it is an arm's length away and not before.\n\nAurochs move through in great herds, placid until startled, and a startled herd becomes a wall of horn and hoof that flattens everything in its lane. Behemoths are barn-sized and nearly unkillable, slow to anger and unstoppable once roused; a wounded behemoth rolls straight through grass, herd, and hunter alike. The true killers are the grass-tigers, striped to vanish in the stalks, which stalk the lone and the wounded and strike from cover, so the one that takes a traveler is the one he never saw.\n\nA behemoth's hide is thick as a door and turns most blades; cured into plates it makes armor only a lance will pierce. Its horns run longer than a man and are harder than iron. A grass-tiger's pelt is vast and striped and prized whole, and its fangs are as long as knives. Aurochs horn and hide are humbler trophies, but the herds are many.",
      "areas": {
        "The Margins": {
          "description": "The grass at the edge stands waist- to shoulder-high, low enough to see over from horseback, and behind it the open grass sea runs flat and pale to the horizon. Ahead, the grass climbs into a green wall taller than a rider, with no gap and no end to it either way. Narrow tracks press into the wall where heavy bodies have shouldered through.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trample",
            "The Wallows"
          ]
        },
        "The Trample": {
          "description": "A wide swath beaten flat through the tall grass, the stalks crushed and the black earth churned and printed with tracks the size of platters. It runs straight a long way before the grass closes over it again, and along its length it is the one place inside the Highgrass where the eye carries any distance. Bleached bone lies half-trodden into the mud where the grass crowds the edges.",
          "paths": [
            "The Margins",
            "The Wallows"
          ]
        },
        "The Wallows": {
          "description": "Broad pits of churned mud and standing water where the ground dips, rimmed by grass flattened in wide circles. Horns, ribs, and the great curved bones of fallen beasts lie bleaching around the water and sunk in the mud.",
          "paths": [
            "The Margins",
            "The Trample"
          ]
        }
      },
