    "The Carcass": {
      "name": "The Carcass",
      "x": -2,
      "y": 41,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Wild Grass Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Carcass is the skeleton of a creature so vast and ancient nobody agrees what it once was, lying half-sunk in the grass with its ribs arching overhead like a hall. Gnoll packs have moved into the bones and made them a warren of dens, stalls, and rope-bridges. Whatever you cannot buy honestly anywhere else in the grass sea, you can probably buy here.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Carcass runs on bluster, extortion, and a black market. Pack alphas hold stretches of the skeleton and carry ridiculous earned titles — the Lord of the Long Grass, the Thrice-Blooded King — and a failed alpha faces a challenger before sundown.\n\nThe gnolls trade in things no one else will touch, take mercenary work no one else will take, and keep the worst banditry concentrated in one place where everyone can see it. The only rule of the market is pay up front.\n\nThe Carcass is the region's broker and rumor-mill. The gnolls sell maps and ways into the old burial-mound, word of where Vaskarn's band is striking and what it is worth, and good steel to anyone with coin — including, it is widely understood, to Vaskarn himself. They will sell the same secret twice and to both sides, and consider that good business.\n\nThe skeleton's origin is unknown. The bones are minerite, harder than stone and faintly warm to the touch.",
      "areas": {
        "The Jaw": {
          "description": "The way in, through the creature's mouth: the lower jawbone forms the threshold, the upper jaw arches overhead, and teeth the size of standing stones flank the gap. Hide awnings and the first stalls crowd the opening, and rope-lines climb from here up into the skull above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ribcage",
            "The Gut"
          ]
        },
        "The Ribcage": {
          "description": "The great hollow of the chest, where ribs arch overhead like the vaults of a hall, strung between with hide tarps for shade. Dens and platforms are built up against the inner curve of the bones at several heights, linked by ladders and swaying rope-walks. A long open floor runs down the center between the ribs.",
          "paths": [
            "The Jaw",
            "The Gut",
            "The Tail"
          ]
        },
        "The Gut": {
          "description": "The ground between and beneath the bones, roofed over by the ribs and platforms above so the light comes down grey and broken. The market lives here: stalls and dens packed into the permanent shade, deals struck in low voices. Narrow lanes wind between stacked goods, bone, and hide.",
          "paths": [
            "The Jaw",
            "The Ribcage"
          ]
        },
        "The Tail": {
          "description": "The long line of the spine runs out from the ribcage into the grass, vertebrae the size of huts strung one after another. Dens are carved and built into the gaps between the bones, the largest at the base of the tail where an alpha keeps a seat. The far end trails off into open grass.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ribcage"
          ]
        }
      },
