    "Bryngard": {
      "name": "Bryngard",
      "x": 17,
      "y": -20,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whitemoor",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Bryngard is a kingdom drowned in the fen, its streets and halls standing under black water. Its dead are still fighting the battle they died in, on and on with no end to it, and the arms and grave-gold of a whole army lie down there among them.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The scattered remnants of two dead armies still fight Bryngard's last battle, neither knowing it died. The rank and file are revenants; the captains and knights are wraiths, faster and far worse, who rally the footsoldiers.\n\nIMPORTANT: the dead ignore the living at first, absorbed in their war. Someone who keeps to the edges and touches nothing can pass through them. They turn on the living when given a reason: stepping between the two forces, taking up arms or a banner of theirs, striking one of them, or making enough noise or light to break their attention.\n\nThe two sides of the battle can be set against each other or slipped past while they are locked together. Raising a fallen standard draws the dead who follow it.\n\nLoot is the war-gear of two drowned armies, scattered thickest where the fighting was worst and richest in the keep and wherever a captain fell: blades, shields, mail, banners, grave-gold, and war-pay. Among it are old blades that cut the restless dead as easily as living flesh, and fallen standards the dead still rally to, following whoever raises one.",
      "areas": {
        "The Dam": {
          "description": "A long earthen dam runs across the head of the basin, torn open through the middle. Streets and squares under a shallow black flood, with rooftops, a leaning tower, and the bulk of a keep standing clear of it. Broken stone and reed make the slope down toward the streets.",
          "paths": [
            "The Drowned Streets"
          ]
        },
        "The Drowned Streets": {
          "description": "The streets of Bryngard run as shallow flood between buildings standing in the water to the height of a door. The water lies no more than thigh-deep along the lanes, dropping away into the odd cellar-mouth or sunk well, so most of the city can be crossed on foot. Side-streets run off in every direction into a sunk market, a row of drowned houses, and a well-yard gone to a pool, any of which can be worked through toward the keep or the broken wall.",
          "paths": [
            "The Dam",
            "The Keep",
            "The Breach"
          ]
        },
        "The Keep": {
          "description": "The keep stands above the flood. A wide stair climbs out of the great hall into galleries and chambers overhead. An armory opens off the hall, its racks and chests still holding old mail and arms. Higher up, a strongroom door stands shut at the end of a gallery, and narrow stairs run on toward the roof and the leaning tower.",
          "paths": [
            "The Drowned Streets",
            "The Breach"
          ]
        },
        "The Breach": {
          "description": "A length of the city wall has been smashed inward here, leaving a bank of broken stone half-buried in the shallows. Siege-ladders and a shattered ram lie where they fell against it, and the ground inside the gap is churned and littered with splintered shields. Shallow water covers the rubble, with deeper pits where the assault tore the ground open. Beyond the breach the open fen shows through the gap.",
          "paths": [
            "The Drowned Streets",
            "The Keep"
          ]
        }
