    "Avelmere": {
      "name": "Avelmere",
      "x": -30,
      "y": -17,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whitemoor",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Avelmere is a wealthy city that died twice: first of a plague that swept through it, then under the flood that closed over what the plague had left. Its riches lie beneath the flat black water still, and its plague-dead wait in it for anyone who wades in after them.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Avelmere's dead are the diseased dead: ravenous, mindless ghouls and the rotted dead that drowned with the city. They lie submerged in the flat water and wait in the dark wet rooms. They swarm, rising out of the flood without warning, dragging the living under, coming on in numbers, and they are thickest toward the great hall at the heart.\n\nIMPORTANT: Avelmere's dead are hostile and attack any living thing among them. They do not parley or relent, and they hunt by swarming, lying still and submerged until the living draw near, then surging up to drag them down and bury them in numbers.\n\nThe dead are clumsy on dry footing and deadliest in open water, where weight of numbers tells and they pull the living under.\n\nLoot: at the heart, with the king, his crown of gold and stones and his sword, a blessed old blade that bites the dead and the cursed far harder than steel. Behind the dais, a strongroom holding a rich kingdom's hoard of plate, coin, and jewels. Lesser grave-gold and the goods of a drowned town lie through the streets, the temple, and the chambers off the hall.",
      "areas": {
        "The Causeway": {
          "description": "A raised stone road runs out from the dry edge into the flooded city, dropping lower until the water closes over it. From it Avelmere lies still and grey under flat water, its streets gone to dark channels and its squares to dead pools. A great hall stands clear of the flood at the city's heart, gold gone dull on its roof and its high windows above the water.",
          "paths": [
            "The Reed Streets"
          ]
        },
        "The Reed Streets": {
          "description": "The streets stand flooded and still between buildings sunk to their upper floors, the water dark and flat and grown at its edges with reeds. Lines of sight close fast between walls and half-drowned roofs, so a stretch of open water gives way to a narrow passage and then to another sunk court. Roofs and the tops of walls stand clear above the flood, dry footing over the deeper channels, and shutters, furniture, and the goods of a town drift caught in the reeds.",
          "paths": [
            "The Causeway",
            "The Temple",
            "The Throne-Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Temple": {
          "description": "The temple stands at the head of a drowned square, its doors open to the water and its floor flooded between rows of pillars. Cots and biers stand crowded the length of the nave where they were set, most under the flat water now, a few on a step of raised floor still clear of it. Side-chapels open off the aisles, a stair runs down into a flooded crypt below, and another climbs into a bell-tower that stands well above the flood.",
          "paths": [
            "The Reed Streets",
            "The Throne-Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Throne-Hall": {
          "description": "The great hall stands above the flood at the heart of the city, water lying flat across its floor and a long aisle running toward a raised dais and a stone throne set clear of it. Gold fittings and the wealth of a rich court show dull along the walls, hangings rotted to threads, and the high tables of a hall still standing in their places. Doors behind the dais open on private chambers and a strongroom, and a gallery runs above the aisle around the hall.",
          "paths": [
            "The Reed Streets",
            "The Temple"
          ]
        }
