    "Carrowgate": {
      "name": "Carrowgate",
      "x": 18,
      "y": -5,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whitemoor",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Carrowgate is a raiders' stronghold out in the bog, a ruined fort held by the worst men on the moor. They rob the dry country and the graves alike, and sell what they take to anyone with the coin and the stomach for it.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The reavers of Carrowgate are marshfolk out of the low fen, a warband that holds the old fort and preys on the moor: raiding the villages, breaking open barrows for grave-gold, and taking captives to ransom. They fear nothing on the moor but the Knights Vigilant and the dead.\n\nIMPORTANT: the reavers are predatory but not mad. They size up a newcomer before they move: anyone who looks hard, useful, or worth a deal is heard out, and they will trade, fence, sell, or hire; anyone who looks weak, lost, or soft and rich is robbed, ransomed, or killed. They respect strength and coin and nothing else. Cheat them, threaten the camp, or move on their plunder or their captives, and the whole warband turns at once.\n\nTheir plunder is the wealth of the moor's dead and its raided living, kept in a vault under the fort: grave-gold, coin, raided goods, and the barrow-silver and blessed arms that bite the dead. They fence it to the Syndicate and to any buyer with coin. Captives are penned in the cells below and held for ransom, and some buyers come out to the bog for those, asking no questions about what they want them for. The chief keeps the best of everything.",
      "areas": {
        "The Landing": {
          "description": "A muddy landing on a bog island, boats drawn up in the reeds and a track leading up into the camp. The ruined fort stands above it, and brown bog water spreads flat on every side.",
