      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Barrowlands are open heath covered in the burial mounds of an older age, where the war-dead were laid with their silver and their gold. The wights that guard those graves rise on anyone who breaks one open, and grave-robbers work the mounds all the same.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The mounds are the graves of an age of war long before the drowned crowns, and a barrow-wight lies in each, bound to its hoard. The Syndicate works the field openly, digging the mounds for grave-silver; its diggers are armed and will fight or deal as it suits them.\n\nIMPORTANT: a barrow-wight lies still until its mound is entered or its grave-goods are touched, then rises and fights without quarter to defend its hoard. The wights are bound to their barrows and do not follow far beyond them, but the older and richer the grave, the worse the thing that holds it.\n\nThe graves hold grave-gold, old arms, and barrow-silver, the bright metal that bites the dead and the cursed harder than steel. The Great Barrow holds the most, and the worst guardian; the Syndicate's dig holds whatever it has pulled up and not yet carried off.",
