    "The Temple of the Sword Vigilant": {
      "name": "The Temple of the Sword Vigilant",
      "x": -1,
      "y": 37,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Whitemoor",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Temple of the Sword Vigilant is the fortress-seat of the Knights Vigilant on the cliff above Aldwall, a sworn order of Galard the Swordbearer. Its knights ride Whitemoor openly against restless dead, return to recount recognized rides in the Feast-Hall, and rise from New-Sworn to Moor-Knight, Banner-Knight, and Champion Vigilant.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Knights Vigilant fight the moor's dead in the open and by force: war-dead of the drowned crowns, barrow-wights, dead riders, drowned things, and death-knights of the Deathless. They are not occult investigators like the Black Tower. They identify what must be put down, ride directly to threatened people and places, and use radiant arms, courage, and fellowship to end it.\n\nThe Feast-Hall also recognizes Galard's Proving-Year custom, which predates the order's estrangement from the Templars Adamant. Any willing person may take up a plain iron Road-Shield without swearing the Swordbearer oath, then have three distinct deeds of courage recognized here or at another Galard site. Completing the proof permits but never requires an oath. Until the aspirant freely swears, they are not New-Sworn, receive no moonstone oath-brooch, and hold no authority in the Knights Vigilant.\n\nGalard the Swordbearer loves the bold and loyal: the knight who rides hardest at the worst of the dead and the knight who never leaves another to them. The Vigilant are proud, competitive, and tightly bound. Glory is social, but advancement rests on recognized rides established before the Feast-Hall through a true account, witnesses, trophies, rescued people, or consequences the order can verify. A knight need not boast personally; others may tell the deed.\n\nA newly sworn member receives a moonstone oath-brooch and begins as New-Sworn. One supervised first ride earns recognition as Moor-Knight and the right to answer independent calls. Three recognized Moor-Knight rides earn a personal banner and elevation to Banner-Knight, trusted to lead other knights and larger rides. Four recognized great rides as Banner-Knight may earn acclamation as Champion Vigilant, with authority to command the order's greatest responses and judge the deeds of others.\n\nThe Temple is where the moor's blessed arms are made. Dwarf silversmiths and moonstone-cutters work its forges, setting silver, moonstone, and sun-gold into weapons, shields, armor, and holy focuses that bite the dead and defend the living. Promotion rewards should suit the knight's actual build rather than assuming every Vigilant uses a sword.\n\nThe Vigilant welcome any bold and honest comer, but they are a proud armed order. Cross them, steal from their stores, or shield necromancers and dead-traffickers, and the whole brotherhood answers in force.",
      "areas": {
        "The Forecourt": {
          "description": "A walled forecourt on the cliff-top behind the Temple's gates, the fortress-monastery rising beyond it in grey stone and tall windows. From the wall the whole of Aldwall lies spread below, and the moor past it, with a long stair cut down the cliff-face to the town.",
          "paths": [
