          "description": "The town's market fills a wide square in the shelter of the carved walls, the cliff and its fortress rising above and the landward gate opening onto the moor. One side runs beneath a stretch of wall worked with the deepest and most intricate runework in Aldwall, knotwork and figures crowded edge to edge. Stalls and shopfronts sell armor and blessed arms, silver and moonstone work, moor-cures, salted provisions, and tack and harness, and a horse-market and pony-lines stand along one side.",
