    "Eelfen Village": {
      "name": "Eelfen Village",
      "x": -34,
      "y": -7,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Great Lagoon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A village of stilt-houses and eel-traps where the lagoon's salt water runs into the marsh, west of Caranthoria. The eelers have worked these flats for generations, the catch is good, and the village is older than the new city by an age.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The village is mixed — humans, frogkin, and lizardfolk eelers who have worked these flats together for generations and want nothing to do with the swamp kingdom in the deep fens.\n\nThe lizardfolk who come for the tithe serve the Children of the Wyrm, the dragon-cult of the Reedmoot fens. Most years the tithe is eels, salt, and goods. Some years they ask for people, and the ones chosen walk west into the reeds and do not come back. The village pays because it is old enough to remember the villages that refused.\n\nThe Solarian prefect comes for the imperial tax and takes a cut to keep his reports quiet, so the tithe goes out into the reeds as it always has.\n\nThe eelers are proud, blunt, and unimpressed by both their masters. They have fed themselves off these flats since before the empire had a name and expect to be here after it falls, and they treat the tax-collector and the swamp's tithe-takers as two kinds of weather to be endured. A stranger who can pull an oar or mend a trap is fed and housed; one who comes asking after the tithe gets blunt answers and a long look.",
      "areas": {
        "The Stilt-Town": {
          "description": "The village raised on pilings over the tidal mud: plank walkways and rope bridges strung between the stilt-houses, boats tied up in the water beneath, and ladders running down to the flats at low tide. Reed-beds close in to the west where the dry pilings give out and the marsh begins.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trap-Flats",
            "The Tide-Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Trap-Flats": {
          "description": "The tidal flats where salt water meets marsh, staked end to end with eel-traps, weirs, and drying-racks. Channels wind between the reed-beds for the flat-boats; at low water the mud stands open and walkable, at high water it is all current.",
          "paths": [
            "The Stilt-Town"
