        },
        "The Tide-Hall": {
          "description": "The village's gathering-hall, the largest platform in the stilt-town, open down one side to the water and built so the high tide runs under the floorboards. Long tables, a great hearth, and barrels of the village's own eel-liquor; the eelers eat, drink, settle their business, and take in travelers off the water here. The carved house-posts holding up the roof are older than Caranthoria, and the eelers will tell you so.",
          "paths": [
