    "The Reedfront": {
      "name": "The Reedfront",
      "x": -43,
      "y": 8,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Great Lagoon",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The western fens, where the Solarian war runs into the swamp. The empire pushes its border west through the marsh and the lizardfolk of the deep fens fight it every yard, raiding the work, ambushing the columns, and falling back into water the legion cannot hold. The free-marsh folk who live here want neither the empire's law nor the swamp kingdom's, and the fighting runs back and forth across their ground.",
      "hiddenInfo": "This is the contested border between the Empire of Light and the dragon-led lizardfolk kingdom of the Reedmoot fens, the region to the west, and the front moves with the season. The Solarian legion drives causeways and embankments west to drain and hold the marsh; the lizardfolk tear the work down and bleed the columns that build it. Neither side holds the Reedfront for long.\n\nThe lizardfolk war-parties serve the Children of the Wyrm and come east out of the deep fens to raid. IMPORTANT: they default hostile to Solarians and to anyone working for the empire, fight from cover and water, and do not parley with the legion's people. They sometimes drive a mire drake ahead of them — a poison-breathed marsh reptile that wallows in the channels and comes up under boats and wading men. Toward the deep-fen tracks west, the war-parties are thicker, surer of the footing, and more willing to give battle.\n\nThe free-marsh folk — humans, frogkin, and lizardfolk fenfolk who have lived here longer than either power — want neither the Empire nor the dragon. They fish, net eels, and move through the reeds by ways the legion cannot find, and they will guide, warn, hide, or sell to those who treat them fairly. Some have lost kin to the tithe; some have lost kin to the legion's press-gangs. They are the ground both sides fight across and the people most worth knowing here.\n\nThe situations the front throws up are constant: a Solarian work-column stalled and waiting to be relieved or finished off, a war-party massing in the holts before a raid, a drake loose in the channels, a marsh family burned out and run off their island, salvage and dead left in the water after a fight, and prisoners taken by one side or the other being moved deeper in.",
      "areas": {
        "The Channels": {
          "description": "Broad reed-fen cut through with winding water-channels: standing reed-beds, stretches of black water and sucking mud, and low islands of firmer ground between them. Sightlines end at the next wall of reeds, and the footing changes with the tide.",
          "paths": [
            "The Sunken Holts"
          ]
        },
        "The Sunken Holts": {
          "description": "Where the fen thickens: dense reed-islands and drowned thickets standing in the water, the channels narrowing between them. Old drowned ground — the tops of field-walls and the stumps of dead trees break the surface, and the firm tracks wind blind between the holts.",
          "paths": [
            "The Channels",
            "The Mire-Paths"
