    "The Greatwild": {
      "name": "The Greatwild",
      "x": -29,
      "y": 39,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Ntar Vanna",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Greatwild is the upriver interior of Ntar Vanna, where the Saranadi is broad and slow and no village stands. The jungle here is the oldest and largest in the region, and so are the beasts: crocodilians longer than a barge, tusked herds that flatten the brush they cross, big cats that hunt from the canopy. Hunters come up from the river towns for ivory, hide, horn, and the strange materials the deep jungle grows.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Greatwild has no settlements, no rulers, and no law. It is open hunting country: river crews come up from the towns to take big game and the materials and go back down to sell.\n\nThe beasts are the region's everyday danger here, all scaled large. Dire crocodiles lie still as logs in the shallows and explode on anything at the waterline. Goliath boars move in tusked herds and trample in a mass, dangerous in number more than singly. Canopy tigers stalk a crew from the branches and drop on the one at the back. River drakes, wingless water-serpents, crest and strike at boats and are the apex of the open water. Thunder-tusks, elephantine giants, reshape the ground by walking and are not aggressive unless pressed, and lethal when pressed. On the far banks the vitality grows things wrong: bloat-spiders, giant spiders swollen past any natural size, den deep, so meeting one means a crew went too far.\n\nIMPORTANT: river bandits called driftmen work the Greatwild and are hostile. They are not one band but scattered outlaw crews who gave up hunting beasts and hunt hunters instead — letting other crews take the game and the risk, then taking the haul. They run fast skiffs, camp on any bank, and move when the hunting moves. They hold no ground and fly no flag, which is why no one has cleared them out.\n\nLoot here is what the beasts yield. Thunder-tusk ivory: a single tusk is a fortune, carving-grade, sold by weight. Goliath boar hide: tans into heavy armor-leather that turns a blade. Canopy tiger pelt: a luxury skin, and the long fangs make weapons. Dire crocodile hide: plate-hard scute for shields and armor-facing. River drake bone: light and strong, prized by bowyers and shipwrights. Bloat-spider venom-sacs: raw poison stock for alchemy.",
      "areas": {
        "The Open River": {
          "description": "The upper Saranadi runs broad and slow, braided around long sandbars and gravel banks. The channel-markers have ended and the forest stands back from the water in high green walls. Boats can put in almost anywhere along the shallows.",
          "paths": [
            "The Floodforest",
            "The Trample"
          ]
        },
        "The Floodforest": {
          "description": "Forest standing in still black water, the trunks rising on buttress roots like walls. Sightlines are short, the channels narrow and winding, and hanging vine closes overhead. A boat can thread the waterways; on foot the roots and water make for slow, broken footing.",
          "paths": [
            "The Open River",
            "The Trample"
          ]
        },
        "The Trample": {
          "description": "Open low ground churned flat — cropped grass, snapped saplings, and wide mud wallows. Sightlines run long here after the forest, and the bare earth shows the tracks of heavy things. The ground is soft and the going is firm only on the higher ridges.",
          "paths": [
            "The Open River",
            "The Floodforest"
          ]
        }
      },
