    "The Swallowed Cities": {
      "name": "The Swallowed Cities",
      "x": 4,
      "y": 34,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Ntar Vanna",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Swallowed Cities are the ruins of the demonborn cities raised here an age ago, burned in a catastrophe no one remembers and overgrown ever since. Roots have split the plazas and tipped the towers, and the walls still carry carvings of a king no one living has seen. Relic crews work the ruins for grave-goods, and the trade that fills New Anthara's markets starts here.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Swallowed Cities are vast demonborn ruins strangled by jungle, and the grave-goods trade begins here. Relic crews dig the ruins for demonborn arms, regalia, and carved stone, then carry the haul down to New Anthara's assay houses. Nothing here is governed; crews work the ruins by force of arms and against each other.\n\nThe jungle has grown the wildlife oversized. Giant constrictors coil in the trees and toppled stone and ambush what passes. Goliath scarabs work the ruins in carrion-swarms, dangerous in number. Dire apes hold the high ruins as territory and own the fallen tower. Stranglevine grows thick enough to seize and hold a person where the roots have broken the ground. A giant crocodile dens in the flooded shrine beneath the great temple — the largest thing in the ruins, and the hardest to reach.\n\nIMPORTANT: rival relic crews and a cult both work the ruins and default hostile. Rival crews fight when the haul is worth it and a target looks beatable. The cult are diggers who serve the buried powers that demons once served and want them back in the world; they go by the Children of Ur, and they are after sealed relics, not grave-bronze. They turn on anyone who finds their diggings.\n\nBeneath the throne-dais, an Ur Spawn hold occupies chambers cut below the Royal Court. Its outer band runs four to six: Gaunt Fiends or Flameskin Imps range the court, a Snatch-Tail Fiend hunts the Strangled Ways, and a Flamewhip Overseer Fiend drives them back toward the dais when they stray. They answer to an Archfiend below.\n\nThe Spawn guard the way down, seize intruders, and make Children of Ur diggers carry relics and prisoners into the hold. The cult calls this service; the archfiend calls it ownership.\n\nLoot is demonborn grave-goods and what the beasts yield. Demonborn grave-bronze: ritual arms and regalia, arcane-touched, valuable and sometimes still holding a working. Vitality-touched amber: a sap-stone grown thick in the old groves, an alchemical reagent and a wardstone. Constrictor hide and scarab shell: armor materials. Ur-ichor: black blood sealed in the demonborn dead, drunk for demonic strength at the cost of the drinker's humanity. Wakeful idols: carved demonborn figures holding a sleeping Ur-thing, rousable for power that claims a piece of the one who wakes it. Cursed demonborn arms and armor: Ur-touched gear that makes the bearer stronger and slowly less himself.",
      "areas": {
        "The Royal Court": {
          "description": "A vast roofless palace-plaza pried open by a single colossal tree growing up through its center, roots heaving the flagstones. A raised throne-dais stands at the far end, and the longest carved walls in the ruins run the length of the court. Toppled statues of horned, tailed demonborn figures lie among the roots, some still upright along the dais. The footing is broken stone and root.",
          "paths": [
