      "basicInfo": "A high-walled cove screened behind tall rock pillars, invisible from open water. Flensing ramps, boiling-pots, and bone-racks stand on the shingle beach inside. This is the butchering ground of the Flensers, the outlaw hunting crew — the one place in the bay they are known to return to.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Flensers do not welcome outsiders and attack most on sight. They fight dirty — hooks, nets, thrown harpoons, a man's own boat set alight under him. If outmanned they retreat to their ships and put to sea, burning their stores and caches rather than leaving them.\n\nThe Flensers are not always in the cove. When they are: ships careened on the beach, pots boiling, lookouts on the rock pillars, a dozen or more armed flensers working fast. When they are not: cold pots, fresh butchering sign, cached bone and oil under guard of a few left-behind hands, and sometimes a chained prisoner in the caves — merfolk herders seized when they caught the crew in the act, kept for leverage or sale.\n\nThe works show what the crew is: calf bones in the racks, merfolk herd-brands on rendered stock. \n\nLoot: cached leviathan bone and calf-bone, casks of rendered oil, the crew's plunder in the caches, and the Flensers' own gear — good harpoons, good hides.",
