      "region": "Bay of Serpents",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "An island crowned by the Stormspire, a bare peak that draws lightning and wears a slow-turning storm most days. The sea around it is wrong: storms rise fast out of clear sky, and the currents run inward, driving ships onto the wreck-choked banks that ring the shore. Centuries of hulls lie piled on the shoals. Sailors say the isle wants ships — and the storm sorcerers who live on it make sure it gets them.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Stormcallers are hostile by default and attack anyone who comes near their caves or the Stormspire. They are storm sorcerers — wild, savage, and sophisticated in nothing but their craft. In a fight they call lightning down on the banks, drive walls of wind that flip boats, and crack thunder that knocks men flat. They are descendants of the wrecked who learned what the isle offered, and they feed the storms with living sacrifices: blood given to the sky brings the weather up, and the weather brings ships.\n\nThe Stormcallers live in cave-mouths in the hillside below the Spire and come down to strip what the sea drives in. Sacrifices are taken alive from grounded ships and held in the caves until the next storm is fed. Generations of looted cargo — coin, cargo, arms, everything the wrecks carried — is piled in the deeper caves.\n\nA storm drake nests on the Stormspire and hunts when the sky darkens. The Stormcallers feed it sacrifices too — they give blood to the sky and the drake alike, and cannot always tell which one answers. Lightning eels swarm the charged water around the wreck-banks in any weather, and touching the sea near a surfaced shoal of them bites like a whip.\n\nLoot: the Stormcallers' hoard in the caves; storm drake scale and charge-glands; lightning eel glands; charge-glass, fused where lightning has struck the banks, prized by enchanters; and the cargo of every age of wreck on the shoals — the richest unworked salvage in the bay, for anyone fast enough to work it between storms.",
      "areas": {
        "The Outer Banks": {
          "description": "Wreck-strewn shoals ringing the isle, passable by small boat in fair weather. Ahead, the island rises to the Stormspire and its turning crown of cloud.",
          "paths": [
