    "Pearl Cave Island": {
      "name": "Pearl Cave Island",
      "x": 1,
      "y": -25,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Bay of Serpents",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A rocky island rising to a sea-cave tall as a cliff — the den of the Mother of Serpents, the vast pearl-white serpent every hunter in the bay measures themselves against. She does not stay here, but she comes: the cave holds the great ships she has broken and carried back across the generations, and its shores glitter with pieces of her shed scales.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Mother of Serpents is as big as a fleet — her back breaching reads as an island, her eye stands taller than a man, and she has bitten warships in half. She is crested and mother-of-pearl, her hide scarred with generations of broken harpoons. She is not hostile by default: she is sovereign. She ignores small things on her island unless her collection is robbed in her presence or she is struck — and then she is absolute. She has surfaced beside crews, looked at them, and left them alive. When she returns to the cave, the water tells it first — the pool stirs, then breathes, then rises. She surfaces from the shaft without warning, anywhere in the cave's water.\n\nShe keeps what she breaks. The finest vessels she has ever destroyed lie laid up in the cave's dark water, carried there by her, and no one can say why. Among them is the bow half of the Serpentsbane, the greatest ship ever built in the bay, bitten in two on the great hunt that founded the city's feuds. Its lost relics — founders' arms, the figurehead — are worth fortunes to the great houses.\n\nThe island's scavengers do the everyday killing. Wreck eels, thick as a leg and vicious, den through every hulk in the cave — looting the collection means reaching past their holes. Scuttle crabs, dog-sized and armored, swarm the rocks and strand in numbers and come to blood. Reef serpents haunt the island's shallows thicker than anywhere else in the bay.\n\nLoot: scale fragments litter the shores. Intact shed scales are rare, found mostly inside the cave, and prising one loose is slow, loud work.",
      "areas": {
        "The Scale Strand": {
          "description": "A shore glittering with shards and worn slabs of mother-of-pearl among the shingle. Reef serpents trace the shallows, and the island climbs from the beach toward the cave-mouth above.",
          "paths": [
