      "basicInfo": "The great hunting port of the southern coasts, built where the shipping lanes cross the richest monster waters in the world. Coriva's crews hunt the sea serpents and leviathans that plague the lanes, and the city has grown rich on the harvest. Its harbor is crowded with hunting ships, and its two ruling houses — Tessaro and Cavarin — fly their colors from half the masts in port.",
      "hiddenInfo": "House Tessaro hunt the bay's monsters and hold that this is what keeps its people alive. They wear silvered scale-armor, carry blessed harpoons, sail ships hung with banners, and parade to the docks before every great hunt. A Tessaro crew never abandons anyone: they will die to the last soul before letting a monster take a fisherman, and a mast flying their colors means help is coming.\n\nHouse Cavarin capture monsters alive and put them to work: their broken beasts tow the fastest vessels in the bay, haul what no crane lifts, and guard their harbors, and their handlers bond hunting-beasts the way others break horses.\n\nBoth houses scout the Water Arena for recruits, and a promising fighter can expect agents from each at their table by nightfall, talking the other house down.\n\nThe Serpentsbane's stern stands in drydock on the plaza — the greatest ship ever built in Coriva, bitten in half by the Mother of Serpents on the great hunt that founded the city's fortunes and feuds. Oaths are sworn on her timbers.\n\nCoriva's streets: humans, halflings, and giantborn hunters; merfolk trading at the waterline; frogkin everywhere. Hunters are celebrities and act like it — entourages, feuds, terrible poems about themselves. Crews recruit loudly on the plaza and lie about their prospects.\n\nThe Coriva League Chapterhouse posts the bay's work: hunts, escorts, rescues, salvage charters, and bounties.",
