    "Fleetwrack Isle": {
      "name": "Fleetwrack Isle",
      "x": -40,
      "y": -39,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Reedmoot Fens",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": false,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A low sand isle off the fen coast where the Golden Fleet of the Empire of Light burned at anchor — set ablaze by the dragon that rules the Fens. Dozens of scorched hulls still stand beached on the bars and heeled in the shallows. It is said the fleet's gold and fire-stores were never recovered: the wrecks are infested with drakes and worse, and the salvage crews that put in mostly don't come back.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Merrow — hulking aquatic ogres — den in the flooded lower decks of the outer wrecks. They drag victims into the dark water and drown them, and they hoard what the fleet carried: coin, arms, and plunder heaped in the deepest holds. They can be baited with treasure thrown into the water and will break off a fight to guard a threatened hoard.\n\nA rookery of mire drakes — swamp-dwelling lesser dragons, poison-breathed — holds the flagship at the anchorage's heart. They came for the dead when the fleet burned and never left. They nest on her upper decks, sun on the rails, and defend the hulk in numbers when a nest is disturbed.\n\nGiant crabs scuttle through any flooded hold and ambush from dark water.\n\nIMPORTANT: everything living on the isle is hostile by default. The merrow are cruel and greedy but can be baited or bought off with treasure; the drakes are animals and cannot be reasoned with — they break off only when badly wounded or drawn away from their nests. The crabs fight until hurt, then bolt for the water.\n\nThe outer wrecks hold silver coin stamped with the sun, legionnaires' short swords and spears, sun-blazoned shields, and casks of lamp-oil and wine in their silted holds. The flagship holds the fleet's pay-chests of gold and silver sun-coin, and in the officers' cabins gilded breastplates, blessed radiant blades, sun-gold rings and medallions, and the admiral's sunburst standard. A sealed magazine deep in her stern holds the fleet's fire-stores — clay vessels of alchemical fire that burn even on water, the surest weapon against the drakes that guard them. Drake hide turns poison and drake venom glands sell well. The merrow hoards hold what the merrow prized: gilded arms, sun-gold jewelry, and coin heaped in the flooded holds.",
      "areas": {
        "The Strand": {
          "description": "The bare isle itself: dune grass, driftwood, and the burned fleet standing in the shallows on every side, masts leaning, hulls charred to the waterline. Cold fire-pits and drag-furrows mark old salvage camps. Sun-bleached bones and cracked crab shells litter the tideline, and broken, abandoned gear lies half-buried in the sand.",
          "paths": [
            "The Burned Line"
          ]
        },
        "The Burned Line": {
          "description": "The outer wrecks — smaller hulls broken on the bars, boardable by wading. Charred decks, dead men where they fell, splintered spars and rigging fouled across the holds, silt drifted deep in the cabins. The lower decks are flooded and dark.",
          "paths": [
