    "Dragon-Brood Mounds": {
      "name": "Dragon-Brood Mounds",
      "x": 3,
      "y": 28,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Reedmoot Fens",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A field of great earthen mounds rising out of the deep fen — the holy ground of the dragon-kingdom of the lizardfolk, where their brood of drakes is hatched and raised. It was here that a priestess entered the oldest mound and came out a dragon, and the kingdom has held the place sacred and forbidden ever since. Outsiders taken in the Fens are brought to the mounds, and they do not come back.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The mounds are the practical seat of the priest-kings — the lizardfolk high priests who rule the Fens in the dragon's name. They keep no city and hold no court; they live among the mounds, tend the brood, lead the rites, and send the war-parties out. Warriors, drake-handlers, and hatchling-tenders live and work across the mound field in numbers.\n\nThe brood is the kingdom's pride: clutches of mire drakes — swamp-dwelling lesser dragons, poison-breathed — hatched in the warm earth of the mounds and raised as war-beasts. Captives taken in the Fens are held in pens near the mounds and given to the drakes at the rites, some at each new moon and more at the great feasts. Captives are kept alive and fed until then — a rescue that comes in time comes home with everyone.\n\nIMPORTANT: everyone and everything at the mounds is hostile to outsiders on sight, without parley and without exception. This is the kingdom's holiest ground, and an outsider walking on it is the worst desecration its people know. They do not take prisoners here — prisoners are already here. They fight to the death in its defense, and horns raise the whole mound field within minutes of an alarm.\n\nThe priest-kings fight with venom-magic and drake-packs at their call. Warriors fight in coordinated bands with spear, shield, and blowgun, and drake-handlers loose their beasts first. The pens are watched but lightly guarded — the kingdom does not imagine anyone would dare — and the mound field between them is broad, dark at night, and loud with drake-calls that cover careful movement.\n\nThe First Mound at the field's heart is the oldest and greatest, ringed with offering-posts, its entrance flanked by drake skulls. Within it the priest-kings keep the kingdom's holiest treasures: offerings of gold and arms taken from the sacrificed, laid up in its inner chamber for the dragon.\n\nLoot: the offering-chamber of the First Mound holds gold, weapons, and armor taken from the kingdom's victims over a generation. Drake eggs are worth a fortune to the right buyer. The priest-kings carry regalia of gold and drake-fang, and their venom-tipped weapons sell high.",
      "areas": {
        "The Reed Flats": {
          "description": "The open fen around the mound field — flat reed-marsh crossed by narrow paths of trodden earth, with the great mounds rising ahead like green hills out of the water. Offering-posts stand along the paths, hung with drake fangs and painted bones. The reeds are tall enough to hide a crouching man.",
          "paths": [
            "The Mound Field"
          ]
        },
        "The Mound Field": {
          "description": "The mounds themselves: dozens of great earthen hills, grass-grown and steaming faintly in the cool air, threaded with paths, hide shelters, drying racks, and fire-pits. Openings in the mound sides breathe warm air from the hatching chambers within. Claw-marks and shed scales litter the ground between them.",
          "paths": [
            "The Reed Flats",
            "The Pens",
            "The First Mound"
          ]
        },
        "The Pens": {
          "description": "A cluster of stake-walled pens on the mound field's edge, floored with mud and roofed with lashed reeds. Rope bindings, feeding troughs, and worn paths ring the stockade. A single gate of heavy timber faces the mounds.",
          "paths": [
            "The Mound Field"
          ]
        },
        "The First Mound": {
          "description": "The greatest mound, at the heart of the field — old enough that trees grow on its flanks. Its single entrance is flanked by two drake skulls the size of horses and framed with gold-leafed posts. A broad rite-ground of packed, fire-blackened earth spreads before it, ringed by standing offering-posts.",
          "paths": [
            "The Mound Field"
          ]
        }
      },
