    "The Slagrun": {
      "name": "The Slagrun",
      "x": -14,
      "y": -26,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "Redrock Sea",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "A canyon of fused black glass cut through the coastal hills by the crash-landing of the Celestial Citadel of Alar, which came down burning, plowed the miles of the cut, and came to rest in the mountain it broke at the canyon's head. The floor is slag, sand, and wreckage shed along the whole length of the fall. Fires burn in the glass with nothing to feed them, and fire-creatures loosed by the crash den among them — the deeper the cut, the worse both get. The Church of the Pyre forbids the wreck to looters, but no one can guard a cut this long — Red-cowl patrols sweep it, and desert folk loot it anyway.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: Red-cowl patrols sweep the cut at unpredictable hours — six to ten footsoldiers of the Church of the Pyre in red cowls, spears and crossbows, one veteran leading. They attack looters on sight, no hail, no questions. They can be fought, hidden from, or outrun; when a patrol finds nothing, it moves on.\n\nEnemies of the cut itself: fire mephits in the slag banks of the lower cut, spiteful and drawn to anything that gleams; salamanders denning among the standing fires of the narrows; fire elementals loose in the cracked glass near the Fallshead — bound things that outlived their bindings when the citadel broke. The standing fires burn without fuel and cannot be put out. Everything worsens toward the Fallshead.\n\nLoot: citadel brass, construct cores, sealed binding-vessels, Sun Kings' ornament, raw black glass. Thin at the Scatter, rich at the Fallshead, where whole hull sections lie unopened.",
      "areas": {
        "The Scatter": {
          "description": "The wide mouth of the cut, where the glass walls stand low and the floor runs broad and open — long sightlines, little cover, footing of drifted sand over slick glass. Debris lies strewn thin: broken fittings, glass-crusted masonry, brass gone green-black.",
          "paths": [
            "The Standing Fires"
          ]
        },
        "The Standing Fires": {
          "description": "The mid-cut, where the canyon narrows to a walled corridor and the heat climbs. Fires burn in clusters straight out of the black glass, and the air above them bends and shivers, breaking sightlines past a stone's throw. Hull-pieces stand half-buried in the floor, big enough to shelter behind or climb into, their torn openings dark. Burrows open in the slag banks between them.",
          "paths": [
            "The Scatter",
            "The Fallshead"
          ]
        },
        "The Fallshead": {
          "description": "The head of the cut, beneath the broken mountain and the citadel resting in it. Hull sections the size of towers lie canted in the glass, making a maze of scorched stone and brass — short sightlines, deep shadows, interiors that go back farther than light reaches. The floor splits into cracks that breathe heat and glow faint red at night, and the fires burn biggest and steadiest here.",
          "paths": [
            "The Standing Fires"
          ]
        }
      },
