    "The Miragelands": {
      "name": "The Miragelands",
      "x": -36,
      "y": 12,
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "Alar Coast",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "Deep desert running inland from the coast, vast and trackless, where heat-shimmer thickens until the horizon cannot be trusted and mirages stand solid enough to walk toward for hours. The Desert Tribes live hidden in this vastness, and the Church cannot control it — Red-cowl columns ride into the sand after them and do not always come back. The Tribes are said to gather at secret places deep in the desert, known only to their own and to the few they choose to guide there.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Red-cowl hunting parties range the outer desert — a dozen riders of the Church of the Pyre in red cowls, lances and crossbows, a veteran leading, hunting any Tribesfolk they can catch. They attack Tribesfolk and known fugitives on sight.\n\nRiders of the Desert Tribes range the whole country and are hostile on sight to Red-cowls. A traveler who is plainly none of these is shadowed, sometimes approached, and sometimes guided in to Meshara — at the Tribes' judgment, not the traveler's asking.\n\nThe Tribes are the survivors and descendants of Gesenthame and of everyone the Church has burned out since. They raid the Church's tribute caravans, and they hide and smuggle fugitives out of the region. An outsider's standing is earned in steps: a stranger is fed at the guest-fire and traded with; one who deals fairly or does the Tribes a service is known; the trusted are offered guiding; and of the very few counted as the Tribes' own.\n\nWhat the Tribes want from outsiders: messages carried to the resistance inside Serendipity, arms and salvage the Church forbids, and information about tribute caravans so they can raid them.",
      "areas": {
        "The Glare": {
          "description": "The outer dunes, where heat-shimmer doubles the horizon and distant shapes ripple and lie — sight is long but nothing seen far off can be trusted. Wheel-ruts and track-lines run in from the coast road and grow aimless deeper in. Caravan wrecks lie scattered along them, cargo still lashed to dead animals, and the dune-crests give high ground to watch the tracks from.",
          "paths": [
            "The Deep Sands"
          ]
        },
        "The Deep Sands": {
          "description": "The interior: high dunes in long ranks, hard gravel flats between them, and no landmarks that keep their place. The dune-valleys hide anything in them until the crest is topped — riders appear and vanish at a ridgeline's distance. Old wells, some dry and some kept, mark the only sure points, and the sand around the kept ones is always fresh with hoofprints.",
          "paths": [
            "The Glare",
            "Meshara"
          ]
        },
        "Meshara": {
          "description": "The Tribes' camp around a deep stone well, tents in loose rings, horse-lines along the swale, everything made to be packed and gone within an hour. Guests are received at a broad fire set apart from the tents.",
          "paths": [
            "The Deep Sands"
          ]
        }
      },
