      "region": "Seadeep Kingdoms",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "basicInfo": "The Copperclad is an ancient elder warship, run aground on a stone shoal an age ago and never sunk. The League of Adventurers mans her now, and outsiders are welcome to shelter aboard: dry decks, hot food, and a bunk for anyone who comes up the side in peace. The merfolk of the deep kingdoms have tried to take her several times, and failed every time.",
      "hiddenInfo": "IMPORTANT: The Copperclad is safe ground and welcoming to outsiders.\n\nThe League came out here because of Orichala: a dragon is said to lair in the drowned city, and the merfolk kingdoms here answer to it. The Copperclad is the League's one foothold in these waters, and they hold it by force of arms. The merfolk have assaulted her several times — coming up through the flooded lower decks and over the sides at night — and been thrown back every time, so far. The lowest decks are flooded, dark, and sealed off, and the garrison watches the seals.\n\nWhat people get up to aboard: rescue runs to fresh wrecks at Manywrecks — a looking-glass on the sterncastle stays trained on it — standing to arms when the merfolk raid, escorting ships through Seadeep water, and expeditions toward Orichala, which is the work the veterans respect and the work that gets people killed. Veterans talk anyone they can out of Manywrecks and outfit the ones they can't.\n\nAboard her: the League garrison, sailors of every people, crews sheltering from weather or worse, and the captains of the ships moored under her protection.",
      "areas": {
        "The Weather Deck": {
          "description": "The Copperclad's open upper deck, reached by a broad gangway up her seaward side, tilted a few degrees to port. Traders' stalls stand along the high rail, and cookfire smoke drifts from the hatches. In her lee, the shoal bends around a pocket of calm water where ships lie moored under the garrison's watch. From the deck, the dead masts of Manywrecks stand on the horizon, and on very clear days, far south, the towers of Orichala.",
