        "Ashfall Pass North": {
          "description": "The Cendrac end of the only road over the range to Velmere: a long grey climb out of the valley between black walls, switchbacking up past the last of the terraces to a saddle where the wind never stops. Ash blows through it constantly and settles on the eastern side, which is how the pass got the name and why Velmere resents it. There is no gate and no garrison, only a stone shelter at the height with a cold hearth in it, and the certain knowledge that the crossing is watched from both ends by people who have no need to stop anybody. Cart traffic goes over in convoy. Everything else goes over alone and quickly.",
