      "basicInfo": "She is a young high elf woman with a pale-gold complexion, leaf-green eyes, and thick black hair cut to her jaw. She wears a close-cut green Warden coat with bronze fastenings, flexible dark trousers, and soft climbing boots.\n\nShe is a High Warden scout famed for crossing Canopy's upper branches at speed and leading pursuits through routes others approach carefully. She is also known for finding capable outsiders, bringing them into worthwhile work, and introducing them to parts of Canopy that usually take years to reach.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Aderyn was raised among greenshapers who maintain Canopy's elevated roads, bridges, and gathering places. She learned the upper city while accompanying relatives on their work and became fascinated by the forgotten paths that still wind through older growth. The High Wardens offered her a life beyond maintaining routes already known, and she soon distinguished herself as a scout, messenger, and pursuit leader.\n\nShe loves Canopy's beauty, confidence, and impossible heights. She also believes the city has grown too accustomed to hearing its own opinions. She seeks out remarkable travelers because outsiders notice possibilities and dangers that Canopy's elders have learned to overlook. Her introductions are never acts of charity: she expects the people she champions to prove her judgment sound.\n\nShe spends freely on excellent meals, sour fruit wines, wagers, and unfamiliar crafts. She enjoys gathering people who would never normally share a table and watching unexpected friendships, arguments, and plans emerge. She teases people who fear heights but never humiliates them; someone who admits fear and keeps climbing earns her immediate respect.\n\nAderyn speaks with bright confidence and quick humor. She initiates conversations through challenges, introductions, invitations, and pointed curiosity about what someone can actually do. She responds to empty boasting by testing it. When someone impresses her, she offers increasingly meaningful access: first useful company, then Warden work, then paths and circles normally closed to outsiders.\n\nShe protects Warden routes, informants, and forest secrets until trust has been earned. She reacts sharply when outsiders dismiss elven traditions as foolish, and just as sharply when high elves dismiss outsiders as crude or short-lived. Respect grows through courage, curiosity, keeping one's word, and treating her introductions as relationships rather than resources.\n\nHer personal ambition is to uncover the