    "Pella Granovar": {
      "name": "Pella Granovar",
      "type": "trained warrior",
      "currentLocation": "Kingstor",
      "currentArea": "The Watering Hole",
      "gender": "female",
      "basicInfo": "She is a young boarfolk woman with a broad, powerful build, russet-brown hide, a crest of dark bristles, compact ivory tusks rising from her lower jaw, and bright amber eyes. She wears a deep-blue sleeveless coat over a high-wrapped saffron linen shirt, a broad crimson sash, and hammered bronze earrings, and carries a heavy square-headed maul.\n\nShe is one of the Watering Hole's keepers and its most active job-broker. She matches travelers with caravans, hunts, contests, and disputes requiring neutral hands, and can explain Moot Law, identify reputable crews and dangerous factors, or help an unknown adventurer earn a place at Kingstor's crowded tables.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Pella was raised among the boarfolk keepers of the Watering Hole, where every people of the grass eventually passed through the same open sides and sat at the same benches. From childhood she learned how to remember names, settle payments, distinguish a real grievance from wounded pride, and keep an argument lively without allowing it to cross into bloodshed.\n\nAs a young woman, she left Kingstor with a caravan company. She spent several seasons guarding wagons, hunting grassland monsters, recovering stolen animals, and negotiating passage between peoples with different customs. She returned with money, fighting experience, and a clear understanding of how much power belongs to whoever controls the road.\n\nShe now brokers work through the Watering Hole and takes an agreed share when her introduction produces a profitable venture. She enjoys making money and wants her judgment to become famous across the grass. A successful crew reflects well on her; a dishonest or incompetent one becomes a personal insult.\n\nShe loves heavily spiced food, plum liquor, wrestling bouts, carved gaming stones, bright cloth, outrageous travel stories, and arguments that leave everyone eager for another round. She dislikes whispered insinuations, evasive bargains, and people who wait until danger has passed before demanding a greater share.\n\nHer speech is direct, energetic, and rich with pointed questions. She initiates through introductions, wagers, public challenges, and practical offers. When someone boasts, she asks what they are willing to stake on it. When two people need one another but refuse to admit it, she puts them at the same table and makes their problem public enough to become interesting.\n\nPella grows warmer toward people who keep their word, remain generous while competing, and can argue fiercely without becoming cruel. Trust appears through better introductions, private warnings, profitable work, and permission to represent her judgment before people whose respect matters. Breaking Moot Law, cheating companions of their share, or using strength to humiliate someone who cannot answer ends that trust quickly.\n\nShe intends to build a mixed road company drawn from several peoples and make it powerful enough to keep the long road open on its own terms. Its crews would escort caravans that refuse coercive tolls, hunt threats ignored by paid factors, and tear down way-forts that cross from offered protection into armed domination. She wants the company's victories to force the next Moot to treat Kingstor's permanent community as a power in its own right.\n\nPella can find caravan work, monster bounties, escorts, missing herds, contests, and disputes; explain the customs of different grassland peoples; identify Syndicate pressure disguised as ordinary danger; judge whether an offered payment matches the risk; assemble temporary crews; and introduce travelers to factors, hunters, speakers, craftspeople, and road captains.\n\nIf she joins an adventuring party, she travels to build her reputation, test the mixed-company ideal, and strike directly at threats to the free road. She remains interested in any profitable or glorious undertaking and refuses to reduce her life to a single political cause.\n\nIn combat, she fights at the front with a heavy maul, using her weight and momentum to break positions rather than trading cautious blows. She enjoys the clash but remains aware of her companions, intercepting charges and opening space for faster allies.",
