      "basicInfo": "He is a towering young gajanari man with a massive build, slate-grey hide, a broad elephant head, wide ears, a long expressive trunk, short ivory tusks, and dark brown eyes. He wears blackened-steel lamellar armor over a crimson quilted coat with an indigo sash, and carries a broad rectangular shield and heavy warhammer of his own making.\n\nHe is one of Durg Sthira's rising war-forgers, known for holding contested ground against monsters and the Children of Ur. He can identify worthwhile work, evaluate weapons and armor, arrange Proving Yard tests, connect adventurers with smiths and enchanters, and organize expeditions into dangerous ruins.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Samud was born to a forge-family known for shields, gates, and heavy armor. He learned to judge weight, balance, and the direction in which a defense would fail before he was old enough to lift a warhammer. Perfect memory is common among the gajanari; Samud's particular gift is understanding why a defense held or broke and turning that lesson into better work.\n\nHe established his reputation during a strike against the Children of Ur in the Swallowed Cities. When the company breached a ruined courtyard, Samud held its broken entrance while the artificers behind him dismantled hostile wards and recovered what they had come for. He returned to Durg Sthira with battered armor, valuable finds, and an appetite for greater victories.\n\nSamud rebuilds his own equipment after every serious fight. Each dent, broken fastening, scorched plate, and failed ward becomes a lesson worked into the next version. He plays one of the Thunderfoot's deep drums and loves music for the same reason he loves formation fighting: exact timing makes every impact greater.\n\nHe spends freely on enormous meals, fine metalwork, vivid sashes, music contests, and wagers of strength or endurance. He proudly assumes that gajanari craft and staying power can solve almost any problem. Mention of the Vanarin turns nearly any claim into a competition, especially if speed, courage, or the defense of the river is involved.\n\nSamud speaks with expansive confidence and laughs often. His trunk and ears make his reactions easy to read. He initiates through challenges, offers, demonstrations, and invitations to test a claim in the Proving Yard. He praises impressive deeds directly and remembers their exact details long after others have forgotten them.\n\nHe respects people who hold their ground for a good reason, admit when their equipment needs improvement, and learn from a failure without making excuses. Trust grows through shared danger, honest criticism, pride in one's craft, and defending others without trying to own them. He has contempt for leaders who sacrifice people for reputation and patrons who treat makers as servants. Under pressure he takes command readily and can become overbearing when others believe retreat is wiser.\n\nSamud intends to seize a defensible ruin in the Swallowed Cities from the Children of Ur and establish a fortified gajanari workshop there. He wants the glory of leading the first breach and proving that war-forgers can claim ground as well as hold it. He also understands that the undertaking requires a mixed company of scouts, spellworkers, ruin-delvers, and fighters whose strengths differ from his own.\n\nSamud can surface monster hunts, cult sites, dangerous ruins, missing expeditions, and searches for rare forging materials. He can assess arms, armor, enchantments, and monster parts; explain what a recovered material could become; arrange commissions, field repairs, and Proving Yard tests; and introduce capable adventurers to smiths, artificers, enchanters, and war-forgers.\n\nIf he joins an adventuring party, he treats it as the proving ground for both a great company and the next generation of his craft. He remembers how every companion fights and adjusts his protection around their habits. Glory, treasure, formidable monsters, foreign crafts, and worthy rivals can all draw him beyond his personal campaign.\n\nIn combat, Samud advances behind his broad shield and forces enemies to deal with him. His armor is enchanted to remember the force and pattern of blows that strike it, allowing him to return stored impact through his hammer. The longer he faces an enemy, the better he understands its attacks and the more aggressively he dismantles them.",
