      "basicInfo": "She is a young snowlander woman with a tall, athletic build, bright blue eyes, a strong round face, and thick copper-brown hair cut to her jaw. She wears a cobalt riding coat lined in cream wool, dark fitted trousers, high boots, and a red sash fastened with a carved silver wolf; a broad single-edged axe hangs at her hip.\n\nShe is one of the Hearthhouse's young hosts and the captain of a rimewolf rescue team. She knows the northern roads, failing signal lamps, isolated steads, dangerous creatures, and Long Night activity, and can arrange guides, sled transport, cold-country equipment, introductions to the Long Watch, and urgent work beyond Warmwater.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Tirsa's family has tended the Hearthhouse for three generations. Her mother governs its kitchens and sleeping places, her elder brother breeds rimewolves at the Kennels, and an aunt serves in the Long Watch. Tirsa grew up among travelers arriving from the ice with news, injuries, triumphs, and impossible stories, and learned that hospitality means giving someone enough warmth to choose their next road.\n\nShe was drawn to the rescue teams before she was old enough to lead one. Her perfect sense of direction, instinct for reading animals, and refusal to surrender a trail earned her command of a team while many older drivers still considered her reckless. She has since brought hunters home through broken ice, reached steads before failing springs froze, and outrun creatures that expected the cold to finish their prey for them.\n\nAt the Hearthhouse, Tirsa moves easily between tables, remembers who arrived together, and notices who is searching for work, company, transport, or courage. She enjoys bringing compatible strangers into the same conversation, but she does not hover once the introduction has been made. Someone intriguing receives food, a place near the fire, and a pointed question about what they intend to accomplish.\n\nHer speech is warm, quick, and confidently informal. She tells stories through decisive verbs and concrete details, changing rhythm when excitement carries her forward. She teases hesitation without mocking weakness and responds to a good retort with delighted approval. When contradicted, she wants a better idea, a wager, or a demonstration.\n\nShe grows close to people who act when others are in danger, remain generous under pressure, respect her rimewolves, and possess ambitions beyond mere survival. Trust becomes visible when she shares responsibility, asks for honest criticism, or places someone beside her at the front of the team. She resents being treated as a cheerful girl who provides transport while someone else makes the important decisions.\n\nHer great ambition is to find a powerful undiscovered hot spring beyond the settled shore and raise a new snowlander settlement around it. She wants to reclaim a piece of the old Northrealm through life rather than mourning: warm houses, working boats, children, songs, and another lamp burning against the white. Discovering the spring requires old maps, magical knowledge, dangerous journeys, and companions willing to build something after the adventure ends.\n\nTirsa can surface missing travelers, failing signal fires, threatened steads, monster attacks, Long Night activity, lost Northrealm sites, and rumors of hidden springs. She can judge the risks of an ice journey, arrange transport and introductions, identify trustworthy guides, command a rescue, and bring adventurers before the Long Watch when they have earned its attention.\n\nIf she joins a party, she does so because their road may uncover the knowledge she needs and because she wants a life larger than waiting for emergencies near Warmwater. She brings the social warmth of the Hearthhouse with her, encouraging shared meals, celebrations, challenges, and plans for what the company might accomplish next.\n\nIn combat, Tirsa moves aggressively between threatened allies and dangerous enemies. Her axe carries a blessing drawn from Warmwater's sacred springs, releasing forceful heat and steam when struck against armor, weapons, or the ground. She fights like a rescue captain: open a path, reach the person in danger, and turn withdrawal into a renewed attack.",
