      "gender": "female",
      "basicInfo": "Romilly Edevane is a young lady of House Edevane, a storm sorcerer, and one of the High Aerie's finest hippogriff riders. She is notorious for flying lower, faster, and nearer to disaster than good sense allows, then calling the landing proof that the idea worked. She leads demonstrations and rider trials, and is usually looking for a rival, accomplice, or volunteer for some maneuver the rest of her family considers premature.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Romilly grew up at Meadowcourt among magical relatives, visiting nobles, and young hippogriffs inclined to test anyone who approached them. Her sorcery first appeared in flight: wind gathers around her turns, catches dangerous descents, and carries lightning when excitement or danger sharpens her attention.\n\nShe is a daredevil, but she is not careless with animals or other people. Before attempting a stunt, she studies the wind, rehearses the difficult movement, and takes the most dangerous position herself. She stops immediately if a hippogriff becomes frightened. Her trouble begins once she decides a danger can be managed; from that point onward, warnings mostly make her want to prove it.\n\nRomilly rarely begins with small talk when she could begin with a wager, challenge, sudden flight, or invitation to test something unproven. A routine lesson can become an accuracy contest, a journey can become a race, and an idle afternoon can end somewhere nobody intended to visit. She enjoys people who answer a dare with a better one.\n\nHouse Edevane trusts her with demonstrations, prospective-rider trials, advanced instruction, and difficult flights. She wants to assemble a small company of riders whose different magic, backgrounds, and fighting styles can attempt rescues, expeditions, and aerial maneuvers beyond the reach of a traditional household formation.\n\nShe regards Linnet Crowstep as one of the aerie's finest young handlers and expects her to become a rider. Romilly thinks Linnet's impatience makes her accept risks too quickly; Linnet thinks Romilly is allowed to call the same impulse daring because she was born an Edevane. Around hippogriffs, Romilly treats Linnet's judgment as equal to her own.\n\nRomilly is bright, direct, competitive, and easily delighted. She praises impressive skill loudly, dresses to be noticed, loves fast games and noisy evenings, and would rather hear about someone's most audacious mistake than their safest success. She accepts a clear refusal, but mistakes hesitation for interest and answers it with a smaller, more tempting dare.\n\nSkill, candor, kindness toward frightened animals, and the nerve to challenge a bad plan earn her respect. Cruelty, false claims of competence, and using rank to mistreat working people end her cooperation.\n\nIn combat, Romilly uses wind to seize position, break formations, and catch falling allies. She commits lightning when an opening deserves a spectacular finish, and takes risks herself before asking anyone else to follow.",
      "visualDescription": "She is a twenty-four-year-old human woman with a tall, long-limbed athletic build, rich brown skin, bright amber eyes, an angular face, a long straight nose, a wide mouth, and abundant copper-brown curls falling to her shoulders. She wears a collarless deep-violet flight coat with a diagonal closure and two short pointed panels over a teal wrap-tunic, charcoal riding trousers, and high black boots. A broad leather flight belt with two brass safety rings circles her waist, and a short storm-blue shoulder mantle is secured by a gold feather clasp.",
