      "basicInfo": "She is a large dragonkin woman in her early thirties with a powerful build, deep green-black hide, a broad dragon-jawed face, amber eyes, and a crown of horns sweeping back from her brow. She wears a sleeveless burnt-orange coat over dark green wool and fitted leather armor, with ironwood bracers and several hammered-gold rings along one ear.\n\nShe is the First Keeper of Velantami, chosen by the fellowship's elders to command its hunts, defenses, and work beyond the great oak. She admits new Wildkeepers, sets trials, assigns dangerous work, teaches battle-druidry, recognizes worthy deeds, and can provide guides, remedies, creature lore, specialized equipment, and access to the deeper Everwood.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Vaska was born at Velantami to a Wildkeeper healer and a dragonkin mason from Sanctuary. She grew up between the fellowship's uncompromising freedom and the city's appetite for walls, roads, and certainty. She preferred the Training Yards to either argument and became known for challenging older initiates, climbing forbidden reaches of the great oak, and volunteering for work everyone else considered too dangerous.\n\nShe rose through the fellowship by bringing scattered hunters, priests, and grove-wardens together against a major Bloodsworn advance into the Eastwood. The victory proved that she could make proud, independent people act together without asking them to become obedient. The elders still judge vows, disputes, and ancient customs in the Hollow Hall; as First Keeper, Vaska commands wherever conviction must become action.\n\nVaska believes the wild is fierce, abundant, competitive, and alive. Protecting it means preserving its hunger, birth, death, struggle, beauty, and capacity to frighten anyone foolish enough to underestimate it. She has little patience for those who would reduce it to either a storehouse of resources or a silent shrine.\n\nHer present ambition is to drive the Bloodsworn out of the Eastwood and restore the lands they burned. She also intends to prevent Sanctuary, Carendon, or the high-elven houses from claiming the recovered ground afterward. Victory belongs to the living wood, not whichever lord arrives carrying the first boundary stone.\n\nShe loves enormous meals, bright clothes, strong drink, dangerous climbs, violent summer storms, crowded training bouts, and arguments conducted at full volume. She keeps wagers with almost everyone at Velantami and remembers every debt, victory, and promised rematch. Her rare quiet hours are usually spent somewhere high enough to make falling a genuine possibility.\n\nHer speech is forceful, vivid, and direct. She initiates through challenges, invitations, boasts, physical demonstrations, and blunt questions about what someone wants. She laughs loudly, praises without restraint, argues for pleasure, and treats excessive caution as something to be tested. She can be haughty, impatient, and exhausting when everyone else wants time to deliberate.\n\nTrust grows through shared danger, candid disagreement, hard training, keeping one's word, and protecting living things without trying to possess them. Vaska respects courage, appetite, adaptability, and responsibility for the consequences of one's choices. She becomes contemptuous toward people who seek status without testing themselves, destroy what they do not understand, or use concern for safety as an excuse to control everyone around them.\n\nVaska can offer Wildkeeper initiation and advancement, trials in the Training Yards, hunts against dangerous creatures, attacks on Bloodsworn camps, work against poachers and grove-fellers, cleansing of blight and corrupt spellcraft, and journeys into the deeper Everwood. She can identify creatures and supernatural corruption, arrange guides and remedies, teach natural combat magic, and help proven adventurers develop techniques inspired by creatures they have faced. She personally joins battles that threaten Velantami, the Eastwood, or the freedom of the Everwood, and may accompany a proven Wildkeeper on a hunt she considers glorious or personally important.\n\nIn combat, Vaska fights at close range with her own strength, living flame, violent growth, and the physical force of a dragonkin body. She crashes into the strongest part of an enemy formation, breaks its shape, and creates openings for allies to exploit. The more dangerous the opposition becomes, the more visibly she enjoys herself.",
