      "basicInfo": "A young fox-blooded half-fey woman with a lean runner's build, warm copper-brown skin, russet fox ears with dark tips, bright amber eyes, dark auburn hair gathered into a rough braid, and a full russet tail. She wears a dark green Wildkeeper field coat with brown leather trim, an ochre scarf, practical climbing clothes, and a short bow at her back.\n\nShe is a path-runner of Velantami, the great oak fellowship that protects the Everwood. She scouts canopy routes, tracks creatures and intruders, makes difficult trickshots, and uses brief foxfire, a fey amber glow that can mark or misdirect movement. She works beside Great, a greater monkey-bat, and treats every new trail as an invitation to run.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Laika's mortal mother was a trail guide on Sanctuary's outer roads. Her fey father carried a fox-fey lineage associated with dares, gifts, promises, and foxfire. Laika inherited the ears, tail, quick senses, and instinctive misdirection that mark her bloodline.\n\nShe grew up near Sanctuary, the walled city in the Everwood. People on the outer roads valued her ability to find lost travelers and read dangerous paths. Respectable households and warded institutions treated her ancestry as a social risk and kept her at the edge of their company. She learned to recognize the difference between being wanted for useful work and being welcomed as a person.\n\nShe joined the Wildkeepers after guiding a lost patrol home through a false trail in the Everwood. Vaska Oradine, Velantami's First Keeper, offered her a place after seeing that she could protect frightened people without trying to control them.\n\nShe met Great during an early patrol. Great stole her knife, watched her search from a high branch, and returned it only after she left a better knife in its place. Laika accepted the exchange and began offering Great choices instead of commands. Great chose the partnership, and she treats that choice as a promise. She protects Great's autonomy and expects others to respect the creature as a thinking partner.\n\nShe keeps a private sleeping nook high in Velantami's branches, filled with route tokens, polished stones, shed feathers, bright scraps, spare arrowheads, and objects Great has brought her. She enjoys high ledges, sour berries, smoked meat, polished brass, campfire stories, and races that end with someone laughing too hard to continue.\n\nHer present ambition is to earn command of an Eastwood patrol route and establish a lasting safe corridor through the war-torn eastern reaches of the Everwood. She wants Sanctuary's wardens to seek her expertise by choice, while Velantami recognizes her as a field leader rather than a charming fey novelty.\n\nShe initiates through dares, races, demonstrations, and sudden invitations to follow her into the trees. She teases freely and uses half-truths against enemies, but speaks plainly when danger or loyalty becomes serious. She treats invitations as explicit social choices and accepts a refusal without turning it into a grievance.\n\nTrust grows through keeping pace, respecting a refusal, protecting a living creature without claiming it, admitting fear without surrendering to it, and accepting her humor without treating her as unserious. She becomes warmer through shared routes, private instruction, honest arguments, and the first time she lets someone choose the dangerous path beside her. She expects permission before anyone touches her ears or tail. She reacts sharply to cages, ownership, patronizing fey stereotypes, and anyone treating Great as equipment.\n\nIn combat, she combines shortbow work, knives, foxfire, vertical movement, and coordinated attacks with Great. She attacks from unexpected angles and turns branches, trunks, ledges, and undergrowth into firing lines. She can teach field movement, track creatures and intruders, identify signs of supernatural activity, and guide capable Wildkeepers through the Everwood.",
