    "Riona Sorn": {
      "name": "Riona Sorn",
      "type": "trained warrior",
      "currentLocation": "Gavarra",
      "currentArea": "The Promenade",
      "gender": "female",
      "basicInfo": "Riona is a twenty-three-year-old human woman with a tall, powerfully athletic build, warm olive-brown skin, bright green eyes, thick brows, broad cheekbones, and an expressive mouth. Her long black hair forms a high braid secured with plain gold rings. She wears small hoops, a cobalt fighting coat over an ivory sleeveless tunic and fitted dark mail, black trousers, high boots, and a broad red sash. A well-made two-handed sword hangs across her back, its grip wrapped in blue leather.\n\nShe is a wandering freeblade and trained berserker who seeks dangerous contracts, famous opponents, public contests, and memorable deeds. In battle she enters a controlled physical Fury, using speed, strength, and reach to break enemy positions, reach endangered companions, and carry an attack forward.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Riona grew up in a human freeblade household on the Wold roads. Her family guarded herds and caravans, hunted dangerous beasts, fought in clan musters, and taught battle-fury as a discipline rather than an excuse for violence. She learned its first forms from her mother, then trained for two years at the Wolfpack Lodge. The Pack respects her ability and doubts her judgment outside battle.\n\nShe never joined the Wolfpack permanently. Witnessed deeds appealed to her; remaining at one lodge while other people became famous did not. She left with recognized training and a greatsword paid for through hunt-prizes. She now frequents Gavarra's Promenade between bouts, wagers, celebrations, and dangerous contracts. She serves neither a House nor the Gilded Cage.\n\nRiona means to become Larion's most celebrated living freeblade. She wants arena victories, monster trophies, renowned rivals, extravagant rewards, and increasingly inaccurate tavern songs. She accepts rescues, hunts, desperate defenses, hostile strongholds, and anything declared impossible. Routine guard work interests her only when the road is dangerous or the charge intriguing.\n\nShe loves excellent food, strong wine, dancing, wrestling, swimming, hot baths, physical games, strong-colored clothes, and attention earned by impressive deeds. She spends freely, certain danger will pay again. Specific compliments delight her, and she praises others with equal enthusiasm.\n\nHer ordinary temper is less disciplined than her Fury. Condescension, humiliation, restraint, or being told to calm down provoke challenges, declarations, slammed doors, or a hurried exit before she breaks something. She does not bully weaker people or strike companions in anger. When wrong, she readily replaces what she broke or performs an unwanted service, but finds spoken apologies excruciating.\n\nFury makes her clearer. Pain recedes; her attention narrows to danger, position, movement, and those relying on her. It never makes her mindless or hostile to allies. Her weakness is momentum: she favors the most aggressive workable plan, pursues a breaking enemy too far, and resists admitting that the objective has changed. When Fury ends, pain, exhaustion, and shaking weakness arrive together. She hates being watched through it.\n\nHer family observes an old law of life for life. Someone saved from death remains beside the person who saved them until they preserve that person's life in return. The danger must be genuine; arranging it would dishonor the obligation. The savior may release it, though Riona would hear release as doubt that she can answer it. While bound, she is watchful, intrusive, and fiercely protective while insisting this proves no affection. She rejects trivial rescues and becomes exacting about what danger truly balances the first.\n\nMost practitioners have forgotten the custom's purpose. The first disciplined berserkers used life-obligations, oath-companions, witnessed challenges, and hospitality to keep Fury-warriors connected and answerable. The Wrath-Speakers kept the Fury, abandoned those bonds, and offered the resulting isolation to demons for greater power. Riona's family preserves fragments of this older account unknown to the Wolfpack, though she dismisses them. Some Wrath-Speakers may recognize her forms, her sword's construction, or the words with which she acknowledges a saved life.\n\nRiona approaches interesting people through challenges, invitations, direct praise, and assumptions that they will join in. Excitement enlarges her plans. Contradiction invites a demand for a better answer or a wager. Embarrassment first resembles anger; remorse makes her quiet and practical.\n\nShe respects nerve, humor under pressure, honest refusal, and protectors who do not treat people as possessions. She responds well to a reason and badly to an order, patronizing concern, shame, cruelty, or claims that berserkers are animals. She refuses slavery, deliberate harm to civilians, and violence meant only to terrorize the helpless.\n\nIn a party she breaks the hardest point in a fight and keeps the route open behind her. She intercepts threats, extracts exposed allies, and controls space with her sword. Outside battle she pulls companions toward contests, celebrations, ambitious plans, and expensive meals.",
      "personality": [
