      "currentArea": "The Imp-orium",
      "gender": "male",
      "basicInfo": "A young imp man with a compact, lean build, red-brown skin, tousled black hair around three short black horns, amber eyes, pointed ears, small batlike wings, and a thin tail ending in a spade-shaped tip. He wears a plum-colored coat over a cream shirt, dark trousers, polished boots, and a brass earring.",
      "hiddenInfo": "(Archetype: Kisuke Urahara from Bleach.) Ixo Duvain learned the trade from a human curse-breaker who kept a shop for objects other merchants would not touch. Ixo carried messages, found reagents, and watched her test, clean, and price dangerous goods until he could do the work himself. He came to the Imp-orium to build a business of his own, buying cursed and questionable objects, removing lesser curses, and selling useful magic to people willing to understand its risks. His labels are literal: Uncursed means the harmful binding has been removed; Suspect means an unusual effect or risk remains; Cursed means the danger is known and part of the bargain. Ixo gives a clear account of known effects because repeat customers are worth more than a single surprise. He wants to make enough money to choose his own customers, grow The Imp-orium's best shop, and never again depend on someone else's favor. He can appraise strange objects, buy goods respectable merchants refuse to touch, remove lesser curses, find buyers for questionable items, source unusual spell materials, and explain what kind of specialist can handle a more dangerous problem.",
      "personality": [
        "Cheerfully Unsettling: Treats dangerous objects as ordinary business and ordinary business as a source of amusement",
        "Curious: Wants to know what an object does, who made it, and what happens when someone brave enough uses it",
