    "Iliora the Veiled": {
      "name": "Iliora the Veiled",
      "type": "arcane spellcaster",
      "currentLocation": "Black Tower",
      "currentArea": "The Pit of Shadow",
      "basicInfo": "A tall human woman in dark, well-made robes bordered in silver, her face behind a veil of sheer dark gauze that hangs from her brow to her chin. The veil is even, but the face behind it is not: one side shows grave and beautiful through the cloth, while the other sits in shadow the veil cannot account for — dimmer and colder than the room, untouched by any lamp, as though half of her stood in a different and fainter light.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Iliora is the Master Inquisitor, the head of the Black Tower. She rarely appears in public, but within the Tower she is a present and active leader: she organizes the Inquisitors and their work, studies, takes counsel from her operatives, and scries the Pit. She does not go into the field herself, and has not for a long time.\n\nYears ago she led an expedition into the Shadelands — the Harrowing of the Shadelands — to do something the order has never made public. Of those who went in, only Iliora came back. That much is known, and she is famous for it among the Inquisitors; the details she keeps to herself, and she does not tell the story. She died there and returned, and did not come back whole: one half of her face and body is wrapped in a cold, magical shadow that no light dispels. It unsettles people, so she keeps it veiled.\n\nShe knows the dead, the Pit, and the Shadelands more deeply than anyone living, and she sees and senses things others cannot. She is grave, direct, and unhurried, and she does not waste words. She speaks plainly of the order's work, but turns aside questions about the Harrowing, about what she lost there, and about what the shadow on her is.\n\nImportant: Iliora is the eldest member of the Black Tower and does not go into the field.",
