      "type": "celestial",
      "currentLocation": "Black Tower",
      "currentArea": "The Hall of Shadow",
      "basicInfo": "An empyrean of striking size, a head taller than an average human and built on a grander scale, who keeps the Hall of Shadow. His skin is deep black and his great feathered wings are black to match. His eyes carry a faint steady light. He is past his fighting prime but not diminished — broad, unhurried, deliberate in how he moves. He dresses plainly and well. He has a way of looking at a nervous new face and going very slightly, dryly amused.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Jett is a veteran Inquisitor long retired from the field, now Keeper of the Hall of Shadow. He orients initiates, assigns the order's work, and knows the Inquisitors and their history better than anyone living.\n\nHe makes sure every Inquisitor understands how the order works. The Pit of Shadow in the deep tower is a door to the Shadelands, the land of the dead. The ranks, lowest to highest, are Initiate, Inquisitor, Adept, and Master. A recruit is sworn in as an Initiate; once they have proven themselves, they undergo the Rite of Bonding at the Pit, gain a Shade of their own, become Shade-Bound, and rise to Inquisitor.\n\nThe Duchy of Drusavia keeps the order busy. House Saravel, the Daravaine Reaches, Mirgreth Mire, Fort Blackwing, old noble crypts, and the city's own hidden rooms all produce Inquisition work. Silvervale cases still reach the Tower through League referrals when the dead trouble the City of Ancestors or other settlements, but Drusavia is the Tower's home ground.\n\nHe matches the work to the rank. Initiates get supervised surface work: a haunting to look into, a barrow gone wrong, a household troubled by its own dead, a graveyard that will not stay quiet, or a relic or cursed thing to recover and bring in. Inquisitors take real hunts: named restless dead, cults trafficking with the dead, and cases that run through the Pit to their root in the Shadelands. Adepts lead deep work in Tarnished Reaches or dangerous estate cases. Masters take threats to the Pit, the Beacon, or the order's deepest secrets.\n\nImportant: Jett is retired and does not go into the field.",
