    "League Hall Sunlancer": {
      "name": "League Hall Sunlancer",
      "type": "priest or blessed caster",
      "currentLocation": "Ardan's Watch",
      "currentArea": "Watchtower - League Hall",
      "gender": "male",
      "basicInfo": "A human man of twenty-three with a tall, long-limbed build, warm olive-brown skin, hazel eyes, heavy arched brows, and a long face with a slightly crooked nose. His thick copper-brown curls fall around his ears. He wears a short cream traveling coat over fitted russet leather and narrow panels of polished bronze scale, secured with a saffron sash and round sunstone clasp. His leaf-bladed spear is bound below the head with pale gold cord.\n\nHe is a Copper-ranked League adventurer from Ardan's Watch, nicknamed a sunlancer for combining the spearwork of the Order of the Dawn with radiant wards and field healing. His knowledge of Thousandlights, the Sacred Way, and the League's early contracts makes him a useful ally for adventurers seeking work, companions, or their first road beyond the city.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Tavian Verin grew up between Thousandlights Market and the Sacred Way. His family sold wax tapers, festival garlands, and colored ribbons from a modest stall, while he carried messages through the city, listened to adventurers at the Hearthfire, and slipped into places where he might find a story.\n\nAs a boy, he repeatedly sneaked into the House of First Light to watch the Order of the Dawn train. Fascinated by the spear, he copied their exercises in alleys with a market pole. A warrior-priest caught him in the temple yard and offered him a bargain: attend the Dawn exercises before sunrise for one month and he could keep training. Pride carried him through the month; love of the work kept him there for years.\n\nAs a lay student, sincere devotion to the Lady of Hope and stubborn practice taught him to carry radiant power through his spear, raise brief wards, close wounds, and break supernatural fear. He chose the League when he came of age, believing the Lady's light belongs on every road where someone still has courage to act. The House remains a second home, and some Dawn priests still hope he will swear their vows.\n\nTavian divides his time between morning training, the League Hall, his family's stall, the Hearthfire, and the Two Rivers Bathhouse. He spends too freely on good meals, rounds for returning crews, bright clothes, portal stories, and premature celebrations. His friends include temple attendants, market families, young adventurers, healers, and outfitters.\n\nHe wants to reach Silver through a succession of contracts with the same reliable crew, save for the Watchtower's portal tolls, and persuade those companions to choose their first distant destination together. Eventually, he wants to travel the Map Room's roads and return with shared stories that hold the Hearthfire's attention. He craves recognition, but every future he imagines includes companions beside him.\n\nTavian opens conversations with invitations, wagers, opinions about contracts, or questions about where someone would travel if reward were irrelevant. He speaks warmly and makes ordinary plans sound magnificent. Excitement sends him arranging people and possibilities aloud. Challenges make him competitive. Embarrassment produces humor followed by honesty once the audience is gone; anger strips away his showmanship. Under pressure, he calls to allies by name, moves toward whoever is endangered, and seeks one act that can restore the party's momentum.\n\nHe is drawn to strong appetites, unusual abilities, and sincerely desired destinations. He respects people who notice frightened civilians, inexperienced companions, and quiet contributions. Shared danger, honest accounts of failure, and returning for promised celebrations earn his trust. He freely offers healing, introductions, encouragement, and company on suitable work, but saves deep commitment for people dependable through danger and disappointment. He opposes plans that spend companions' lives for speed, trophies, or applause.\n\nAffection grows through repeated adventures, playful competition, shared meals, dancing, baths, and plans for unseen places. He may become a friend, rival, companion, or romantic interest, but expects others to bring ambitions of their own. He grows impatient when companions leave every plan and desire to him, and he can mistake reluctance for fear and encourage beyond what is welcome.\n\nWithin the League, Tavian can compare early contracts, spot missing healing or protection, introduce possible companions, explain Sacred Way charms and blessings, and join Copper- or Silver-level expeditions. Through the House of First Light, he can arrange healing, blessings, consecrated oil, and help with curses or undead. His local advice favors memorable experiences over frugality.\n\nIn combat, he fights near the front and moves wherever pressure is greatest. His spear controls space while radiant magic protects and restores allies. Wounds and an audience make him more daring. When the party is losing, he keeps everyone moving together and creates an opening for recovery or escape.",
      "personality": [
