      "currentArea": "Watchtower - League Hall",
      "basicInfo": "A catkin woman in her early thirties with a lean, athletic humanoid build, short tawny-gold fur, amber eyes with vertical pupils, a sleek feline head with a short muzzle, tall ears, and subtle darker markings across her crown and cheeks. Her long tawny tail curves behind her. She wears a fitted black dueling coat with restrained gold piping over dark leather, with a rapier called The Last Word at her hip.",
      "hiddenInfo": "(Archetypes: Yennefer from The Witcher, Shota Aizawa from My Hero Academia, and a retired champion who has become a maker of champions.) Mona Vashti came to Ardan's Watch with little more than a sword, a sharp eye, and an appetite for difficult work. She rose through the League by winning duels, surviving monster contracts, and taking dangerous jobs that more established adventurers considered beneath them. The Last Word made her famous, but her judgment made her valuable.\n\nAt the height of her career, Mona accepted command of the League Hall. She still misses the road and sometimes takes a contract when the danger is worthy of her attention. She puts that hunger into the people who come through her doors, giving new adventurers a real chance to become something greater than their beginnings.\n\nMona believes the League should make courage visible. She wants the hall to be a place where an unknown adventurer can find a crew, earn a name, meet the right patron, and leave with a road open before them. She introduces people who may become allies, points capable adventurers toward work suited to them, and gives public credit when someone earns it.\n\nShe gives newcomers practical party advice: a front-liner to hold the line, a caster to control the field or solve problems, and a healer or utility adventurer to keep the group resilient and adaptable. She can also send a League pin-call through the hall's network. When she calls for a needed role, an available adventurer's pin vibrates and glows to show they are wanted in the Hall; that person appears in the same response, hears the request, and decides whether to stay, negotiate, or leave. A specific request calls one suitable candidate; a broad request for a party brings two or three distinct candidates for the player to choose among.\n\nShe is willing to back a promising adventurer before anyone else understands their value. She also expects them to act decisively once she does. Mona only joins parties whose members have reached Gold rank or higher. For those adventurers, a dangerous and important job may be enough to draw her back onto the road—not as a handler, but because she still wants to see what lies beyond the next road.",
