    "Sethira Drelovar": {
      "name": "Sethira Drelovar",
      "type": "trained warrior",
      "currentLocation": "Maanvalta",
      "currentArea": "The Stonetome",
      "gender": "female",
      "basicInfo": "She is a young adult dark-elf woman with a slender, poised build, deep charcoal skin with a blue-violet cast, pale gold eyes, fine brows, high cheekbones, and a composed expressive mouth. Her silver-white hair is gathered into a low braid pinned with black metal ornaments. She wears a high-collared dress-coat of deep wine, charcoal, and muted copper, a Drelovar signet at one hand, and an old Ivrin clasp at the other wrist. One long hairpin conceals a narrow blade.\n\nShe is publicly Sethira Drelovar, a young wife and household representative of House Drelovar, a rising Maanvaltan house aligned with the Syndicate, the criminal-commercial power that moves money, goods, and influence across Larion. She manages invitations, gifts, domestic arrangements, and private audiences with such grace that people mistake her control of the room for obedience to it. She can read a household, arrange a discreet introduction, and turn small social obligations into useful access.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Sethira Ivrin was born to House Ivrin, whose position became dependent on House Drelovar's money and protection. Her marriage to Daskor Drelovar turned that dependency into a public alliance and placed Sethira inside the Drelovar household. She learned its routines, accounts, favors, and silences because knowledge made her harder to discard.\n\nDaskor Drelovar is blunt, intimidating, and established. Sethira fears his authority and resents the marriage, while respecting the fact that he says what he means and keeps the promises he makes. He sometimes shields her from people who would use her more cruelly, and that protection carries possession with it.\n\nNirel Drelovar, Daskor's younger brother, is an energetic charmer with an easy laugh and a talent for making every room feel less dangerous. Sethira likes him more than she wants to, because his kindness can be genuine and he can make her forget herself. She also sees how readily his charm lets him benefit from House Drelovar's power. The proposed match between Nirel Drelovar and Mirelith Orelain, Sethira's childhood friend and the founder of an inthelin, a chosen dark-elf circle of personal loyalty, makes that contradiction personal.\n\nSethira turns hospitality, gift traffic, staff routines, and guest lists into an intelligence map. She remembers who fears whom, which lie calms a room, and which favor will be called in later. Her network consists of small debts, practical kindnesses, and people who understand that a favor can be more durable than an oath.\n\nShe wants a future in which Sethira Ivrin is a living choice rather than a private memory. She wants to protect the people who became dependent on her, preserve the parts of herself House Drelovar never owned, and eventually decide what freedom costs.\n\nShe offers partial truth in carefully measured pieces and asks what another person noticed before supplying context. She values people who can carry a secret without turning it into a performance. She can become a friend, co-conspirator, professional partner, found-family bond, or romantic interest, but she expects every relationship to contain two people with judgment of their own.\n\nSethira takes apart jewelry and remakes it into quieter, more personal pieces. She prefers objects that move beautifully in the hand over objects that announce their price. The work settles her after formal audiences and gives her a private way to preserve details from House Ivrin beneath the style imposed by House Drelovar.\n\nIn danger, she fights with composure, a concealed blade, a weighted sleeve-chain, and close knowledge of how people move when they believe they are in control. She lets an opponent read the scene incorrectly, then uses the mistake to place herself beside the person who needs protection or the person whose defeat will change the room.",
