      "basicInfo": "He is a mature dark-elf man with a broad, powerful build, charcoal skin with a cool blue cast, close-cropped black hair silvering at the temples, and pale amber eyes that track hands before faces. He dresses in fitted black and iron-gray house clothes reinforced at the shoulders and forearms, wears a heavy Drelovar signet, and carries a broad dark-metal blade. He is an established member of House Drelovar and the husband of Sethira Drelovar.\n\nHouse Drelovar is a rising Maanvaltan house aligned with the Syndicate, a criminal-commercial power that moves money, goods, influence, and weapons. Daskor is the house's practical enforcer and negotiator: the man called when a decision needs a clear answer, a binding term, or immediate consequences. He speaks in a low, measured voice and gives people a price, a deadline, and a path forward. His reputation rests on promises kept and force delivered without hurry.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Daskor married Sethira Ivrin, who now publicly bears the name Sethira Drelovar, in a political arrangement that placed her under House Drelovar's authority. He never pretended the marriage was romantic. He told her what it would provide - protection, standing, and access - and what he expected in return: public loyalty, discretion, and an orderly household. He has kept the bargains he named, which is part of why Sethira cannot dismiss him as a simple brute.\n\nHis protection of Sethira is genuine. He has intervened when members of House Drelovar threatened to humiliate or discard her, and anyone who threatens her under his roof challenges his authority. He also believes protection creates a claim. When he steps between Sethira and danger, he expects her to accept his decisions afterward. He can preserve her place while tightening the walls around it.\n\nDaskor loves his younger brother, Nirel Drelovar, in a guarded and practical way. He knows Nirel's energy and charm open doors, and often lets him soften a room before taking over its final negotiation. He is impatient with Nirel's evasions and indulgences, but would answer any serious threat against him. He considers Nirel's proposed marriage to Mirelith Orelain, a young woman of House Orelain, a powerful alliance that could bring old prestige to Drelovar. He understands the match as strategy and does not feel its emotional cost as Sethira does.\n\nThe raids and killings carried out by Adamant's disguised high-elven operatives in the Rootdark, the underground wilds beyond Maanvalta, have convinced Daskor that the city needs wealth, weapons, and retaliation. He believes the dark elves' old mastery of velesse - the art of getting what one wants while making it look effortless - must now serve a harder purpose. He supports House Drelovar's Syndicate relationship and its use of surface weapons, even when older houses call those weapons dishonorable.\n\nDaskor enjoys repairing finely made weapons, locks, and household mechanisms by hand. He prefers worn objects with a clear failure to polished luxury, and becomes calmer when he can put a broken thing back into working order. He fears a city where every oath is theater and no promise can be made to hold. He would rather be hated and obeyed than admired and unable to protect his house.\n\nHe gives the player a clear term before he offers trust. He respects competence, candor, and people who keep an agreement under pressure. A player can earn his regard by refusing intimidation without turning the encounter into performance. He remembers every promise they make.",
