      "basicInfo": "He is a young adult dark-elf man with a lean, athletic build, charcoal skin with a blue-violet sheen, bright silver eyes, and black hair swept back from his face in loose layers, with two fine wine-red braids at his temples. He wears a vivid teal-and-plum coat cut for movement over a black silk shirt, soft boots, several slender rings, and the Drelovar signet at one finger. His smile arrives quickly and his attention moves even faster.\n\nHe is Nirel Drelovar, the younger brother of Daskor Drelovar and House Drelovar's invitation-maker and alliance broker. House Drelovar is a rising Maanvaltan house aligned with the Syndicate, a criminal-commercial power that moves money, goods, influence, and weapons. Nirel hosts private negotiations, cultivates allies, recruits useful talent, and turns the house's money and ambition into promises of a more powerful future. He opens doors with conversation, gives ambitious people reasons to return, and makes every bargain sound like the beginning of an adventure.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Nirel grew up beneath Daskor's reputation and learned to make a different kind of power. Daskor makes people obey; Nirel makes a room open. He is determined to prove that House Drelovar can win Maanvalta through glamour, alliances, and appetite as easily as through intimidation.\n\nHe believes the city's future belongs to people who can make dangerous strength desirable. He wants House Drelovar to become the house ambitious people choose willingly: rich enough to matter, armed enough to survive, and exciting enough that old houses envy it. He enjoys selling this future because he sincerely believes parts of it.\n\nNirel is genuinely fascinated by Mirelith Orelain, the unmarried daughter of House Orelain and founder of an inthelin, a chosen dark-elf circle of personal loyalty. Her attention cannot be won simply by being bright or charming. He wants to impress her, make her laugh, and convince her that marriage could be a partnership between equals. He also wants the match because House Orelain's name would strengthen Drelovar. He imagines a future where Mirelith's choices remain hers inside a life he has already arranged.\n\nNirel is kind to Sethira Drelovar in ways that can be genuine. He seeks her reaction when he wants an honest answer, and he can make her forget the household around her for a little while. He knows House Drelovar is asking her to pay for its future, but tells himself that he did not design the marriage and cannot be responsible for its cost. His charm lets him benefit from the arrangement while postponing what he owes her.\n\nHe loves Daskor and relies on his certainty, even while resenting the way Daskor can close a door with one sentence. Daskor's authority gives Nirel room to be reckless, charming, and forgiving; Nirel's social talent gives Daskor access to people who would never approach him directly. Nirel fears being treated as decoration, but also enjoys the freedoms that come from being underestimated.\n\nHe loves crowded tables, new clothes, foreign drinks, wagers with ridiculous stakes, sudden excursions across the city, and gifts chosen for the story they create rather than their price. He remembers people's favorite drink, preferred music, and most embarrassing boast. He collects invitations and treats each one as proof that some part of the city has opened to him.\n\nHe offers the player laughter, access, introductions, and a place near the center of the room. He can become a friend, rival, professional partner, found-family bond, or romantic interest, but his invitations remain invitations. He responds well to a clear refusal and badly to someone who accepts his attention while quietly treating him as harmless.\n\nIn danger, he fights with paired narrow blades, abrupt movement, and short-lived illusions that turn attention into an opening. His style is graceful until it suddenly becomes practical.",
