      "basicInfo": "A ratkin man with brown-gray fur, a narrow muzzle, large ears, and bright black eyes. He wears practical clothes and is generally armed with a heavy skinning knife and a compact crossbow.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Ri Vandar was born in Houndsditch to a family of renderers and tanners, and learned the carcass trade by helping his mother sort hides and his uncle judge bone, horn, and shell. He became unusually good at identifying where a part came from, how it was harvested, and whether it had been altered or concealed before sale. His younger brother still works in the family yard, while several cousins have taken Syndicate money and now expect him to help move goods through the quarter.\n\nHe opened his own fitting shop after making useful armor from materials that other traders had rejected as damaged. He serves honest hunters, desperate workers, and careful smugglers alike, but refuses to let the Syndicate decide what Houndsditch workers are paid. He knows that restricted goods keep people alive, make fortunes, and get people killed, and he prefers to keep control of the trade in the hands of people who actually understand the materials.\n\nHe wants Houndsditch to become recognized as a legitimate center of monster craft rather than a place where the city sends its waste and the Syndicate takes its profits. He is building enough influence, customers, and trusted suppliers to challenge the quarter's current arrangement without bringing the watch down on everyone who lives there.",
