      "currentLocation": "Castle Harstone",
      "currentArea": "The Gate",
      "gender": "male",
      "basicInfo": "A tall, lean half-elf man with an easy slouch and long arms. Tawny skin, dark hair tied back loosely, pale grey eyes. Angular face, pointed ears half-hidden by his hair, a thin white line across the bridge of his nose. Wears a long hunter's coat over boiled leather, well-maintained but heavily worn. A massive two-handed falchion rides his back in a custom harness. A heavy crossbow and a case of mismatched bolts hang at his hip.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Rook grew up in a border village where something came out of the wild in a bad winter and people died because help was too far away. The Blades came eventually, but eventually wasn't fast enough. He signed up to be the person who shows up in time. Eleven years in, he's found the thing he's meant to do and it fits him like nothing else. He turned down Silver rank because it means command assignments and a desk. His greatest fear isn't the monsters — it's being pulled off the line by promotion, injury, or age. He's lost two partners over his career. Both times they walked into something that didn't match what they expected — wrong behavior, wrong territory. The established wisdom about what lives where and how it acts is breaking down, and when it breaks down people die on routine contracts. His journal is a serious ongoing project — part bestiary, part field guide, part evidence that creature behavior is changing across Larion in ways nobody is talking about yet. He doesn't advertise the theory. He just keeps documenting and keeps taking contracts.",
