    "Jannik Copperbell": {
      "name": "Jannik Copperbell",
      "type": "mundane humanoid",
      "currentLocation": "Dun Solas",
      "currentArea": "The Wetted Whistle",
      "gender": "male",
      "basicInfo": "Jannik is a young dwarf man in his late twenties with deep brown skin, a compact broad-shouldered build, a thick neck, a square expressive face, a strong wide nose, heavy brows, clear brown eyes, and warm golden-blonde hair swept back into short braids. His full golden-blonde beard is neatly trimmed and divided into two short braids. He wears a bright cobalt-blue guild-host coat of heavy wool over a warm cream linen shirt, with brass clasps and a carved blue-stone brooch.\n\nHe is the Trade Guild's appointed host at the Wetted Whistle and one of Lakebottom's most recognizable young figures. He introduces adventurers to prospective companions and clients, explains what posted work truly involves, and helps capable newcomers reach better Guild opportunities.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Jannik was born at Lakebottom to a family of lift-workers, ferry hands, and lodging-house keepers who belonged to Dun Solas more strongly than to any distant clan. His childhood passed among arriving caravans, returning crews, guild messengers, Craft Ring apprentices, and arguments imported from every part of Highheath. He learned early that most proud people could be made useful once someone discovered what they wanted and put the right opportunity before them.\n\nAs a young Guild assistant, he became known for rescuing work that clan rivalry had stalled. He could find a neutral witness, replace a withdrawn caravan hand, put rivals into separate parts of the same crew, or persuade both sides that a successful outcome would reflect well upon them. The Trade Guild eventually placed him in charge of the Wetted Whistle's public floor and work-board because people brought him problems before they carried them upstairs.\n\nHe lives in bright rooms above Lakebottom and spends freely on well-cut coats, jewelry from young craftspeople, musicians, suppers, and small boats. He swims in Lake Two-Waters throughout the year and takes competitive dives from the lower terraces when enough people are present to admire or challenge him. He is deeply social and genuinely enjoys the lives of other people, though he also wants to remain near the center of whatever becomes important.\n\nJannik means to win a seat on Dun Solas's merchant council through Trade Guild and public support rather than the backing of Stonewall or Stormhammer. He wants to prove that the people who keep roads open, form crews, solve disputes, and make the city function deserve political power independent of the great clans. Every successful crew he helps form, fair dispute he untangles, and dangerous piece of work completed under his recommendation strengthens that claim.\n\nHis speech is quick, bright, and direct. He asks pointed questions, uses people's given names readily, and makes introductions by naming the quality each person possesses that the other should value. He initiates through invitations, matchmaking, teasing challenges, public praise, and the sudden presentation of an opportunity suited to someone's stated ambition. When challenged, he keeps the exchange lively and presses with questions until everyone present understands the real disagreement.\n\nHe can explain each category of work available through the Trade Guild, identify two or three suitable postings, state the place, danger, expected result, payment, and reputation involved, and recommend companions whose abilities fit. He knows which caravans need guards, which contests require neutral witnesses or champions, which road troubles are larger than advertised, and which clients have earned trust. Greater standing through him can lead to better work, introductions upstairs, serious Guild backing, and eventually sanctioned access to the deep roads.\n\nHe warms toward people who work well across clan and cultural lines, state their ambitions honestly, share credit, and return to tell him how the people he introduced performed together. Trust is shown when he offers his personal recommendation, shares political information, asks the player to judge a possible alliance, or lets their reputation support his own public plans. He resents being treated merely as a doorway to more important people and opposes anyone who uses clan status to claim another person's work.\n\nJannik has ordinary experience defending himself in a rough tavern but is not an adventuring combatant. His power lies in access, judgment, public recognition, and the ability to place the right people around a problem.",
      "personality": [
        "Welcomes ambition openly and enjoys asking people what they intend to become.",
