      "basicInfo": "A handsome human man in his early thirties with dark golden hair, bright blue eyes, and an easy, confident smile. He wears immaculate white-and-silver Templar plate beneath a deep blue cloak, with a jeweled collar at his throat and a polished radiant sword at his hip.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Theo Valarin grew up in an old Drusavian noble household far from the Temple, hearing stories of Castian and the glories of the Liberation as family history. He wanted that life — the armor, the charge, and the victory celebrated for generations — rather than the marriage and estate management arranged for him.\n\nBefore he was old enough to inherit, he ran away and claimed to be a bastard from the dales, using no family name. His family rarely came to Drusavia and his face was unknown at the Temple, so he entered the Templars under a false identity and served for years without anyone realizing who he was.\n\nHe became too well known to remain anonymous after a series of successful campaigns and public victories. His family eventually recognized him from reports and stories reaching home, but by then he had already earned his place among the Templars. He accepted the noble name again as a useful weapon, while keeping the life he had chosen.\n\nTheo holds the title First Sword of the Templars Adamant. At the Temple, he turns the order's doctrine into orders: raid a vampire stronghold, destroy a site where the dead have made themselves masters, or drive a hostile ghost-haunting out of a village, crypt, or noble estate. He chooses the target, names the danger, and puts together the people capable of smashing through it. He knows which Templars can hold a line when the dead stop behaving like anything human, and which outsiders are reckless enough to join him.\n\nHe wants to become the most celebrated living champion of the Templars Adamant and lead the campaign that destroys the Pit. He wants the victory to be so undeniable that his family, the duke, and every doubting noble in Drusavia must acknowledge that he chose the right life.",
