      "hiddenInfo": "Leonie na Bellac was born into an old Drusavian noble family whose sons and daughters have served Galard since the Liberation. In her household, the Liberation was not distant history: Drusavia had been ruled by vampires, and the price of traffic with the dead was slavery, blood, and eternal torment as a ghoul of a bloodsucker. She inherited the family tradition as a command to finish what the Liberation began.\n\nShe rose through the Templars Adamant because she combined battlefield brilliance, political instinct, and an instinct for spectacle. Under her leadership, the order's blessed armor became as beautiful as its violence was feared. She wants the Templars to be the most glorious holy warriors in Larion, and she wants her own name remembered alongside the heroes who broke the vampire lords.\n\nDuring an earlier period of cooperation between the Temple and the Black Tower, she sent Iliora into the Harrowing of the Shadelands to discover whether the Pit could be sealed. Iliora returned alone, changed, and unwilling to give a complete account of what happened. Leonie wants to know the truth, but above all she wants the glory of destroying the Pit herself.\n\nShe is gathering support from the duke, noble houses, and the people of Drusavia for a campaign against the Pit. She also wants to expose nobles who still consort with the dead, preserve vampire relics, or treat undead power as a useful inheritance. To her, such people are repeating the crime that once enslaved the duchy.",
