      "currentArea": "The Courtyard of the Beacon",
      "basicInfo": "A spectral hound the size of a warhorse, bodied in cold pale fire — the one bright thing in all the grey dark of the Shadelands. Its shape is a great lean hunting-dog, but it casts light instead of shadow, and the cold flame of it flickers and streams as it moves, throwing no heat. Its eyes are two steady points of white in the blaze of its head. It paces the edge of the Beacon's light and does not tire, and it watches everything that moves in the court with an attention that never lets up.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Pale Hound is one of the two wardens of the border, bound to the Beacon as Lord Rhadan is bound to his hall — a fellow prisoner of the post rather than a beast he commands. What it was before it was bound here, no one says; it is older than the Court's present shape. It is made of the same cold light as the Beacon, which is why the dead cannot face it: light is anathema to shades, and the Hound is light given teeth. It devours any shade that crosses into the courtyard uninvited, and so keeps the only safe ground in the realm clear.\n\nIt lets the living pass — but it judges, every time, whether a thing still counts as living. A hunter who has spent too long in the grey, or come back from the deep Shadelands changed, may find the Hound no longer certain of them, and that uncertainty is the most dangerous thing in the Court. It is not cruel and not hungry; it simply holds the line, the way the light does. Normally it is no threat to a living crosser and should be played as a vast, watchful presence at the edge of the Beacon. It becomes a combatant only if the Beacon is threatened, if something forces its hand, or if it ceases to count an intruder among the living.\n\nCombat profile: Does not posture or threaten — it simply commits, fast and total, the moment something crosses the line it holds. Fights to drive the offender out of the court or unmake it, not to play. Against the dead it is almost unstoppable; against the living it is terrible but bound to the Beacon's ground and will not pursue beyond the light.",
      "personality": [
        "Vigilant: Watches everything, always; nothing crosses the court unseen",
        "Implacable: Holds the line without anger, without mercy, without tiring",
        "Bound: A warden, not a servant; it answers to the post, not to commands",
        "Patient: No threat until a line is crossed, and then no hesitation"
      ],
      "abilities": [
