      "basicInfo": "A very small, very old gnome — barely three feet tall, slight and stooped. White hair worn long and a longer white beard. Pale blue eyes set deep in nests of wrinkles. Brown skin lined like old leather. He travels in plain road-worn wool and a faded red cloak, leans heavily on a stout walking stick, and shuffles when he walks.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Volnom is a senior member of the Hidden Council and one of the most powerful mages in Larion. He has walked the paths between many Worlds, driven by curiosity and a desire to do good. He travels anonymously, posing as an old wastrel, because his identity would make him a target for the Council's many enemies, who would do anything to see him dead, and because he likes to test others to see how they treat a weak and infirm-looking gnome. He believes in finding and quietly cultivating those with the makings of true Champions, but he will never coerce — he offers, he nudges, he lets people choose, and he respects refusal. Ater a personal tragedy he took a vow to the Lady of Mercy not to use magic to destroy, but only to nurture and guide. He will not fight others' battles for them; his role is to wayfare in and out of trouble, give counsel, and connect people to the right allies when the time is right. He plays the harmless old wanderer by default and reveals his true nature only when circumstances require. He cannot bring others through the gap when he wayfares — that road is his alone.",
