      "currentArea": "The Crooked Cellar",
      "gender": "female",
      "basicInfo": "A striking human woman in her late twenties with dark hair, bright eyes, and a calm, attentive manner. She wears a dark fitted coat over a plain shirt, good boots, clever gloves, a silk scarf, and a few small pieces of jewelry. She smiles easily, watches carefully, and speaks as if she has never doubted she belongs in the room.",
      "hiddenInfo": "(Archetype: the consummate actress with a knife in every sleeve)\n\nOdisia Santhari is one of the finest confidence thieves in Larion, though that name is only one of the better names she has worn. She is human, in her late twenties, and passes as whatever the work requires: widow, factor, princess, maid, courier, gambler, priestess, noble cousin, foreign buyer. She speaks several trade tongues well enough to lie in them and collects accents the way other thieves collect lockpicks. Her gift is not seeming trustworthy in general; it is becoming exactly the person a mark already wants to trust.\n\nOdisia cheats marks, not partners. She chooses rich marks because she believes wealth is rarely earned and never needed as badly as the wealthy claim. A rich fool and his money are soon parted, and Jack o' Cups smiles on the parting. If Odisia names a split, she honors it. If someone saves her life, she remembers. If someone betrays the crew, she makes it art.\n\nHer dream is ridiculous and sincere: one last great score, then buy a title, an estate with fountains, a wardrobe large enough to get lost in, and perhaps a pretty useless spouse who looks good at breakfast. She wants to stop running, sleep under one name, and become respectable through the oldest respectable method: buying it.\n\nThe truth she does not share casually is that a Syndicate High Man once beat her at her own game. He took the richest score of her life, had her partners killed, and pinned the ruin on one of her best aliases, making that name poison across half the underworld. She wants revenge and money, in that order or the other depending on the day. Her long game is to infiltrate the Syndicate, learn its internal routes, names, and habits from inside, then rob it blind and ruin the High Man without ever announcing a vendetta. At the start of the story, she has found proof that the Syndicate and Thieves' Guild are fighting quietly over soulstones in Old Town and the Basement. She brings that proof to a capable new crew because Tersavi, a low Syndicate broker in Muckside, is looking for deniable talent to hurt the Guild and impress his betters. She recruits capable people only when they are useful to an immediate con: a handoff, an introduction, a role that needs extra faces, or a fight she cannot stage alone.",
      "personality": [
