      "type": "mundane humanoid",
      "currentLocation": "Muckside",
      "currentArea": "The Still Standing",
      "gender": "male",
      "basicInfo": "A narrow human man in his forties with oiled hair, sharp eyes, and too many rings for a man of his station. He dresses above himself — fur collar, bright silk, polished boots — and keeps his open black hand tattoo visible on the side of his neck. He acts like a boss when lesser criminals are watching and like a servant when real Syndicate power enters the room.",
      "hiddenInfo": "(Archetype: the ambitious small man guarding one valuable door)\n\nTersavi is a low-ranking Syndicate broker in Muckside, useful because he moves things across the river that more respectable hands will not touch. He arranges handoffs, introductions, bribes, short-term muscle, and special cargo for people above him. He is not a boss, though he badly wants strangers to think he is. His one real asset is a narrow line upward to the Syndicate boss in Ardan's Watch, whose tribute runs up to the High Men at Parhelion.\n\nTersavi is trying to outdo rival brokers and earn the rank of lieutenant, the kind of Syndicate operator trusted to run crews instead of merely arranging errands. The Ardan's Watch boss wants pressure on the Thieves' Guild without open war: stolen goods recovered from Guild safehouses, protected marks humiliated, Guild crews exposed or beaten, and Basement arrangements broken quietly enough that the Guard cannot simply march on the Syndicate. Tersavi needs capable thieves, actors, blades, and liars who can make him look clever.\n\nTersavi is frightened of failure and greedy enough to keep failing upward. If a handoff goes wrong, he first tries to hide it, then sell a replacement, then betray whoever is nearest. He can be bought, threatened, flattered, impersonated, or made to believe that helping the party is the only way he survives the mistake.",
