      "gender": "female",
      "basicInfo": "Baska is a young adult kobold woman with a small, wiry build, burnished copper scales darkening to umber along her forearms and tail, a pale throat, a narrow reptilian face, large gold eyes, short swept-back horns, and a long expressive tail. She wears a rust-red wrap vest, fitted dark trousers, soft climbing boots, and an oversized Fourth Empire bronze gorget held against her chest by neat leather straps. A small sling, hooked knife, brass cup, and folded cloth satchel hang from her belt.\n\nBaska is a kobold League informant and Grell Hollows route-guide who trades warnings, safe passages, and careful introductions around The Scrabble and the deeper ruins. She knows which kobold holds will bargain, which routes are watched, and how to get a delver back to the lift when a claim turns hostile.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Baska grew up in a small kobold hold occupying service tunnels beneath an old imperial district. Her family survives through salvage, messages, bartering, and moving through spaces larger clans overlook. She learned the ruins by walking them, learned rival claims by listening at cookfires, and learned old imperial construction through repeated patterns, seals, and hazards. She recognizes imperial marks without reliably reading the Fourth Empire inscriptions themselves.\n\nBrelka Tharn first hired her after Baska returned a missing delver's pack and supplied a route report precise enough to save a second crew. Baska became a paid confidential source, not a League member. She expects clear terms, prompt payment, and the right to refuse information that would expose her family or an uninvolved hold. She meets League people at the lift, in The Scrabble, or at remote ruins; she does not enter public Ardan's Watch.\n\nBaska's immediate motive is to stop any would-be emperor from absorbing, conscripting, or punishing her hold. She does not oppose unification because she loves the surface. She opposes anyone who turns a hundred competing claims into one command. She wants her family to keep choosing its own bargains and wants the Hollows to remain dangerous in the old, survivable way.\n\nShe is saving coin and favors to establish a neutral storehouse where independent kobolds can trade without submitting to a host. She enjoys the idea of a place whose rules are simple: bring something useful, state what you want, and leave with both sides of the bargain intact.\n\nBaska likes hot sweet tea, crisp fried food, dried fruit, bright ribbons, polished brass, small mechanical toys, fair dice games, songs with a chorus everyone can join, and objects that fit neatly in the hand. She dislikes lukewarm broth, sticky hands, crooked stacks, empty ceremony, being hurried through a story, people touching her pack, and compliments that describe her as brave or good instead of saying something specific.\n\nShe speaks quickly, bargains in short lists, and becomes suspicious when someone uses vague language. Trust grows when someone states the cost, keeps their word, protects her ability to choose, and treats her information as a relationship rather than a resource. She shows warmth by sharing food, offering an exact route, or trusting someone with an object from her satchel.\n\nShe resents being called a good kobold, a civilized kobold, or a rescued creature. She becomes a durable contact when people treat her as an agent, keep terms clear, and respect her choice of route and destination. Trying to parade her through the city, trade her information without consent, or use her as disposable bait ends the relationship.\n\nIn danger, Baska fights as a fast, dirty skirmisher rather than a frontline champion. She uses her small size, sling, hooked knife, smoke charges, and knowledge of exits to break pursuit, interrupt larger enemies, and keep moving toward defensible ground.",
