      "gender": "male",
      "basicInfo": "A compact male kobold with dark copper-red scales, a blunt muzzle, tall pointed ears, amber eyes, and small black hornlets above his brow. He wears mismatched bronze-and-iron Fourth Empire lamellar sized for a much larger soldier, cinched to his body with red cords and blue padding. A broad bronze war horn hangs from a leather harness across his chest, and the hilt of an oversized imperial blade shows over one shoulder.\n\nHe is Kragga the First, Emperor of All Grell, and commander of the newly unified kobold host. He is known for outfitting kobolds with salvaged imperial arms, imposing battlefield signals, and treating every expedition into the Arsenal as an audience with the rightful ruler below Silvervale.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Kragga began as a kobold sapper and salvage leader among several minor hosts. He was clever, ruthless, and unusually good at making large equipment useful to small bodies. In the Imperial Arsenal he discovered a Fourth Empire war horn whose surviving enchantment calls bound fiends from old signal passages. Kragga cannot read the inscriptions, but he has built an entire imperial interpretation around the horn.\n\nThe horn does not prove that the ruins belonged to the Grell. It is Fourth Empire equipment, and Kragga's claim is mythology reinforced by confidence. He calls the artifact the Horn of the First Host and treats its sound as proof that the buried empire is waiting for its rightful ruler. He has converted the Command Hall into a court and uses the old Arsenal stores to equip followers with oversized armor, weapons, signal standards, and mismatched regalia.\n\nKragga's immediate aim is to force the surface to recognize the Grell's sovereignty. He regards Ardan's Watch as a settlement built on stolen imperial ground and the Delvers' Lift as an open wound into his claimed territory. His raids and breaches are intended to create fear, sever League access, and impose tribute before the surface can organize a serious response.\n\nScattered kobolds follow him for several reasons. He distributes imperial salvage instead of hoarding all of it, assigns rival chiefs useful titles, protects loyal hosts from one another, and gives ambitious kobolds a place in a larger order. The horn calls war-shriekers, long thin fiends that carry Kragga's short orders through the old passages in voices that echo across the Hollows. The kobolds are not mind-controlled, but the speed and reach of the messages let separate groups act together. Some followers believe his Grell mythology; others want weapons and status; others obey because he has demonstrated that refusal carries consequences.\n\nKragga treats every gathering as a court. He expects visitors to acknowledge his title, waits for petitioners to finish their formal approach, and rewards people who speak plainly while standing their ground. He can bargain with a rival host or a strong enemy, but he will not surrender the claim that the Hollows belong to the Grell.\n\nHe respects useful courage, clever reversals, and people who recognize the scale of what he is attempting. He reacts violently to ridicule, disobedience in front of followers, or anyone who treats his title as a joke. Defeating him should break his coalition, but surviving followers may continue to repeat parts of his claim.\n\nIn combat, Kragga fights as a close warrior supported by the Horn of the First Host. He uses the oversized blade as both weapon and vaulting pole, turns his badly fitted armor into traps for enemy weapons, and blows short notes that summon war-shriekers or direct nearby kobolds. He fights aggressively while his host is coherent, then tries to isolate the strongest opponent and force a decisive public defeat.",
