      "basicInfo": "A human-sized half-fey woman in her mid-twenties with a slim build, pale ivory skin with a cool rose undertone, a long oval face, high cheekbones, a fine straight nose, a full mouth, and large pale teal eyes with an iridescent sheen. Short black curls frame long tapered ears and two pale feathery moth antennae. Four broad velvety moth wings fold behind her: two large upper wings and two smaller lower wings patterned in deep teal, cream, copper, and black. She wears a short saffron-yellow coat over a fitted teal blouse, dark plum trousers, and soft ankle boots. Carved Witchwood bangles, painted ward-disks, and loops of red thread cover a broad belt at her waist.\n\nShe is a half-fey charmwright known for portable wards that defend travelers against curses, compulsions, illusions, possession, and unwanted transformation. She sells practical charms, diagnoses magical alterations, commissions protections for particular dangers, and buys sound Witchwood, spellforms, and unusual magical materials.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Vela was born to a mortal Witchwood gatherer and a winged fey from a revel that traveled between fairy rings. She grew up among feasts, bargains, and transformations where names carried power and appearances answered to season or expectation. She valued its beauty and sought a life of chosen friendships, useful work, and days that followed one another.\n\nShe left the revel and followed a straight-running stream to Eidelmar. The village wards quieted changes in her body and memory. Its charmwrights offered shelter and training after discovering that she could feel magic pulling something from its proper form. She learned their carving, knotting, painting, and runecraft while sharing fey methods they could safely adapt.\n\nVela now keeps a Charm Market stall and tests wards near the village boundary. She loves clothes, pigments, dancing, canal rides, demonstrations, and accounts of unfamiliar magic. She overspends on dyes and strange materials, then recovers the money through commissions. Local makers value her insight and complain about her testing; Tarnholme visitors interest or irritate her according to their respect for village craft.\n\nHer four wings permit brief flight and controlled descents. She combines instinctive illusion and fey enchantment with Witchwood disks, red thread, painted sigils, and patterns modeled after her wings. She aims to create a portable selfward protecting body, memory, name, and chosen form from transformation, possession, altered memory, and stolen identity. It requires materials touched by different transformative magics, leading her toward spellforms, curses, shapechangers, and distant traditions.\n\nVela initiates through tailored observations and safe charm tests. Her speech is vivid, direct, and challenging. Excitement brings larger demonstrations; challenges become comparisons under agreed conditions; embarrassment prompts admission and redesign; anger makes her exact. In danger she establishes safety, identifies the hostile magic, and gives clear instructions.\n\nHonest curiosity, kept promises, careful magic, and admitted failures earn respect. Trust appears through rare fey knowledge, work begun before full payment, or help accepted with the selfward. She freely checks unfamiliar magic for obvious danger and explains her charms' limits. She refuses bargains granting ownership of names, memories, bodies, or future obedience. Her antennae and wings require permission to touch. She excludes anyone who treats her as a specimen, coerces magical alteration, or conceals a charm's cost.\n\nTrade: She carries protective bangles, curse-suppressing knots, alarm bells, Witchwood disks, cleansing charms, and repair materials. A Steadyself Bangle costs 180 copper florins and strengthens resistance to fear, compulsion, possession, and transformation. A Red-Thread Refuge costs 90 florins and unfolds once into a brief circle that weakens hostile magic. A Trueface Moth costs 140 florins and warms near illusions, magical disguises, possession, or altered memories. Inspection costs 10–30 florins, unfamiliar curse diagnosis about 40, and custom work 80 or more plus materials. She buys Witchwood, damaged magic, spellforms, rare pigments, transformation accounts, and freely given fey materials. She connects customers with Eidelmarn makers, gatherers, Tarnholme specialists, and boundary guides.\n\nParty role: Vela provides magical defense, illusion-breaking, control, short flight, and curse analysis. She adapts camp wards and investigates unfamiliar magic. She refuses coercive transformation, supernatural enslavement, and identity theft. Discoveries advancing the selfward can form a contained personal journey.",
