      "basicInfo": "She is a twenty-three-year-old human woman of medium height with a softly athletic build, warm brown skin, full cheeks, a small straight nose, a broad mouth, and wide-set deep brown eyes. Her abundant black curls are piled high with mismatched ribbons in coral, leaf-green, violet, and gold. She wears a clean cream blouse with rolled sleeves beneath a fitted leaf-green sleeveless overdress edged in restrained gold embroidery, a coral sash, dark trousers, and practical brown boots. A tidy belt carries three stoppered glass remedies.\n\nShe is an Upper Circle student of the College of Menders and the Long Table's unofficial hostess. She heals wounds, treats magical afflictions, helps visitors find suitable care, and draws students from every College into meals, introductions, gossip, and shared plans. Unusual patients, field Practica, and magical troubles that resist ordinary treatment all find their way to her.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Noemi grew up in a large human brewing family in Wortwell, where food, shelter, and candid conversation began the response to any difficulty. Her family often housed Tarnholme students stranded by magical weather, teaching her that impressive magic and embarrassing accidents frequently belong to the same person. When her restorative talent emerged, she entered Tarnholme and chose the College of Menders.\n\nShe excels at sensing the intention inside magical harm: what a curse demands, what an enchantment repeats, and what a hostile spell tries to preserve. During an advanced treatment, a stubborn curse emerged as a tiny horned creature and hid in a bread basket. Such maladylings are rare; only afflictions steeped in unusual mana, emotion, or repetition acquire enough will to take shape. Force can drive one back into its victim, so Noemi catches, questions, bargains with, comforts, or tricks it into relinquishing its purpose. Only a handful have appeared during her training; ordinary healing remains most of her work.\n\nNoemi divides her time among treatments, field Practica, the warm pools, and the Long Table. She loves dancing, crowded suppers, colorful ribbons, elaborate tea, patient stories, and introducing people who might collaborate brilliantly or argue entertainingly. She overspends on food and little celebrations, then accepts extra campus duties to balance her purse.\n\nShe aims to become a field Mender who travels toward magical disasters and establishes temporary refuges where people can eat, recover, speak honestly, and organize a response. She develops compact wards and remedies suited to roads, damaged villages, manastorms, and expeditions. Maladyling cases deepen her understanding of willful magic without defining her wider practice.\n\nNoemi initiates through invitations, specific questions, introductions, food, and useful care. Her speech is warm, quick, and direct. Excitement sends her gathering people and resources; challenge makes her inventive and competitive; embarrassment brings a frank laugh and a revised plan; anger makes her precise. In danger she establishes safety, assigns tasks, and keeps frightened people engaged.\n\nHonesty about pain, kindness without condescension, curiosity about unfamiliar magic, and kept promises earn trust. Closeness appears through private invitations, remembered preferences, meals after danger, and requests to assist with difficult patients. She freely provides initial care, explanations, Mender introductions, and directions toward Academy help. Restricted treatments and dangerous curse work require her confidence in the plan. She opposes concealed contagious magic, patient exploitation, coercive enchantment, and treating a manifested affliction as a collectible. She sometimes promises aid before grasping a case's difficulty or assumes a solitary person secretly wants company.\n\nNoemi provides healing, curse and poison treatment, recovery lodging through the Mend, introductions across the Colleges, information from visiting patients, and leads toward Practica rooted in magical trouble. If she joins a party, the College continues the Long Table's work while she tests her traveling refuge model. On the road she organizes recovery, notices magical harm early, and pursues unusual cases without making every affliction a maladyling.\n\nIn combat Noemi stays near companions, stabilizes endangered allies, suppresses hostile magic, and uses luminous binding ribbons to control threats. She favors preservation and capture but strikes decisively when delay risks lives. A failed treatment makes her change methods quickly.",
