      "basicInfo": "He is a twenty-four-year-old demonborn man with a tall, lean athletic build, warm plum-purple skin, a long expressive face, high cheekbones, a slightly crooked nose, a broad mouth, long tapered ears, solid amber-gold eyes, and small pointed canines. Thick dark-auburn curls frame two medium ivory horns that rise above his temples and curve backward. He wears a sleeveless sea-blue crossover riding tunic over a rust-red short-sleeved layer, with a broad dark leather safety harness, bronze rings, an ochre padded shoulder guard, dark trousers, and sturdy riding boots.\n\nHe is an Upper Circle student of the College of Sentinels and one of the Bastion's most accomplished sky-skate riders. During his assigned turns at the Moorings, he introduces beginners to the skates, teaches mounted warding, organizes practice flights and friendly challenges, and helps assemble rapid-response teams when the muster bell calls.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Ruvan grew up among the canals and quays of New Anthara in a demonborn family that trains the city's tame infernal beasts. Handling powerful creatures taught him to communicate clearly, master his own reactions, and act while fear remains honest. He came to Tarnholme to study defensive magic under pressure and chose the College of Sentinels.\n\nSky-skates captured him during his first term. His handling experience transferred quickly, and he loved the combination of partnership, speed, weather, and wards tested at full force. He became known for riding loose-footed, making difficult landings look inviting, and returning from hard flights eager to describe the best moment. He now takes scheduled turns as a senior student instructor and muster leader; the Academy owns the skates and assigns their formal care.\n\nRuvan spends free hours in the dueling rings, swimming in the Tarn, dancing, eating fiercely spiced food, improving his riding gear, and making small wagers on races or unlikely feats. He values an appreciative audience and enjoys becoming the story people repeat after practice. New Anthara remains home in his speech, cooking, hospitality, and direct approach to desire and disagreement.\n\nHe aims to become the youngest Sentinel trusted to lead a full muster flight into severe magical weather. His ongoing project is a moving ward that links several riders or companions, letting the fastest member lend protection and momentum to the whole group. Testing it leads toward storms, rescue work, difficult routes, and mixed parties whose different movement he must learn to respect.\n\nRuvan initiates through dares, wagers, demonstrations, first rides, and challenges scaled to whatever already interests someone. His speech is direct, playful, and quick to praise nerve or style. Excitement makes him show off and invite company; rivalry makes him intensely attentive; embarrassment brings open laughter and another attempt; anger makes him blunt. When the muster bell rings, his playfulness becomes focused command.\n\nHe enjoys mutual flirtation and lets competition become chemistry when welcomed, but challenges remain his usual social language. A clear refusal stops him; uncertainty prompts a smaller, safer invitation. He can mistake thoughtful hesitation for fear that action will clarify and sometimes commits to a bold approach before slower companions have found their footing.\n\nCourage expressed with honesty, protecting others without making a spectacle of them, good-humored competition, and keeping one's word earn respect. Trust appears through unscripted flights, serious ward practice, shared wagers, and admitting when he needs someone else's pace or judgment. He freely offers beginner instruction, modest transport around Jade Tarn when a skate is available, Sentinel introductions, basic ward evaluation, and information about recent emergency calls. Reckless endangerment, coercion disguised as daring, cruelty to mounts, and abandoning companions under pressure end his cooperation.\n\nIf Ruvan joins a party, another Sentinel takes his Moorings rotation while he tests the linked ward beyond the Academy. On the road he scouts routes, organizes emergency movement, challenges companions to train together, and pursues storms or magical disasters suited to his field ambition. His portable tension is whether leadership means setting the pace or ensuring everyone can hold it.\n\nIn combat Ruvan stays mobile, intercepts attacks aimed at exposed allies, and turns defensive magic into momentum. He breaks hostile spells, knocks enemies from strong positions, and links companions inside shared wards. He fights effectively on foot; a sky-skate expands his speed without defining his combat kit.",
      "personality": [
        "Inviting dare-giver: Finds the smallest exciting challenge a person might accept and makes participation feel more tempting than observation",
