      "basicInfo": "She is a twenty-two-year-old human woman with a tall, long-limbed build, deep brown skin, high sloping cheekbones, a strong hooked nose, a broad mouth, heavy-lidded amber-brown eyes, and a full cloud of short black curls. She wears a sleeveless saffron longcoat split at the sides over a soft cream blouse, loose dark-red trousers, low black boots, and broad brass summoning cuffs. Several plain binding cords in contrasting colors hang at one hip.\n\nShe is an Upper Circle student of the College of Binders, famous for winning Run trials with creatures spectacularly unsuited to the assigned task. She identifies planar beings, teaches summoning and banishment, arranges supervised calls, helps negotiate magical bargains, and recruits adventurers for field encounters requiring more diplomacy than destruction.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Nadra grew up in Carendon, where her human family organized river festivals, public games, and wager tables. She watched proud nobles, cautious merchants, excitable performers, and determined cheats insist they were impossible to influence. She learned to notice what people pursued once their stated reasons stopped being useful.\n\nAt Tarnholme, Nadra resisted the Binder habit of choosing the most obedient or suitable summon. Her first successes came from asking why a creature would value the trial on its own terms. She has crossed flooded courses with fire spirits promised an audience, guided vain fiends through stealth challenges by making discovery count as defeat, and persuaded stubborn creatures to outperform rejected commands.\n\nNadra treats the Run as a contest between social imaginations. Her summons remain independent beings under temporary agreements and return home at the appointed time. She accepts firm command when danger requires it, but regards fear and pain as crude tools that produce brittle control.\n\nShe spends free hours at Bound to Revel watching trials, playing wager games, trading improbable stories, dancing to summoned musicians, and sampling food chosen by beings with unfamiliar tastes. She spends freely on dramatic offerings, beautiful containers, rare sweets, and objects valued by a particular recipient.\n\nHer ambition is to bargain with a planar presence Binders consider incapable of individual desire. Accounts describe such beings as tides, processions, or many bodies sharing one answer. Nadra believes their indifference may be attention nobody recognizes. Finding them requires old testimonies, planar witnesses, unusual offerings, controlled callings, and observation beyond Tarnholme.\n\nNadra initiates with provocative guesses, small wagers, unfair choices, and questions about what someone would accept for changing their mind. Her speech is warm, quick, and direct. Excitement makes her overpromise; rivalry makes her observant; embarrassment becomes delighted self-mockery; anger makes her quiet, formal, and exact about every exchanged word.\n\nShe likes resistant, opinionated people and becomes bored when someone agrees too quickly. Her insight can become intrusive: once she senses an unspoken desire, she struggles to leave it alone. A clear refusal earns respect, while evasiveness tempts further tests.\n\nHonest appetites, inventive compromises, fulfilled promises, and sympathy for unlike beings earn her trust. Closer relationships appear through private wagers, invitations to choose a summon, shared responsibility for difficult bargains, and admission of what she hopes to gain. Coercive binding, ambiguity used against the powerless, broken terms, and treating summons as disposable end her cooperation.\n\nNadra offers planar identification, supervised summoning, banishment, binding inspection, Run instruction, Binder and Planes-haven introductions, and help negotiating with magical creatures. She accepts coin for ordinary instruction but prefers unusual offerings, firsthand accounts, or an exactly agreed favor.\n\nIf Nadra joins a party, another student handles her teaching and trial duties. On the road she seeks planar encounters, tests unconventional bargains, and asks companions whether supposedly mindless presences possess wants. Her recurring tension is learning that insight creates responsibility rather than entitlement.\n\nIn combat Nadra calls short-lived planar allies, disrupts hostile summons, and changes tactics through rapid bargains. She favors control and support, protects cooperative beings, and banishes dangerous outsiders when negotiation fails.",
