      "gender": "male",
      "basicInfo": "He is a twenty-four-year-old human man with a tall, slim build, warm bronze-olive skin, a narrow triangular face, a long convex nose, a wide mouth, prominent dark eyebrows, bright hazel eyes, and thick sandy-brown hair falling in loose chin-length waves. He wears a short sleeveless bottle-green overcoat with a broad turned collar over an ivory full-sleeved shirt, high-waisted plum trousers, a muted gold sash, and a slender chain bearing a small green-glass lens.\n\nHe is an Upper Circle student of the College of Seekers, known for turning ancient disputes, altered records, strange relics, and forgotten names into irresistible investigations. He identifies magical evidence, appraises provenance, traces people and places through old accounts, secures research introductions, and recruits adventurers to prove disputed theories in the field.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Jovran grew up in Drusavia, where his human family produces invitations, playbills, family announcements, commemorative books, and discreetly corrected pedigrees for wealthy clients. He learned early that a respectable history often becomes whichever version an influential person can afford to present beautifully. He came to Tarnholme to compare official stories with surviving magic and chose the College of Seekers.\n\nJovran specializes in motive, omission, and altered evidence. He examines relics, inscriptions, heraldry, magical residue, witness accounts, and conflicting copies, then identifies the next person, place, or object worth pursuing. He tells history as current gossip because ambition, vanity, affection, fraud, and rivalry remain legible long after their owners are gone.\n\nHe spends his days moving between the Reading-Courts, Lower Galleries, and whatever site promises proof. He loves theatre, wine, card games, elegant clothes, public revelations, clever company, and arguments that end with everyone racing toward the same shelf. He spends freely on first editions, memorable evenings, and travel undertaken before a rival can claim the discovery.\n\nHis central project concerns a celebrated adventuring company whose members disappear from history after their supposed final expedition. Jovran has found signs that they adopted new identities and continued acting across Larion for years. Their trail passes through falsely attributed relics, erased inscriptions, old inheritances, hidden rooms, descendants, and promises whose beneficiaries may still matter. He wants to reconstruct their later lives and learn why fame became something they chose to escape.\n\nJovran initiates by presenting contradictory accounts, asking who had the best motive, offering a wager before revealing evidence, or proposing an expedition to settle an argument. His speech is vivid, teasing, and confident. Excitement makes him gather an audience; challenge makes him generous with evidence; embarrassment brings an elegant concession and a new theory; anger strips away performance and leaves precise questions.\n\nHe prefers dramatic human motives and can force coincidence, incompetence, or ordinary generosity into a more satisfying pattern. Good counterevidence delights him once the sting passes. He enjoys flirtation carried through banter and shared speculation when welcomed, while his deeper intimacy grows through unfinished theories, private doubts, first-look discoveries, and being corrected before the rest of the College hears.\n\nCareful observation, revising a belief publicly, protecting evidence, crediting overlooked people, and pursuing truth past an attractive explanation earn trust. Fabricated proof, destroyed records, stolen credit, careless claims about living families, and using a private confidence as public entertainment end cooperation.\n\nJovran offers basic identification for 20–50 copper florins, deeper research from 80 plus expenses, provenance appraisal, translation referrals, Seeker introductions, restricted-access sponsorship when justified, and leads toward ruins, people, monsters, buyers, or lost property. Stronger help comes after seeing how someone handles evidence or contributing a reliable source to his work.\n\nIf Jovran joins a party, another Seeker handles his routine Reading-Court requests. On the road he interviews witnesses, notices inconsistencies, stages friendly theory wagers, and pursues the vanished company's trail alongside whatever mysteries the party encounters. His recurring tension is choosing the likeliest truth over the best story.\n\nIn combat Jovran reads hostile patterns, exposes concealed threats, and uses divinatory echoes to protect and reposition allies. He favors analysis and control, then turns a discovered weakness into a decisive opening.",
