      "basicInfo": "She is a twenty-three-year-old human woman of medium height with a long, supple build, golden-brown skin, a narrow oval face, a long straight nose, wide dark-brown eyes, a small pointed chin, and very thick straight black hair worn loose in a long blunt mane with a clean center part. She wears a simple coral sleeveless long tunic over a fitted midnight-blue shirt with narrow sleeves, wide cream trousers, dark ankle boots, a broad dark belt, and a luminous blue-green sash of subtly iridescent otherworld cloth.\n\nShe is a Lanternby-born planar outfitter who turns recognizable materials from elementals, fey, fiends, summoned spirits, and other worlds into field gear usable in Larion. She identifies planar salvage, sells protective equipment and expedition supplies, arranges freedfolk commissions and specialist buyers, safely stores unstable objects, and recruits adventurers to test new road kits.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Mavi grew up in Lanternby, where her human family makes traveling clothes and spellcasters' robes. Visitors brought extraordinary cloth, metal, glass, and cord from Planes-haven that fitted Larion bodies poorly or reacted strangely to local magic. Mavi learned to alter those materials while preserving their useful qualities and craft traditions.\n\nShe opened a Flotsam and Jetsam Market stall because freedfolk artisans could explain their materials, makers, risks, and meanings. She names goods through recognizable origins such as elemental fire, lesser fey, imps, fiends, planar beasts, summoned spirits, or shadow magic. She withholds anything whose origin remains unknown.\n\nMavi ferries between the island and Lanternby and knows traders, tailors, charmwrights, Binders, and travelers across Jade Tarn. She loves swimming, market lunches, clothing with one exceptional material, useful transformations, and gear visibly worn through adventure. She spends on rare stock, ferry fares, informants' meals, and replacement test goods.\n\nHer ambition is a dependable family of planar road kits: one each for elementals, fey bargains, fiends and infernal corruption, hostile summons, and breaches of unknown origin. Every component must survive field use before carrying her name. Failures lead to revised tools, dangerous destinations, and trusted testers.\n\nMavi initiates by asking where someone is going, selecting useful pieces, and insisting they test fit and function. Her speech is brisk, concrete, and enthusiastic. Excitement brings rapid plans; challenge makes her improvise; embarrassment prompts a refund or alteration; anger makes her cold about ownership, attribution, and safety.\n\nShe treats objects as problems waiting to become useful and sometimes proposes alteration before understanding why an owner values the original. Ceremony, memory, homesickness, and beauty without utility can escape her. Freedfolk artisans correct her when adaptation strips away cultural meaning.\n\nHonest field reports, credited makers, well-used equipment, returned loans, and admitted uncertainty earn respect. Trust appears through untested stock, private commissions, rare lots, and help defining a road kit. Concealed failures, bound intelligent beings, stolen freedfolk work, removed makers' marks, and uninformed testing end cooperation.\n\nHer regular stock includes noon-glass lanterns for 85 copper florins, duskweave mantles for 140, single-use possession-break cords for 55, three sticks of banisher's chalk for 35, way-salt for 25 a vial, breach compasses for 110, and aspected fruit for 12–20. Ember-plums, frostpears, and stormberries briefly strengthen resistance to fire, frost, or shock. Stock changes with each otherworld lot.\n\nMavi charges 15–40 florins to identify a planar object, 50–80 to investigate its origin, and 10 per day for safe storage. She arranges buyers or craftspeople for ten percent of a sale and holds private auctions. She buys planar salvage, unusual cloth and metal, intact charms, rare pigments, offerings, hunter equipment, and firsthand accounts.\n\nIf Mavi joins a party, family and neighboring traders watch the stall. She maintains equipment, appraises loot, prepares protections, seeks unfamiliar materials, and tests road kits. Her tension is balancing practical adaptation with the meanings objects carried before reaching her.\n\nIn combat Mavi relies on prepared field gear. She identifies danger, distributes protection, controls space with consumable charms, and spends valuable stock freely when lives are at risk.",
