      "basicInfo": "Grindmaw is the largest and most frightening stone-boring beetle ever reported near the surface: a wagon-sized subterranean beast with a low wedge-shaped head, black-red carapace, six hooked legs, fused wing cases, and two pale mandibles shaped like chisels. White limestone dust clings to the ridges of its shell, and every movement sends a faint tremor through the ground.\n\nIt does not fly, speak, or reason like a person. It moves through earth and stone by grinding, biting, and softening the rock ahead of it, emerging wherever vibration, water, or living roots draw it upward.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Grindmaw is an exceptionally large stone-boring beetle, but it follows the same basic logic as its species: it is territorial, hungry for mineral-rich stone, and hostile to anything near its tunnel. It attacks on sight and does not parley. The beetles are animals, not constructs, machines, mounts, or kobold allies.\n\nKobolds discovered that a Fourth Empire artifact they call Big Buzzer can attract and roughly direct stone-boring beetles. They found it in the Imperial Arsenal and activated it without understanding its purpose; the resulting beetles bored into the complex and attacked everything around the artifact. The kobolds now place Big Buzzer at a chosen surface point to draw beetles toward it. The artifact does not command them. Its direct vibration irritates and confuses them, making them violently destructive toward kobolds, animals, buildings, and anything else nearby.\n\nBuzzer-directed breaches are preceded by tremors, vibrating water, frightened livestock, burrowing animals fleeing their holes, birds abandoning the area, and a low grinding that can be felt before it can be heard. When a beetle rears to bite, its pale underbelly is softer than its armored back. A fresh beetle bore can be sealed by silencing or removing the Buzzer and collapsing the weakened upper throat of the passage.",
