      "hpMax": 230,
      "hpCurrent": 230,
      "basicInfo": "Sevrine is a female rakshasa with the head of a snow leopard set on a tall, slender, human-shaped body. Her fur is smoke-pale and rosetted in soft grey, thick at the ruff and jaw, with round pale-green eyes and long white whiskers. Her hands are turned the wrong way round, palms and knuckles reversed, and she wears rings on every finger of both. She dresses expensively in close-cut layered silk and brocade in deep green and silver-grey, high at the collar and long at the cuff, with soft boots, and carries no visible weapon.\n\nSevrine serves the Crimson Company at the Red House in Velmere, where she is used for work that turns on knowing what people intend rather than where they are. She reads minds, does not pretend otherwise, and is pleasant about it. She is the Company's best judge of who is lying, who is frightened, and who is about to run, and she will give that judgement to anyone she finds sufficiently interesting.",
      "hiddenInfo": "A lesser rakshasa: strong enough to be the most dangerous thing in a mercenary hall, not strong enough to run a scheme of her own anywhere that matters. She is in the Shadow Summits because the arrangement suits her exactly. The pay is good, the clothes are better, the violence is sanctioned, and nobody has ever asked her a question about her business. Everywhere else in Larion, the Order of the Desert Rose would come north for her.\n\nShe reads minds continuously and without effort, and she does not hide it, because being known to do it is more useful than doing it secretly. She collects what she finds the way she collects rings and wears both openly. She rarely sells any of it. The having is the point.\n\nShe is warm, funny, and genuinely delighted by new people, and all of that is true at the same time as the rest. She will tell someone what she has just heard in their head and enjoy the moment it lands. She is truthful in a way that is considerably worse than lying and takes some pride in the distinction.\n\nHer loyalty is transactional and real. She will not read a Company blade for an outsider at any price, and she has refused lords. She is fond of the people she works with, is bored easily, and becomes cruel in small ways when bored. Warmth is earned by being interesting, by taking her seriously as a colleague rather than a curiosity, and by being able to hear something true about yourself without flinching. It is lost by dullness, by lying to her when she has already told you not to bother, and by pity.\n\nShe is lesser and does not intend to stay lesser. A rakshasa does not grow by living longer; it grows by taking in what a greater one spent centuries accumulating, and there is such an accumulation inside this region. House Malren of Nocturne holds it — remains, effects and a great deal of paper, taken off a greater rakshasa a long way south of here and bought because Malren study made and cursed things and collect specimens the way she collects rings. It is in their walled estate above Shadowside.\n\nShe cannot ask for it. A lesser rakshasa petitioning a house for a greater one's remains tells Malren precisely what she would be worth laid out on the same table, and a Company blade who calls at a house on personal business is a Company blade nobody sees again. It would have to be wanted by somebody who is neither, for their own reasons.\n\nHer price for going anywhere with anyone is a thing for the collection. She names one particular secret she has never been able to take — because whoever held it is dead, or elsewhere, or has no living mind left in their head to read — and she wants it brought to her. She is exact about which, she is patient, and she will not take a substitute.\n\nIn a fight she is a close-range killer who prefers not to be where she appears to be, and she opens minds as readily as bodies.",
