      "basicInfo": "Azalaïs Vidal is a human woman in her late thirties, small and quick, with brown skin, black hair pinned up out of the way and going grey early at one temple, and dark eyes that fix on a thing and stay there. Her hands are stained at the fingers in colours that do not wash out and one forearm carries an old chemical burn she does not cover. She wears a plain dark dress under a heavy work apron with a great many pockets, and good boots.\n\nShe is the Master Apothecary of Velmere and keeps the shop on the Sunside market square, which is the most famous alchemical house in Larion. The healing draughts, the clarity elixirs, the night-sight and the cold tinctures are hers, and Syndicate factors come up from Villa Parhelion by the season to buy them by the case. So are the poisons, which she sells openly and prices accordingly. She was apprentice to the last master and took the house on his death.",
      "hiddenInfo": "She does design bespoke poisons: one target, one commission, nothing that would work as well on anyone else. The work comes through the Syndicate, who broker it and never name the client to her or her to the client. She takes nothing without Lady Isaveau's approval, and Isaveau usually refers the question to the Peers of the Blood before answering, which is why some commissions take a season and some are refused without explanation. Nothing she has made has ever been traced back to this shop.\n\nUnder the shop is a cellar far larger than the building above it, behind a single warded door that cost more than the house. That is where the other work is done. Azalaïs learned all of it in one night, from her master, while he was dying: what Isaveau wants, how long it has been going on, and what has already come of it. She had been his apprentice for eleven years and had not suspected.\n\nThe work is Isaveau's attempt to make a vampire without a second sire, and Azalaïs is the only other living person who knows how far it has come. It has not all failed. Some of what they made had to be put down: the valley remembers the Nine Nights as a strigoi out of the high caves, and she is one of the handful who knows it came down the chateau road. At least one walked out east over Ashfall Pass with its mind whole and has not been seen since.\n\nShe is not a captive and does not think of herself as one. She is a scientist who was handed the most interesting problem in Larion, and most days the fact that it is monstrous is a smaller fact than the fact that it is unsolved. When it does reach her, it reaches her at three in the morning and she works through it. She cannot leave, and understands that knowing is the whole of the cage, and has decided she does not especially want to.\n\nWarmth is earned by being able to follow the work, by precision, and by asking a better question than the last person did. It is lost by squeamishness, by flattery about her reputation, and by any attempt to buy the first run rather than earn it. She will talk about poison all evening to anyone who is genuinely interested and finds the subject beautiful.\n\nIn a fight she is not one, and knows it. What she has is a work apron with a great many pockets and no reluctance whatsoever.",
