    "Hunter/Hunted": {
      "name": "Hunter/Hunted",
      "firstQuest": "",
      "description": "MYSTERY\n\nYour trial hunt as an Initiate of the Order of the Silver Sword. A hunting party vanished inside a lord's private preserve. Find them, uncover what called them into the trees, and prove you are ready to return to Castle Harstone, earn your silver, and be admitted as a Silverblade.",
      "storyStart": "Set the scene at the edge of the Dauvigne Preserve in the Kingdom of Carendon, late morning. The player is an Initiate of the Order of the Silver Sword undertaking their trial hunt under Veteran Silverblade Garran Valere. The player belongs to the Order as a candidate, but has not been admitted as a Silverblade, carries no silver blade pin, and has not yet earned an Order-silvered weapon, silver-faced shield, or silver-bound focus or implement. Garran is present to observe, advise, and prevent a catastrophic failure, but not to lead or solve the hunt. If the player discovers the hunters' fate and decisively resolves what took them, Garran can attest that the trial is complete and the player may return to Castle Harstone to tell the hunt before the Great Hall and ask to be admitted as a Silverblade.\n\nA nervous servant named Colm leads them to where the hunting party was last seen two days ago. Colm explains that Lord Tristram Dauvigne's son Sebastian rode out with four companions for a morning hunt. Colm was with the beaters. They heard the hunters calling out, excited as though they had spotted game, and then nothing. Sebastian's horse returned riderless. The household guard found no bodies, blood, or trail. Garran examines the brush and finds tracks leading deeper into the preserve. The hunters did not run; they followed something. Garran checks his crossbow and axe, then makes clear that this is the player's trial and the player decides how to work it. End with the wrong-sounding calls, the tracks into the trees, and the player's first investigative choice immediately available.",
      "locations": [
