    "Enter the Academy": {
      "name": "Enter the Academy",
      "firstQuest": "",
      "description": "SANDBOX\n\nJoin Tarnholme Academy as a First Circle mage, choose your first field Practicum and senior partner, explore the five Colleges, and begin building a magical specialty of your own.",
      "storyStart": "Set the scene in Tarnholme Academy's Great Hall during the welcome gathering for new students. The player has just been admitted as a First Circle student and receives a small silver First Circle pin. Use a few concrete details to establish the hall and Academy life without surveying the whole gathering. Omit smells and keep background students unnamed.\n\nIntroduce exactly one named Academy guide: an attractive, dynamic young adult upper-Circle student with a distinctive appearance, a clear magical specialty, practical field abilities, and an ambition beyond welcoming newcomers. Prefer Hessa Morcant when she fits the generated context; otherwise create a recurring student of comparable specificity. Do not use an elderly professor, generic clerk, or interchangeable mentor as the principal character.\n\nThe guide has chosen to give this player personal attention for a concrete reason grounded in the player's traits, background, magical interests, or apparent potential. Show that interest through what the guide notices and asks rather than flattery. They may be considering the player for a future Practicum crew, testing whether their talents complement the guide's own, or remembering what it was like to arrive without a place. The interaction should create the possibility of an ongoing friendship, rivalry, mentorship, collaboration, or other bond without deciding which it becomes.\n\nLet the essentials emerge through conversation: First Circle students undertake one supervised field Practicum; completing it makes them eligible for Second Circle; later Circles bring harder work and greater independence. Do not explain the five Colleges, list Practica, deliver a lecture, or generate a crisis or immediate chore. One harmless magical incident may occur in the background only if it gives the guide a chance to demonstrate personality or useful magic.\n\nEnd with the guide making a specific personal offer or asking a pointed question about what the player hopes to become at Tarnholme. The player's answer should matter to whether this person wants to remain involved.",
      "locations": [
        "The Main Island"
      ],
      "locationAreas": [
        "The Great Hall"
      ],
      "isDefault": false,
      "startingQuests": [
        "Earn Second Circle",
