    "Overboard": {
      "name": "Overboard",
      "firstQuest": "The first quest is to survive the Feathered Fleet boarding — beat the pirates back, strike a deal, or turn the fight around and take the Windreaver itself. Keep the first quest small and completable: one boarding action, won, survived, or escaped. The arc theme should emerge from Coral and her ship — the mutiny that cost her the Windreaver, the lockbox Scraw could never open in the captain's cabin, and what is inside it that is worth more than the galley's whole cargo. Secrets should progress from 'Coral is more than a friendly passenger' to 'the lockbox holds something the whole Fleet would kill for' to 'here is what it opens, and who else is hunting it.' The arc goal is Coral's reckoning with the Feathered Fleet — her ship retaken or lost for good. Keep Scraw vicious but stupid; keep the tone salty and quick.",
      "description": "COMBAT\n\nPirates attack the merchant galley you're traveling on. For better or worse, your new friend knows these particular pirates very well.... An action adventure start.",
      "storyStart": "Set the scene aboard a Spice Isles merchant galley in the North Canal, bound for Tevantia. Sun on the deck, salt spray, colorful sails snapping in the wind. Briefly introduce the party members and why they're traveling—trade, adventure, escaping trouble, chasing opportunity. Make the introductions light and funny where appropriate. Introduce Coral, a striking woman with sea-green tinged skin and faintly webbed fingers who's been friendly company on the voyage. The lookout screams. A sleek raider emerges from behind a rocky isle, flying the black flag of the Feathered Fleet. The crew panics—everyone's heard of the seabird pirates. But Coral goes pale for a different reason. 'That's my ship. The Windreaver. I was captain until my first mate Scraw led a mutiny.' She watches the pelican and albatross pirates swinging grappling hooks, preparing to board. 'Scraw's vicious but stupid. He'll have kept my lockbox in the captain's cabin—never could pick the lock. There's something in there worth more than this whole cargo.' She draws a long knife. 'So. Do we just survive this, or do we take my ship back?'.",
      "locations": [
