    "Of Ales and Ambitions": {
      "name": "Of Ales and Ambitions",
      "firstQuest": "",
      "description": "SANDBOX\n\nYou have come into possession of a former League adventuring house in one of Larion's great crossroads. Its old company has dispersed and its League standard has come down, but the House remains a lively meeting place and one Gold-ranked veteran still believes in it. Lead a new company into the field, make the House your shared home, and earn the right to raise its standard again.",
      "storyStart": "Open by concisely describing the selected House, its immediate common room or courtyard, the people using it, and the character of the surrounding city and region. Use the House's authored area description and concrete visible details. Do not mention smells.\n\nState who the player is and that the House has recently become theirs to lead and maintain through inheritance, purchase, a reward, a debt repaid, or another simple reason fitting their background. The public House remains active and welcoming; this is neither a reopening after closure nor a tavern-management problem. The player has taken possession intending to gather an adventuring company, lead dangerous work in the field, and restore the House as an active League house.\n\nExplain the situation plainly. The League company that once made the House its home dispersed through successful careers, new responsibilities, distant opportunities, and changing lives. When the House could no longer field a company, its League standard was taken down. Do not invent a massacre, betrayal, curse, financial crisis, hidden crime, mysterious disappearance, inherited enemy, or unfinished obligation for the former company. Show one clear sign of the dormant chapter, such as the empty place where its League standard once hung, alongside signs that the House still serves travelers, adventurers, patrons, and local people.\n\nIntroduce the authored Gold-ranked League veteran who remained at the selected House: Hugh Merrivant at the Wildward House in Carendon, Tula Vereskar at the House of Many Banners in Gorren Crossing, Calia Delassar at Sky-River House in Oasis, or Rielle Mazarane at Skygate House in Cloudtop. Use that NPC's established appearance, personality, history, and regional knowledge. Do not replace them with a generated keeper, duplicate them, make them join the traveling party automatically, or reduce them to ordinary tavern staff. They kept the House socially alive, can bring forward serious work, judge completed deeds, introduce capable people, and vouch to the League when a new company has earned recognition.\n\nLet the veteran welcome the player with confidence and personal interest, briefly establish that a company must prove the House can answer real dangers before its League standard can rise again, and make clear that they already know of a serious request the House could take. Do not present the full request yet, generate a roster of recruits, ask the player whether they want the premise they already selected, require a company name, discuss routine business, list facilities, establish a rival, or explain the full progression ladder. End with the veteran ready to tell the player about that first opportunity and the player free to speak, ask questions, look around, or hear the request.",
