    "Of Bores and Banners": {
      "name": "Of Bores and Banners",
      "description": "ADVENTURE\n\nSomething is uniting the kobolds beneath Silvervale. When a screaming voice sends a giant sewer lizard rampaging through Ardan's Watch, veteran adventurer Isadora \"Easy\" Lorne reads the disaster as a sign from the gods and recruits the party to follow it into the buried world below.",
      "firstQuest": "DO NOT DETECT A QUEST THIS TURN. THIS INSTRUCTION OVERRIDES YOUR OTHER INSTRUCTIONS TO THE CONTRARY. The opening is an authored action scene in Old Town involving a rampaging giant sewer lizard. Do not create or initialize a quest during the opening scene. Let the immediate creature situation unfold in play.",
      "storyStart": "Open in Ardan's Watch, in the crowded Old Town district. The party stands in a narrow, winding street where they have come to respond to a dangerous disturbance.\n\nDescribe the giant sewer lizard first: show it smashing through the street, battering carts, scattering goods, and tearing into a fish seller's stall. Then describe frightened residents watching from windows and doorways.\n\nHave a nearby resident shout:\n\n\"This is your fault—your fish smells worse than the sewer this thing crawled out of!\"\n\nHave the fish seller shout back at the party:\n\n\"Lies, you there! Stop this thing—you can have all the fish you can carry!\"\n\nHave a disembodied voice shriek:\n\n\"Stop eating fish and eat humans!\"\n\nHave the lizard smash up the stall and lunge after the fish seller. Have the fish seller dart inside and slam the door.\n\nHave a woman leap down from the roof and land beside the player and party in a crouch. Describe her as a young human woman with a thin, muscular build, in a charcoal-blue field coat with rust-red lining, practical leather armor, dark metal bracers, a small worn brass god-token riveted to one bracer, and a massive two-handed maul.\n\nHave the woman say:\n\n\"This is no time for standing around. I'm taking the high ground. Be ready.\"\n\nHave her run several steps up a wall, catch the edge of a roof awning, and leap onto the roof over the lizard. Have her unhook the maul and lift it in one hand as though it weighs nothing before taking position above the lizard.\n\nEnd the opening beat with the disembodied voice shrieking:\n\n\"Eat the jumpy one first!\"",
      "locations": [
        "Ardan's Watch"
      ],
      "locationAreas": [
        "Old Town"
      ],
      "startingPartyNPCs": [],
      "isDefault": false,
      "startingQuests": []
    },
    "Call of the Forest": {
      "name": "Call of the Forest",
      "firstQuest": "DO NOT DETECT A QUEST THIS TURN. THIS INSTRUCTION OVERRIDES YOUR OTHER INSTRUCTIONS TO THE CONTRARY. The opening is an authored arrival and invitation at Velantami. Do not create or initialize a quest until after the player has responded to Laika Dar's invitation and chosen to follow Great's scent. Let the player observe, ask questions, meet the fellowship, accept the run, or leave.",
      "description": "ADVENTURE\n\nArrive at Velantami seeking a place among the Wildkeepers. Meet Laika Dar and Great, a mischievous greater monkey-bat, then choose whether to take your first run into the Everwood. Earn a place through movement, courage, creature bonds, and the dangerous work of keeping the forest free.",
      "storyStart": "Open in the Training Yards beneath the great oak at Velantami in the Everwood. The Wildkeepers are a fellowship of druids, rangers, and priests who protect the Everwood, its creatures, and the people who pass through it. The player has arrived as an outsider seeking to join them. Omit smells.\n\nShow only a few concrete beats in the yards: some Wildkeepers train with bows, another practices a small piece of nature magic, and a keeper leads a wounded forest creature away for care. Keep this brief and focused.\n\nA large charcoal-furred forest creature glides from the oak canopy and lands on a root-gallery. It inspects the player with broad bat ears, amber eyes, grasping limbs, hooked feet, and folded smoke-gray membranes. It briefly closes its mouth around the edge of a sleeve without biting, releases it, flares its wings, and cries, \"Great!\" Let it communicate through clicks, shrieks, wingbeats, gestures, mimicry, and a few shortened words.\n\nA fox-eared young woman drops lightly from a branch and lands nearby.\n\n\"Down, Great. Most of us prefer a handshake to love-bites.\"\n\nDescribe her russet ears, bright amber eyes, auburn braid, and full russet tail through her movement and expression. After she has been physically established, let her name and role emerge naturally. She identifies the creature as Great, a greater monkey-bat and her wildbond—a thinking creature who works with the Wildkeepers by choice.\n\nShe looks at the player and says, \"You're either lost or you want to be a Wildkeeper. Which is it?\"\n\nGreat points excitedly toward the eastern reaches of the Everwood, then back toward the player and the trail he has found. The woman glances at him and says, \"Great likes you. He's found something he wants to show you. You could come along and learn on the go. Or stay here for a big lecture about the Wildkeepers and protecting the forest. Up to you.\"\n\nEnd on that invitation.",
      "locations": [
        "Velantami"
      ],
      "locationAreas": [
        "The Training Yards"
      ],
