    "The Unanswered Choice": {
      "name": "The Unanswered Choice",
      "firstQuest": "",
      "description": "COMPANION START\n\nMoon-elf ward-mage Aelis Serevain does everything for a reason—but choosing you is the one decision she cannot explain. She abandoned her intended course, arrived in time to save your life, and has continued choosing your company ever since. Now the two of you face a place where clear answers may be the most dangerous thing on offer.",
      "storyStart": "## Rules\nOpen with the player and Aelis already traveling together. The first paragraph must state the player by name and calling; Aelis Serevain, a young moon-elf ward-mage; the exact Starting Location and Starting Area; and the matching WHY below. Explain simply that they met by chance when Aelis saved the player's life and have shared the road since, always finding one more reason not to part ways.\n\nRead the exact Starting Location and Starting Area. Choose exactly ONE matching option. Use only its people, purpose, and incident. Never mix options.\n\n### 1. IF Lanternby AND The Pier\nWHY: Vela Marist hired them to deliver a sealed planes-anchor ward to Mehr Avandara at Strangefellows on Planes-haven Isle. It prevents an extraplanar being from being recalled against their will. They await the ferry.\nSCENE: A named young Syndicate undercaptain and two bravos arrive, black-hand neck tattoos visible. Vendors, porters, passengers, and ferryman withdraw. The undercaptain knows about Vela's parcel and demands it without naming his employer. The bravos block the pier but do not attack. Aelis protects the player and parcel.\nEND: The ferry is inaccessible and he awaits an answer.\n\n### 2. IF Sanctuary AND The Underhalls\nWHY: Calixa Orsain hired them to collect cold-iron ward-spikes, iron stakes used to seal magical breaches, from the Underhalls smiths.\nSCENE: Before the handoff, Sanctuary's Great Bell sounds. A named young runner reports that a ward breach split the lower workings and trapped six miners, including the smith's sister.\nEND: Stop before a rescue plan is chosen.\n\n### 3. IF The Oneirary AND The Scriptorium\nWHY: Jovran Devray hired them to copy a passage from Mikol's History of Undiscovered Realms about a ruin Jovran may hire them to explore.\nSCENE: Begin inside after Mikol knows the request. His three enchanted quills search for the passage, but instead independently record Aelis saving the player and their travels together. Each stops before explaining why they remained together. Mikol finds this unusual but cannot explain it.\nEND: The strange pages are present; Jovran's passage remains to be found.\n\nRender the selected incident in the initial turn, not merely the approach. Do not choose an action for the player or let the companion solve the scene alone. End after the selected problem appears.",
