  "skills": {
    "acrobatics": {
      "name": "acrobatics",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Balance, tumbling, falls, and fitting where bodies shouldn't go.\nEasy: walk a wide beam, roll out of a low fall, slip through a crowd untouched.\nMedium: cross a narrow ledge, vault a table mid-fight, land a one-story drop clean.\nHard: fight on a rope bridge, tumble through a melee unscathed, squeeze through a gap half your size.\nExtreme: run a crumbling rooftop line, fall two stories and keep running, dodge through a volley.\nRaw power — lifting, forcing, brute climbing — is athletics.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "athletics": {
      "name": "athletics",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "strength",
      "description": "Running, climbing, jumping, swimming, lifting — the body at full effort.\nEasy: climb a knotted rope, swim a calm pond, clear a ditch.\nMedium: climb a rough wall, swim against a current, force a stuck door.\nHard: climb a sheer cliff, swim armored through rapids, leap a gap most would balk at.\nExtreme: scale a fortress wall in the rain, out-swim a riptide, lift what two men couldn't.\nBalance, tumbling, and tight squeezes are acrobatics.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "intimidation": {
      "name": "intimidation",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "charisma",
      "description": "Menace as a tool: threats, presence, interrogation.\nEasy: back down a drunk, move a loiterer along, make a pickpocket think twice.\nMedium: make a thug reconsider, get a name out of a frightened informant, silence a heckler.\nHard: stare down an armed man, break a hardened prisoner's silence, cow a room.\nExtreme: back down a foe who outmatches you, make a fanatic hesitate, hold a gate by presence alone.\nFear moves people only within what fear can reach; some cannot be cowed.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "investigation": {
      "name": "investigation",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "wisdom",
      "description": "Finding things out: searching, noticing, connecting.\nEasy: spot the scratches on a forced lock, notice who left the room, find what's hidden carelessly.\nMedium: search a room properly, notice the detail that doesn't belong, reconstruct last night from what's left.\nHard: find the hidden compartment, connect three thin threads into one answer, catch the lie in a tidy story.\nExtreme: solve what the city watch gave up on, find the one altered line in a ledger of thousands, name the culprit from almost nothing.\nWhat a fact means is often lore. Reading the person telling it — sincerity, intent, whether they believe themselves — is insight.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "performance": {
      "name": "performance",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "charisma",
      "description": "Holding an audience: music, story, acting — and playing a role, on stage or off.\nEasy: a tavern song well received, a story that holds a table, pass as staff with the right clothes.\nMedium: win over a cold room, busk a day's wages, hold a borrowed name through small talk.\nHard: play a court without a misstep, move a crowd to tears or anger, hold a cover under pointed questions.\nExtreme: perform for a king and be remembered, hold a hostile hall spellbound, live a false face among people who'd kill the real one.\nDisguise checks are acting checks: the donning is prep — the moments under scrutiny are performance. One-off lies are persuasion.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "persuasion": {
      "name": "persuasion",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "charisma",
      "description": "Moving people with words: convincing, charming, haggling, bluffing, and lying.\nEasy: friendly directions, a small discount, a plausible excuse for being somewhere.\nMedium: talk your way past a minor rule, win a stranger's small favor, hold a simple lie to a casual listener.\nHard: talk a guard into looking away, haggle a merchant well below his floor, lie to a suspicious questioner.\nExtreme: turn a hostile witness, talk a mob out of violence, sell a falsehood to someone paid to catch them.\nLies move people only as far as they could plausibly believe. Threats are intimidation; holding a false identity over time is performance.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "survival": {
      "name": "survival",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "wisdom",
      "description": "Living off the land: travel, forage, shelter, weather, fieldcraft.\nEasy: find water in green country, make camp before dark, read tomorrow's weather in the sky.\nMedium: forage a meal in lean country, keep direction in deep forest, weather a cold night without fire.\nHard: cross a desert on planning alone, find food where there's none to find, keep a party alive through a blizzard.\nExtreme: survive weeks in dead country, lead a crossing veterans call impossible, read ground for what's buried — water, ore, the old road.\nFieldcraft includes prospecting and reading terrain. Following game is tracking; navigation at sea is sailing.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "insight": {
      "name": "insight",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "wisdom",
      "description": "Reading people: sincerity, intent, mood, and whether a story holds together.\nEasy: tell nervous from hostile, notice someone is pleased, see that a child is lying.\nMedium: catch a rehearsed answer, read who in the room actually decides, tell real grief from performed grief.\nHard: spot a practised liar's single tell, read a hostile negotiator's limit, tell which of two accusers believes themselves.\nExtreme: read a professional deceiver under their own roof, name the motive someone is hiding from themselves, tell truth from a compulsion or a planted memory.\nThis reads people, not evidence. Physical traces, searched rooms, and documents are investigation. What a custom or symbol means is lore. Persuading, frightening, or charming someone is a charisma skill.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "fire magic": {
      "name": "fire magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Calling, shaping, and quenching flame.\nEasy: light or snuff a candle, warm yourself, a flame in the palm.\nMedium: a hurled firebolt, ignite a campfire from nothing, burn a rope at distance.\nHard: a sheet of flame across a street, melt an iron lock, hold fire steady in rain.\nExtreme: a firestorm, flame shaped to spare allies, turning an elemental's fire back on it.\nDeals fire damage. Easier near abundant flame; falters in downpour and deep cold.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "water magic": {
      "name": "water magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Shaping water and ice: pull it from the air, freeze it, drive it like a fist.\nEasy: purify a cup, frost a windowpane, gather drinking water from mist.\nMedium: a lance of ice, freeze a lock solid, part a stream.\nHard: freeze a river crossing, a crushing wave, ice armor that holds under blows.\nExtreme: freeze a harbor, walk a storm-sea, pull the water from a living thing.\nDeals frost damage as ice, impact as driven water. Easier near abundant water; falters in desert air. Weather belongs to storm magic.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "storm magic": {
      "name": "storm magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Wind, lightning, and weather.\nEasy: a gust that snuffs candles, a static snap, fill a sail.\nMedium: a lightning bolt, knock a man down with wind, cushion a fall.\nHard: chain lightning through several foes, a gale that clears a street, lightning from a clear sky.\nExtreme: ride the wind aloft, turn a storm aside, a thunderbolt that splits a tower.\nDeals shock damage. Easier under open sky and gathering weather; falters underground and in still air.\nThe Extreme line carries you aloft for one immediate movement; remaining in flight or using the sky as a road requires Ride the Storm, wings, or another concrete means.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "earth magic": {
      "name": "earth magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Stone and soil: cracking, raising, shaping.\nEasy: shape a handful of clay, sense hollow ground underfoot, loosen packed earth.\nMedium: a hurled stone fist, crack a flagstone, raise a knee-high wall.\nHard: raise a rampart from bare ground, open a trench under charging foes, seal a tunnel clean.\nExtreme: drop a cliff face, swallow a siege engine whole, shape stone fine as a mason's year in a moment.\nDeals impact damage. Strongest on rock and soil; falters on water and in the air.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "divine magic": {
      "name": "divine magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Wielding holy power: blessing, smiting, banishing, consecrating.\nEasy: a blessing over a meal, light a shrine-candle with holy fire, steady a frightened soul.\nMedium: smite an undead thing with radiant force, bless a blade, sanctify a doorway against evil.\nHard: turn a pack of undead, break a curse, consecrate ground a fiend cannot cross.\nExtreme: banish a demon to its plane, sanctify a defiled temple, a radiance that routs an undead host.\nDeals radiant damage. Easier in sacred places; falters on corrupted ground. Mending flesh belongs to healing magic. Becoming the god's vessel is divine channeling.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "healing magic": {
      "name": "healing magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Mending living bodies: wounds, poison, sickness.\nEasy: close a small cut, dull pain, ease a fever.\nMedium: knit a deep wound, purge a common poison, set and mend a broken bone.\nHard: pull someone back from death's edge, cure a wasting disease, grow clean flesh over burns.\nExtreme: restore a withered limb, purge a magical plague, hold a dying soul in its body.\nHealing ordinarily mends the living only. The dead are necromancy's country; True Resurrection is the sole rite that calls one fully back. The undead cannot be mended. Willing patients are easier; magical wounds and curses resist.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "warding magic": {
      "name": "warding magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Protection, barriers, and the unmaking of other magic.\nEasy: deflect a thrown stone, seal a door for the night, snuff a candle-small spell.\nMedium: a shield that holds through a skirmish, unravel a simple curse or lock-spell, ward a camp against beasts.\nHard: a barrier that stops a charging ogre, dispel a mage's working mid-cast, ward a house against the dead.\nExtreme: a dome that holds against an army's volleys, strip the enchantment from an artifact, suppress a true curse until the scene ends.\nDispelling contests the caster: the stronger the working, the harder the unraveling. Lasting protections bound into objects are enchanting.\nSimple hexes, lock-spells, and temporary suppression belong to this ladder. Permanently breaking a lasting trait-backed affliction or an item's binding requires Sunder the Binding, an authored rite, or a consecrated shrine. Warding deals no damage; it raises barriers and unmakes workings.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "enchanting": {
      "name": "enchanting",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Binding magic into objects so it holds.\nEasy: a light that lasts the evening, warm a blade's edge, mark an object to find again.\nMedium: a blade that burns for one fight, a lock sealed against picks, a cloak that sheds rain for a season.\nHard: a lasting work — a sword of flame, armor that turns arrows, a ward-stone that guards a door for years.\nExtreme: bind a spell any hand can loose, armor proof against a damage type, work that outlives its maker.\nSlow, deliberate craft — done at a bench, not in a fight. Battle-cast protections are warding magic.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "conjuration magic": {
      "name": "conjuration magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Calling things from elsewhere and binding them to your will.\nEasy: dismiss your own active conjuration, a darting light-sprite, a conjured tool that fades by morning, call a small bound servant.\nMedium: summon a lesser beast to fight, a bridge of solid force, dismiss what another novice called.\nHard: summon a dangerous creature and hold it, keep a servant bound past sunset, call something by its true name.\nExtreme: summon a greater being and bargain, hold a door between places open, bind a creature to a year of service.\nConjured force deals arcane damage; summons fight with their own. What you call must be held — a slipped leash is your problem. The dead answer necromancy, not conjuration. A successful dismissal of your own conjuration takes effect immediately unless another power is actively holding it in the world.\nHolding open a found or existing way is this ladder's Extreme. Threshold Step permits one visible step; making a new way between known places requires The Ways Between.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "illusion magic": {
      "name": "illusion magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "False senses: making people see what isn't there and miss what is.\nEasy: a flicker of light, change your cloak's color, throw your voice.\nMedium: a convincing figure that holds at a distance, mask a face, hide a doorway.\nHard: an illusion that bears close inspection, cloak a group from sight, a scene with sound and motion sustained.\nExtreme: an illusion true at arm's length, veil a building, deceive a watching crowd at once.\nEasier against the distracted and those who want to believe; harder against wary, keen eyes. Illusions have no substance and deal no damage; touching the mind itself is psionics.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "divination magic": {
      "name": "divination magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Seeing what is hidden and what is coming.\nEasy: sense nearby magic, find true north, feel whether you are watched.\nMedium: find a lost thing nearby, read an object's recent past, glimpse a familiar person far away.\nHard: scry a distant place, read tomorrow's danger in signs, trace one man through a city.\nExtreme: a clear vision of what comes, find a single soul across a kingdom, pierce wards woven to blind seers.\nThe future shows in glimpses and symbols, never certainty. Warded places and people resist; the willing and the known come easier. Divination deals no damage.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "nature magic": {
      "name": "nature magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "The living wild: green growth and beasts.\nEasy: coax a flower open, calm a small animal, ripen an apple on the branch.\nMedium: roots that grab and bind, speak with beasts, quicken a garden by a season.\nHard: a wall of thorn, call a pack of beasts to your aid, draw blight out of a field.\nExtreme: wake a tree to fight, command the beasts of a whole valley, turn a barren hill green in a day.\nThorn and briar deal piercing damage; venoms deal poison. Strong in the wild; falters on dead stone and deep city streets. Wearing a beast's shape is shape shifting.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "necromancy magic": {
      "name": "necromancy magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Power over the dead: speaking with them, raising them, drawing on death itself.\nEasy: sense recent death, quiet a restless grave, a corpse-candle light.\nMedium: question a fresh corpse, raise a skeleton servant, command a lesser shade.\nHard: raise several dead at once, bind a ghost to service, draw power from a battlefield.\nExtreme: raise a champion of bone, command an unwilling wraith, hold a soul back from the Shadelands.\nDeals shadow damage. Easier in places of death; falters on consecrated ground. Curses on the living are dark magic; living blood is blood magic.\nRaised servants begin to fail at dawn. Keeping any beyond it requires an available Gray working; the working used determines how many can remain.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "dark magic": {
      "name": "dark magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Curses, dread, and shadow given shape.\nEasy: deepen the shadows around you, a chill of dread down a neck, wither a flower in the hand.\nMedium: a lash of shadow, a curse of stumbling misfortune, blind a foe in darkness for a breath.\nHard: a curse that rides a man for weeks, terror that breaks a fighting line, shadow shaped into grasping hands.\nExtreme: a withering curse on a whole household, darkness that smothers light and warmth, dread that routs a war-host.\nDeals shadow damage. Falters on consecrated ground and against the stout of heart. The dead belong to necromancy; the body's blood to blood magic.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "blood magic": {
      "name": "blood magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Power through blood in a living body—your own or another’s—and blood freshly shed from one.\nEasy: close one of your own small cuts; sharpen your senses with a token drop; feel fresh blood touching or very close to you.\nMedium: shape blood freely given or already spilled; trade a deliberate cut for a brief surge of speed, strength, or force.\nHard: force a resisting living foe’s wound to remain Bleeding; drain vigor from a resisting living foe; knit one of your own deep wounds in battle; still a limb through its blood.\nExtreme: drain several resisting living foes at once; stop a heart; rip the strength from a giant; burn years of your life for one impossible moment.\nWilling targets are easier. Bloodless, dead, and incorporeal targets cannot be bled or drained. Mending another person is healing magic; moving or binding the dead is necromancy; curses at a distance are dark magic. Blood spilled as a weapon deals piercing damage; life drained through blood deals shadow damage.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "psionics": {
      "name": "psionics",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Thought and will acting beyond the body: moving matter, touching minds, and extending perception.\n\nEasy: move a small unattended object, sense a strong nearby emotion, or draw someone’s attention.\n\nMedium: speak silently with a willing person, hurl a loose object, sense a nearby thinking presence, or read an unguarded surface thought.\n\nHard: restrain a resisting creature with unseen force, probe a guarded mind for an answer, induce a strong emotion, or strike directly at a mind.\n\nExtreme: move a great weight, reach several minds together, enter a sleeper’s dream, or penetrate trained mental defenses.\n\nMental intrusion is harder against strong wills and trained minds. Mindless creatures cannot be read, influenced, or harmed psychically, but physical objects and telekinetic force can still strike them. Direct mental attacks deal psychic damage; physical attacks use the damage type of the object or force.\n\nPossession and alteration of established memories require a specific ability or other explicit license.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "shape shifting": {
      "name": "shape shifting",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "wisdom",
      "description": "Taking and holding another shape, and fighting in it.\nEasy: hold a familiar shape at rest, shift in calm, take a small harmless form.\nMedium: shift under pressure, fight in a familiar shape, hold a form through pain.\nHard: shift mid-fight, take a shape studied but never worn, hold a form against wards.\nExtreme: take a shape many times your size, shift as a blow lands, take a shape seen only once.\nWhile shifted, shape shifting is the active skill for attacks and exceptional physical feats that depend on that body. Claws and fangs deal slashing or piercing damage; a great form's bulk deals impact damage. A shifted body cannot wield or use gear it cannot physically fit. What that body cannot do, you cannot do in it.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "spirit channeling": {
      "name": "spirit channeling",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Letting a spirit ride your body, and acting as one while it does.\nEasy: carry a small familiar spirit for an hour, let it sharpen one sense, speak a dead tongue it knows.\nMedium: fight with an ancestor's skill at your hands, hold a channel through pain, carry a spirit through a rite it knows.\nHard: channel a powerful spirit in battle, hold two wills in one body under duress, refuse a rider's demand mid-channel.\nExtreme: carry a great spirit of place or storm, hold the channel while near death, expel a rider that will not leave.\nWhile a spirit rides you, spirit channeling is the active skill for attacks and supernatural feats supplied by the rider. Damage follows the rider's nature—an ancestor's blade deals slashing, a storm-spirit deals shock, and a grave-spirit deals shadow. The spirit has a will: what it would not do, it will not do through you. A willing named spirit already in the character's court is easier to carry; a stranger, hostile rider, violated taboo, or request against the spirit's nature is harder. Dealing with spirits from outside is spirit magic.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "divine channeling": {
      "name": "divine channeling",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Giving your body to your god's power, and acting as its vessel.\nEasy: carry the presence through a vigil, let it steady your hands, speak one word in its voice.\nMedium: fight as the vessel, strike with radiant force, hold the presence through pain.\nHard: channel through a full battle, keep the vessel while your faith is tested, make the presence visible across a crowded hall.\nExtreme: carry radiance enough to contest a great shadow-thing, hold the presence while near death, survive more power than a mortal body should bear.\nWhile the presence fills you, divine channeling is the active skill for attacks and supernatural feats of the vessel; its attacks deal radiant damage. A Vow Focus makes the specific divine aspect it carries easier for that paladin to channel. The god chooses what flows: the vessel serves, it does not command. Prayers and workings cast from your own strength use divine magic.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "gadgetry": {
      "name": "gadgetry",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Fighting with made things: spring-arms, wound wheels, clatter-boxes, sparkers, and whatever the bench built this week. Damage follows the device — a striking arm deals impact, a needle-thrower piercing, a sparker shock, a vial-slinger what the vial holds. Signature work: the weapon nobody has seen before, the fight won by winding something up in advance, the device that does two jobs at once. Thrown blades and stones are throwing; a rigged trap waiting on the ground is trapcraft; building and mending the device is engineering.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "sword": {
      "name": "sword",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "strength",
      "description": "The blade in all its forms: arming swords, longswords, sabers, rapiers, greatswords. Deals slashing damage. Signature work: the precise parry, the disarm, the duel won clean.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "axe": {
      "name": "axe",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "strength",
      "description": "Hand axes through great axes. Committed, shield-splitting blows. Deals slashing damage. Signature work: breaking guards, hewing through cover, the overhand finish.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "blunt weapons": {
      "name": "blunt weapons",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "strength",
      "description": "One-handed maces, clubs, flails, cudgels, morningstars. Deals impact damage. Signature work: denting plate, stunning blows, fighting in a press where blades can't swing. Two-handed hammers and mauls are warhammer.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "warhammer": {
      "name": "warhammer",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "strength",
      "description": "Two-handed hammers, mauls, great-clubs. One swing, one answer. Deals impact damage. Signature work: ruining armor, breaking shields, stopping a charge dead. One-handed maces and flails are blunt weapons.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "spear": {
      "name": "spear",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Spears, pikes, polearms, lances. Reach and control of the space between. Deals piercing damage. Signature work: holding a line, keeping three foes at the point, the mounted charge.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "staff": {
      "name": "staff",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Quarterstaves and walking staves: two ends, all angles. Deals impact damage. Signature work: sweeps, trips, defense against multiple attackers, winning without killing.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "dagger": {
      "name": "dagger",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Daggers and knives at a range most people fear. Deals piercing damage. Signature work: fighting inside a foe's guard, the grapple-and-blade, the strike before the draw.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "archery": {
      "name": "archery",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Bows and crossbows. Deals piercing damage. Signature work: the long shot, the moving target, the arrow through a gap in armor.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "throwing": {
      "name": "throwing",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Thrown knives, axes, javelins, stones, and slings. Damage by what's thrown — piercing for points, impact for weight. Signature work: the turning throw, two targets in a breath, pinning a sleeve to a door.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "shield": {
      "name": "shield",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "constitution",
      "description": "Bucklers to tower shields: turning blows, covering others, striking with the rim. Bashes deal impact damage. Signature work: holding a doorway, covering an ally under volley, the shield-wall.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "unarmed combat": {
      "name": "unarmed combat",
      "type": "combat",
      "attribute": "strength",
      "description": "Fists, elbows, knees, headbutts, grapples. Deals impact damage. Signature work: disarming a blade barehanded, the chokehold, ending a fight in one motion.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "riding": {
      "name": "riding",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "constitution",
      "description": "Mounts under saddle: riding hard, fighting mounted, staying on when others come off.\nEasy: ride a trained horse at a walk, stay seated at a canter, lead a pack animal.\nMedium: gallop rough ground, jump a fence, calm a mount that's caught a bad scent.\nHard: fight from the saddle, ride down a fleeing man, stay on through panic.\nExtreme: leap a chasm mounted, ride an unbroken stallion to a standstill, thread a battlefield at full gallop.\nTaming and bonding wild beasts is animal handling; exotic mounts ride harder by their nature.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "sailing": {
      "name": "sailing",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "constitution",
      "description": "Boats and ships: handling, navigation at sea, reading weather and water.\nEasy: row a calm harbor, trim a sail in fair wind, tie off properly.\nMedium: sail a coastal run, hold course in chop, bring a boat alongside clean.\nHard: ride out a storm, navigate by stars on open water, thread a reef passage.\nExtreme: sail through a hurricane's edge, run a blockade at night, bring a crippled ship home.\nNavigation on land is survival.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "stealth": {
      "name": "stealth",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Moving unseen and unheard: hiding, sneaking, shadowing, and breaking attention. To become Hidden, describe a plausible means of concealment—cover, darkness, silence, smoke, crowds, confusion, misdirection, or a broken sightline—and make a Stealth check. Failure leaves you exposed; active opposition always makes this a check.\nEasy: leave casual notice using good cover, drift out of a crowd, or follow someone down a busy street.\nMedium: become Hidden amid a confused fight using real cover, cross a guarded yard in shadow, or hide while searchers are nearby.\nHard: break the attention of enemies actively watching for you, slip past an alert sentry at close range, or vanish from a close pursuit.\nExtreme: disappear under concentrated observation, cross open torchlit ground unseen, or shadow a trained spy who expects pursuit.\nHidden is concealment, not invisibility. An attack or another obvious action ends it after that action resolves unless an ability says otherwise. Wearing a false face is performance; locks are lockpicking.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "lockpicking": {
      "name": "lockpicking",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Opening locks and sealed mechanisms without the key.\nEasy: a crude padlock, a jammed latch, a strongbox with a worn-out lock.\nMedium: a house door, a merchant's chest, working by feel in the dark.\nHard: a guildmaster's safe, a prison cell under time pressure, a lock built to break picks.\nExtreme: a master locksmith's life's work, a vault door, a lock picked silently an arm's length from its guard.\nTraps on the lock are trapcraft; magical seals are warding's to break.",
      "startingItems": [
        {
          "item": "Lockpick Set",
          "quantity": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    "trapcraft": {
      "name": "trapcraft",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Traps and snares: spotting them, disarming them, setting them.\nEasy: spot a tripwire in good light, rig a simple snare, disarm a known trap at leisure.\nMedium: sweep a corridor for pressure plates, set a trap that takes a wolf, disarm a dart trap cleanly.\nHard: disarm a trap mid-mechanism, find the trap hidden by a professional, rig a trap that takes an armed man.\nExtreme: unmake a master trapwright's gauntlet, disarm by touch in pitch dark, trap a corridor so well it ends a pursuit.\nGame snares are also tracking's country. Larger contraptions and devices are engineering; magical wards are warding magic.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "pickpocketing": {
      "name": "pickpocketing",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "dexterity",
      "description": "Light hands: lifting, palming, planting, sleight of hand.\nEasy: palm a coin, lift an unwatched purse, swap two similar objects on a table.\nMedium: cut a purse in a market crowd, slip a ring off a distracted hand, plant a token in a pocket.\nHard: lift a key from a guard's belt, work a wary mark, take something the owner checks often.\nExtreme: lift a blade from its sheath, rob a man mid-conversation with you, plant evidence on a spymaster.\nCrowds and distraction make it easier; watchful marks and quiet rooms make it harder.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "leadership": {
      "name": "leadership",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "charisma",
      "description": "Command: rallying, coordinating, being followed.\nEasy: organize willing hands, keep a small group on task, settle a minor dispute.\nMedium: steady nervous recruits, coordinate a search, be obeyed by people who don't know you.\nHard: rally a breaking line, command veterans older than you, hold a crowd at the edge of panic.\nExtreme: turn a rout, lead strangers through fire, take command of those sworn to someone else.\nInspiring through art is performance; the clever plan itself is tactics.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "tracking": {
      "name": "tracking",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "wisdom",
      "description": "Following sign to find and close on a quarry, animal or person: trail, spoor, blood, and the age and direction of passage.\nEasy: follow fresh tracks in soft ground, follow a blood trail, tell a horse passed from a cart.\nMedium: follow a day-old trail over mixed ground, count a party from its camp, stalk within bowshot of wary game.\nHard: track over rock, through water, or along a crowded street, tell a laid false trail from a real one, track by night.\nExtreme: follow a week-old trail after rain, track a creature hiding its trail, name what killed something from the kill alone.\nThis finds and follows; the shot itself is archery, spear, or throwing. Living off the land, weather, and shelter are survival. Snares are shared country with trapcraft. Reading a person's intent is insight; befriending a beast is animal handling.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "animal handling": {
      "name": "animal handling",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "wisdom",
      "description": "Winning beasts over: calming, training, bonding.\nEasy: calm a nervous dog, approach a skittish horse, quiet hens at night.\nMedium: calm a spooked horse mid-panic, teach a dog real commands, handle an animal that's been mistreated.\nHard: approach a wild predator without violence, train a hunting hawk, steady animals as fire spreads.\nExtreme: befriend a creature that's killed men, calm a war-maddened beast, earn a wild animal's lasting loyalty.\nRiding trained mounts is riding; speaking with beasts in words is nature magic.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "farming": {
      "name": "farming",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "constitution",
      "description": "The homestead: crops, livestock, orchards, fishponds, hives, and the turning of seasons.\nEasy: plant a kitchen garden, milk and muck without trouble, judge ripe from not.\nMedium: bring in a harvest before the rain, pull a difficult lambing through, read blight early enough to act.\nHard: save a crop the frost should have taken, nurse a prize animal back from the brink, make poor soil yield.\nExtreme: bring a harvest out of drought, save a herd from a spreading murrain, turn waste ground into a working farm inside a year.\nIncludes fishing, beekeeping, and husbandry. Bonding and training beasts is animal handling; quickening growth by magic is nature magic.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "lore": {
      "name": "lore",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Knowing things: history, legend, heraldry, custom, and what things are worth.\nEasy: name the local lord, recall a famous battle, spot a fake coin.\nMedium: read an old map's conventions, place a stranger by dress and speech, appraise a merchant's stock fairly.\nHard: identify an ancient ruin's builders, recall the weakness in a monster's legend, value a relic no market has priced.\nExtreme: piece together a forgotten dynasty from fragments, know the true name behind a myth, read the meaning of a dead language's inscription.\nKnowing is lore; finding is investigation. Appraisal and street-knowledge live here.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "tactics": {
      "name": "tactics",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Reading and shaping a fight: positioning, plans, the moment to press.\nEasy: pick the defensible corner, spot the obvious flank, know when to back off.\nMedium: set a simple ambush, read which foe leads, position a small group well.\nHard: turn bad ground to advantage, predict the enemy's plan in motion, coordinate a fight on two fronts.\nExtreme: beat numbers with ground and timing, read a master commander's trap before it closes, win the battle in the placement.\nThe plan is tactics; being followed is leadership.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "medicine": {
      "name": "medicine",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "wisdom",
      "description": "Healing without magic: wounds, bones, sickness, poison.\nEasy: clean and bind a cut, splint a finger, dose a fever with the right herb.\nMedium: stitch a deep wound, set a broken arm, recognize a poison by its signs.\nHard: stop bleeding that should be fatal, treat a crushed limb so it heals straight, pull someone through a killing fever.\nExtreme: surgery by lamplight that saves a life, identify and counter a rare poison in time, keep the dying alive until real help comes.\nSlower and humbler than healing magic, and works where magic is spent or absent. Brewing remedies at a bench is alchemy.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "alchemy": {
      "name": "alchemy",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "The bench arts: potions, poisons, reagents, transformations of matter.\nEasy: brew a simple remedy, render fat to tallow, identify a common reagent.\nMedium: brew a healing draught, distill a clean poison, stabilize a volatile mixture.\nHard: brew from a formula half-lost, counter a poison from its symptoms alone, work with reagents that punish mistakes.\nExtreme: create a draught no recipe describes, refine a legendary reagent without ruining it, brew under fire with a field kit.\nEasier in a proper laboratory; harder with improvised tools. Binding magic into objects is enchanting.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "engineering": {
      "name": "engineering",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Making things work: contraptions, machines, siegeworks, and clever construction.\nEasy: fix a wagon wheel, rig a pulley, judge whether a floor will hold.\nMedium: repair a mill mechanism, rig a hoist for a heavy load, brace a failing tunnel.\nHard: build a working siege engine from parts, divert a stream through a camp, understand an ancient mechanism by inspection.\nExtreme: crack the workings of old-world magitek, bridge a gorge with what's on hand, build a machine no one's seen before.\nTraps and snares as such are trapcraft; lasting magic in the work is enchanting.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "smithing": {
      "name": "smithing",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Metalwork: forging, repairing, and finishing — from horseshoes to blades to jewelry.\nEasy: mend a hinge, sharpen a blade true, judge good ore from bad.\nMedium: forge a serviceable sword, repair mail, set a stone in a simple ring.\nHard: forge a fine weapon worth a name, work a difficult metal clean, finish jewelry a noble would wear.\nExtreme: forge a masterwork blade, rework an ancient piece without ruining it, smith a thing other smiths come to study.\nJewelry and ore-sense live here. Enchanting the work is enchanting.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "carpentry": {
      "name": "carpentry",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Building in wood and stone: framing, joinery, masonry.\nEasy: mend a fence, hang a true door, lay a straight course of brick.\nMedium: frame a shed that stands square, repair a roof properly, build solid furniture.\nHard: raise a house from foundation to ridgepole, repair a bridge that carries carts, vault a stone ceiling.\nExtreme: build what masters would sign, restore ancient stonework seamlessly, raise a hall in a season.\nMasonry and building live here; machines and mechanisms are engineering.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "leatherworking": {
      "name": "leatherworking",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Hide and leather: tanning, cutting, stitching, armoring.\nEasy: patch a boot, oil and mend tack, cut a clean strap.\nMedium: make good boots to measure, craft a sturdy pack, repair leather armor properly.\nHard: craft armor that turns a blade, work an exotic hide without waste, finish goods a guild would stamp.\nExtreme: armor from a creature's hide that keeps its virtue, masterwork a guild would display, restore a relic of old leather.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "tailoring": {
      "name": "tailoring",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "intelligence",
      "description": "Cloth and thread: cutting, sewing, fitting, finery.\nEasy: hem and mend, patch invisibly enough, take in a coat.\nMedium: sew a garment to measure, copy a fashionable cut, repair fine cloth without a trace.\nHard: dress someone for court, work silk and cloth-of-gold, fit armor's padding so it saves lives.\nExtreme: a gown that sets the season's fashion, recreate a lost weave, finery fit for a coronation.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "cooking": {
      "name": "cooking",
      "type": "utility",
      "attribute": "wisdom",
      "description": "The kitchen and the kettle: meals, preserving, brewing.\nEasy: a solid camp meal, bake honest bread, brew passable ale.\nMedium: feed a full table well, preserve a harvest through winter, brew ale people ask for by name.\nHard: a feast that honors a hall, cook a memorable meal from poor stores, brew a batch worth trading.\nExtreme: a dish spoken of for years, feed an army from a moving kitchen, brew what connoisseurs travel for.\nBrewing and preserving live here. Remedies and poisons are alchemy.",
      "startingItems": []
    },
    "spirit magic": {
      "name": "spirit magic",
      "type": "magic",
      "attribute": "attunement",
      "description": "Perceiving, addressing, bargaining with, invoking, warding, and driving out spirits connected to ancestors, elements, places, objects, and strong memories.\nEasy: sense a nearby spirit, recognize spiritual disturbance, offer a respectful greeting, hear a faint ancestral warning.\nMedium: converse with a nearby spirit, learn what holds it to a place, ask a known spirit for direct practical aid, ward a doorway against lesser spirits.\nHard: drive a hostile spirit from a person or place, call an ancestor into visible presence, negotiate meaningful aid from a powerful local spirit, break a spiritual curse.\nExtreme: bargain with a great spirit, cross bodily into the spirit world, end possession by an ancient power, establish a lasting covenant between a spirit and a people or place.\nSpirits have wills. Success secures attention, communication, a fair bargain, or aid within a spirit's nature; it does not make every spirit obedient. Familiar spirits and fitting offerings make workings easier. Hostility, violated taboos, alien places, and requests against a spirit's nature make them harder. Elemental manifestations use their element's damage type; direct spiritual assaults deal psychic damage; ancestors acting through weapons use the weapon's damage type.\nIts Extreme bodily crossing is one crossing through a rite, thin place, gate, or guide. The Graywalk permits an unaided crossing made at will. Being ridden by a spirit is spirit channeling.",
      "startingItems": []
    }
  },
