    "Human": {
      "name": "Human",
      "description": "Humans live fast and refuse to accept it. Where longer-lived races measure ambition in centuries, humans measure it in decades — and somehow get more done. They fill every role, chase every calling, and build kingdoms in a single generation through sheer restless drive. What they lack in raw power or ancient wisdom, they make up for with stamina, charm, and a refusal to stay down. No race in Larion is more varied in temperament or talent, and none spreads faster.\n\nThe most physically diverse people in Larion. Skin from pale to deep brown, hair from flaxen to black, builds from slight to broad. Heights range from just over five feet to well past six. No single look defines them — a human from the Bright Kingdoms and a human from Aurora might not recognize each other as kin.\n\nCommon enough in every corner of Larion that a human face rarely draws a second glance. They walk into taverns, trading posts, and throne rooms without raising eyebrows — a convenience that rarer folk don't enjoy. Other races find them ambitious to a fault, always building something new before the last thing is finished. Respected for their energy. Exhausting to keep up with.",
