    "Dwarf": {
      "name": "Dwarf",
      "description": "Built for stone and deep places. Dwarves live in clan-holds carved into mountain roots, bound by ties of kinship, craft, and duty that outlast human kingdoms. They measure worth by what you make and whether you keep your word. A dwarf who breaks an oath is already dead to their clan — and most would rather die than prove it true. They live two centuries or more, and every year makes them more stubborn.\n\nBroad and dense-boned, rarely more than five feet tall but often nearly as wide at the shoulder. Thick-fingered hands built for hammer and chisel. Skin tones from ruddy bronze to deep granite-grey. Hair worn long and often braided — copper, black, iron-grey, or stark white regardless of age. Heavy brows, deep-set eyes, and defined jawlines.\n\nA dwarf's word is taken seriously everywhere in Larion, and so is their coin. Merchants offer fair prices, smiths acknowledge a peer, and strangers assume competence. But no one expects a dwarf to be flexible, funny, or fast. Seen as reliable, immovable, and predictable — which suits most dwarves just fine.",
