    "Halfling": {
      "name": "Halfling",
      "description": "Small, quick, and easy to underestimate: just how most halflings like it. They stand about three feet tall and make up for it with fast hands, sharp instincts, and more charm than anyone expects. Halflings turn up everywhere: running market stalls, cooking for mercenary companies, scouting for armies, or quietly running the best tavern in town. They prize comfort, good food, and good company, but don't mistake that for softness. A halfling who's survived the road has done it by being quicker, cleverer, and more likeable than whatever was trying to kill them.\n\nSmall and slight with nimble builds. Round faces, bright eyes, and curly hair in shades of brown, auburn, copper, or straw-blond. Bare feet by preference — the soles toughen like leather — though boots are worn when the terrain demands it. Halfling hands are deft and nimble, a boon for locksmiths, tailors, and thieves alike. \n\nPeople like halflings. They can't help it. A halfling in the room lowers the tension, and most folk are disarmed before they realize they've let their guard down. The flip side: nobody takes them seriously at first. Guards look past them, warlords dismiss them, and shopkeepers assume they can't afford the good stock. Halflings who've learned to use that blind spot tend to do very well for themselves.",
