    "Orc": {
      "name": "Orc",
      "description": "Orcs are a people of witnessed oaths, clan memory, fierce competition, and blunt affection. Their homeland is the Orc Wolds, where Clan Drokash rides the open steppe and Clan Vorren builds in the iron hills, but generations of war scattered orc communities across Larion. Strength earns respect; keeping your word earns trust. An oath spoken before an elder is sacred, and an orc who breaks one loses more than reputation. Orcs mock the people they love, eat from shared platters, argue loudly, and find polite evasions far more insulting than an honest challenge.\n\nTall, broad, and heavy with muscle. Green or brown skin, prominent lower tusks, and deep-set eyes in shades of amber, black, or copper. Thick jaws, heavy brows, and builds that run to powerful rather than lean. Most stand over six feet. Hair is worn in braids, topknots, or shaved close, often decorated with clan tokens or bone rings.\n\nWithin the Orc Wolds, tusks, clan tokens, contests, and hard truths are ordinary. Elsewhere, strangers often see a fighter first and ask questions second. Guards watch orcs a little longer and merchants speak a little more carefully, but those who have lived or worked beside them know the other reputation: fierce loyalty, communal generosity, cheerful insult, and a promise that means exactly what it says.",
