    "Dragonkin": {
      "name": "Dragonkin",
      "description": "Descended from true dragons through bloodlines no one fully understands. Dragonkin carry that heritage in their bones — the scales, the horns, the elemental fire in their veins, and the instinct to dominate any room they enter. They're drawn to power the way their ancestors were drawn to hoards, though what a dragonkin hoards varies: gold, followers, knowledge, territory. Most feel the pull of elemental magic whether they train in it or not. A dragonkin who ignores their draconic nature entirely is rare and usually unhappy.\n\nLarge and powerfully built, standing six to seven feet tall with dense, scaled skin in shades of bronze, crimson, obsidian, emerald, or pale silver. Pronounced horns curve back from the skull — shape and size vary by lineage. Vertical-slit pupils, heavy clawed hands, and a broad chest built for the deep breath that precedes something terrible. Tails are common but not universal. Some lineages show more human features, others look barely humanoid at all.\n\nDragonkin don't walk into a room unnoticed. This isn't fear exactly — it's the recognition that something powerful just arrived. In the Bright Kingdoms and Westmarch, dragonkin often find doors opened for them simply because no one wants to be the one who said no. The assumption is always strength first, subtlety never. Dragonkin who prefer books to battlefields spend a lot of time correcting first impressions.",
