    "Moon elf": {
      "name": "Moon elf",
      "description": "Moon elves withdrew from the world after the Kindred War split elvenkind, and they've spent the centuries since accumulating knowledge the way other races accumulate coin. They live five hundred years or more, and it shows in everything they do. They take the long view on matters other races consider urgent, and the very long view on everything else. Magic comes to them as naturally as breathing, and most moon elf children can read a ward before they can read a book.\n\nTall and slender with silver-pale skin. Hair ranges from white-platinum to deep blue-black, worn long. Eyes are large and luminous — silver, violet, pale gold, or solid black — adapted for perfect vision in darkness. Their features are angular and fine-boned, with a stillness to their expressions that other races often misread as coldness.\n\nMoon elves are treated as authorities on magic and history whether they've earned it or not. A moon elf who walks into a library or academy is assumed to belong there. A moon elf who walks into a tavern gets watched — not because anyone necessarily minds, but because everyone assumes the moon elf is sizing them up. The reputation for arrogance isn't entirely unfair. Some moon elves may be patient with ignorance, but they rarely bother to hide that they consider it ignorance.",
