    "High elf": {
      "name": "High elf",
      "description": "High elves are the surface kindred of the Everwood and the people of Canopy, heirs to the silverleaf cities and the long peace called the Sundering. They build in living wood, preserve the old arts of greenshaping and wardcraft, and believe a good life should show discipline, beauty, and care for what must last. They are not all nobles or Wardens: high elves include scholars, artisans, rangers, soldiers, traders, and exiles from the Council's slow politics.\n\nTall and slender, with fine-boned faces and long pointed ears. Skin ranges from ivory and rose-gold through olive and warm brown; hair from silver, pale gold, copper, chestnut, or black; eyes are often green, gold, grey, or clear blue. Their clothing favors layered cloth, worked wood, leaf-metal, house colors, and practical gear suited to the heights of Canopy.\n\nA high elf is recognized as one of the forest's people even far from Elfwood. In Canopy, lineage and bearing carry weight; elsewhere, strangers may read their poise as refinement or condescension. They are expected to understand old obligations and the Sundering, but an adventuring high elf may uphold that inheritance, question it, or simply want to see the world below the branches.",
