    "Wood elf": {
      "name": "Wood elf",
      "description": "Wood elves never left the forests. When the Kindred War tore elvenkind apart, they chose neither side — they chose the trees. They live in scattered communities through the deep woodlands of Larion, particularly the Everwood, building with living wood and answering to councils of elders rather than kings. Where moon elves hoard knowledge and dark elves prize cleverness, wood elves value connection — to the land, the seasons, the signs that something is wrong before anyone else notices. They live as long as their moon elf cousins, but count their years in seasons and harvests rather than books read.\n\nLean and long-limbed with sun-darkened skin in shades of brown, olive, and weathered bronze. Hair tends toward earth tones — chestnut, deep red, black, mossy green — often worn loose or tied back for practicality. Their eyes are bright and watchful: green, amber, hazel, or deep brown. They move quietly by habit, and most have the kind of stillness that lets them disappear into a treeline without trying.\n\nWood elves are trusted in wild places and treated as outsiders in cities. Farmers and villagers on the forest edge welcome them as trading partners and wardens. In larger towns, they're regarded as capable but odd — people who could live comfortably but choose bark and rain instead. Most folk assume a wood elf knows the answer to any question about weather, beasts, or which mushrooms will kill you.",
