    "Catkin": {
      "name": "Catkin",
      "description": "Feline folk with the reflexes and restlessness to match. Catkin are found across Larion but never in large numbers — they don't build cities or hold territory the way other races do. They drift, settle for a while, drift again. Most are drawn to work that rewards quick reflexes and independent judgment: scouting, hunting, rooftop courier work, the kind of job where being able to land on your feet matters literally. They're social on their own terms, affectionate when they choose to be, and gone without warning when they don't.\n\nLithe builds covered in short fur ranging from tawny gold to charcoal, tabby-striped, calico, or solid black. Cat-shaped ears sit high on the head and move independently, tracking sound before the catkin consciously reacts. Eyes are large with vertical pupils — green, gold, copper, or pale blue — and see well in near-darkness. Retractable claws on both hands and feet. Tails are expressive and hard to control, giving away mood even when the face stays composed.\n\nPeople find catkin charming in small doses and unsettling in large ones. The way they watch, the way they go still before they move, the fact that they're always closer than you thought — it reads as predatory even when it isn't. Most folk enjoy a catkin's company but wouldn't trust one with a key to the shop. Whether that caution is earned depends entirely on the catkin.",
