    "Demonborn": {
      "name": "Demonborn",
      "description": "Demonborn descend from the people who escaped the Primordial Plane of Ur during the Excession and made a new life in Larion. Their greatest communities stand in Ntar Vanna, especially New Anthara, with others across the southern isles, eastern deserts, and every port where trade carries them. Otherworldly power still answers readily through their blood, but demonborn culture is built around freedom from Ur: passionate, direct, fiercely hospitable, and committed to the deliberate self-mastery that keeps power from becoming another master. The Children of Ur reject that freedom; they are a proscribed cult, not the measure of the people they betray.\n\nDemonborn vary dramatically in appearance. Horns range from small nubs to sweeping curves. Skin may be deep crimson, ashen grey, bruise-purple, or other unnatural colors, sometimes patterned or faintly luminous. Clawed fingers, pointed teeth, tails, and eyes of solid gold, red, black, or silver are common, while builds vary as widely as those of other peoples. No demonborn passes wholly for human — something about them is always visibly, unmistakably other.\n\nIn Ntar Vanna and many southern ports, demonborn features are ordinary and their traditions are understood. Elsewhere, horns and glowing eyes still draw stares, superstition, fascination, or suspicion. Demonborn learn to read that first look quickly, but they do not define themselves by it: they are the descendants of people who escaped the High Princes and chose their own future.",
