    "Giantborn": {
      "name": "Giantborn",
      "description": "Giantborn trace their ancestry to the ur-giants said to have shaped Larion's northern mountains. They stand head and shoulders above most other peoples, with the size, strength, and valley-carrying voices of that old blood. Their strongest communities live in Highheath's cattle-vales, where families such as Tuskhollow raise enormous herds, settle pride through feats of strength, and remember favors and insults for generations. Giantborn are not all warriors: their size also makes them prized as herders, porters, smiths, builders, and anyone who can turn a two-person task into a one-person job. Their joy tends to be loud, their hospitality generous, and their anger hard to miss.\n\nMassive. Seven feet is average, eight not unusual. Thick-limbed and heavy-boned with broad hands that make human weapons look undersized. Skin tones mirror human ranges but often carry a stony undertone — slate-grey, ruddy granite, pale quartz. Hair is coarse and heavy, ranging from black and brown to stone-white. Their features are blunt and strong, with heavy brows and deep-set eyes.\n\nGiantborn are impossible to miss. People step aside, perhaps less from fear than from simple necessity — a giantborn in a crowded space parts the crowd without trying. Stools buckle, market awnings catch on shoulders, and every doorway is a reminder to duck. People remember a giantborn: they are the easiest witness to recall, the hardest person to lose in a crowd, and often the first person asked to lift, carry, fight, or take the blame.",
