    "Dark Elf": {
      "name": "Dark Elf",
      "description": "Driven into the Rootdark after the Kindred War, dark elves built Maanvalta into a wealthy realm beneath the Elfwood and made exile look enviable. Within Elfwood, the Sundering confines them to the deep and to Ilunethel on the surface; beyond the high elves' realm, their houses reach the wider world through tunnel-roads, trade, agents, and coin. Dark elves prize velesse — the art of getting exactly what you want while making it look effortless. Wit, craft, style, illusion, and a useful lie all earn respect; being dull is often treated as a worse failure than being wrong.\n\nSilver-white or blue-black hair contrasts with skin ranging from charcoal grey to deep obsidian. Eyes adapted for total darkness may be pale violet, silver, amber, or faintly luminous red. Dark elves tend to be lean and sharp-featured, and they dress with intention even when they own very little. The way they carry themselves often suggests they know something you do not.\n\nDark elves carry a reputation for beautiful craft, dangerous charm, illusion, theft, and intrigue, and many of them enjoy keeping the stories alive. Cosmopolitan cities hire them as spies, enchanters, entertainers, and negotiators; Ilunethel openly trades in their work; Nocturne's outcasts in the Shadow Summits rarely object to another elegant danger. More conservative communities remain suspicious, and anyone who assumes charm and danger are separate qualities tends to learn otherwise.",
