    "Serpentkin": {
      "name": "Serpentkin",
      "description": "Cold-blooded in more senses than one. Serpentkin are reptilian humanoids with snake-like heads, fanged jaws, and a way of thinking that other races find alien and a little frightening. They don't rush. They don't panic. They let a situation play out before they move, and when they move, they don't miss. Serpentkin societies in Ntar Vanna are ancient and layered — built on obligation, hierarchy, and the understanding that venom is only one of several tools available. Outside their homeland, most serpentkin operate alone or in small enclaves, and they prefer it that way.\n\nScaled skin in patterns of jade, amber, obsidian, sand-brown, or deep emerald, sometimes banded or diamond-patterned. Serpentine heads with lidless eyes — gold, slit-pupiled, unblinking. Forked tongues that read scent the way others read expressions. Lean, flexible builds with deceptive strength in the grip. Fangs carry mild venom in most bloodlines, though potency varies. They move with an unsettling smoothness — no wasted motion, no fidgeting, no tells.\n\nSerpentkin make people nervous. The unblinking stare, the tongue-flick, the absolute stillness before they speak — it all reads as predatory even in friendly conversation. Merchants deal with them fairly because serpentkin have long memories and longer grudges. Alchemists and poisoners seek them out for their expertise. Most folk are polite, careful, and quietly relieved when they leave. Serpentkin are aware of this effect and few go out of their way to soften it.",
