    "Cleric": {
      "name": "Cleric",
      "description": "Main Attributes: Attunement and Wisdom\n\nClerics are people who answer a call and learn the rites that let that call act through them. Their power lives in prayers, hands, vows, symbols, water, oil, bells, salt, fire, scripture, and the stubborn work of care. A cleric can close a wound, steady the dying, bless a road, name a curse, turn the profane, or make a frightened room remember what it believes.\n\nClerics serve temples, shrines, orders, battlefields, villages, roads, or a faith they carry without walls. Some are gentle healers, some hard-eyed exorcists, some battlefield priests, some keepers of burial rites. What they share is presence under pressure: they bring mercy where bodies break, judgment where corruption festers, and ritual where chaos wants to make people forget themselves.\n\nSpecial Starting Gear: Holy Symbol",
