    "Lizardfolk": {
      "name": "Lizardfolk",
      "description": "Older than the elves and unimpressed by the fact. Lizardfolk have lived in the marshes, rivers, and coastal shallows of Larion since before anyone started writing things down, and they regard the rise and fall of kingdoms with the polite disinterest of someone watching weather pass. They're not primitive — they build, trade, worship, and wage war — they just don't see the point of doing any of it faster than necessary. A lizardfolk hunts when hungry, fights when threatened, and rests without guilt. Other races call this lazy. Lizardfolk call it sane.\n\nBroad and solid, standing five and a half to six and a half feet tall with dense, scaled hide in shades of green, brown, slate-grey, or muddy gold. Blunt snouts, heavy jaws, and eyes set wide on the skull — amber, yellow, or dark brown with horizontal pupils. Thick tails used for balance and swimming. Clawed hands and feet. Their faces are largely unreadable to mammalian eyes — the muscles aren't built for the same expressions, and most lizardfolk don't bother learning to fake them.\n\nLizardfolk confuse people. They're not hostile, not friendly, not rude, not polite — they're just there, watching with those flat unblinking eyes, saying exactly what they mean in as few words as possible. Most folk find the honesty refreshing for about ten minutes and then deeply unsettling. Lizardfolk don't do small talk, don't feign interest, and won't laugh at a joke they don't find funny. In the Great Lagoon and Ntar Vanna this is understood. Elsewhere, people assume they're either stupid or angry. They're usually neither.",
