    "Goblin": {
      "name": "Goblin",
      "description": "Goblins are small, wiry people of volcanic forge-towns, independent caravans, border camps, and raiding bands. The Black Fells hold their largest settlements, where goblin makers work obsite, metal, dragonfire, and whatever a clever hand can keep alive. Some serve the Greater Goblinate; many do not. Goblin life prizes quick judgment, useful craft, and knowing when a fair fight is a stupid one.\n\nMost goblins stand well below human height, with wiry builds, pointed ears, sharp features, and skin ranging from sallow green to grey-brown. Their hands are quick, their eyes watchful, and their tools are often repaired more times than anyone can count. A goblin's best possession is usually the thing they can make work when it should have failed.\n\nIn most settled communities, people do not welcome a goblin by default. Guards may assume raider or Goblinate agent, innkeepers may ask who vouches for you, and strangers may watch your hands. This is not universal hostility: Black Fells communities, independent caravans, craft circles, people who need a fixer, and people who know your deeds may offer conditional respect.",
