    "Vanarin": {
      "name": "Vanarin",
      "description": "The Vanarin—High Vanarin to themselves—hold Citadel Uchaghar in the southern jungles of Ntar Vanna. They are quick, agile, canopy-dwelling people who fight in three dimensions, launch from ropes and branches, and treat boldness as a form of good manners. Their pride is enormous, their generosity is real, and their loyalty is fierce once earned.\n\nVanarin have expressive monkeylike faces, short fur in dark, copper, russet, or gold-brown shades, long arms, nimble hands, rounded ears, and powerful prehensile tails. They move as comfortably above a river or street as most people move across level ground. A Vanarin warrior is expected to see the route nobody else can reach.\n\nOutside Ntar Vanna, Vanarin are rare and conspicuous. Strangers may stare, misunderstand Vanarin customs around generosity and possession, or distrust quick hands near valuables. In Uchaghar and other southern communities, boldness, generosity, and courage can earn recognition quickly; elsewhere, trust usually begins with a demonstration rather than an assumption.",
