    "Gnoll": {
      "name": "Gnoll",
      "description": "Gnolls are hyena-headed people of packs, caravan roads, and the burnt cities of lower Redrock. Their princes build power through raids, tribute, captives, and public contests of strength, but not every gnoll accepts a prince's rule. Packs break, exiles travel, and a gnoll who refuses a bad alpha may become a hunter, guard, guide, or rebel far from the people who named them.\n\nGnolls are tall and powerful, with long arms, sloping shoulders, coarse fur marked in ochre, brown, grey, or black, rounded ears, broad jaws, and teeth made for tearing. Their senses and pack habits make them dangerous trackers and ambushers. A gnoll who chooses a different life still carries the body and reputation of the pack.\n\nMost settled people read a gnoll as a raider or pack enforcer. Guards, merchants, and caravan towns may demand proof, toll, or distance. A gnoll who breaks with a prince can also be treated as a traitor by gnoll powers. This is suspicion and political danger, not automatic violence: independent caravan folk, rebels, and people defended by the character may become allies.",
