    "Empyrean": {
      "name": "Empyrean",
      "description": "Empyreans are rare, scattered winged people whose ancestors ruled land, sea, and sky from the Third Empire. The old empire was proud and tyrannical; the empyreans alive today are not responsible for it, though their height, wings, inner-lit eyes, and ancient names make the history difficult to forget. The Empire of Light at Caranthoria claims the old crown's foundations while opening citizenship to every people, and an empyrean may be welcomed there, recruited, watched, or all three.\n\nEmpyreans stand taller than most humans and are built on a grander scale, with strong features, broad feathered wings, and skin and feathers ranging from white through red, black, bronze, and shades between. Their eyes hold a faint steady light. Wings are part of their body and identity, not proof of holiness.\n\nAn empyrean is rare and impossible to ignore. People may assume imperial, celestial, or ancient tyrant ancestry; the Empire of Light may expect service or loyalty. In Caranthoria and among people who know modern empyreans, recognition can open doors, but most settlements begin with attention and assumptions rather than easy trust.",
