    "Druid": {
      "name": "Druid",
      "description": "Main Attributes: Attunement and Wisdom\n\nDruids work with the living world as it is: root, rain, rot, thorn, soil, animal sign, river mud, bark, hunger, shelter, and blight. Their magic is not a lecture from nature. It is a practiced relationship with land that answers in useful ways when danger comes. A druid knows when a forest has gone too quiet, when a field is sick, when water has been fouled, and when a path is trying to close behind someone.\n\nIn Larion, druids protect wild places, guide settlements through weather and plague, read the health of farms and forests, and make the terrain itself part of the answer. They can call roots around an enemy's feet, wrap an ally in bark and bramble, borrow a beast's sense or a tree's patience, and help living things hold together when poison, panic, or violence would tear them apart.",
