    },
    "Fighter": {
      "name": "Fighter",
      "description": "Main Attribute: Strength\n\nFighters are not just people with weapons. They are the ones who know where to stand, when to move, how to read a grip, how to punish bad footing, and how to make a chaotic fight obey them for one more breath. A fighter can be an academy duelist, mercenary veteran, pit champion, guard captain, caravan blade, village defender, or self-taught survivor, but the core is the same: practiced violence under pressure.\n\nIn Larion, fighters keep roads open, hold doors while others run, break charges before they land, and turn ugly brawls into winnable exchanges. Magic can fail, bargains can sour, courage can crack. A trained fighter still knows how to put steel, shield, armor, body, and timing between danger and the people or prize that matter.\n\nA fighter can bring practiced control to any weapon, even one snatched from an enemy or improvised from what lies at hand. They may use a trained weapon skill of their choice instead of the weapon's matching skill. Before level 10, doing so carries a -5 modifier; at level 10, that modifier disappears.",
