      ],
      "unlockedBy": [],
      "excludedBy": [],
      "requirements": [],
      "traitNarrativeEffects": "A monk can command their own living body beyond ordinary mortal limits: change how it bears weight and force, harden or loosen it, act without sight, bring impossible timing to a movement, hold breath or poison at bay, or urge a fresh wound to close. A learned Form perfects one such command into a repeatable technique. Teachers and rival practitioners may answer a demonstrated breakthrough with instruction or a harder ordeal."
    },
    "Paladin": {
      "name": "Paladin",
      "description": "Main Attributes: Attunement, Strength, Wisdom, and Charisma\n\nPaladins turn divine service into vows and vows into action. Each serves one or more patron divinities, pledging to carry divine will into the world through action. A vow may bind a paladin to defend a temple, order, homeland, company, cause, or sacred ideal, but the patron divinity is the power that witnesses and answers it. It is a promise with armor on: the paladin names what they will do, fulfills it under pressure, and returns in prayer for the patron's answer.\n\nSome paladins guard pilgrims and sanctuaries. Some hunt undead, fiends, tyrants, oathbreakers, or monsters that prey on the helpless. Some serve old orders, and some carry a vow no institution fully understands. What they share is not softness or certainty, but commitment under pressure: the courage to stand between danger and the vulnerable, and the authority to make a fight about more than survival.\n\nSpecial Starting Gear: Devotion Clasp",
