    "Ranger": {
      "name": "Ranger",
      "description": "Main Attributes: Dexterity and Wisdom\n\nRangers are scouts, hunters, guides, wardens, and ambushers who understand how movement works when roads end and sightlines lie. They read tracks, weather, cover, water, animal sign, patrol habits, and bad footing as quickly as other people read faces. A ranger does not need a fair fight. A ranger needs the right ground, the right route, and one clean moment when the target steps where they should not.\n\nEvery frontier settlement, logging camp, border fort, and trade caravan knows the value of a good ranger. They find the pass before snow closes it, spot the raiders before the horn sounds, guide travelers around danger, and put an arrow or blade into trouble from the angle it forgot to guard. The best rangers make the world feel larger to their allies and much smaller to anything being hunted.\n\nRangers can tame and train wild beasts, and one that comes to lasting trust may become an enduring companion in travel and battle. Their finest shots can follow trajectories no ordinary archer could make.",
