    "Tinker": {
      "name": "Tinker",
      "description": "Main Attributes: Intelligence and Dexterity\n\nTinkers solve problems with kit, nerve, and hands that keep moving: clamps, springs, wire, lenses, vials, gears, oil, chalk marks, tiny charms, and field repairs that hold exactly long enough. Some build companions or elaborate constructs, but the core trade is more immediate than that. A tinker sees where pressure goes, where a mechanism wants to fail, and what small device can make the next few seconds belong to them.\n\nIn Larion, tinkers fix wagons, open old locks, read broken mechanisms, rig traps, patch armor, tune spellgear, and make dangerous little tools from whatever is on hand. In a fight, they do not need to be the strongest person in the room. They need a hinge, a wire, a weak plate, a vial, a spark, and one good moment when the device works.\n\nSpecial Starting Gear: Artificer's Toolkit; a Spring-Fist; a Needle Trap of Poison and its blueprint; a Stormsteel Burstwheel of Shock and its blueprint; two bundles of Mechanical Components; and one Venomwood Extract.",
