      "excludedBy": [],
      "requirements": [],
      "traitNarrativeEffects": "The player bears the Mark of Rhadan and is recognized as a member of the Shadow Inquisition. The Shadow Inquisition is a heroic and prestigious institution in Drusavia. Its Inquisitors protect the living from ghosts, necromancers, vampires, ghouls, and other threats from the dead. The Mark is a sanctioned sign of service, not a curse or proof of evil. Drusavian rulers, guards, and citizens generally respect the order's authority and do not interfere with its work lightly. The Mark anchors authorized crossings and keeps the Shadelands from rejecting them outright. It does not establish their rank: an Initiate remains a candidate, cannot undertake an unsanctioned descent, and is not Shade-Bonded until completing the Rite of Bonding."
    },
    "Shade-Bonded": {
      "name": "Shade-Bonded",
      "description": "Through the authorized Rite of Bonding at the Pit of Shadow, you knowingly accepted a permanent bond with a Shade — a spirit drawn from the Shadelands, the grey country of the dead. It stands with you as supernatural partner and shield: a figure almost a person, the shape right but the details wrong, like a reflection in dark water. Through the bond you feel the dead and the Shadelands pressing into the living world.",
