    "Path of the Blade": {
      "name": "Path of the Blade",
      "description": "You are trained in serious weapon combat. This Path covers soldiers, duelists, guards, mercenaries, knights, pit fighters, and anyone who has learned to stay alive when steel comes out. The Order of the Silver Sword and other martial schools can give this beginning a place in the world, but the Path is broader than any one order. Its foundation is the body that carries the weapon: footwork, wind, balance, and the conditioning that decides who is still standing in the third minute.\n\nTo pursue Novice rank, first declare a concrete martial feat before attempting it, explicitly naming Novice of the Blade as the rank you seek. Enact the declaration as a vow, promise, pledge, or sworn undertaking to a god, master, witness, opponent, institution, or yourself. Name the feat, a meaningful danger or constraint, and a clear success condition. A suitable Novice feat requires disciplined weapon use under genuine danger; for example, swear to disarm a dangerous opponent without killing them or hold a named position until others escape.",
