    "Shaman": {
      "name": "Shaman",
      "description": "Main Attributes: Attunement, Wisdom, and Constitution\n\nShamans deal with the unseen inhabitants of the world. Spirits gather in wind and flame, earth and water, old roads, homes, battlefields, treasured objects, strong memories, and the honored dead. They are not gods, and they are not creatures dragged from elsewhere and bound like conjured servants. They have their own natures, desires, loyalties, and grudges.\n\nA shaman learns to perceive them, address them, bargain for their aid, ward against them, challenge them, and sometimes welcome them into the body. Every shaman gradually gathers a spirit court: the ancestors and other powers that know their name and may answer when called. A novice has only a few such relationships. A great shaman can open the way for many spirits to act together.\n\nIn danger, spirits strike through wind, flame, stone, water, weapon, and voice. They guard boundaries, expose what is hidden, lend their nature to a shaman's body, and take form beside the living. Spirit Magic is not Conjuration: conjurers call and bind creatures from elsewhere, while shamans deal with spirits connected to this world and must reckon with why they answer.\n\nSpecial Starting Gear: Spirit Mask",
      "attributes": [],
      "skills": [
        {
          "skill": "spirit magic",
          "modifier": 5
        },
        {
          "skill": "divination magic",
          "modifier": 5
        },
        {
          "skill": "survival",
          "modifier": 5
        },
        {
          "skill": "spirit channeling",
          "modifier": 5
        }
      ],
      "resources": [
        {
          "resource": "mana",
          "modifier": 40
        }
      ],
      "startingItems": [
        {
          "item": "Spirit Mask",
          "quantity": 1
        }
      ],
      "abilities": [
        "Soulstrike",
        "Second Wind",
        "Draw Power"
      ],
      "unlockedBy": [],
      "excludedBy": [],
      "requirements": [],
      "traitNarrativeEffects": "A shaman is a spirit-worker who can see and speak with the unseen inhabitants of the world: spirits of places, objects, and elements; ancestors; and presences born from powerful memories. They read the signs spirits leave, learn their wants and taboos, and win their aid through respect, offerings, shared purpose, leverage, or bargains. A shaman’s spirit court is the circle of named spirits that have chosen lasting bonds with them and may answer when called. A spirit enters that court through a bond formed in the character’s past or during play. After a meaningful victory or discovery, a local spirit may make its notice concrete—a voice from an object, an element taking a face, an ancestor stepping into view—leaving the player to approach, answer, or walk away. If a lasting bond forms, the spirit may mark it with a physical token."
    },
