  "npcTypes": {
    "aberration": {
      "name": "aberration",
      "description": "The reality-wrong: mimics, doppelgangers, gibbering mouthers, corpse-eaters, psychic horrors, and the ancient minds in black water. Wrongness is the register — anatomy that should not work, hungers that should not exist, minds that press against yours (psychic). Kinds: the mimic is the chest, and sometimes the door — ration it, the trick dulls; the doppelganger wears stolen faces and is an intrigue engine before it is a combatant; the aboleth-tier horror gets one seat in the world's deepest water, and it remembers — it is never a wandering encounter. Aberrations are wrong for reality anywhere; the deep-things are merely adapted to the dark — do not confuse the families. In combat: wrongness as tactics — false surfaces, stolen shapes, minds assaulted directly (psychic); a point finds no vitals because there are none where they should be (piercing resist); holy radiance forces the wrong shape back toward reality (radiant vulnerability); fighting one should feel like the rules bent.",
      "vulnerabilities": [
