        "arcane"
      ],
      "immunities": []
    },
    "fey": {
      "name": "fey",
      "description": "The fey and the old wild: dryads, satyrs, sprites, treants, unicorns, redcaps, will-o'-wisps, and the hags. Kinds: dryads are bound each to her tree and grove, and the grove's law is hers; satyrs are revels, music, and wagers — trouble more than threat; sprites are tiny armed wardens, fierce out of all proportion; treants are the wood's slow shepherds, terrible when it is wronged; unicorns are the deep wood's blessing, appearing only to the worthy; redcaps squat iron-booted at old battle-sites, and they murder; will-o'-wisps lead travelers off the causeway at night; hags bargain, and the bargain always costs more than asked. Every fey has a law, a price, and a boundary — name all three. Fey keep bargains to the letter and punish the spirit; they mislead rather than lie; they are moved by beauty, novelty, insult, and obligation, never by coin alone. Never write fey as generic forest spirits or harmless whimsy. In combat: charm, misdirection, and the wild itself turned hostile (arcane, psychic); the martial fey — redcaps, sprites — fight with vicious precision (piercing, slashing); treants crush (impact) and fear fire without wielding it.",
      "vulnerabilities": [],
      "resistances": [
        "arcane"
      ],
      "immunities": []
    },
    "fiend": {
      "name": "fiend",
      "description": "Devils, demons, and the infernal. Their appetites are wrath, hunger, vanity, despair, and acquisition.\n\nThe Hunger is Ur's contagion in Larion: Gaunt Fiends climb and drop from above; Maw Fiends break formed lines and shields; talking Ravener Fiends hold breaches until hunger overtakes curiosity. Radiant force, silver, and moonstone bite them.\n\nThe Ur Spawn cross bodily and rule whatever they can: fire-spitting Flameskin Imps ignore ordinary flame but water and killing cold snuff them; a Snatch-Tail Fiend drags one victim away (piercing) but flees if its tail is severed; a Flamewhip Overseer Fiend drives lesser spawn with fire and their nerve breaks when it falls; an Archfiend darkens the air (shadow), fixes on one mind (psychic), knows every subordinate's name, and keeps bargains to the letter. Stone-Hided Fiends use the armored fiend type.\n\nOther fiends include the dead-face-wearing, compulsively lying Ghul; the burning Nightmare; The Imps of the Basement, settled merchants; War-shriekers whose signal network survives any one death; and backwards-handed Rakshasa. Not every fiend is hostile. Holy power burns them (radiant); fire and shadow are home (resist). They target the weak, wounded, and beloved, escalate theatrically, and flee shamelessly when losing.",
      "vulnerabilities": [
        "radiant"
