      "resistances": [],
      "immunities": []
    },
    "ooze": {
      "name": "ooze",
      "description": "The creeping dissolvers: gray oozes, black puddings, gelatinous cubes. The corridor's janitor — mindless, patient, and utterly without malice, dissolving flesh, leather, and metal alike. They hunt nothing; they are simply where the food walks. A clean corridor in a filthy dungeon is the tell. Blades pass through (piercing/slashing resist); poison means nothing (immune); frost slows and stiffens them (vulnerability). In combat: slow engulfment and acid contact (acid); they cannot be frightened, fooled, or bargained with; the play is to see them first, and the horror is being caught.",
