    "shadow creature": {
      "name": "shadow creature",
      "description": "The darkness-sustained: shades, void-touched beings, smoke spirits, and nightmare things. They are not undead — darkness feeds them the way air feeds the living, and light is not merely painful but starving. They gather where the world's shadow pools: bleed-sites, tainted ground, and the deep places light has never reached. The bonded Shades of the Black Tower's inquisitors are this family's disciplined exception — leashed, worked, and studied. In combat: they strike from darkness and retreat into it, drink warmth and light from flames and lanterns, and press hardest when the last light gutters; point and edge pass through the darkness that holds them, while mass can scatter the shape (piercing and slashing resist); holy radiance burns them (radiant vulnerability), and cold and dark are home (shadow, frost resist).",
      "vulnerabilities": [
        "radiant"
      ],
      "resistances": [
        "shadow",
        "frost",
        "piercing",
        "slashing"
      ],
      "immunities": []
    },
    "spectral undead": {
      "name": "spectral undead",
      "description": "The bodiless dead: ghosts, specters, wraiths, banshees, and shadows. A ghost stays for unfinished business, and the business is the story — find it and the haunting can be laid without a blow struck, which is often the better play. Specters are bodiless malice that chill what they touch; wraiths are hate without a body, withering the living where old battles were fought; the banshee keens before a death in the old families, and harming her invites the death she sang; a shadow peels off its victim's own shadow and hunts lightless places. Weapons pass through them (piercing, slashing, and impact resist); a direct attack on the mind reaches what no weapon can (psychic vulnerability); holy power burns (radiant vulnerability); cold and dread announce them before they are seen. In combat: they ignore armor and flesh-logic, striking at warmth, breath, and courage; they defend the place, grief, or hate that holds them and cannot leave it far behind.",
      "vulnerabilities": [
        "radiant",
        "psychic"
      ],
      "resistances": [
        "piercing",
        "slashing",
        "impact"
      ],
      "immunities": [
        "poison"
      ]
    },
    "stone construct": {
      "name": "stone construct",
      "description": "The stone guardians: gargoyles, stone golems, and animated statues. The gargoyle was always watching — it perched among the ornaments for years before the moment it moved. Stone constructs guard temples, tombs, and thresholds with the patience of their material; they are bound to a place and an order, and pursuing beyond it breaks their purpose. Stage the stillness first: statue-count wrong, dust disturbed, a head that has turned. In combat: immense weight and crushing blows (impact); blades chip uselessly (piercing/slashing resist); acid eats the binding stone (vulnerability); they defend their ground and do not chase far.",
      "vulnerabilities": [
        "acid"
