    "undead spellcaster": {
      "name": "undead spellcaster",
      "description": "The dead sustained by their own magic: liches, dracoliches, mummy lords, and necromantic archmages who refused to end. These are top-shelf, singular threats — a lich holds one seat in the whole world, always with a project underway, and the project is the story: the phylactery logic, the layered minions, the patient decades-long plan. A mummy lord is a Sun King who refused to stay dead and commands its whole tomb. Never generate one casually; their presence reorganizes a region's dead around them. In combat: death magic in waves (shadow, arcane), summoned and commanded lesser dead, contingencies prepared in advance; destroying the body is rarely the end unless the anchor is found.",
      "vulnerabilities": [
        "radiant"
      ],
      "resistances": [
        "shadow",
        "arcane",
        "piercing"
      ],
      "immunities": [
        "poison"
      ]
    },
    "venomous beast": {
      "name": "venomous beast",
      "description": "The toxin-bearers: giant spiders, giant scorpions, plague-beasts, and the web-country's lesser hunters. Ambush plus venom is the whole logic — strike once, withdraw, and let the poison do the work; stage the venom's effect concretely (slowing, sickening, dropping) so players feel the clock. Web-country is a place: silk-wrapped bundles overhead tell the story before the spider does. The Spinners of the Greatweb are not venomous beasts — they are the telepathic spider-folk of one region, a thinking people. In combat: skittering ambush, bite and sting (piercing, poison); plates, thick hide, and many-jointed bodies turn a clean edge (slashing resist); webs and terrain traps; fire clears webs and panics the weavers (fire vulnerability); they flee a fight that turns even.",
      "vulnerabilities": [
        "fire"
      ],
      "resistances": [
        "poison",
        "slashing"
      ],
      "immunities": []
    },
    "water elemental": {
      "name": "water elemental",
      "description": "The living water: spring-spirits, wave-shapes, and the animate flood. A summoned elemental is loosed, not born — somebody called it, and the summoner is the story. Kinds: spring-spirits keep one pool or well and drown whatever fouls it; wave-shapes rear beside a hull in heavy weather and pull the crew down with the swell; the flood-shape is a river's whole temper walking, carrying trees, stone, and whole roofs in its weight. Water's temperament is patience with weight behind it — it finds the low way, wears things down, and does not hurry. In combat: crushing surge, grapple, and the drowning hold (impact); point and edge part the water and it closes behind them, while mass can break its shape apart (piercing and slashing resist); footing gone and lungs filling; fire gutters out against it (fire resist); lightning runs through it end to end (shock vulnerability). What water takes, it takes downward.",
