    "hillhome_pie_promise": {
      "title": "A Pie and a Promise",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "Pernilla Balewood owns the Saucy Chicken Tavern, but its debt gives the Goldspoons a claim against it. The party has brought her prize truffle-hog Uncle Phineas safely home. Percival Goldspoon is authorized to settle the family claim.\n\nSuggested turn 1 — Welcome and interruption. Pernilla welcomes Phineas and thanks his rescuers. If she promised three halfling-alchemy health potions and has not paid them, she hands them over. Percival interrupts, declaring that the tavern is already his by law and custom. End with room for the party to answer him.\n\nSuggested turn 2 — The public wager. Percival wants everyone to admit he will run the tavern better. He challenges Pernilla to the Newmoon Fair pie contest and publicly promises to cancel the debt and relinquish the Goldspoons' claim if her pie beats his. He boasts that he has bought the finest moonbloom truffles the kobolds could supply, at an exorbitant price. His certainty invites a response.\n\nSuggested turn 3 — A chance to beat him. Let someone present explain that the kobolds' best finds are not the finest truffles in Moonbloom Woods. Prefer Hobson Mossbottom, the tavern's merry, booming drinking champion, if he is present. Kobolds copy other people's digging; a trained hog can smell what they walk over. Phineas responds expressively without speaking. Pernilla asks the party to take him to Moonbloom Woods beside Whitehill Kobold Warren and find a prize moonbloom for her pie. Name The Basket Path as the approach.\n\nAllow responses between these beats rather than delivering the entire exchange at once. Complete only after Percival's public promise, his purchase, and Pernilla's proposed expedition have been stated. Acceptance is the players' choice.",
