    "hillhome_kitchen_brief": {
      "title": "Where Is the Butter?",
      "targetTurns": 1,
      "beats": "Pernilla Balewood is preparing a moonbloom pie to beat Percival Goldspoon at the Newmoon Fair and save the Saucy Chicken Tavern. Percival has publicly promised to cancel the debt and surrender the Goldspoons' claim if her pie wins. The party's prize truffle is ready in the kitchen. The Fair is about to open; pie entries close later at the judging table.\n\nPernilla delights in the truffle, then discovers that the butter and eggs are missing. Bark and Dandy each insist the other was collecting them. She needs enough butter and eggs for one large pie. Tobin Greenbottle at Greenbottle's Goods can supply butter; Rosie Butterworth at the Sleeping Bear Inn can spare eggs. The rest of the kitchen supplies are ready. Give the party these two destinations clearly, and let them offer supplies or substitutes of their own instead.\n\nKeep this a brisk comic kitchen scene with room for a response. End after the two needs, their sources, and the deadline have been stated. Do not narrate the errands or move the party to the shops.",
