      "targetTurns": 2,
      "beats": "Pernilla Balewood and her helpers are making the Saucy Chicken's moonbloom pie for the Newmoon Fair. The party has provided the prize truffle, butter, and eggs; the rest of the ingredients are ready. Beating Percival Goldspoon's entry will cancel the tavern's debt under his public wager. Entries are still open.\n\nSuggested turn 1 — Choose one kitchen crisis: the pastry lid collapses, helpers argue over the recipe, Phineas demands his share, or too many willing hands interfere with the same task. Put the problem before the party and let them decide how to help. Use established relationships and earlier mishaps.\n\nSuggested turn 2 — Follow their attempt through to a finished pie. Failure creates flour-covered clothes, dented pride, an owed favor, or a peculiar-looking crust, not a ruined expedition. Pernilla can rescue an imperfect attempt. The finished pie tastes excellent. Name it Pernilla's Moonbloom Pie and let the party or a helper they choose take charge of it. The judging table is at The Fairground in Hillhome.\n\nKeep the scene in the tavern kitchen. Do not bring Ember here; he belongs to Hearthhome. Complete when the pie is finished and entrusted for delivery. Do not narrate travel to the Fairground.",
