    "grell_isadora_offer": {
      "title": "Isadora Lorne: A Sign Below",
      "targetTurns": 2,
      "beats": "Keep the scene in The Fist & Flagon in Ardan's Watch. Isadora \"Easy\" Lorne is present as a young, thin, muscular veteran adventurer with a huge two-handed maul within reach and a small brass god-token riveted to one bracer. Let the practical leather armor, field coat, bracers, and weapon make her identity immediately legible. Give her an easy confidence and direct warmth; do not frame her as a fortune-teller, a circus performer, or a formal officer delivering a briefing.\n\nHave Isadora explain her simple faith if the player asks why she takes difficult work: when the gods put a problem in her path, they are giving her a chance to do something that matters. She does not spend time decoding omens or claim that the player is fated to help. If asked why she approached the party, have her say in substance: \"The gods put this problem in front of me and put you here when it arrived. I intend to follow the sign. A sign is an invitation, not a command.\"\n\nHave Isadora explain the ordinary pattern below the city in short, clear pieces: Grell kobolds raid upward, the League contains the incidents, and rival hosts usually keep one another divided. Then make the change concrete. Rumor says a kobold warlord calling himself an emperor is distributing oversized Fourth Empire arms, imposing discipline, and unifying the hosts. Baska, a kobold League informant who opposes the unification, has information the League needs. She will meet the party at the Imperial Shrine to Avarice. Isadora needs the party to go below with her and help her make contact with Baska; do not frame Baska's eventual movements as an escort obligation.\n\nMake the stakes discreet rather than abstract. A public raid could kill civilians, cause a panic, drive unprepared people into the Hollows, and give the Syndicate an excuse to seize control of salvage or the Delvers' Lift. Isadora should explain that she is taking the quiet route because the problem matters, not because she enjoys hiding behind League procedure. Let the player challenge that choice.\n\nHave Isadora state the route plainly: the only way down from Ardan's Watch into Grell Hollows is the Delvers' Lift in the Basement beneath Old Town; it descends to The Scrabble. She will accompany the party to the Lift and into the Hollows. End with a clear offer to investigate the new unification, meet Baska, and stop the escalation before it becomes a surface war, with good pay of one hundred florins for each person in the party. This event is complete once the offer, the Lift route, the sign-based reason for recruiting the party, and the stakes are clear and the player is free to accept, decline, or ask questions. Do not assume acceptance, romance, or permanent recruitment.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "write-string",
          "key": "grell_stage",
          "operator": "set",
          "value": "investigation_offered"
        },
        {
          "type": "quest-init",
          "operator": "set",
          "value": "Meet with Baska"
        },
        {
          "type": "party-next-step-set",
          "text": "Accept Isadora's offer, then go with her to the Delvers' Lift in the Basement beneath Old Town and descend to The Scrabble in Grell Hollows.",
          "source": "objective"
        }
      ]
    },
    "grell_baska_ambush": {
      "title": "Baska at the Shrine",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "Keep the scene at The Shrine Mouth of the Imperial Shrine to Avarice. Baska is already waiting in the entry among the broken portico and toppled columns. She has asked the party to come because she wants surface witnesses to see something, not merely hear her report. From deeper inside the shrine come the clatter of gear, boots and claws, shouted counts, banners snapping, and a heavy repeated rhythm. The walls and distance are thick enough that the kobolds inside cannot hear the party's approach. Baska says that rival hosts are reporting for duty under the new emperor's command.\n\nBefore Baska can lead the party to a concealed view, two specialized kobolds jump them in the entry: a kobold heavy wearing oversized Fourth Empire scrap and a kobold skirmisher with a jury-rigged ranged weapon and climbing gear. They attack immediately, using the columns, steps, and broken portico to block passage. Do not let them wait as a passive scout, and do not replace the attack with signs or a warning. Baska remains in the scene and may point out danger, take cover, or fight beside the party, but she does not solve the fight.\n\nOnce the two guards have been defeated, driven off, bypassed, or otherwise dealt with, Baska brings the party to a concealed overlook. They see a sizeable group of formerly squabbling kobolds reporting for duty: different host banners gathered beneath a larger imperial standard, oversized Fourth Empire armor strapped into place, and weapons carried with new discipline. A long serpentine war-shrieker emerges from an old signal passage and repeats a short order in Kragga's voice, telling the assembled kobolds to march out. Most of the muster obeys and leaves through the drowned halls, while a few kobolds remain behind as a rearguard. Baska explains what the sight means: Kragga has found the Horn of the First Host and uses old imperial signal passages to call bound war-shriekers that repeat his orders across the Hollows.\n\nThe remaining kobolds block the routes out and attack the party and Baska to silence the witnesses. Make the blockade physically and tactically legible; egress requires defeating, evading, bargaining past, or otherwise breaking the attackers' hold. Baska fights to survive and helps the party read the ruin, but she must remain alive. Do not invent an unnamed League contact, kill Baska, or resolve the scene by teleporting the party away. Complete the event when the immediate rearguard has been broken or bypassed and the party has witnessed the muster. Baska remains a living League contact; do not require the party to escort her to Ardan's Watch or state that she has already reached the surface.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "write-boolean",
          "key": "grell_muster_witnessed",
          "operator": "set",
          "value": true
        },
        {
