    },
    "grell_volnom_council_report": {
      "title": "The League Report",
      "targetTurns": 2,
      "beats": "Stage this in Watchtower - League Hall in Ardan's Watch, with Mona Vashti receiving the party's report at the League's main table or in a quieter corner of the hall. The party may already have delivered the report to Mona, Volnom the Wayfarer, or another clearly established League representative elsewhere in Ardan's Watch; if so, treat this scene as the formal League recording and response, not as a demand that the party repeat facts they have already established. Baska need not be present and must not be assumed to have been transported into Ardan's Watch; the League is acting on the information the party brought back from the shrine.\n\nConfirm the essential report in natural conversation: Baska showed the party an organized kobold muster; Kragga has found the Horn of the First Host in the Imperial Arsenal; and the horn's surviving signal passages call and coordinate bound war-shriekers. Establish that the long serpentine fiends repeat short orders in Kragga's voice across the Hollows, giving separate kobold hosts a reach and timing they never had before. The horn carries commands; it is not Big Buzzer and it does not attract beetles. Do not require the player to recite every detail again if the report has already been delivered.\n\nLet Mona or the receiving League representative ask only the questions needed for containment: what the party saw, how the signals travel, what Kragga is trying to unify, and how much the surface knows. Keep the response discreet and inside the League Hall; do not turn it into a public announcement, do not require Isadora's presence, and do not begin the Greenmeadow incident in the same scene. Complete the event once the League has accepted the report and has a concrete reason to watch for the next surface breach.",
