    "dq_briefing_drael": {
      "title": "Dragon Queen Briefing: Draelkharion",
      "targetTurns": 1,
      "beats": "Continue the briefing with Draelkharion, Prince of the Dead.\n\nRennick names Draelkharion as the nearest Harbinger and the first practical target: a dracolich in Silvervale, lairing deep in the City of Ancestors with one fragment of the Seal of Suleyvan. The dead are rising around the necropolis because of him.\n\nAlayne explains the local obstacle. A Pyre altar hidden beneath Muckside is feeding a false-fire ward over the deep routes into the City of Ancestors. That ward blinds scouts, fouls portal work, and makes stronger League strike teams vanish from sight or turn back before they can reach Draelkharion.\n\nMake the logic clear in the briefing: Draelkharion is the Harbinger, the City of Ancestors is his lair, and the Pyre altar is the obstacle keeping better adventurers from reaching him. The rookies are not being sent to kill a dragon today. Their first useful job is smaller and local: investigate the fires in Ardan's Watch, find the Pyre cultists, and break the altar that is keeping the way to Draelkharion closed.\n\nEnd the beat with a clear handoff that the briefing is not over, pivoting to the next Seal fragment and Nuur-Suthra, the Flame Undying.",
