    "dq_briefing_nuur_suthra": {
      "title": "Dragon Queen Briefing: Nuur-Suthra",
      "targetTurns": 1,
      "beats": "Continue the briefing with Nuur-Suthra, the Flame Undying.\n\nRennick names Nuur-Suthra as another Harbinger and the holder of another Seal fragment. Nuur-Suthra is a dragon of living fire worshipped along the Alar Coast and laired in the fallen Celestial Citadel of Alar.\n\nAlayne explains why killing it is not enough. Nuur-Suthra returns from death because a single anchor-fire burns at the heart of the citadel, bound into a great sun-diamond in the engine below. As long as that anchor-fire remains, the Flame Undying can collapse to embers and come back.\n\nMake the path clear in the briefing: reach the Celestial Citadel of Alar, get past the dragon-worshippers and old defenses holding its outer halls, extinguish or break the anchor-fire, then confront Nuur-Suthra and recover its Seal fragment.\n\nEnd the beat with a clear handoff that the briefing is continuing, pivoting from fire and sky to Astarieth the Risen in the drowned fens.",
