    "dq_briefing_form_up": {
      "title": "Dragon Queen Briefing: Forming Up",
      "targetTurns": 1,
      "beats": "After the briefing, stay in the Watchtower - League Hall as the room breaks into urgent, noisy motion. The briefing is over; this beat is about giving the player social and practical options before the first field step.\n\nSurface a few possible people or small groups the player could work with, speak to, recruit, impress, avoid, or rival. Give the AI permission to make them vivid and capable: dashing, sharp, fearsome, funny, strange, hungry for glory, competent under pressure, or already carrying a useful lead. Favor youth, color, chemistry, and momentum. Do not reduce them to generic labels like human warrior, dwarf fighter, or elf archer. They do not all need names, and none should be forced into the party.\n\nUseful options can include a confident low-rank adventurer looking for a partner, a small crew with a missing role, a local fire-witness who needs help, a mapper or scout with a route toward Muckside, a healer or arcanist with nerve, or a rival who wants the same first lead. Keep the options broad enough that the player can choose direction.\n\nEnd with the player clearly free to act: talk to someone, form up, investigate the fires in Ardan's Watch, follow a lead toward Muckside, check maps or postings, or leave the hall.",
