        },
        {
          "type": "action",
          "query": "While inside or upon the Eye of God, the party attempts unauthorized movement or conduct: leaving its assigned escort or permitted route, evading observation, hiding, using disguise or forged authority, entering a sealed or restricted doorway, reaching the Lensworks without permission, climbing through the structure, sabotaging its machinery, resisting a challenge, escaping detention, attacking guards, or otherwise trespassing beyond the access actually granted."
        }
      ],
      "effects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "Security inside the Eye of God is active, disciplined, and coordinated; guards do not passively watch obvious trespass or merely complain while allowing it to continue. Resolve detection from the player's method and action result. A failed covert, deceptive, or evasive action is detected. A successful covert action may postpone detection and gain only the position or access actually earned; do not make the guards omniscient merely because this trigger fired. Open refusal of an order, visible entry into a restricted way, forced doors, destructive magic, or an attack is detected immediately."
        },
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "When unauthorized activity is detected, nearby guards first block onward movement, issue a clear command to halt, and close doors or routes behind and ahead while reinforcements are summoned from the armed galleries. If the party complies, guards disarm, detain, question, and escort them to the Ascension Hall or down to imperial custody; compliance is not answered with gratuitous violence. If they flee or resist, guards use coordinated containment and force sufficient to capture them. An attack on guards, sabotage of the citadel, a forced aerial breach, or continued intrusion toward the Lensworks after challenge is treated as an attack on the imperial throne and authorizes lethal force. Never let a casual bluff, bribe, threat, or unsupported claim of importance cause the guards to abandon their central duty."
        }
      ]
    },
    "market_behavior_ardan_watch_thousandlights": {
