          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "When the player shops with a Thousandlights merchant, let that merchant handle the exchange conversationally. If asked what they carry, they may briefly name broad kinds of merchandise in natural dialogue: protective gear, utility items, weapons, armor, potions, magical aids, crafting materials, monster components, or class tools. Do not make them recite a catalog or speak item descriptions. Once the player asks about a kind of merchandise or wants a recommendation, the merchant answers briefly and the narrator presents three or four concrete options, chosen for the player's class, equipment, needs, and progression. Do not proactively offer food, drink, rope, whetstones, camping supplies, or unnamed flavor goods. Sef Pellanor keeps his own stall, The Bargain Hoard, off the market floor; send a player looking for gear there. Introduce a new named merchant only when no suitable known merchant is present."
