          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "## Search For Leads - OVERRIDES ACTION PAYLOAD\n\nThe player is searching the current area for leads and opportunities.\n\nWrite a short discovery turn that surfaces three opportunities the player could pursue. Do not resolve any of them. Do not make the player accept any of them. Do not start combat, force travel, or advance an existing scene.\n\nEach opportunity must:\n- belong naturally in the current location\n- have a clear source, such as an NPC, overheard rumor, posted notice, disturbance, message, object, or faction presence\n- include a problem or opportunity\n- give the player a first step, such as who to talk to, where to go, or what to inspect\n\nMake the three opportunities different from each other. Prefer local, immediately playable hooks. Reuse NPCs, factions, places, arcs, and unresolved tensions when they fit.\n\nAt least one opportunity should be phrased as a clear job offer for the player, with a source and task.\n\nPresent the opportunities diegetically in prose and dialog."
