      "script": "storage.guilds = storage.guilds || {}\nconst blood = storage.guilds.blood\nif (!blood || !blood.member) { skip = true }\nif (!skip && storage.inCompanySpace !== true) { skip = true }\n\nif (!skip) {\n  const rank = blood.rank || storage.bloodRank || 'hired_blade'\n  const instructions = {\n    'hired_blade': 'The party are Hired Blades of the Crimson Company: outsiders on the writ, useful and watched. IF Company work is surfaced, keep it local, survivable, paid, and varied. Culls are the staple but no more than a third of it: strigoi on the terraces, ghouls in Charnel Mountain’s upper workings, a wolf pack on the pass road, something in a barrow nobody has opened since the Schism. The rest is people and searching: a lordless band out of a valley with no lord left, taking the pass road; a watchpost that stopped answering; a pressing crew that went up the high terraces and did not come down; a tincture wagon that never arrived. Each job should quietly teach one rule of this country — the levy, the truce, what silver does, what a stranger is worth here. Do not offer house-interior work, court business, or anything that assumes standing among vampires. Disregard this instruction if no Company work is being offered or discussed.',\n    'redblade': 'The party are Redblades of the Crimson Company, marked by the lord they serve so that no other vampire may feed on them. IF Company work is surfaced, it is the houses’ own business rather than valley work: carrying something between rivals under the Black Gate truce, finding out what House Vyrel is doing, bringing House Malren a specimen or a page intact, finding who is selling where a lord sleeps by day and getting there first, putting down a vampire made six weeks ago who cannot control it, hunting an old Company blade who turned and knows exactly how it is done, quiet problems a lord would rather not have in writing, and errands that put the party inside courts and estates. The pay is better and the failure is worse. Disregard this instruction if no Company work is being offered or discussed.',\n    'fledgling': 'The party hold the Blood and a Crimson Company captaincy: made vampires with soldiers under them. IF Company work is surfaced, it assumes command and it assumes night: leading Company blades on a cull or a raid, work that requires being somewhere no mortal could go or survive, standing for a lord where a mortal would not be listened to, and answering for what the soldiers do. The Company no longer issues them silver. Disregard this instruction if no Company work is being offered or discussed.',\n    'blooded': 'The party are Blooded and deal with the houses as principals. IF Company work is surfaced, it is house business at the top: the Ferals at Hollowfast, whatever is coming through at Wardfall, rivals moving against a lord, the Syndicate’s price for something, and anything touching the Vale Sable and what is still alive inside it. Work at this level creates enemies who answer back. Disregard this instruction if no Company work is being offered or discussed.',\n  }\n  const instruction = instructions[rank]\n  if (instruction) { effects.push({ type: 'story', instruction: instruction }) }\n}",
