      "script": "const area = check({ type: 'party-area' }) || 'The Upper Workings'\nconst PAYOFF = {\n    'The Headworks': 'Pay it off small and surface-honest: a prospector\\'s cache in a collapsed counting-office, 10 to 30 florins in coin and scrap, mining kit, and the effects of somebody who did not come out. Use exact catalogue names such as Smith\\'s Hammer, Craftsman\\'s Toolkit, Iron Dagger, Leather Boots, or Stamina Draught.',\n    'The Upper Workings': 'Pay it off in silver: a stope with the seam still showing, worth 40 to 90 florins to anyone who can carry it down, plus what a dead delver was carrying. Use exact catalogue names such as Silver-Tipped Bolts of Radiance, Iron Shortsword, Leather Jerkin, Light Crossbow, or Mongo\\'s Medium Health Potion. Silver out of Charnel is what arms the whole region against the curse, and the party should be told what it is worth to the Crescent House.',\n    'The Deep Diggings': 'Pay it off richly and make the weight real: the deep seams run 100 to 200 florins of silver per load, and a load is heavy enough to change how a fight goes. Add what the dead down here were carrying. Use exact catalogue names such as Moonstone Dagger of Radiant, Silver Binding Chain, Silver-Tipped Bolts of Radiance, or Greater Stamina Draught. State plainly that everything taken from this depth has to be carried back up through what they came past.',\n  }\nconst instruction = PAYOFF[area] || PAYOFF['The Upper Workings']\neffects.push({ type: 'story', instruction: 'The party has just resolved something in Charnel Mountain. Pay it off now, tied to the level they are on. ' + instruction + ' Name what they find. Then telegraph one thing deeper: a richer seam showing in a wall, a draught of colder air, a winze going down, or the sound of a flock moving somewhere below. If the party chooses to go back up with what they have, respect that.' })",
