  "imagePromptConfiguration": {
    "npcs": "Write one cohesive GPT Image 2 portrait prompt; output only that prompt. Use only source text. Preserve supplied gender, species, anatomy, coloring, clothing, equipment, identifying features, and broad age category using the allowed terms below. Use role or temperament only when stated. Keep unspecified details simple. Stage expression, pose, light, and composition visually, not biographically.\n\nSTYLE\nBegin with:\n\"Painterly-drawn fantasy character art: opaque planes, designed values, broken contours, and brush strokes define face, grouped hair/fabric, armor, equipment; some edges dissolve into paint. No vector outlines, comic inking, photoreal detail, flat cel fills, airbrushed skin, or glossy CGI. Coherent light, chromatic shadows, harmonious color, polished 2D finish. Adult proportions and expression; natural eyes and jaw; no pointed chin, oversized eyes, childlike, or chibi anatomy.\"\n\nCOMPOSITION\nFor humanoids, hybrids, and humanoid undead, make a portrait from head to thigh. Put the face in the upper half and keep the silhouette square-readable. Default to a near-frontal pose with squared shoulders and a slight head or weight shift. Use another view only when the source calls for it. Keep the full head, hair, shoulders, outer arms, and body inside the canvas with generous clear margins from every border. Show hands free, visible, empty, and unobstructed. Keep the body and silhouette clear of foreground objects; source-supported worn clothing and equipment may remain visible. Use posture for energy without literal combat, jumping, or motion blur. Adapt nonhumanoid subjects to show defining anatomy clearly and keep their silhouette within clear margins.\n\nSUBJECT AND ANATOMY\nUse a source-supported expression and one load-bearing identity detail. If the source explicitly gives a role, occupation, faction, or temperament, let it guide pose and environment; never infer a role from clothing. State supplied species, gender, anatomy, facial structure, and distinctive features before clothing; preserve nonhuman proportions. An ordinary animal keeps its natural animal anatomy and posture; never turn it into a humanoid, beastfolk person, mascot, or clothed character unless the source explicitly establishes that form. Keep unknown traits simple; treat hair, fur, feathers, flame, and foliage as bold masses.\nFor humanoids, use only child, young adult, adult, or mature as age descriptors; mature is the highest age level. Never output a numbered age, decade, or terms such as old, older, elderly, aged, or middle-aged. Translate stronger source age language to mature. Convey maturity through hair, posture, expression, facial structure, costume, or role, never through facial surface.\nDo not describe facial surface or skin texture. Never output pores, wrinkles, creases, crow's feet, etched or age lines, weathered or sun-creased skin, rough skin, or similar surface language. Skin coloration remains allowed.\nSpecies anatomy: catkin—feline face, short muzzle, fur, pointed ears, whiskers, slit pupils; wolfkin—lupine face, canine muzzle, fur, pointed ears; dragonkin—reptilian face, scales, ridged brow, dragon jaw, supplied horns; demonborn—humanoid face, horns, supplied coloration; gajanari/elephantfolk—elephant head, broad ears, long trunk, supplied coloration; imp-kin—small horned humanoid, colorful nonhuman coloration; hobgoblin—angular humanoid features; bugbear—broad flat face, heavy fur, large build; lizardfolk—reptilian face, scales, flat snout; frogkin—amphibian face, wide mouth, large eyes; bearkin—ursine face, broad muzzle, heavy fur; ratkin—rodent face, narrow snout, large ears, whiskers, bristled fur; foxkin—vulpine face, narrow muzzle, pointed ears, fur; boarkin—porcine face, broad nose, bristles, supplied tusks; hawkkin—avian face, hooked beak, feathers, sharp eyes; serpentfolk—ophidian face, scales, slit pupils, no external nose.\n\nROLE REGISTER\nFor a source-identified bandit, outlaw, raider, ambusher, or highway robber, use a ready stance, practical layers, and a wilderness-road or ruin vignette; keep action poised.\n\nBACKGROUND\nCreate a portrait background in idealized world-vignette style: a believable scene fragment with equal compositional care. Use cropped foreground, readable middle-ground cue, quieter distance, overlap, scale change, perspective, and one shared light.\nChoose it from concrete source cues—stated location, role, activity, clothing, materials, tools, magic, species, or weather. Use broad environmental language tied to the supplied character and setting. Keep value behind the face calm and the silhouette clear; use saturated harmonious subject-derived color with complementary separation. Keep the background unlettered: no text or words; decorative symbols are acceptable. End with one concise \"Background:\" sentence naming scene, palette, and light.\n\nOUTPUT\nOutput one cohesive natural-language portrait prompt only. Keep it 150-210 words, max 230, and stop when complete.",
    "locations": "Write one cohesive natural-language prompt for GPT Image 2 and output only that prompt. Preserve supplied architecture, terrain, materials, climate, and season. Do not invent ruins, wreckage, corpses, banners, or signage. Do not name artists, franchises, or media. Do not include text or lettering.\n\nSTYLE\nBegin with:\n\"Contemporary Western environment illustration in opaque gouache and bold modern-print shapes. Build the scene from large connected local-color planes and three grouped value levels. Establish architecture and terrain as a few big designed masses first, then add surface marks only where a material needs declaring — stone coursing, roof texture, foliage clumps, water movement — leaving the large planes otherwise intact. Broad directional brush strokes, calm readable large areas, finer marks reserved for the focal structure. Alternate clean shape boundaries with visible painted edges. Muted designed palette of three or four hues with one saturated accent carrying the scene. Shadows stay chromatic and keep visible form; no flat black silhouettes. Separate distance by value and hue shift rather than haze. Warm, characterful, and highly legible at thumbnail size.\"\n\nNo photographic texture frequency, no airbrushed gradients, no lens bloom, no volumetric rays, no linework or graphic outlines.\n\nCOMPOSITION\nLandscape 16:9 frame for a full-viewport VN backdrop. Eye-level arrival view as someone walking in would see it; the camera stands among the subject, never above it looking down.\n\nThe middle of the frame carries the identifying subject and the horizon, and must read as this specific place on its own, because object-cover and narrow-screen crops preserve this band. The upper portion carries sky, canopy or upper structure with designed shape interest. The lower portion carries a near foreground that frames rather than informs — a wall corner, a rail, foliage, a stretch of ground. Keep the identifying silhouette and horizon inside the center-safe band, and keep the lower centre quiet in value so dialogue and character overlays remain readable.\n\nGive the scene two temperature families: warm lit planes against cool shadow, or the reverse. Avoid single-hue scenes and avoid images that sit entirely in the middle of the value scale.\n\nInclude boats, carts, or distant figures where the place would plausibly be busy.\n\nVary camera distance, time of day, weather, and dominant hue between locations so neighbouring places do not share a palette.",
    "areas": "Write one cohesive natural-language prompt for GPT Image 2 and output only that prompt. Preserve supplied architecture, materials, furnishing, climate, and season. Do not invent ruins, wreckage, corpses, or signage. Do not name artists, franchises, or media. Do not include text or lettering.\n\nSTYLE\nBegin with:\n\"Contemporary Western environment illustration in opaque gouache and bold modern-print shapes. Build the scene from large connected local-color planes and three grouped value levels. Establish architecture and terrain as a few big designed masses first, then add surface marks only where a material needs declaring — stone coursing, roof texture, foliage clumps, water movement — leaving the large planes otherwise intact. Broad directional brush strokes, calm readable large areas, finer marks reserved for the focal structure. Alternate clean shape boundaries with visible painted edges. Muted designed palette of three or four hues with one saturated accent carrying the scene. Shadows stay chromatic and keep visible form; no flat black silhouettes. Separate distance by value and hue shift rather than haze. Warm, characterful, and highly legible at thumbnail size.\"\n\nNo photographic texture frequency, no airbrushed gradients, no lens bloom, no volumetric rays, no linework or graphic outlines.\n\nCOMPOSITION\nLandscape 16:9 frame for a full-viewport VN backdrop. Standing eye level at conversational distance inside the space, as though you have stopped a few steps in. Never an overview, never a framed view through a doorway.\n\nThis image is a stage that characters will be composited in front of. Keep the central column of the frame, from the lower edge up to roughly two-thirds height, quiet in value, chroma and detail — floor, ground, water, plain wall, or open air. Push the identifying features of the space into the left and right thirds and the upper third: a hearth, a window, shelving, a stair, hanging tools, a bar, a canopy, rigging.\n\nWhen the defining feature of a space sits at its centre, move the camera off-axis so that feature occupies a side third and open floor holds the middle.\n\nKeep the space in a mid-value range with soft internal contrast; avoid deep gloom and avoid glare. The space recedes through softness, not through darkness. Place the single saturated accent off-centre.\n\nState one clear light direction and hold it consistent across the frame.\n\nSmall, low-contrast figures may appear in the background above the central column; keep the central foreground column clear of people. No animals.",
